14:36:38.389 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":22,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A mild morning with rain Wind SSW. Cleared up in the afternoon Dined at home &amp; having a cold went to bed early</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":19,"lock":null}
14:36:38.389 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/19/23
14:36:38.389 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":23,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning. On going out, found the harbour in dreadful state of confusion &amp; much damage done in consequence of the immense land floods driving the ships adrift. Rode to Newcastle with J Tinley, saw W Chapman. He offered to take my bill at 6 months with another approved name to it, for 1000 or 1200. Refused &amp; dined with J Tinley. Wrote to William. Wind SW. Many ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":20,"lock":null}
