14:36:38.398 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":34,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but cold. Wind SSW. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":31,"lock":null}
14:36:38.398 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/31/35
14:36:38.398 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":35,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day &amp; mild. Wind SSW to WSW. Engaged in the morning in examining my father's old papers &amp; accounts in search of the Ariel's vouchers and burning such papers as were out of date &amp; useless. Dined at home &amp; at the whist club in the evening.</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":32,"lock":null}
14:36:38.398 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.399 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/31/35
14:36:38.399 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":35,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day &amp; mild. Wind SSW to WSW. Engaged in the morning in examining my father's old papers &amp; accounts in search of the Ariel's vouchers and burning such papers as were out of date &amp; useless. Dined at home &amp; at the whist club in the evening.</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":32,"lock":null}
14:36:38.399 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/1/4/8
14:36:38.399 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":8,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Again at Newcastle. Saw J Smith Senior &amp; Junior: the old gent: very kind, asked me to dine, &quot;no go&quot; entered upon the subject of the Ariel, showed them W S Brewer's accounts, they seemed to be of our opinion &amp; against any arbitration. Dined with Dixon, had a long conversation about his assisting me. He was extremely kind in his expressions, but said it was out of his power, from his heavy advances to others &amp; having heavy payments to make himself to but that he would consider about it. memo: Its what I expected, not much disappointed. A promise ought to be held sacred. Cold day with rain afternoon</p>","pageId":686,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":5,"lock":null}
14:36:38.399 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
