14:36:38.402 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":13,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got captain Hallam to moor the Hope securely by carrying an anchor out astern. Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at Mrs Greenhours, met a large party, a regular squeeze; quadrille &amp; broke up at 12 o'clock. It was cold with snow in the evening</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":10,"lock":null}
14:36:38.402 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/1/293
14:36:38.402 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":293,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Walked into the city. The Hope not to be out, the country craft having been sunk. Met <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Carr who went out of the city with us, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; in the evening went to Covent Garden Theater &amp; saw at &frac12; price the latter part of Hamlet &amp; Peter Welkins</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":277,"lock":null}
14:36:38.402 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/1/293
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":293,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Walked into the city. The Hope not to be out, the country craft having been sunk. Met <span class=highlight_yellow>Mr</span> Carr who went out of the city with us, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; in the evening went to Covent Garden Theater &amp; saw at &frac12; price the latter part of Hamlet &amp; Peter Welkins</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":277,"lock":null}
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/10/303
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":303,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind WSW with a shower of rain at 1 o'clock. Mr Mark went on board the Hope with me &amp; had some soup at 4 o'clock pm. The Hope load up &amp; at 5 o'clock got to sea with a fine leading wind &amp; beautiful weather &amp; prospect of making a quick passage. Burdon Main loaded her for 15 keels &amp; 6 char. Dined with J Tinley, J Dale, mark &amp; Temple there. Won at whist 16/6 Gave Stephenson 35 to pay pilotage etc. with.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":287,"lock":null}
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/10/303
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":303,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind WSW with a shower of rain at 1 o'clock. Mr Mark went on board the Hope with me &amp; had some soup at 4 o'clock pm. The Hope load up &amp; at 5 o'clock got to sea with a fine leading wind &amp; beautiful weather &amp; prospect of making a quick passage. Burdon Main loaded her for 15 keels &amp; 6 char. Dined with J Tinley, J Dale, mark &amp; Temple there. Won at whist 16/6 Gave Stephenson 35 to pay pilotage etc. with.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":287,"lock":null}
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/11/304
14:36:38.403 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":304,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about WNW. Went to Newcastle &amp; saw the Dixons, Smith of Joyston &amp; returned with J Tinley to dinner. Wrote to William of the sailing of the Hope. A few ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":288,"lock":null}
