14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":325,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Continuance of fine weather &amp; wind NNW. Out shooting &amp; killed 1 &frac12; braces of birds. Wrote to Mr Vernon &amp; R Snowdon</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":308,"lock":null}
14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/4/296
14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":296,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind WSW. Cleared up towards the middle of the day &amp; turned out a fine afternoon. Went down to the ship about 1 o'clock pm. Found her nearly out. Watt came on board. Sailed about 3 o'clock &amp; got below Woolwich &amp; brought up, where Watt left us. A breeze springing up got underway again about 9 o'clock against the flood but obliged again to let go our anchor about 11 o'clock for want of wind! For the night William slept on board. Brought today a life preserver for 18/- Some white &amp; coloured neckcloths for &pound;2</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":280,"lock":null}
14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
