14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":297,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind South. Got underway from off _____ at 11 o'clock am with a fresh breeze, landed William at Gravesend. At 1 o'clock pm. At 4 o'clock passed through Shoe Hole 8 o'clock abreast of Harwich &amp; 10 o'clock off the Lowestoft Light &amp; turned in for the night. Blowing fresh.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":281,"lock":null}
14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/298
14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
14:36:38.421 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/298
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/299
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":299,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>About 7 o'clock got bound. Flamborough Head at 10 o'clock. Off Robin Hoods bay blowing hard with squalls at 11 o'clock between the bay &amp; Whitby met a fleet of London vessels. Blowing hard. Nearly run down one vessel owing to his own obstinacy or keeping a bad lookout. Stowed trysail &amp; main sail &amp; took in jib. Very dark ahead. At 12 o'clock or little after it, clear weather but continued to blow off Hunt Cliff Foot. Turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":283,"lock":null}
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/6/299
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":299,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>About 7 o'clock got bound. Flamborough Head at 10 o'clock. Off Robin Hoods bay blowing hard with squalls at 11 o'clock between the bay &amp; Whitby met a fleet of London vessels. Blowing hard. Nearly run down one vessel owing to his own obstinacy or keeping a bad lookout. Stowed trysail &amp; main sail &amp; took in jib. Very dark ahead. At 12 o'clock or little after it, clear weather but continued to blow off Hunt Cliff Foot. Turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":283,"lock":null}
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/7/300
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":300,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 5 o'clock am off Sunderland with fine weather. Wind about WSW. Got a pilot on board. At 6 o'clock brought up off Shields Bar, turned out dressed &amp; landed in Tynemouth Haven. Breakfasted in Dockwray Square. Mrs Scott not up being rather unwell. Went up to Newcastle but the Carrs busy from a fortnight to three weeks, returned to Shields by steam &amp; fixed the Hope to take Burdon main to be load up under the spout on Friday. The ship towed safe into the harbour by a steam boat. Blowing a gale of wind from about WSW. Dined with Mrs Scott. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":284,"lock":null}
14:36:38.422 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/7/300
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":300,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 5 o'clock am off Sunderland with fine weather. Wind about WSW. Got a pilot on board. At 6 o'clock brought up off Shields Bar, turned out dressed &amp; landed in Tynemouth Haven. Breakfasted in Dockwray Square. Mrs Scott not up being rather unwell. Went up to Newcastle but the Carrs busy from a fortnight to three weeks, returned to Shields by steam &amp; fixed the Hope to take Burdon main to be load up under the spout on Friday. The ship towed safe into the harbour by a steam boat. Blowing a gale of wind from about WSW. Dined with Mrs Scott. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":284,"lock":null}
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/8/301
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":301,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Received a letter from William with the Hope's Balance Note for &pound;63.18/-  Engaged all the morning on board ship. Got the ballast out. Dined at home. Mrs Scott not well. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. W Temple there. Won 10/- at whist. Several ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":285,"lock":null}
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/8/301
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":301,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Received a letter from William with the Hope's Balance Note for &pound;63.18/-  Engaged all the morning on board ship. Got the ballast out. Dined at home. Mrs Scott not well. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. W Temple there. Won 10/- at whist. Several ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":285,"lock":null}
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/10/9/302
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":302,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Made the Hope's book up. On board the ship under the spout. Got some keels in. Set the new for-topmast backstays. The Lady Jane arrived from Greenland with 15 fish, a full ship. Gave Stephenson &pound;30. Made an agreement with the washerwoman for the quarter at 1 &frac12; guinea. Dined with J Tindley. Won at whist 4/-</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":286,"lock":null}
14:36:38.423 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
