14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":349,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day, but blowing hard from SSW. On board the Amity. Went over the water to see Mr P Laing respecting Che Harry's account, but did not see him, he being in London. Dined at home. Suppered with H Harry. Received a letter from William.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":332,"lock":null}
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/25/350
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":350,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly pleasant day. Wind W by S. Employed all the morning in unpacking the <span class=highlight_yellow>tenure</span> books we brought from Ireland. Dined at Mr Craiges, a large party.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":333,"lock":null}
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/25/350
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":350,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly pleasant day. Wind W by S. Employed all the morning in unpacking the <span class=highlight_yellow>tenure</span> books we brought from Ireland. Dined at Mr Craiges, a large party.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":333,"lock":null}
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/26/351
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":351,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair day. Wind W. Received a letter this morning from William of Frys &amp; Chapmans failure which surprised me much, the consequence was a run upon Chapmans <span class=highlight_yellow>House</span> here, but which I believe ended towards the evening. The bank are otherwise not affected by Frys failure having known for a fortnight it was to happen &amp; consequently preparing for a run, they suffer no losses. At the theatre in the evening. Much amused.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":334,"lock":null}
14:36:38.433 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/26/351
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":351,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair day. Wind W. Received a letter this morning from William of Frys &amp; Chapmans failure which surprised me much, the consequence was a run upon Chapmans <span class=highlight_yellow>House</span> here, but which I believe ended towards the evening. The bank are otherwise not affected by Frys failure having known for a fortnight it was to happen &amp; consequently preparing for a run, they suffer no losses. At the theatre in the evening. Much amused.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":334,"lock":null}
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/27/352
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":352,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind NW to W &amp; WSW towards the evening. Took a walk with Emma &amp; called upon Mrs Paul &amp; Sharp. Wrote to William but forgot to put the letter into the post. At the whist club in the evening. No run upon Chapmans today. All quiet &amp; business going as usual.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":335,"lock":null}
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/27/352
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":352,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind NW to W &amp; WSW towards the evening. Took a walk with Emma &amp; called upon Mrs Paul &amp; Sharp. Wrote to William but forgot to put the letter into the post. At the whist club in the evening. No run upon Chapmans today. All quiet &amp; business going as usual.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":335,"lock":null}
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/28/353
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":353,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind about West. Attended a meeting of the Commissioners under the new act to appeal against the rate of the House in Dockwray Square &amp; got it reduced from &pound;50 to &pound;45. Took a walk with Emma &amp; showed her the glass exhibition. Received a letter from William. No account of the Hope. Drew upon Chapmans for &pound;5 for self.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":336,"lock":null}
14:36:38.434 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.435 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/28/353
14:36:38.435 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":353,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind about West. Attended a meeting of the Commissioners under the new act to appeal against the rate of the House in Dockwray Square &amp; got it reduced from &pound;50 to &pound;45. Took a walk with Emma &amp; showed her the glass exhibition. Received a letter from William. No account of the Hope. Drew upon Chapmans for &pound;5 for self.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":336,"lock":null}
14:36:38.435 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/11/29/354
14:36:38.435 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":354,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day. Wind ESE. A few light ships got in. Finished a long letter to William a continuation to that which I forgot to put into the post on Thursday &amp; enclosing Turner's letter from Carlow, sent them off. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at Mr Allens. A very wet afternoon &amp; night.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":337,"lock":null}
14:36:38.435 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
