14:36:38.445 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/19/374
14:36:38.445 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":374,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing a gale of wind from NW with a little rain. Captain Bunbury, Mr Mark &amp; I went over to Sunderland &amp; dined at the mess of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; spent a very agreeable day, the dinner given to colonel Cookson who was for many years commanding officer of the regiment in India. Slept at <span class=highlight_yellow>Joyscys</span> Inn</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":357,"lock":null}
