14:36:38.445 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":374,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing a gale of wind from NW with a little rain. Captain Bunbury, Mr Mark &amp; I went over to Sunderland &amp; dined at the mess of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; spent a very agreeable day, the dinner given to colonel Cookson who was for many years commanding officer of the regiment in India. Slept at <span class=highlight_yellow>Joyscys</span> Inn</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":357,"lock":null}
14:36:38.445 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/2/357
14:36:38.445 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":357,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by S towards evening the wind got up &amp; increased to a perfect gale from the S by W &amp; excessively cold. Understand that several ships, all on shore, some near Sunderland. Walked with Mr Mark &amp; called upon Captain Bunbury &amp; Mr Hopkins. Dined at home. In the evening went to the Commercial to see Mr Ildeston who was waiting there for Mr Tibbs. Received an invitation &amp; suppered with the committee of Association for prosecuting felons. Sat rather late.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":340,"lock":null}
14:36:38.445 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
