14:36:38.447 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":377,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly wet day. Wind about W or W by S. Received a letter from William &amp; answered it ordering by W Taylors desire the Morning Journal &amp; Morning Herald newspapers. At 5 guineas for the Newsroom. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":360,"lock":null}
14:36:38.447 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/23/378
14:36:38.447 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":378,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a damp day. Wind E &amp; ESE. Dined at J Tinleys. A pleasant day. There Captain Bunbury, Mr Hopkins 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Parr &amp; Doctor White. Afterwards went to the ball. Very well attended for the first time. Upwards of 60 there. Danced with a Miss Paine of Faversham, a very fine girl.</p>\r\n<p>Paid apprentices one quarters wages, &pound;1.8.9 Repaid ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors &pound;50 borrowed of them. Gave Stephenson &pound;25 to pay wages</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":361,"lock":null}
14:36:38.447 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/23/378
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":378,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a damp day. Wind E &amp; ESE. Dined at J Tinleys. A pleasant day. There Captain Bunbury, Mr Hopkins 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Parr &amp; Doctor White. Afterwards went to the ball. Very well attended for the first time. Upwards of 60 there. Danced with a Miss Paine of Faversham, a very fine girl.</p>\r\n<p>Paid apprentices one quarters wages, &pound;1.8.9 Repaid ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors &pound;50 borrowed of them. Gave Stephenson &pound;25 to pay wages</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":361,"lock":null}
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/24/379
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":379,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Rather damp with rain in the evening. Wind SE. The Hope arrived safe in the evening &frac12; past 6 o'clock. Dined at home. Received the Hope's ac<font color=#BFBFBF>count</font>s along with a balance of &pound;51.11/-</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":362,"lock":null}
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/24/379
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":379,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Rather damp with rain in the evening. Wind SE. The Hope arrived safe in the evening &frac12; past 6 o'clock. Dined at home. Received the Hope's ac<font color=#BFBFBF>count</font>s along with a balance of &pound;51.11/-</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":362,"lock":null}
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/25/380
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":380,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. A fine day. Wind SSW. Went to church in the morning &amp; afterwards walked up to Benton to dinner &amp; stayed all night. Wrote to William to take the Hope off risk of British Club</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":363,"lock":null}
14:36:38.448 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/25/380
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":380,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Xmas day. A fine day. Wind SSW. Went to church in the morning &amp; afterwards walked up to Benton to dinner &amp; stayed all night. Wrote to William to take the Hope off risk of British Club</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":363,"lock":null}
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/26/381
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":381,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; sharp frost. Wind SSW. Walked into Newcastle. Took the Hope on for a turn of <span class=highlight_yellow>townley</span> &amp; gave notice to the Hope Club of my intention to lay her up. Received from Carr &amp; Co &pound;21.6/- on account of WBS. Balance of freight acct <span class=highlight_yellow>o/s</span> Hope. Came down to Shields to dinner &amp; in the evening attended the whist club. The Hope got under the crane to take her manure out for Mr J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>i</font><sup>o</sup><font color=#BFBFBF>r</font> Finewick of Preston Villa. Gave Mrs Scott a draft on Chapmans for &pound;75 her annuity.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":364,"lock":null}
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/26/381
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":381,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; sharp frost. Wind SSW. Walked into Newcastle. Took the Hope on for a turn of <span class=highlight_yellow>townley</span> &amp; gave notice to the Hope Club of my intention to lay her up. Received from Carr &amp; Co &pound;21.6/- on account of WBS. Balance of freight acct <span class=highlight_yellow>o/s</span> Hope. Came down to Shields to dinner &amp; in the evening attended the whist club. The Hope got under the crane to take her manure out for Mr J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>i</font><sup>o</sup><font color=#BFBFBF>r</font> Finewick of Preston Villa. Gave Mrs Scott a draft on Chapmans for &pound;75 her annuity.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":364,"lock":null}
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/27/382
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":382,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonable day, rather cold &amp; frosty. Wind S by W. On board the Hope all the morning. Along side the crane getting manure out for which I received of Mr Fenwick &pound;2 there being 80 tons. The people engaged unbending sails &amp; taking down running rigging etc preparatory to laying ship up. Dined at home. In the evening at the whist club at Tom Weights</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":365,"lock":null}
14:36:38.449 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
