14:36:38.450 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":382,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonable day, rather cold &amp; frosty. Wind S by W. On board the Hope all the morning. Along side the crane getting manure out for which I received of Mr Fenwick &pound;2 there being 80 tons. The people engaged unbending sails &amp; taking down running rigging etc preparatory to laying ship up. Dined at home. In the evening at the whist club at Tom Weights</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":365,"lock":null}
14:36:38.450 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/28/383
14:36:38.450 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":383,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning &amp; a heavy fall of rain during the whole day. Wind W by S. Cleared up in the evening. At church in the morning. Miss <span class=highlight_yellow>Heevson</span> dined with me. Wrote to William informing him of my having received of Mr Shakers &pound;10.11.2 on account of Messrs Lees, which I carry to WBS Cr. Spent the evening at J Tinleys.</p>","pageId":718,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":366,"lock":null}
14:36:38.450 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
