14:36:38.452 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":358,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day and wind about W by N. Walked to Tynemouth called at Tibbs upon Mr Ildeston who returned to Shields with me. Dined at home &amp; in the evening met Mr Ildeston at Mr Baskers to take wine. Mr Mark there.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":341,"lock":null}
14:36:38.452 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/30/385
14:36:38.452 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":385,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather thick. Wind SW. Dined at home. Paid into Chapmans on my own account &pound;10.11.2</p>","pageId":719,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":368,"lock":null}
14:36:38.452 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.452 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/30/385
14:36:38.452 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":385,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather thick. Wind SW. Dined at home. Paid into Chapmans on my own account &pound;10.11.2</p>","pageId":719,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":368,"lock":null}
14:36:38.453 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/31/386
14:36:38.453 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":386,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Wind WNW. Engaged in the morning drawing &amp; on board of ship. Sails all on shore at Mr Hearns. Ordered the running rigging to be taken to Mr Sharps, as there's nothing safe on board from the nightly visits the thieves pay. Thus ends the year, a very poor one for ship &amp; owners. I for one can safely say that I have not made one farthing. I only hope the next year will be productive of more good or I know not what will be the consequence. Dined at home &amp; in the evening attended the theatre. The <span class=highlight_yellow>bespeak</span> of the Subscriber to the Assemblies. A very fair house, as things <span class=highlight_yellow>are</span>.</p>","pageId":719,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":369,"lock":null}
14:36:38.453 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
