14:36:38.454 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":360,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day, but rather cool &amp; wind SW. Dined at Mr Tibbs at Tynemouth. Mr &amp; Mrs Tinley, Miss Hewson, Mr &amp; Mrs L Fenwick, Mr &amp; Mrs I Fenwick, Misses Drury, Captain Bunbury &amp; self the party</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":343,"lock":null}
14:36:38.454 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/12/6/361
14:36:38.454 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":361,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Fresh breeze from SW. The two Mrs Dixons came down from Benton, lunched &amp; took Emma back with them. Dined at home. In the evening attended the whist club at <span class=highlight_yellow>Greenhows</span>. Towards night it began to blow very hard. Mr Harry, H French, Mr Mark &amp; I took wind at the George. Ps Sub<font color=#BFBFBF>scription</font> 1G to newsroom</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":344,"lock":null}
14:36:38.454 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
