14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":111,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning at 3 o'clock &amp; left South Shields at &frac12; past 4 o'clock coach for Carlow. A fine day, arrived at Leeds at 6 o'clock where I stay all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":106,"lock":null}
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/15/112
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":112,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Much annoyed at finding I should not get to Liverpool in time to catch the Post Office packit for Dublin. Deceived by the people at the coach office. Left Leeds by coach at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Outside a cloudy morning, soon began to rain &amp; continued very heavy all day. Reached Huddersfield at 10 o'clock. I think where I had to wait an hour &amp; change coach. Got to Manchester at 1 o'clock &amp; found to my surprise &amp; vexation the coach would not proceed until 5 o'clock. Kicked up a row at the office, got part of any money returned &amp; fortunately caught a coach about to start for Liverpool where I arrived at 6 o'clock &amp; immediately embarked on board the &quot;Bereuenyham&quot;  steam boat which as luck would have it, was that evening going to start for Dublin. Wind WSW</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":107,"lock":null}
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/15/112
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":112,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Much annoyed at finding I should not get to Liverpool in time to catch the Post Office packit for Dublin. Deceived by the people at the coach office. Left Leeds by coach at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Outside a cloudy morning, soon began to rain &amp; continued very heavy all day. Reached Huddersfield at 10 o'clock. I think where I had to wait an hour &amp; change coach. Got to Manchester at 1 o'clock &amp; found to my surprise &amp; vexation the coach would not proceed until 5 o'clock. Kicked up a row at the office, got part of any money returned &amp; fortunately caught a coach about to start for Liverpool where I arrived at 6 o'clock &amp; immediately embarked on board the &quot;Bereuenyham&quot;  steam boat which as luck would have it, was that evening going to start for Dublin. Wind WSW</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":107,"lock":null}
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/4/16/113
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":113,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the whole of last night we had a heavy sea &amp; foul wind blowing WSW very hard, to contend with but fortunately a fine boat under us. As it was low water when we started, we overtook to steam Office packit at anchor, at the Rock not able to proceed for want of water, having left 2 &frac12;  hours before us so that after all, I lost no time, no thanks to the rascally clerks at the coach office. We kept company all night &amp; after a tedious passage arrived at the custom House quay, Dublin at 3 o'clock PM. Took my luggage to Mackens Hotel, Dawson Street where I stayed all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":108,"lock":null}
14:36:38.489 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
