14:36:38.522 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":183,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day with a few light showers of rain. Mr Walker received the L<font color=#BFBFBF>ord</font> Chancellors orders from Mr Carmichael &amp; served Mrs Falkener with a copy &amp; notice. Entered into an agreement with Mr Digan to grant him a lease when legally authorized of the house in Dublin street &amp; gave him possession upon his paying one year's rent in advance reg:&pound;35 less &pound;2 allowed him for the difference in time between the 30<sup>th</sup> May the day the lease is to be taken from to this day. Dined with Dr Reed</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":173,"lock":null}
14:36:38.522 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/2/166
14:36:38.522 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":166,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy day with heavy showers of rain. Had some conversation with Mr Walker. Determined upon going to Dublin to administer to the amount of sale of furniture only &amp; take out letters of guardianship. Received from Mr Cleer &pound;1.11 for whisky &amp; malting. Dined at home Finished my letter to William &amp; put it into the post. Ordered a car to be with me at 7 o'clock in the morning if fine to go to Athy to see Mr Pope</p>","pageId":698,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":156,"lock":null}
14:36:38.522 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
