14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":185,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Heavy rain towards afternoon with thunder. Took walk with the boys &amp; got wet through. Dined at Cossays</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":175,"lock":null}
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/22/186
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":186,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Left Carlow for Dublin to attend an appointment before Mr Townsend, a master in chancery tomorrow Arrived in Dublin &frac12; past 4 o'clock &ndash; after a pleasant journey. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":176,"lock":null}
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/22/186
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":186,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Left Carlow for Dublin to attend an appointment before Mr Townsend, a master in chancery tomorrow Arrived in Dublin &frac12; past 4 o'clock &ndash; after a pleasant journey. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":176,"lock":null}
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/23/187
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":187,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Called the first thing upon Mr Carmichael. Attended the master at 11 o'clock at the Four Courts. Damm the law say I. My patience is exhausted, got nothing done this day, for want of an affidavit that there were no other next of kin having but Mr Falkener &amp; ourselves. Dined at Mackens. Suppered at the Steades with Ian Gale</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":177,"lock":null}
14:36:38.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/23/187
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":187,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Called the first thing upon Mr Carmichael. Attended the master at 11 o'clock at the Four Courts. Damm the law say I. My patience is exhausted, got nothing done this day, for want of an affidavit that there were no other next of kin having but Mr Falkener &amp; ourselves. Dined at Mackens. Suppered at the Steades with Ian Gale</p>","pageId":700,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":177,"lock":null}
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/24/188
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":188,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. This being a holy day at the Court of Chancery, we could do nothing. I therefor went in the steam boat to Kingstown &amp; dined with J Thompson on board the Royal Charlotte. The Mayor of Anglesey came down &amp; took a sail in his yacht the Pearl. Lieutenant M  Paget came on too and the Royal Charlotte to whom I was introduced. No great honor as it is not likely he will know me again.</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":178,"lock":null}
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/24/188
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":188,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. This being a holy day at the Court of Chancery, we could do nothing. I therefor went in the steam boat to Kingstown &amp; dined with J Thompson on board the Royal Charlotte. The Mayor of Anglesey came down &amp; took a sail in his yacht the Pearl. Lieutenant M  Paget came on too and the Royal Charlotte to whom I was introduced. No great honor as it is not likely he will know me again.</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":178,"lock":null}
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/25/189
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":189,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Attended the Master Townsend, who appointed us guardians. Dined at Mackens Before dinner had a hot &amp; dusty walk to Phoenix Park</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":179,"lock":null}
14:36:38.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.526 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/25/189
14:36:38.526 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":189,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Attended the Master Townsend, who appointed us guardians. Dined at Mackens Before dinner had a hot &amp; dusty walk to Phoenix Park</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":179,"lock":null}
14:36:38.526 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/26/190
14:36:38.526 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":190,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceptionally hot day. Attended the Master again for him to look over draft of report, when he thought it would be better to appoint me sole guardian. I cannot make up mind to take in so much trouble difficulties &amp; anxiety that I feel very unhappy. Cannot stand it much longer. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":180,"lock":null}
14:36:38.526 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.526 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/26/190
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":190,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceptionally hot day. Attended the Master again for him to look over draft of report, when he thought it would be better to appoint me sole guardian. I cannot make up mind to take in so much trouble difficulties &amp; anxiety that I feel very unhappy. Cannot stand it much longer. Dined at Mackens</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":180,"lock":null}
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/27/191
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":191,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another hot summers day. Called at Mr Carmichael's &amp; from the difficult situation in which I am placed, determined upon asking my brother to come to Ireland &amp; going to Carlow tomorrow there to remain until I either see him or have a letter from him in answer to one I wrote this day. Wrote also to Mrs Scott. Dined at Mackens &amp; went to the Lying In Hospital Gardens where there was an immense assembly of company</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":181,"lock":null}
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/27/191
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":191,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another hot summers day. Called at Mr Carmichael's &amp; from the difficult situation in which I am placed, determined upon asking my brother to come to Ireland &amp; going to Carlow tomorrow there to remain until I either see him or have a letter from him in answer to one I wrote this day. Wrote also to Mrs Scott. Dined at Mackens &amp; went to the Lying In Hospital Gardens where there was an immense assembly of company</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":181,"lock":null}
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/28/192
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":192,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very hot day. Left Dublin for Carlow The Heat most oppressive &amp; clouds of dust. We did not reach Carlow until 7 o'clock. The coach wheel taking fire Dined at Mr Jamesons. Letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":182,"lock":null}
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/28/192
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":192,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very hot day. Left Dublin for Carlow The Heat most oppressive &amp; clouds of dust. We did not reach Carlow until 7 o'clock. The coach wheel taking fire Dined at Mr Jamesons. Letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":182,"lock":null}
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/29/193
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":193,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another very hot day. Attended morning service at Graigh Church to hear a sermon preached by Mr Vernon. For the education of poor children, a collection was made Dined at Mr Jameson. Bathed in the Barrow A letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":183,"lock":null}
14:36:38.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/29/193
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":193,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another very hot day. Attended morning service at Graigh Church to hear a sermon preached by Mr Vernon. For the education of poor children, a collection was made Dined at Mr Jameson. Bathed in the Barrow A letter from William</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":183,"lock":null}
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/3/167
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":167,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlos at &frac12; past 7 o'clock in a car &amp; went to Athy to breakfast in 1 &frac12; hours being 11 &frac12; miles. Saw Captain Pope respecting the property there, but could learn nothing satisfactory. He said it was a divided property. His father having 2/3 one of which he sold &amp; the other 1/3 was the Galbraeths &amp; to prove it was a divided property he said the Galbraiths had granted a lease of their part consisting of an old house now in ruins &amp; a tanyard in the rear. He further said that the original lease had somehow or other got out of his hands, but that I could see it at Mr Warrens, Jarvis Street Dublin. That he would be glad to give me every information &amp; assistance &amp; allow me to see all papers that are in his possession. Returned to Carlow in the afternoon. Dined alone. Mr Vernon having gone to Coopers Hill &amp; went to a pleasant quadrille party at Mrs Whilliam Fishbourn. We kept it up until 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":157,"lock":null}
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/3/167
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":167,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Left Carlos at &frac12; past 7 o'clock in a car &amp; went to Athy to breakfast in 1 &frac12; hours being 11 &frac12; miles. Saw Captain Pope respecting the property there, but could learn nothing satisfactory. He said it was a divided property. His father having 2/3 one of which he sold &amp; the other 1/3 was the Galbraeths &amp; to prove it was a divided property he said the Galbraiths had granted a lease of their part consisting of an old house now in ruins &amp; a tanyard in the rear. He further said that the original lease had somehow or other got out of his hands, but that I could see it at Mr Warrens, Jarvis Street Dublin. That he would be glad to give me every information &amp; assistance &amp; allow me to see all papers that are in his possession. Returned to Carlow in the afternoon. Dined alone. Mr Vernon having gone to Coopers Hill &amp; went to a pleasant quadrille party at Mrs Whilliam Fishbourn. We kept it up until 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":157,"lock":null}
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/30/194
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":194,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Very little to do Received a letter from William. Saw Mr Turner who thought he would be able to give security Paid Carroll for spirits 19/- &amp; Haughton for funeral expenses &pound;8.18/-. Dined at Mr Vernon's &amp; took a long walk in the evening. Bathed in the morning</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":184,"lock":null}
14:36:38.528 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
