14:36:38.529 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":194,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Very little to do Received a letter from William. Saw Mr Turner who thought he would be able to give security Paid Carroll for spirits 19/- &amp; Haughton for funeral expenses &pound;8.18/-. Dined at Mr Vernon's &amp; took a long walk in the evening. Bathed in the morning</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":184,"lock":null}
14:36:38.529 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/6/4/168
14:36:38.529 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":168,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Quite a deluge of rain. Confined to the house all the morning by the wet. Engaged in covrtey for wrote a letter to Mr Buther of Athy. Asking to whom he pays rent for the tanyard. Dined at home with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":699,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":158,"lock":null}
