14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":226,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2852-image-black-middens.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>The Black Middens</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/1/227
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":227,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Cloudy with wind SW Several ships got to sea in the morning. In the afternoon a few light ships got down after a 12 days passage amongst them the Hope, went on board at &frac12; past 4 o'clock, when off the Black Middens &amp; got her papers. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed her for Carr's Walls before 6 o'clock either on my own account or 10/- freight, optimal to give an answer tomorrow.</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":216,"lock":null}
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/1/227
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":227,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":1,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Cloudy with wind SW Several ships got to sea in the morning. In the afternoon a few light ships got down after a 12 days passage amongst them the Hope, went on board at &frac12; past 4 o'clock, when off the Black Middens &amp; got her papers. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed her for Carr's Walls before 6 o'clock either on my own account or 10/- freight, optimal to give an answer tomorrow.</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":216,"lock":null}
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/10/237
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":237,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am rose. Ship a little to the north of Flamborough Head &amp; stood in on the eastbound tack. Wind about W &amp; W by N. Made Robin Hood's bay at 11 o'clock am tacked &amp; stood to the southward again wind &amp; weather now moderate, set main staysail. At 12 o'clock let a reef out of top sails at 1 o'clock set main sail. Turned out a beautiful summers afternoon with a fine breeze, about 6 o'clock lay too under Flamborough head, unbent &amp; repaired foresail at 8 o'clock, again got underway with a fine westerly breeze to cross the Dups. Drank a glass of porter, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":225,"lock":null}
14:36:38.547 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/10/237
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":237,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am rose. Ship a little to the north of Flamborough Head &amp; stood in on the eastbound tack. Wind about W &amp; W by N. Made Robin Hood's bay at 11 o'clock am tacked &amp; stood to the southward again wind &amp; weather now moderate, set main staysail. At 12 o'clock let a reef out of top sails at 1 o'clock set main sail. Turned out a beautiful summers afternoon with a fine breeze, about 6 o'clock lay too under Flamborough head, unbent &amp; repaired foresail at 8 o'clock, again got underway with a fine westerly breeze to cross the Dups. Drank a glass of porter, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":225,"lock":null}
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/11/238
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":238,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock. Found the ship off Dunlengton Church with a fine leading wind from W by S about two points worse than last night. A fine morning, towards evening began to blow fresh. Found the fore topmast backstay spring, secured it with a tackle &amp; took in a reef being rather squally Turned in about &frac12; past 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":226,"lock":null}
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/11/238
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":238,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock. Found the ship off Dunlengton Church with a fine leading wind from W by S about two points worse than last night. A fine morning, towards evening began to blow fresh. Found the fore topmast backstay spring, secured it with a tackle &amp; took in a reef being rather squally Turned in about &frac12; past 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":226,"lock":null}
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/12/239
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":239,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Looked out a little after 4 o'clock am. Found we had got a change of wind about 2 o'clock from about WNW. An agreeable change for us, making all sail. The ship passed the floating light at 3 o'clock, reached Cromer at ____. Passed through Yarmouth Roads at 11 o'clock &amp; brought up being high water, at &frac12; past. Off Golaton, the <span class=highlight_yellow>Dalryaple</span> &amp; Nancy in company. Wind about W &amp; by S. The latter ship from Archangel Captain Stormont came on board to dinner. At 5 pm being low-water got underway with a light breeze from the W by S &amp; sailed out of St Nicholas Gateway &amp; beat to the southern water highwater between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock, when we brought up for the tide between the reefs points about 4 miles to the south of Southwold, between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock am. After supper, turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":227,"lock":null}
14:36:38.548 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/12/239
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":239,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Looked out a little after 4 o'clock am. Found we had got a change of wind about 2 o'clock from about WNW. An agreeable change for us, making all sail. The ship passed the floating light at 3 o'clock, reached Cromer at ____. Passed through Yarmouth Roads at 11 o'clock &amp; brought up being high water, at &frac12; past. Off Golaton, the <span class=highlight_yellow>Dalryaple</span> &amp; Nancy in company. Wind about W &amp; by S. The latter ship from Archangel Captain Stormont came on board to dinner. At 5 pm being low-water got underway with a light breeze from the W by S &amp; sailed out of St Nicholas Gateway &amp; beat to the southern water highwater between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock, when we brought up for the tide between the reefs points about 4 miles to the south of Southwold, between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock am. After supper, turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":227,"lock":null}
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/13/240
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":240,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock having a slight cold &amp; a little rheumatism upon me. A fine warm summers day we have had for the last five weeks. Wind about south, but little of it, between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock. The United Kingdom steam ship passed us bound to London at &frac12; past 11 o'clock. When off Orford the [wind] changed to the east, a fair wind, but we want a little more of it. I hope it will continue. The breeze continued &amp; we got down to the south end of the Middle Sand where we brought up for the night, not being able to run through the Shoe Hole in the dark. After we got to bed, the wind increased &amp; blew hard with a heavy swell, a great many ships around, which gave us a foul berth extremely dangerous in that part should a gale come on from the ESE. &amp; cause of the loss of so many ships and lives we had in the March gale about five years ago.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":228,"lock":null}
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/13/240
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":240,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock having a slight cold &amp; a little rheumatism upon me. A fine warm summers day we have had for the last five weeks. Wind about south, but little of it, between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock. The United Kingdom steam ship passed us bound to London at &frac12; past 11 o'clock. When off Orford the [wind] changed to the east, a fair wind, but we want a little more of it. I hope it will continue. The breeze continued &amp; we got down to the south end of the Middle Sand where we brought up for the night, not being able to run through the Shoe Hole in the dark. After we got to bed, the wind increased &amp; blew hard with a heavy swell, a great many ships around, which gave us a foul berth extremely dangerous in that part should a gale come on from the ESE. &amp; cause of the loss of so many ships and lives we had in the March gale about five years ago.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":228,"lock":null}
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/2299
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2299,"version":14,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 3 o'clock. A dismal &amp; wet morning, blowing hard from the east. Had not light enough to get us underway until about 4 o'clock, when the whole fleet were in motion, fortunately, at last with a fair wind. Being excessively wet &amp; unpleasant I got into bed again &amp; lay till &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; then found the ship off Leigh above Southend &amp; still raining hard. Brought up off Greenwich at &frac12; past 3 &amp; o'clock landed with ...</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2239,"lock":null}
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/2299
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2299,"version":14,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 3 o'clock. A dismal &amp; wet morning, blowing hard from the east. Had not light enough to get us underway until about 4 o'clock, when the whole fleet were in motion, fortunately, at last with a fair wind. Being excessively wet &amp; unpleasant I got into bed again &amp; lay till &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; then found the ship off Leigh above Southend &amp; still raining hard. Brought up off Greenwich at &frac12; past 3 &amp; o'clock landed with ...</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2239,"lock":null}
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/241
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":241,"version":8,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the ship papers, entered her &amp; went up to Richmond's, a very unpleasant walk. Richmond was going out to dinner. Got my boots etc. dried &amp; then went to Millers coffee house, Red Lyon Square, where I found William and Bob Marsh &amp; had my dinner. They not a little surprised to see me. Slept at Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":229,"lock":null}
14:36:38.549 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/14/241
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":241,"version":8,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the ship papers, entered her &amp; went up to Richmond's, a very unpleasant walk. Richmond was going out to dinner. Got my boots etc. dried &amp; then went to Millers coffee house, Red Lyon Square, where I found William and Bob Marsh &amp; had my dinner. They not a little surprised to see me. Slept at Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":229,"lock":null}
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/15/242
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":242,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW Took the Greenwich passage boat at the tower &amp; went down to the Hope off Greenwich &amp; found her just getting underway for the pool, on my return pesance conveyances much surprised at meeting Watt. Carr's Walls such a bad coal than none of the Hope was sold today. Wrote to Mrs Scott. Dined with Richmond &amp; met Tom Griffeth. Played a few rubbers in the evening &amp; lost &pound;3.15/- Got home  to Nottingham Place at 2 o'clock am Saturday</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":230,"lock":null}
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/15/242
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":242,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW Took the Greenwich passage boat at the tower &amp; went down to the Hope off Greenwich &amp; found her just getting underway for the pool, on my return pesance conveyances much surprised at meeting Watt. Carr's Walls such a bad coal than none of the Hope was sold today. Wrote to Mrs Scott. Dined with Richmond &amp; met Tom Griffeth. Played a few rubbers in the evening &amp; lost &pound;3.15/- Got home  to Nottingham Place at 2 o'clock am Saturday</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":230,"lock":null}
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/16/243
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":243,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW Went to the city as yesterday on the Paddington coach. Engaged during the morning with Captain Dawson of the Dalryaple swearing affidavit respecting timbers etc. walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. We went with Mr Vincent, hired a boat &amp; rowed up to Putney, where we had tea, mutton chops etc. &amp; returned to town at 9 o'clock after a very pleasant evening</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":231,"lock":null}
14:36:38.551 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/16/243
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":243,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW Went to the city as yesterday on the Paddington coach. Engaged during the morning with Captain Dawson of the Dalryaple swearing affidavit respecting timbers etc. walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. We went with Mr Vincent, hired a boat &amp; rowed up to Putney, where we had tea, mutton chops etc. &amp; returned to town at 9 o'clock after a very pleasant evening</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":231,"lock":null}
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/17/244
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":244,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW with rain during the day. Bob March breakfasted with us. Went to the chapel in Vere Street. I afterwards walked round by Gower Street &amp; called upon the Lumleys, they [had] gone down to Stanmore for the day. Continued upon and saw the Linskills in York terrace, Regants Park. Walked round by Hyde park, very little to be seen. Town exceedingly dull. Took a beef steak at the Blue Posts in Cork Street &amp; drank wine in Nottingham place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":232,"lock":null}
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/17/244
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":244,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW with rain during the day. Bob March breakfasted with us. Went to the chapel in Vere Street. I afterwards walked round by Gower Street &amp; called upon the Lumleys, they [had] gone down to Stanmore for the day. Continued upon and saw the Linskills in York terrace, Regants Park. Walked round by Hyde park, very little to be seen. Town exceedingly dull. Took a beef steak at the Blue Posts in Cork Street &amp; drank wine in Nottingham place</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":232,"lock":null}
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/18/245
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":245,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A Beautiful day. Wind SW Went into the city this morning by the Paddington stage about 80 fresh ships got up to market, 2 or 3 of Carr's Walls? The coals bear such a bad character on the market that we could not sell any of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city, called upon Bob March, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; took wine in Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":233,"lock":null}
14:36:38.552 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/18/245
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":245,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A Beautiful day. Wind SW Went into the city this morning by the Paddington stage about 80 fresh ships got up to market, 2 or 3 of Carr's Walls? The coals bear such a bad character on the market that we could not sell any of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city, called upon Bob March, dined at the Blue Ports &amp; took wine in Nottingham Place</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":233,"lock":null}
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/19/246
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":246,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Such a change. Quite cheering after the stormy weather we had. Wind WSW Did not go into the city. At 12 o'clock walked down to Hartley the dentists in mags Building &amp; had my teeth examined &amp; cleaned. Called at fosby's &amp; Bob March's &amp; afterwards walked home with William to drufs. Dined at 7 o'clock with Mr Linskill, met Mrs &amp; Miss Payin Mr Ro Bill &amp; spent a pleasant day. Lady Campbell came in to tea</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":234,"lock":null}
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/19/246
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":246,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Such a change. Quite cheering after the stormy weather we had. Wind WSW Did not go into the city. At 12 o'clock walked down to Hartley the dentists in mags Building &amp; had my teeth examined &amp; cleaned. Called at fosby's &amp; Bob March's &amp; afterwards walked home with William to drufs. Dined at 7 o'clock with Mr Linskill, met Mrs &amp; Miss Payin Mr Ro Bill &amp; spent a pleasant day. Lady Campbell came in to tea</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":234,"lock":null}
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/2/228
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":228,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold cloudy morning. Wind about NNW. Went to Newcastle &amp; agreed to take 10/- freight. It turned out a very wet day. Dined with J Tinley. Ship went to the spout. Gave Stephenson &pound;40</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":217,"lock":null}
14:36:38.553 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
