14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":247,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SSW Went into the city by a Paddington stage. A few fresh ships up. Could not sell the Hope. Bob March, Mr Vincent, William &amp; I went down by water &amp; dined on board.  In the evening at English Opera House</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":235,"lock":null}
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/21/248
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":248,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet &amp; disagreeable day. Wind SW. Took the Paddington coach into the city. Called at Lees &amp; left the policy of the Hope Club. Dined at I Loblengs, a large party</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":236,"lock":null}
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/21/248
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":248,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet &amp; disagreeable day. Wind SW. Took the Paddington coach into the city. Called at Lees &amp; left the policy of the Hope Club. Dined at I Loblengs, a large party</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":236,"lock":null}
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/22/249
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":249,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day. Wind from NW to N Went into the city at &frac12; past 11 o'clock by the Paddington stage. With some difficulty got the Hope sold at 30/s Walked out of the city with William &amp; dined with Richmond, met Rob Jobling Played at whist &amp; won 4/-</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":237,"lock":null}
14:36:38.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/22/249
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":249,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery day. Wind from NW to N Went into the city at &frac12; past 11 o'clock by the Paddington stage. With some difficulty got the Hope sold at 30/s Walked out of the city with William &amp; dined with Richmond, met Rob Jobling Played at whist &amp; won 4/-</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":237,"lock":null}
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/23/250
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":250,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind West Walked round the Regents park. Took an early dinner with Richmond who afterwards drove me down to Stanmore to stay the night. Left town at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. A beautiful evening. Took tea and went to bed in good time.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":238,"lock":null}
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/23/250
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":250,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind West Walked round the Regents park. Took an early dinner with Richmond who afterwards drove me down to Stanmore to stay the night. Left town at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. A beautiful evening. Took tea and went to bed in good time.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":238,"lock":null}
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/24/251
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":251,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine Day. Hot summer weather. Richmond &amp; I after breakfast took a long walk. Upon our return found Mr &amp; Mrs Lumly had arrived. Mr &amp; Mrs Griffiths also came down before dinner &amp; Jobling came after we had sat down. We spend a very aggregable &amp; pleasant  day &amp; returned to town  in the evening.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":239,"lock":null}
14:36:38.555 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/24/251
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":251,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine Day. Hot summer weather. Richmond &amp; I after breakfast took a long walk. Upon our return found Mr &amp; Mrs Lumly had arrived. Mr &amp; Mrs Griffiths also came down before dinner &amp; Jobling came after we had sat down. We spend a very aggregable &amp; pleasant  day &amp; returned to town  in the evening.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":239,"lock":null}
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/25/252
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":252,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A hot day, wind west. Went into the city by a Paddington stage. On the market,  coal lower. Walked out of the city. Dined at 6 o'clock with Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Whenbury</span> in Gower Street; a quiet party only Richmond there. He &amp; I went in the evening to Vauxhall Gardens to meet Bob Marsh, Vincent &amp; William. A great many people there, but of the inferior classes. Got home between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":240,"lock":null}
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/25/252
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":252,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A hot day, wind west. Went into the city by a Paddington stage. On the market,  coal lower. Walked out of the city. Dined at 6 o'clock with Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Whenbury</span> in Gower Street; a quiet party only Richmond there. He &amp; I went in the evening to Vauxhall Gardens to meet Bob Marsh, Vincent &amp; William. A great many people there, but of the inferior classes. Got home between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":240,"lock":null}
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/26/253
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":253,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, but exceedingly hot. Wind SE. Breakfasted with Richmond who afterwards drove me into the city &amp; then to Stone Stairs &amp; we went on board the Hope. Took a Paddington stage home. Dressed &amp; dined at Joblings. A large party.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":241,"lock":null}
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/26/253
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":253,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, but exceedingly hot. Wind SE. Breakfasted with Richmond who afterwards drove me into the city &amp; then to Stone Stairs &amp; we went on board the Hope. Took a Paddington stage home. Dressed &amp; dined at Joblings. A large party.</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":241,"lock":null}
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/27/254
14:36:38.556 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":254,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SE. left town at 9 o'clock am. By the Portsmouth coach with Bob Marsh, where we arrived at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, crossed over by the steam boat to Ryde to stay with Mr Lee. Dined between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock. Mr Lee living at Navarino House, beautifully. Situated about &frac12; a mile west of the town, upon the side of the hill which descended to the sea of which it commands a most beautiful view, with the mainland, Portsmouth</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":242,"lock":null}
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/27/254
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":254,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SE. left town at 9 o'clock am. By the Portsmouth coach with Bob Marsh, where we arrived at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, crossed over by the steam boat to Ryde to stay with Mr Lee. Dined between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock. Mr Lee living at Navarino House, beautifully. Situated about &frac12; a mile west of the town, upon the side of the hill which descended to the sea of which it commands a most beautiful view, with the mainland, Portsmouth</p>","pageId":706,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":242,"lock":null}
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/28/255
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":255,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Wind east. Got up before 7 o'clock &amp; bathed. Breakfasted at Mr Lees at Navarino House. At 11 o'clock went on the pier to see the Regatta, but dull work, being small boats. Dined with Mr Lee &amp; afterwards attended the Ball at the Library, a very poor one &amp; company bad. Not a pretty girl in the room.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":243,"lock":null}
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/28/255
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":255,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Wind east. Got up before 7 o'clock &amp; bathed. Breakfasted at Mr Lees at Navarino House. At 11 o'clock went on the pier to see the Regatta, but dull work, being small boats. Dined with Mr Lee &amp; afterwards attended the Ball at the Library, a very poor one &amp; company bad. Not a pretty girl in the room.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":243,"lock":null}
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/29/256
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":256,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very foggy morning, wind NE. Cleared up towards 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a delightful day. Rebecca Captain &amp; Mr Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, William &amp; I went in a sailing boat to Portsmouth to see the Victory &amp; much pleased with our trip. The wind being  against us, we were obliged to land &amp; walk about two miles to Gosport. Returned to Navarino at &frac12; past 7 o'clock to dinner</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":244,"lock":null}
14:36:38.557 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
