14:36:38.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":260,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":4.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2855-image-navarino-house-map.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>Map showing Navarino House</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
14:36:38.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/30/261
14:36:38.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":261,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<p>Rather cloudy in the morning. Wind NE but afterwards turned out an exceedingly fine day. Started at &frac12; past 10 o'clock am with the following party in two sociables &amp; a gig upon a tour round the island viz: Mr Rebecca &amp; Laura Lee, Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS, self &amp; two servants. Stopped &amp; saw Shanklin Chine, called &amp; left our luggage at Ventnor. Drove on to &amp; saw Appuldurcombe the seat of Lord Yarborough containing several fine paintings &amp; finely situated. Returned to Ventnor to dinner &amp; slept. A very pleasant &amp; agreeable party</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":245,"lock":null}
14:36:38.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/30/261
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":261,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<p>Rather cloudy in the morning. Wind NE but afterwards turned out an exceedingly fine day. Started at &frac12; past 10 o'clock am with the following party in two sociables &amp; a gig upon a tour round the island viz: Mr Rebecca &amp; Laura Lee, Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS, self &amp; two servants. Stopped &amp; saw Shanklin Chine, called &amp; left our luggage at Ventnor. Drove on to &amp; saw Appuldurcombe the seat of Lord Yarborough containing several fine paintings &amp; finely situated. Returned to Ventnor to dinner &amp; slept. A very pleasant &amp; agreeable party</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":245,"lock":null}
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/31/262
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":262,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather cloudy. Wind NE. F Barclay &amp; I got up early &amp; bathed. Started after breakfast &amp; travelled along undercliff &amp; saw the difficult gentlemans seats. Most beautiful &amp; romantic well wooded &amp; cliffs very grand. Stopped at Blackgang Chine, immense high cliffs with waterfall, continued our journey through a beautiful &amp; well cultivated country to Freshwater Bay, where we had lunch about 4 o'clock. Captain Lewis &amp; the ladies went by land to see the Needles. F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS and self &amp; two servants went by water &amp; got very well to the Needles which with the cave &amp; majestic chalk cliffs, were very grand. But our return was attended with much unpleasantness to say the least, having an ebb tide &amp; strong wind against us &amp; being in a bad and cranky sea boat, we all got most uncomfortably wet by the spray of the sea. With much difficulty got back to Freshwater Bay to an 8 o'clock dinner. This is a very retired &amp; pretty place</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":246,"lock":null}
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/31/262
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":262,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather cloudy. Wind NE. F Barclay &amp; I got up early &amp; bathed. Started after breakfast &amp; travelled along undercliff &amp; saw the difficult gentlemans seats. Most beautiful &amp; romantic well wooded &amp; cliffs very grand. Stopped at Blackgang Chine, immense high cliffs with waterfall, continued our journey through a beautiful &amp; well cultivated country to Freshwater Bay, where we had lunch about 4 o'clock. Captain Lewis &amp; the ladies went by land to see the Needles. F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS and self &amp; two servants went by water &amp; got very well to the Needles which with the cave &amp; majestic chalk cliffs, were very grand. But our return was attended with much unpleasantness to say the least, having an ebb tide &amp; strong wind against us &amp; being in a bad and cranky sea boat, we all got most uncomfortably wet by the spray of the sea. With much difficulty got back to Freshwater Bay to an 8 o'clock dinner. This is a very retired &amp; pretty place</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":246,"lock":null}
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/8/4/230
14:36:38.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":230,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 4 o'clock this morning Went to the spout. Brought a lot of beef on my way up at 40/- Returned to breakfast &amp; went by steam to Newcastle where I learned  that the act gave them the power of loading any ship under 6 keels before larger vessels. Dined with J Tinley. Mrs Scott got from Toyston</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":219,"lock":null}
