14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":286,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most extraordinary fine weather, with wind SW. Strolled about the pier &amp; town</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":270,"lock":null}
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/25/287
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":287,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Not a cloud to be seen. Wind SW. After breakfast Lewis, Fanny, Bob Marsh took a boat &amp; sailed round to Brading Harbour. Much pleased with the views of the country &amp; coast &amp; delighted with our sail. Got back at &frac12; past 3 pm. Received a letter from William of the arrival of the Hope but too late for yesterdays market.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":271,"lock":null}
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/25/287
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":287,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Not a cloud to be seen. Wind SW. After breakfast Lewis, Fanny, Bob Marsh took a boat &amp; sailed round to Brading Harbour. Much pleased with the views of the country &amp; coast &amp; delighted with our sail. Got back at &frac12; past 3 pm. Received a letter from William of the arrival of the Hope but too late for yesterdays market.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":271,"lock":null}
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/26/288
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":288,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW to W. After breakfast walked to Binstead parsonage, about 1 mile, from Naravinos. In my opinion the prettiest &amp; most picturesque place in the island. The grounds laid out with great taste &amp; kept in the highest order. The views from them very fine. Wrote to William of my intention to be in town on Sunday.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":272,"lock":null}
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/26/288
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":288,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW to W. After breakfast walked to Binstead parsonage, about 1 mile, from Naravinos. In my opinion the prettiest &amp; most picturesque place in the island. The grounds laid out with great taste &amp; kept in the highest order. The views from them very fine. Wrote to William of my intention to be in town on Sunday.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":272,"lock":null}
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/27/289
14:36:38.573 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":289,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW to SW. Cleared up before 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a pleasant day. Booked outside place by the Rocket coach from tomorrow morning. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 32/3</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":273,"lock":null}
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/27/289
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":289,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW to SW. Cleared up before 12 o'clock &amp; turned out a pleasant day. Booked outside place by the Rocket coach from tomorrow morning. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 32/3</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":273,"lock":null}
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/28/290
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":290,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A good deal of rain in the night. Wind SW. Left Ryde at 9 o'clock am. Steam for Portsmouth. Took an outside place in the Rocket coach &amp; arrived in London at &frac12; past 7 o'clock pm having had a few showers of rain on the road. Got a bed in Nottingham Place. William out of town at his friend <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphants</span>. Found a note from him that Stephenson had been obliged to leave the Hope &amp; return to the North in consequence of the illness of his uncle. Spent a very pleasant month with my friends, the Lees at Ryde&amp; sorry to leave there.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":274,"lock":null}
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/28/290
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":290,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A good deal of rain in the night. Wind SW. Left Ryde at 9 o'clock am. Steam for Portsmouth. Took an outside place in the Rocket coach &amp; arrived in London at &frac12; past 7 o'clock pm having had a few showers of rain on the road. Got a bed in Nottingham Place. William out of town at his friend <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphants</span>. Found a note from him that Stephenson had been obliged to leave the Hope &amp; return to the North in consequence of the illness of his uncle. Spent a very pleasant month with my friends, the Lees at Ryde&amp; sorry to leave there.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":274,"lock":null}
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/29/291
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":291,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SW. Went into the city by a Paddington Stage. Saw William. Attended the market &amp; afterwards went down the river and dined on board the Hope. Walked home in the evening on our way drinking tea with <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span> at Cockspur Street.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":275,"lock":null}
14:36:38.574 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
