14:36:38.576 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":265,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. Wind variable between NE &amp; NW but returned to the old quarter NE in the afternoon again. Strolled about the town &amp; pier all day. Dined at Navarino</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":249,"lock":null}
14:36:38.576 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/30/292
14:36:38.576 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":292,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning during the day showers of rain. Wind SW. Walked into the city. Brought a new hat of <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span>. Paid &pound;3 for the Hopes ballast &amp; took a Greenwich boat into the pool to her. Gave the mate charge for the passage to Shields. Returned to the city &amp; had a basin of turtle soup at Bleadens. Afterwards took a Paddington Stage &amp; went with William to see the Zoological Society garden in the Regent park. Well worth the walk. In the evening went to the Argyle rooms &amp; was much amused with <span class=highlight_yellow>Fumtas</span> chin</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":276,"lock":null}
14:36:38.576 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
