14:36:38.576 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":292,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning during the day showers of rain. Wind SW. Walked into the city. Brought a new hat of <span class=highlight_yellow>Oliphant</span>. Paid &pound;3 for the Hopes ballast &amp; took a Greenwich boat into the pool to her. Gave the mate charge for the passage to Shields. Returned to the city &amp; had a basin of turtle soup at Bleadens. Afterwards took a Paddington Stage &amp; went with William to see the Zoological Society garden in the Regent park. Well worth the walk. In the evening went to the Argyle rooms &amp; was much amused with <span class=highlight_yellow>Fumtas</span> chin</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":276,"lock":null}
14:36:38.577 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1828/9/4/266
14:36:38.577 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":266,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind NE. Changed to NW &amp; N with thunder &amp; lightning &amp; apparently heavy rain in Hampshire, but returned to the old quarter at night. F Barclay left us this morning for London. Sorry to loose him, a pleasant fellow. Mr Lee &amp; Laura in the chaise &amp; the rest walked to Binstead to see the abbey of which there is little remaining, after lunching on the grass with difficulty &amp; getting our feet covered with mud. We returned home by the beach.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":250,"lock":null}
