14:36:38.602 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":727,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet <font color=#BFBFBF>day</font>. Still raining, very heavy. Wind I think NNW. Walked to Burnhopeside to breakfast. <span class=highlight_yellow>Bressed</span> &amp; Joe <span class=highlight_yellow>Reshar</span>, Allen Hutchinson &amp; I went with Mr Potts, who came for us in his carriage to Mr Whites at Woodlands where we dined &amp; spent a very pleasant &amp; jolly day &amp; after supper returned to Burnhopeside. <span class=highlight_yellow>Kit</span> &amp; Miss R stayed all night at Mr Whites</p>","pageId":779,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":682,"lock":null}
14:36:38.602 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/15/728
14:36:38.602 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":728,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind ___. Excessively jacked &amp; tired from the good living of the last two days. Took a walk with my gun, thinking the exercise would do me good. Shot a brace of birds. Dined at home &amp; completely knocked up. Edward White dined with us.</p>","pageId":779,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":683,"lock":null}
14:36:38.602 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
