14:36:38.610 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":745,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. Wind WNW. Again engaged the morning in drawing. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; I went to the Commercial &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>punished</span> two bottles of port. His treat having heard of the safe arrival of the Choice at Hull from <span class=highlight_yellow>Wybarz</span> making the voyage in two months. In the evening at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Lays</span> at Tynemouth. Drank tea &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":699,"lock":null}
14:36:38.610 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/31/746
14:36:38.610 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":746,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind changeable between NNW &amp; NNE. Sea high, having blown very hard early this morning from NE. Emma Galbraith came to spend the day with Mrs Scott. Took a walk with her round by Preston Lane etc. Dined at 5 o'clock with Allen, J Craig, J Wright, W Harrison &amp; Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> there. Spent a pleasant day &amp; won of W Harrison &pound;6</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":700,"lock":null}
14:36:38.610 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.611 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/31/746
14:36:38.611 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":746,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind changeable between NNW &amp; NNE. Sea high, having blown very hard early this morning from NE. Emma Galbraith came to spend the day with Mrs Scott. Took a walk with her round by Preston Lane etc. Dined at 5 o'clock with Allen, J Craig, J Wright, W Harrison &amp; Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> there. Spent a pleasant day &amp; won of W Harrison &pound;6</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":700,"lock":null}
14:36:38.611 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/10/4/714
14:36:38.611 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":714,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning very fine but afterwards turned dull &amp; like rain. Wind WNW blowing hard in the afternoon at W. Went to church in the morning. Mrs Dixon Fanny &amp; Bell Smith came down to see Mrs Scott. In the afternoon walked down to Tynemouth &amp; dined at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>Note from William</span>. Metcalf, Henry &amp; his wife there &amp; Mr &amp; Mrs J Dale in the evening</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":672,"lock":null}
14:36:38.611 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
