14:36:38.616 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":758,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Blowing hard from the SE. Walked to Shields with Tom Smith. He set off for Togston, being such an unpleasant morning. Fanny remained. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry &amp; J Cunningham at the Commercial.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":712,"lock":null}
14:36:38.616 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/14/759
14:36:38.616 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":759,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick &amp; very damp morning, having been a great deal of rain. Wind South. Fanny Smith left for Togston. Dined with Boswell on board the William Shard. Mark, H Harry &amp; Richardson took wine with us. Spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":713,"lock":null}
