14:36:38.624 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":773,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and damp morning. Wind SW. Received a letter from Stephenson of the Hope being out on Saturday having delivered 279 loads 49 feet of timber equal to 320 loads with deals of broken stowage.</p>\r\n<p>Took Emma to church with me. Dined at home &amp; afterwards took wine with Boswell. H Harry &amp; Allen there.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening at mother Maxwell's</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":727,"lock":null}
14:36:38.624 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/3/749
14:36:38.624 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":749,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another mild morning. Wind WSW. A number of light ships arrived this morning.  N Boswell arrived the morning in his ship the <span class=highlight_yellow>William</span> Shand, a fine vessel, about 280 tons <span class=highlight_yellow>coppond</span><span class=highlight_yellow> called</span> on board. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; I took wine together at the Commercial with Bill Jervis <font color=#BFBFBF>in the </font>afternoon.</p>","pageId":781,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":703,"lock":null}
