14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":753,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind NW. In consequence of the account of J Galbraith's death, did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening went &amp; drank tea with J Tinley. Turned out a boisterous night.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":707,"lock":null}
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/9/754
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/11/9/754
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/1/775
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":775,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; damp morning. Wind S. Afterwards got to SE blowing very hard towards night with heavy rain. Mrs Scott so unwell obliged to keep her bed &amp; not able to see any person. Dined at home. Drank tea &amp; spent the evening at J Tinley's</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":729,"lock":null}
14:36:38.628 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
