14:36:38.629 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":784,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind WSW. On board the Hope. One man at work replacing the after <span class=highlight_yellow>raft</span><span class=highlight_yellow>p</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>rts</span>. Paid Walker block maker &pound;8.13/- for making new mainmast in 1828 outfit. H harry &amp; I walked up to Tynemouth &amp; had some whiskey toddy with J Cunningham &amp; afterwards attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":738,"lock":null}
14:36:38.629 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/11/785
14:36:38.629 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":785,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind SW. On board the Hope. The carpenter still employed at the <span class=highlight_yellow>raftport</span>. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott.</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":739,"lock":null}
