14:36:38.632 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":791,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning. Rather foggy. Wind WSW. Took a long walk with Captain Webb round Cullercoats, Tynemouth. Dined at home. Wrote to Boswell at <span class=highlight_yellow>Refe</span> informing him of the <span class=highlight_yellow>odesoan</span> freights being &pound;4 per ton &amp; 10 pct for <span class=highlight_yellow>tullers</span>. At the whist club &amp; with Bell Jarvis</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":745,"lock":null}
14:36:38.632 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/18/792
14:36:38.632 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":792,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind NNW. On board the Hope. The carpenter's busy with the stern <span class=highlight_yellow>bolling</span>. The timber ends etc &amp; going to put in another hook, having finished the after <span class=highlight_yellow>raftport</span>. Drew &pound;5 cash out of Chapmans. Dined at home. Spent the evening with Allen. Paid E Reed's mother &pound;2.9 the balance of his wages. Turned out a very wet night.</p>","pageId":786,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":746,"lock":null}
