14:36:38.641 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/7/781
14:36:38.641 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":781,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather, rather frosty. Wind SW &amp; SSW. The Hope arrived safe last night at 11 o'clock. Determined upon laying her up &amp; therefore took her off risk in the Premium &amp; Hope Clubs. Gave Stephenson &pound;20 to pay wages. The William Shand, Mr Boswell sailed today for <span class=highlight_yellow>Ryes</span> to take on passengers for New York. A great many colliers also got to sea. Dined with the Committee of the ____ &amp; in the evening went to the theatre, it being the bespeak of the Bachelors of North Shields.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":735,"lock":null}
