14:36:38.642 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":782,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day &amp; frosty. Wind WNW. On board the Hope all the morning. The people busy unrigging. Mr Allen &amp; I dined on board. Took wine and spent the evening at J Tinley's. Mr Temple there.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":736,"lock":null}
14:36:38.642 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/12/9/783
14:36:38.642 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":783,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine seasonable morning &amp; a hard frost. Wind SW. On board the Hope all the morning, where I dined. Hauled her upon Platty ways to get upained in the safe port etc. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; went to the theatre at half price, it being the Officers <span class=highlight_yellow>bespeak</span>.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":737,"lock":null}
