14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":441,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Blowing fresh from the WNW &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>lo</span>. Wrote to J Young requesting a few days to communicate with my brother. Walked up to the ship with J Tinley in the morning, who wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Netern</span> to send down the deed of release. All letters <span class=highlight_yellow>be</span> relative to our composition. Dined at home. In the evening had an <span class=highlight_yellow>ryotes</span> supper at the Northumberland. <span class=highlight_yellow>Won</span> a bet lost by <span class=highlight_yellow>Locklder</span> &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Holroryd</span>. Sat down 13 &amp; spent a pleasant evening</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":423,"lock":null}
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/24/442
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":442,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW &amp; afterwards changed to East with snow. Walked to Tynemouth. Attended a sale of old furniture at Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenskerths</span>. Mrs Dixon came down to see Mrs Scott. Dined at J Tinleys. A large party.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":424,"lock":null}
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/24/442
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":442,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW &amp; afterwards changed to East with snow. Walked to Tynemouth. Attended a sale of old furniture at Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenskerths</span>. Mrs Dixon came down to see Mrs Scott. Dined at J Tinleys. A large party.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":424,"lock":null}
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/25/443
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":443,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A hard frost. Wind E by S. Has been a little snow in the night. Last night the <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room was on fire but was discovered in time to get put out before much damage was done. In a short time it would broken out &amp; spread that the whole building would have been destroyed. The floor rafters and ceiling of <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room partly burnt. Walked with Boswell to Tynemouth. Dined at J Dales. Met a large party &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":425,"lock":null}
14:36:38.651 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.652 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/25/443
14:36:38.652 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":443,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A hard frost. Wind E by S. Has been a little snow in the night. Last night the <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room was on fire but was discovered in time to get put out before much damage was done. In a short time it would broken out &amp; spread that the whole building would have been destroyed. The floor rafters and ceiling of <span class=highlight_yellow>mews</span> room partly burnt. Walked with Boswell to Tynemouth. Dined at J Dales. Met a large party &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":425,"lock":null}
14:36:38.652 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/26/444
14:36:38.652 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":444,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from E. Received a letter from William with a copy of his answer to J Young. Paid Morton &amp; Thompson for the Hope's bowsprit pump for &pound;25.7/-. Dined with H Dale, Mr Mark &amp; Mr Jackson of the 80<sup>th</sup> regiment. Spent a pleasant evening. Walked to the ship in the morning. Turned out a very wet night. Sleet</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":426,"lock":null}
