14:36:38.653 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":446,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw cold foggy morning. Wind SW. Drove up to Newcastle with Mr Tinley, called upon Mrs Dixon, went to the Quay side, but could not do anything for the Hope. Returned to Shields by steam boat. Dined with J Tinley &amp; went to the whist club at Mr Richmonds in the evening.</p>","pageId":725,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":428,"lock":null}
14:36:38.653 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/3/421
14:36:38.653 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":421,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; hard frost. Wind W &amp; W by S. A French &amp; I walked round the town with Mr Chapman of <span class=highlight_yellow>Elseneur</span> to call upon his friends. Dined at 2 o'clock with A Harry. On board the Choise, A French, A Nicholson, <span class=highlight_yellow>Drewing</span>, Cunningham, Mark ____, self &amp; Captain ____ Mr Bradshaw came on board. After dinner we spent a very pleasant day.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":403,"lock":null}
