14:36:38.655 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":425,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild morning. Wind NNW. Employed the first of the morning in drawing. Went to the <span class=highlight_yellow>news</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>jbetenaid</span> room. Dined at home. In the evening at the club at J Tinley's. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Walowstegs</span> ship that Fenwick fixed by Mr Allen in Quebec &amp; East coast at the shipowners rates.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":407,"lock":null}
14:36:38.655 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/8/426
14:36:38.655 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":426,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning, having been a great deal of rain during the night. Wind NNW. Mrs Scott very ill. Wind variable during the day between NNW &amp; N by E. At church in the morning. The newspapers countenancing the speeding in Parliaments of the news as to declaring their intention  to grant Catholic emancipation which caused a great sensation here, but particularly to the <span class=highlight_yellow>incomcas</span> to it in both houses of parliament. Dined at J Tinley's. The two Carrs there.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":408,"lock":null}
