14:36:38.656 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/8/426
14:36:38.656 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":426,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning, having been a great deal of rain during the night. Wind NNW. Mrs Scott very ill. Wind variable during the day between NNW &amp; N by E. At church in the morning. The newspapers countenancing the speeding in Parliaments of the news as to declaring their intention  to grant Catholic emancipation which caused a great sensation here, but particularly to the <span class=highlight_yellow>incomcas</span> to it in both houses of parliament. Dined at J Tinley's. The two Carrs there.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":408,"lock":null}
14:36:38.656 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/2/9/427
14:36:38.656 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":427,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind NW. Engaged in the morning drawing. Dined at home. Went over the water &amp; joined H Harry, Boswell, French &amp; Nicolson at Bullocks &amp; took wine. Went to the theatre in the evening at North Shields. Received a letter from William. Mrs Scott suffering dreadful pain.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":409,"lock":null}
14:36:38.656 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
