14:36:38.657 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":427,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind NW. Engaged in the morning drawing. Dined at home. Went over the water &amp; joined H Harry, Boswell, French &amp; Nicolson at Bullocks &amp; took wine. Went to the theatre in the evening at North Shields. Received a letter from William. Mrs Scott suffering dreadful pain.</p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":409,"lock":null}
14:36:38.657 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/1/447
14:36:38.657 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":447,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW &amp; cool, rather frosty during the night. Went to church. On my return found Mr Dixon, Bell Smith &amp; Tom had come down to see Mrs Smith. In the afternoon walked to Tynemouth &amp; called upon Mr Jackson 80<sup>th</sup> regiment. In the evening at the Mulstrum. Had all <span class=highlight_yellow>Laserio</span></p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":429,"lock":null}
