14:36:38.659 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":459,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind NNS &amp; N by E. A heavy sea on the bar. Paid Clark, coopers for the Hope &pound;1.9/- Dined at home</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":441,"lock":null}
14:36:38.659 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/14/460
14:36:38.659 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":460,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Went to Newcastle by steamer. Ordered the Hope's coal down. Returned home to dinner. At the whist club in the evening at Allens. J Tinley received a letter from H Dale stating that he had C Young &amp; Sons orders to proceed against us for their debts.</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":442,"lock":null}
