14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":460,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Went to Newcastle by steamer. Ordered the Hope's coal down. Returned home to dinner. At the whist club in the evening at Allens. J Tinley received a letter from H Dale stating that he had C Young &amp; Sons orders to proceed against us for their debts.</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":442,"lock":null}
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/15/461
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":461,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; frosty. Wind NW. Changed during the day to NEE &amp; SE. Went to church in the morning. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum with Bell Jarvis</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":443,"lock":null}
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/15/461
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":461,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; frosty. Wind NW. Changed during the day to NEE &amp; SE. Went to church in the morning. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined at home. In the evening at the Mulstrum with Bell Jarvis</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":443,"lock":null}
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/16/462
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":462,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold &amp; Wind SW. A great number of light ships coming in. On board the Hope. Moved her from the Quay (Smiths) &amp; laid her upon the shore to have her keel surveyed for the Liberal Premium Club. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott. With Bell Jarvis at her sister Mary's</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":444,"lock":null}
14:36:38.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.661 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/16/462
14:36:38.661 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":462,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but cold &amp; Wind SW. A great number of light ships coming in. On board the Hope. Moved her from the Quay (Smiths) &amp; laid her upon the shore to have her keel surveyed for the Liberal Premium Club. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott. With Bell Jarvis at her sister Mary's</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":444,"lock":null}
14:36:38.661 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/17/463
14:36:38.661 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":463,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; blowing fresh from the SW &amp; cold. Another large fleet coming in. Borrowed off Robert &pound;5. On board the Hope. Two keels alongside. People engaged <span class=highlight_yellow>lending</span> sails. Walked up to the spout/<span class=highlight_yellow>huroonaschs</span> &amp; took lunch on board the 3 Brothers with A French, H Harry, Allen, W Harrison, J Wright there. Dined with J Tinley a party &amp; in the evening went to the ball which was thinly attended but a very pleasant one.</p>","pageId":727,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":445,"lock":null}
14:36:38.661 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
