14:36:38.665 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":471,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Frosty weather. Wind changed to NW. Walked to the newsroom about 2 o'clock &amp; read the papers. Wind in the afternoon changed to about N by E &amp; NNE. The Lady Jane sailed for the <span class=highlight_yellow>fishery</span>. Gave Mrs Scott her &frac14; year annuity &pound;75</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":453,"lock":null}
14:36:38.665 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/3/26/472
14:36:38.665 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":472,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, rather cool. Wind ENE to SSE. At the newsroom &amp; walked to Milburn Place with Mr Mark. Mrs Dixon came down to see Mrs Scott &amp; dinner. Attended the whist club for the last time this season.</p>","pageId":728,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":454,"lock":null}
