14:36:38.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":487,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Weather moderating and fair having been very strong all night. Wind about E by S. Several ships arrived this morning. Among them the Hope having left London on Tuesday. A schooner loaded with grain got upon the hard Sand, the sea higher than has been this winter. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed the Hope to load <span class=highlight_yellow>Townty</span><span class=highlight_yellow> main</span> again the price <span class=highlight_yellow>20/ chat</span> &amp; to be applied 8/6 freight. Returned by steam to dinner. Wind changed to SW &amp; then to SE.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":469,"lock":null}
14:36:38.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/11/488
14:36:38.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":488,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair morning. Wind WNW. About 11 o'clock began to rain. Drew &pound;40 out of Chapmans to pay wages &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>hadesmens</span> bells for the Hope. Mr Mark <span class=highlight_yellow>sit </span>took our dinner on board. Wind got to ESE again. Attended the whist club at R Pearts. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":730,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":470,"lock":null}
