14:36:38.677 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":495,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but has been rain early. Wind WNW. Paid the pilot of the Hope &pound;1.15/. Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Twi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>g</span><span class=highlight_yellow>el</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bragier</span> for the Hope &pound;12.13/-. Call upon &amp; saw about Richard's funeral. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the evening suppered at the Albion upon some oysters, given by A Cunningham. <span class=highlight_lime>With Ann!!!!!!</span></p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":477,"lock":null}
14:36:38.677 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/19/496
14:36:38.677 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":496,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning. Wind NW. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;166.5.1 &amp; returned it to Geo Dunn&amp; Sons. Continued raining heavily until 4 o'clock when it cleared up. Dined at home. With Bell Jervis in the evening. Turned out a very rainy night.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":478,"lock":null}
