14:36:38.679 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":500,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cold morning. Wind easterly. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with J Tinley. In the evening called upon Mr J Young &amp; had a long conversation both with him about taking our dividend without surveying. Also he did not seem so determined in his opposition. He desired me to see H Dale &amp; talk to him.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":482,"lock":null}
14:36:38.679 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/24/501
14:36:38.679 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":501,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of cold weather &amp; ENE wind. Dined at home &amp; afterwards went with H Harry &amp; R Peart &amp; drank whisky on board the Ardineaple  steamer Captain Cunningham. On our return when the boat reached the shore, Cunningham stumbled &amp; falling upon me, we both rolled overboard. Got a good dunking. Wrote to Mrs Scott of my determination not to make her an allowance.</p>","pageId":731,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":483,"lock":null}
14:36:38.679 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
