14:36:38.681 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":503,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Quite summer weather. Wind S &amp; changed before 12 o'clock to SE. Attended morning service. Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. On our return had a bottle of port at the George. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":485,"lock":null}
14:36:38.681 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/27/504
14:36:38.681 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":504,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning. Wind N by W. In the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon brought Emma down again. Dined at house. In the evening went up to the castle &amp; played a rubber at Dacres rooms.  With rum I think!!!</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":486,"lock":null}
14:36:38.681 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
