14:36:38.681 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":504,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning. Wind N by W. In the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon brought Emma down again. Dined at house. In the evening went up to the castle &amp; played a rubber at Dacres rooms.  With rum I think!!!</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":486,"lock":null}
14:36:38.681 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/4/28/505
14:36:38.681 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":505,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A showery morning &amp; blowing fresh from the N &amp; W by N and increased to a very heavy gale of wind varying between NNW and NNE which brought on a tremendous sea, a small sloop in coming in got upon the Heard Sand. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":487,"lock":null}
