14:36:38.689 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":522,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine spring weather. Wind NE. Mr Mark, Mr Sadler &amp; I walked up to Cramlington Spout. Found the Hope hauling off &amp; she shortly after proceeded down the river having only taken in 14 keels. Dined with Mr Sadler. With Bell Jarvis in the evening.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":504,"lock":null}
14:36:38.689 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/16/523
14:36:38.689 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":523,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful summers morning. Wind ENE. Received a letter from William agreeing to offer Younger 10/- in the &pound;. Drew &pound;20 out of Chapman. &pound;15 for Stephenson &amp; &pound;5 for self. Drew &pound;5 more in the afternoon. Stephenson wanting &pound;20. Dined at home. In the evening called upon A Dale to propose to join Younger's 10/- in full. Dale <span class=highlight_yellow>sacfe</span> for Younger, who I afterwards found much to my relief of mind had agreed to our proposal. Spent the evening with Mr Allen. With Bell Jervis.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":505,"lock":null}
14:36:38.689 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
