14:36:38.690 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":523,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful summers morning. Wind ENE. Received a letter from William agreeing to offer Younger 10/- in the &pound;. Drew &pound;20 out of Chapman. &pound;15 for Stephenson &amp; &pound;5 for self. Drew &pound;5 more in the afternoon. Stephenson wanting &pound;20. Dined at home. In the evening called upon A Dale to propose to join Younger's 10/- in full. Dale <span class=highlight_yellow>sacfe</span> for Younger, who I afterwards found much to my relief of mind had agreed to our proposal. Spent the evening with Mr Allen. With Bell Jervis.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":505,"lock":null}
14:36:38.690 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/17/2302
14:36:38.690 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2302,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... in the morning. Packed my cloths up. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening &amp; took some gin punch with <span class=highlight_yellow>Daises</span>. Took leave of Mrs Scott &amp; slept on board the Hope. Our <span class=highlight_yellow>from</span><span class=highlight_yellow> all</span> passengers. Anne Stoke also on board.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2242,"lock":null}
