14:36:38.691 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":524,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. The Hope was loaded on Friday but we could not go to sea in consequence of Young business. Determined not to sail until the morning tide. Walked to Tynemouth with H Harry. Took a warm bath. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; Mr Dadler took wine with me. Wrote to William of my intention to sail ...</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":506,"lock":null}
14:36:38.691 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/18/525
14:36:38.691 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":525,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock am got under way &amp; sailed from Shields with a westerly breeze &amp; fine weather. At 10 o'clock am becalmed off Sunderland, the wind having got round to SE. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock the breeze freshened a little but we made little way, being ebb tide. At 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> went to bed, the ship being abreast of the Tees</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":507,"lock":null}
