14:36:38.691 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":525,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock am got under way &amp; sailed from Shields with a westerly breeze &amp; fine weather. At 10 o'clock am becalmed off Sunderland, the wind having got round to SE. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock the breeze freshened a little but we made little way, being ebb tide. At 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> went to bed, the ship being abreast of the Tees</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":507,"lock":null}
14:36:38.691 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/19/526
14:36:38.691 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":526,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>has been blowing pretty fresh all night from the SE &amp; SSE. Got up at 8 o'clock am. The ship abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Hunt</span><span class=highlight_yellow>c</span><span class=highlight_yellow>li</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span><span class=highlight_yellow>f</span> Foot. The wind the same but moderate &amp; fine weather. Anne very unwell, but more frightened not having been at sea before. Towards evening wind very calm again. Turned in at 10 o'clock.  The ship in <span class=highlight_yellow>a very</span> little wind.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":508,"lock":null}
