14:36:38.692 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":509,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning blowing rather fresh from NW by W. Walked with Tom Smith down to Low Town &amp; afterwards to Alec Sadlers at Whitle Point. Dined at home &amp; after tea again walked to Whitle Point but the sloop had not come down.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":491,"lock":null}
14:36:38.692 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/20/527
14:36:38.692 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":527,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NE. Turned out a 8 o'clock am. The ship off Robin Hoods but the ebb tide &amp; heavy SE swell setting against us drove us <span class=highlight_yellow>back</span> to Whitby. In the afternoon with the <span class=highlight_yellow>fload</span> a better breeze spring up &amp; set us ahead again &amp; 10 o'clock pm bed time, we were off Scarborough. A fine moonlit night.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":509,"lock":null}
