14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":535,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind NE. Wrote to Mr Vernon to send <span class=highlight_yellow>Inspector</span> Galbraith to London. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>changers</span>. Did nothing. Dined with Richmond.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":517,"lock":null}
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/29/536
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":536,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine weather. Wind still NE &amp; ENE. Mr Lee drove me into the city. Attended the local exchange. Sold 63 more of the Hope's coals. Went to the Royal Ex. Could not fix. Walked out of the city. Dined at Mr Lees. Mr &amp; Bob Marsh &amp; F Barclay there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":518,"lock":null}
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/29/536
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":536,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine weather. Wind still NE &amp; ENE. Mr Lee drove me into the city. Attended the local exchange. Sold 63 more of the Hope's coals. Went to the Royal Ex. Could not fix. Walked out of the city. Dined at Mr Lees. Mr &amp; Bob Marsh &amp; F Barclay there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":518,"lock":null}
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/3/510
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":510,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning after a few showers of rain during the night. Wind W by S. Tom Smith, Emma &amp; I went to church &amp; after <font color=#BFBFBF>[the] </font>service, Tom &amp; I walked up through the country to Benton, dined &amp; stayed all night. A very windy day &amp; unpleasant walking.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":492,"lock":null}
14:36:38.697 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/3/510
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":510,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning after a few showers of rain during the night. Wind W by S. Tom Smith, Emma &amp; I went to church &amp; after <font color=#BFBFBF>[the] </font>service, Tom &amp; I walked up through the country to Benton, dined &amp; stayed all night. A very windy day &amp; unpleasant walking.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":492,"lock":null}
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/30/537
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":537,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cloudy morning. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. He &amp; his father walked with me down to the Hope. Saw the St Catherine Docks in our way &amp; the most perfect &amp; comfortable perhaps of thing of the sort all the warehouses &amp; upon so good a place. Had lunch on board &amp; I afterwards attended changes but did nothing for the ship. Walked out of the city with Inspector Chapman &amp; dined with him. His brothers the captain, Thomas, Ben, Mr Graham &amp; a Mr Day there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":519,"lock":null}
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/30/537
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":537,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cloudy morning. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. He &amp; his father walked with me down to the Hope. Saw the St Catherine Docks in our way &amp; the most perfect &amp; comfortable perhaps of thing of the sort all the warehouses &amp; upon so good a place. Had lunch on board &amp; I afterwards attended changes but did nothing for the ship. Walked out of the city with Inspector Chapman &amp; dined with him. His brothers the captain, Thomas, Ben, Mr Graham &amp; a Mr Day there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":519,"lock":null}
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/31/538
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":538,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind about N. Went with the Miss Lees to the chapel in Vern Street. Afterwards called upon Mr &amp; Mrs Lumley in Gower Street. Mr Lee very unwell, consumption, going to leave this <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span>. Called upon Mr Linskill. Went to see Mary &amp; Emma in Sloan Street &amp; then to the park. Dined with Mr ward &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":520,"lock":null}
14:36:38.698 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/31/538
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":538,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind about N. Went with the Miss Lees to the chapel in Vern Street. Afterwards called upon Mr &amp; Mrs Lumley in Gower Street. Mr Lee very unwell, consumption, going to leave this <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span>. Called upon Mr Linskill. Went to see Mary &amp; Emma in Sloan Street &amp; then to the park. Dined with Mr ward &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":520,"lock":null}
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/4/511
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":511,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. But still blowing hard from the NW. Amused ourselves for a short time in the plantations with the beagles. Mrs Dixon took us into Newcastle in the carriage. Tom Smith transacted his business there &amp; we afterwards walked down to St Anthon's to see a sloop he had purchased for his colliery. Returned to Shields by steam to dinner.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":493,"lock":null}
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/4/511
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":511,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning. But still blowing hard from the NW. Amused ourselves for a short time in the plantations with the beagles. Mrs Dixon took us into Newcastle in the carriage. Tom Smith transacted his business there &amp; we afterwards walked down to St Anthon's to see a sloop he had purchased for his colliery. Returned to Shields by steam to dinner.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":493,"lock":null}
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/5/512
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":512,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning with showers. Wind SSW. Several light ships arrived. Tom &amp; Mrs Smith left us this morning for Benton. Dined at home. Accepted a bill at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>months</span> dated 16 April for polices &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Insurance</span> 1 &amp; 2 coal voyages in general Premium Club &pound;13.7.10. With Bell Jervis in the evening</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":494,"lock":null}
14:36:38.699 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
