14:36:38.700 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":513,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Called upon &amp; spent an hour with Fergusson the artist. Dined at home. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth with Fergusson to sketch the ruins. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Davies</span> Rooms at the Castle</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":495,"lock":null}
14:36:38.700 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/7/514
14:36:38.700 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":514,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant spring morning. Wind NNW. Changed during the day to NE &amp; again at night to W. Took a walk round by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. A beautiful summers day. Dined with Jackson 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment at the Castle. H Dale, Dacres, RA. Newton &amp; a Lieutenant Hamilton Brown there. (with 1<sup>st</sup> term)</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":496,"lock":null}
