14:36:38.701 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":514,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant spring morning. Wind NNW. Changed during the day to NE &amp; again at night to W. Took a walk round by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. A beautiful summers day. Dined with Jackson 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment at the Castle. H Dale, Dacres, RA. Newton &amp; a Lieutenant Hamilton Brown there. (with 1<sup>st</sup> term)</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":496,"lock":null}
14:36:38.701 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/5/8/515
14:36:38.701 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":515,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning . A fine mild rain. Wind W by N. Called upon Fergusson Dined at home. The Hope arrived this evening after a fine passage. Left Gravesend on Wednesday morning.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":497,"lock":null}
14:36:38.701 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
