14:36:38.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":572,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... The slightest air possible during the whole of the day &amp; making such little way that we were enabled to catch a couple of coldlings by our lines going near the bottom. At 6 o'clock pm a slight breeze sprung up from the NNE which run us pretty near against the north end of Bornholm, where at 9 o'clock it suddenly changed to against us, but died away to a dead calm. Had our whisky &amp; water &amp; turned in. Bornholm a very fine island as sun with the glass.</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":549,"lock":null}
14:36:38.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/24/573
14:36:38.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":573,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock after a sound snooze. After a dead calm, the whole of the night, at 6 o'clock this morning a breeze sprung up from NW &amp; when we got upon deck, found we were gradually loosing slight of the island. Got studding sails set, but not at any time going more than four knots, sometimes not so much.</p>\r\n<p>Most beautiful weather, but the sun not so scorching as yesterday. Accompanied the whole day by thousands of large dragon flies that flew about &amp; alighted upon our rigging which was at times covered with them. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock, went below &amp; had our rum &amp; water &amp; when we went to bed at &frac12; past 9 o'clock, the wind continued favourable &amp; a fine breeze.</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":550,"lock":null}
14:36:38.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/24/573
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":573,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock after a sound snooze. After a dead calm, the whole of the night, at 6 o'clock this morning a breeze sprung up from NW &amp; when we got upon deck, found we were gradually loosing slight of the island. Got studding sails set, but not at any time going more than four knots, sometimes not so much.</p>\r\n<p>Most beautiful weather, but the sun not so scorching as yesterday. Accompanied the whole day by thousands of large dragon flies that flew about &amp; alighted upon our rigging which was at times covered with them. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock, went below &amp; had our rum &amp; water &amp; when we went to bed at &frac12; past 9 o'clock, the wind continued favourable &amp; a fine breeze.</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":550,"lock":null}
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/25/2306
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2306,"version":7,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock &amp; most delightful morning, with a fine breeze from NW. been going 5 &amp; 6 knots all night. After breakfast going 6 knots &amp; steering an ENE course. At few of our companions, the dragon flies still with us. At 12 o'clock took observation &amp; by it, <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> in lat:56.36. long: 18.41</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2246,"lock":null}
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/25/2306
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2306,"version":7,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock &amp; most delightful morning, with a fine breeze from NW. been going 5 &amp; 6 knots all night. After breakfast going 6 knots &amp; steering an ENE course. At few of our companions, the dragon flies still with us. At 12 o'clock took observation &amp; by it, <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> in lat:56.36. long: 18.41</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2246,"lock":null}
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/25/574
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":574,"version":3,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... knots. At &frac14; past 4 o'clock supposed to two abreast <font color=#BFBFBF>of </font>the south end of the Ireland of Gotland &amp; when we going with a fine NW breeze at the rate of 7 &frac12; knots. Suddenly &amp; in a moment, taken all aback, got lower &amp; topmast studdingsails in, wind in the courses of a few minutes, flying all round the compass in the most extraordinary way. At last <span class=highlight_yellow>sumed</span> to settle at east.</p>\r\n<p>A large ship upon our weather bow. Supposed to be a republican frigate. The captain amused himself today in painting the covering boards &amp; waterways. The men this afternoon employed in washing the beef, the whole of which is unfortunately very much tainted. In the course of the evening the wind got to the WSW so that we laid up ENE going on 3 &amp; 4 knots. At 8 o'clock took our grog &amp; turned in at 11 o'clock. Wind more favourable</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":551,"lock":null}
14:36:38.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
