14:36:38.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":575,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2892-image-baltic.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>Voyage for Copenhagen to St Petersburg</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
14:36:38.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/26/576
14:36:38.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":576,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning at a little after 7 o'clock. Bob &amp; I had some difficulty in making our minds up to turn out, the morning being so tremendously wet. The rain coming down in torrents with heavy thunder &amp; lightning, one peal so close to us that it sounded as if it was our top gallant mast head. In fact we were enveloped in clouds, thunder &amp; lightning, much too near to be agreeable. This deluge of rain has continued since 4 o'clock. However the wind was fair for us, a fresh breeze at SW &amp; giving 6 knots, our course NE by E. At 9 o'clock the rain eased &amp; by 10 o'clock we had fine weather, warm wind the <span class=highlight_yellow>lamed</span> &amp; going 5 &frac12; knots, with studding sails set. At 12 o'clock we were by observance in lat: 58.3 long: 20.50. Having come 110 miles since yesterday at noon. Little or nothing has ...</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":552,"lock":null}
