y were the most hideous likenesses to the human face that <span class=highlight_yellow>there</span> could be. Before each was a <span class=highlight_yellow>candle</span> which was kept constantly burning &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>how</span> every one of the poor ignorant devils on payment stopped crossing themselves, bowing &amp; seeming to repeat ...</p>","pageId":747,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":558,"lock":null}
14:36:38.722 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/4/543
14:36:38.722 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":543,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 11 o'clock. Breakfasted at the Fountain &amp; saw Ann safe to her aunty. Walked into the city. Called at the country house. William gone. Returned to Nottingham Place with Mr Lee. Went with the Lees to dine with A Patterson at Clapton, a party. A very fine but extremely hot day. Wind WNW &amp; NW. Received a letter from Mr Vernon of J Galbraith setting off for London.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":525,"lock":null}
