14:36:38.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/8/2303
14:36:38.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2303,"version":6,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Petersburg&nbsp;voyage&nbsp;commences</p>","pageId":737,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2243,"lock":null}
14:36:38.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/8/551
14:36:38.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":551,"version":1,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NW. A good deal of rain after a breakfast. Walked into the city. Brought a filtering machine for the ship. Gave Stephenson &pound;25.  Settled the freight account with William &amp; received the balance &pound;30.4/-. Called at the Russian consul for passports.  Dined at Richmonds. Hard J Jobling Chambers &amp; there. When I got home, found J Gilbraith had arrived.</p>","pageId":737,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":529,"lock":null}
14:36:38.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/8/551
14:36:38.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":551,"version":1,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NW. A good deal of rain after a breakfast. Walked into the city. Brought a filtering machine for the ship. Gave Stephenson &pound;25.  Settled the freight account with William &amp; received the balance &pound;30.4/-. Called at the Russian consul for passports.  Dined at Richmonds. Hard J Jobling Chambers &amp; there. When I got home, found J Gilbraith had arrived.</p>","pageId":737,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":529,"lock":null}
14:36:38.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/6/9/552
14:36:38.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":552,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but rather dull. Wind NNE. <span class=highlight_yellow>Later</span> J Galbraith &amp; I took a coach from Nottingham Place for the city with our cloths <span class=highlight_yellow>for</span> the ship's boat with four hands at Billingsgate to carry all our things to the ship. <del>Called upon the Russian Consol.</del> The party with one Vinccent carrying &frac12; dozen wine with us took a waterman at the Customs House &amp; went down to the ship to dinner. In the evening attended Greenwich Fair which was not so crowded as I have seen it &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>letto</span><span class=highlight_yellow> run</span>. I called upon G Watts. William, Lee &amp; Vincent left us &amp; Bob Marsh J.G. &amp; I returned to the ship a little after 10 o'clock to sleep. Bob &amp; I smoked a cloud, wet both eyes &amp; turned in.</p>","pageId":737,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":530,"lock":null}
14:36:38.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
