14:36:38.735 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2316,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... filled with ancient armour, arms &amp; belonging to various nations and exceedingly curious, colours &amp; standards taken battle, models of fortifications, cannon &amp; mortars, the cloths, arms &amp; accoutrements belonging to peter the Great, the late Emperor Alexander &amp; several Generals etc. etc. etc. all very curious &amp; well worth seeing, particularly the funeral car for the late Alexander, a most magnificent vehicle.</p>\r\n<p>After leaving the Arsenal Me Lindsley accompanied us to the market near the Cesan Church where we purchased several articles as presents for the Lees etc.</p>\r\n<p>Came home to dinner, Mr Lindsley with us had <span class=highlight_yellow>Sadaek</span> for dinner, <span class=highlight_yellow>these</span> fish and another called <span class=highlight_yellow>Saggee</span> are fine flavoured &amp; most excellent.</p>\r\n<p>The pay of the Russian soldiers &amp; officers is very trifling. That of a <span class=highlight_yellow>S</span><span class=highlight_yellow>aba</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ll</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ere</span> &pound;16 a year &amp; a private 11 Rubbles, not much more than 9/- English. The private of the bodyguard have 13 Rubbles</p>\r\n<p>Being rather tired in the evening we only took a short walk down the Newsky Prospect</p>","pageId":757,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2256,"lock":null}
14:36:38.735 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/15/616
14:36:38.735 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":616,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Immediately after breakfast to <span class=highlight_yellow>drivzkeys</span> &amp; went to the Arsenal where we found the Baron had been as good as his word. A soldier was in waiting for us, who took us over the different departments. They were very busy making brass cannon. The machinery for boring &amp; polishing them very beautiful. Several rooms ...</p>","pageId":757,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":580,"lock":null}
