14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/21/623
14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":623,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Could not get to Peterhoff without our papers, which Stephenson required to clear the ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Stayed</span> to give it up. Dined on board the David. Turned out a rainy afternoon. Came down in torrents. Engaged to take tea with Mr Ross but the rain prevented us. Did not leave the ship. </p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":587,"lock":null}
14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/21/623
14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":623,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Could not get to Peterhoff without our papers, which Stephenson required to clear the ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Stayed</span> to give it up. Dined on board the David. Turned out a rainy afternoon. Came down in torrents. Engaged to take tea with Mr Ross but the rain prevented us. Did not leave the ship. </p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":587,"lock":null}
14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/7/22/624
14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":624,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from the Westward. Several ships arrived. Among them the Herald Yacht with Lady Heytesbury on board, the wife of the British ambassador. We ourselves are cleared and ready for sea, but wind bound. Brought four pairs of boots &amp; two pairs of slippers for which I only gave 30 rubbles equal to about 25/-. Dined on board. Brought seven Caviar for <span class=highlight_yellow>jrbling</span>. Richmond etc. Drank a glass of punch with the Ross &amp; afterwards called at ____.</p>\r\n<p>Much annoyed with a swollen face arising from a decayed tooth &amp; cold. Walked round the man of wars <span class=highlight_yellow>mold</span> &amp; went on board one of their new 74's. the Russian fleet returned from a cruise to be inspected by the Emperor, who it is reported has returned to Petersburg</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":588,"lock":null}
14:36:38.741 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
