14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/11/649
14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":649,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the west which soon caused a tremendous sea. Obliged to him too under close reefed topsails until about 4 o'clock when we <span class=highlight_yellow>wone</span> ship &amp; lay too under close reefed main topsail. What with the howling of the wind, the rolling &amp; tossing of the ship &amp; creaking of tallow casks besides being leaky &amp; upon a lee shore, we had spent a most uncomfortable day. Did not attempt to go to bed, indeed mine was so damp I could not, but I lay down upon the captains about midnight all standing </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":611,"lock":null}
14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/11/649
14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":649,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the west which soon caused a tremendous sea. Obliged to him too under close reefed topsails until about 4 o'clock when we <span class=highlight_yellow>wone</span> ship &amp; lay too under close reefed main topsail. What with the howling of the wind, the rolling &amp; tossing of the ship &amp; creaking of tallow casks besides being leaky &amp; upon a lee shore, we had spent a most uncomfortable day. Did not attempt to go to bed, indeed mine was so damp I could not, but I lay down upon the captains about midnight all standing </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":611,"lock":null}
14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/12/650
14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":650,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Spent a miserable night, having had little or no sleep. Looked  out about 5 o'clock. The gale as heavy as ever &amp; without any appearance of change, although the sky very clear. At 11 o'clock Masskand Castle in sight distant about 4 leagues, when we determined no longer to contend with the winds but bore away for Gottenburg &amp; in the course of half an hour those wise few that did not follow our example at &frac12; past 3 o'clock we reached Wings sound &amp; before 5 o'clock brought up in the harbour of Warga, a small channel between two docks, rejoicing with the prospect of obtaining a good nights rest. </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":612,"lock":null}
14:36:38.761 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/12/650
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":650,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Spent a miserable night, having had little or no sleep. Looked  out about 5 o'clock. The gale as heavy as ever &amp; without any appearance of change, although the sky very clear. At 11 o'clock Masskand Castle in sight distant about 4 leagues, when we determined no longer to contend with the winds but bore away for Gottenburg &amp; in the course of half an hour those wise few that did not follow our example at &frac12; past 3 o'clock we reached Wings sound &amp; before 5 o'clock brought up in the harbour of Warga, a small channel between two docks, rejoicing with the prospect of obtaining a good nights rest. </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":612,"lock":null}
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/13/651
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":651,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear day, but still blowing hard from the westward.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast, Bob the Captain J Galbraith &amp; I landed. One of the fishermen's yawls (large size) fine sea boats &amp; safe &amp; sailed up to Gothenburg where we spent the day in seeing the town, which is much better than I expected &amp; larger, the country around entirely rock, having a novel wild &amp; beautiful appearance altogether being interspersed with valleys &amp; rivers which were the only spots that could be cultivated &amp; were made the most of. They had one of their annual fares which lasts eight days, but did not seem well attended. After having had our dinner at one of their inns, considering the country very comfortable, we again embarked at 4 o'clock&amp; the winds being against us, we had a <span class=highlight_yellow>turning</span> passage of it, &amp; did not reach the ship until near 8 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>And after having our tea blowing a cloud &amp; discussing a glass of grog, turned in before 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":613,"lock":null}
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/13/651
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":651,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear day, but still blowing hard from the westward.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast, Bob the Captain J Galbraith &amp; I landed. One of the fishermen's yawls (large size) fine sea boats &amp; safe &amp; sailed up to Gothenburg where we spent the day in seeing the town, which is much better than I expected &amp; larger, the country around entirely rock, having a novel wild &amp; beautiful appearance altogether being interspersed with valleys &amp; rivers which were the only spots that could be cultivated &amp; were made the most of. They had one of their annual fares which lasts eight days, but did not seem well attended. After having had our dinner at one of their inns, considering the country very comfortable, we again embarked at 4 o'clock&amp; the winds being against us, we had a <span class=highlight_yellow>turning</span> passage of it, &amp; did not reach the ship until near 8 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>And after having our tea blowing a cloud &amp; discussing a glass of grog, turned in before 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":613,"lock":null}
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/14/652
14:36:38.762 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":652,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock. In the middle of the night it became quite calm &amp; the wind changing to the eastward enabled us to get underway. Between 8 &amp; 9 o'clock &amp; to leave a place that I never again wish to see under similar circumstances. As the wind changed with the moon, it will carry us safely to England ...</p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":614,"lock":null}
