14:36:38.763 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":653,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... should it continue. At 6 o'clock passed the Scaw Light with a fresh breeze &amp; every appearance of it increasing, the sea making very much. Turned <font color=#BFBFBF>in </font>at about our usual hour</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":615,"lock":null}
14:36:38.763 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/15/2321
14:36:38.763 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2321,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the stateroom scuttle light, wet my bed &amp; I did not expect to have had one to sleep in tonight, indeed had the gale continued I should not have cared about it, but I contrived by placing canvas between the bed and sides of the vessel to fortify it pretty well from the wet &amp; thus gained a better nights rest than I anticipated.</p>\r\n<p>My face beginning to swell again, but no pain.</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2261,"lock":null}
14:36:38.763 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.763 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/15/2321
14:36:38.764 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2321,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the stateroom scuttle light, wet my bed &amp; I did not expect to have had one to sleep in tonight, indeed had the gale continued I should not have cared about it, but I contrived by placing canvas between the bed and sides of the vessel to fortify it pretty well from the wet &amp; thus gained a better nights rest than I anticipated.</p>\r\n<p>My face beginning to swell again, but no pain.</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2261,"lock":null}
14:36:38.764 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/15/654
14:36:38.764 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":654,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up this morning at a little before 8 o'clock after a very boisterous night, the wind having increased to more than half a gale with a tremendous sea, right aft so that we made good way, though at the sacrifice of our comfort. Everything above &amp; below being wet &amp; in confusion. At 5 o'clock this morning a tremendous heavy sea pooped us, stove &amp; carried away our jolly boat &amp; alarmed us so much fearing it had stove in the dark lights &amp; if it had so happened we of course should have been waterlogged. Knowing the delicate state of the <span class=highlight_yellow>archboard</span>, where she was making a great deal of water, the fear of another heavy sea striking us kept me in a very uncomfortable state the whole of the day. Towards evening however both wind &amp; sea fell considerably. We have been going today from 6&frac12;  to 7 knots. Ship laboured very much &amp; made a deal of water. We consider we have got this evening considerably to the westward of the Naze of Norway, say 50 miles.</p>\r\n<p>A great deal of water having come into ...</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":616,"lock":null}
14:36:38.764 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
