14:36:38.775 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":672,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... made ourselves decent &amp; comfortable Bob &amp; I walked up to George in the Red Lion Square where we made &amp; enjoyed a hearty dinner of pigeon &amp; veal pies &amp; cold <span class=highlight_yellow>mullion</span>, discharged a good glass of punch &amp; returned to Chambers. With the <span class=highlight_yellow>appearance</span> of Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Furmedye</span>, Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>laudress</span>, I made myself a good perch for the night with Bob's <span class=highlight_yellow>mallrafs</span> in the corner of his room, turned in &amp; enjoyed an excellent nights rest, although the bed was rather a hard one.</p>\r\n<p>Thus ends our Petersburg voyage which upon the whole we have enjoyed, but we could have dispensed with the tumultuous bad weather we experienced. Thank God we have got back safe &amp; without any accident worth mentioning to the ship.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":634,"lock":null}
14:36:38.775 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/3/640
14:36:38.775 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
14:36:38.775 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.776 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/3/640
14:36:38.776 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
14:36:38.776 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/8/30/673
14:36:38.776 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":673,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up much refreshed. More moderate weather. Wind NE rather cloudy. We fully intended to have gone to church, but Bob &amp; I took up so much linin in the washing &amp; cleaning ourselves that it was past the hour before we were aware of it. Turned out a very fine day. We called upon Mr Ward who had gone to Paris will William. Walked through St James park up to Hyde Park where we strolled till 6 o'clock. Very few people or carriages there. Town exceedingly thin from thence came we went to Mr Piazza Covent garden &amp; enjoyed a comfortable dinner &amp; a good bottle of old port. Returned to Chambers between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":635,"lock":null}
14:36:38.776 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
