14:36:38.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":646,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at the usual hour &amp; found the ship off the Koll having got underway at 9 am with a fresh breeze at W by S, proceeding at the rate of 6 or 6 &frac12; knots during the whole of the day. Passed Anholt at about 6 o'clock in the evening</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":608,"lock":null}
14:36:38.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/1/675
14:36:38.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":675,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day &amp; showery. Walked into the city &amp; down to the docks. Found them employed in moving the ship to a birth &amp; then began to deliver her cargo before I left. Went to <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mbers</span> &amp; afterwards walked westward. Dined with Jobling in the Adelphi, only ourselves. Spent a pleasant day. Got rather too much wine. Slept all night in Villiers Street</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":637,"lock":null}
14:36:38.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
