14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":675,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day &amp; showery. Walked into the city &amp; down to the docks. Found them employed in moving the ship to a birth &amp; then began to deliver her cargo before I left. Went to <span class=highlight_yellow>cha</span><span class=highlight_yellow>mbers</span> &amp; afterwards walked westward. Dined with Jobling in the Adelphi, only ourselves. Spent a pleasant day. Got rather too much wine. Slept all night in Villiers Street</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":637,"lock":null}
14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/10/689
14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":689,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery weather. Wind S W. Took a cab into the city and afterwards walked to the docks. Found the people employed hauling the ship out, intending to take her down to Dukes shore. Received from Stephenson &pound;89.7.6 for the lathwood. <span class=underline_double>With Maryann</span>.  Attended chambers. H Harry never made his appearance. Did nothing. Went by a Paddington stage to Nottingham Place where Bob Marsh &amp; I dined with William &amp; enjoyed ourselves much.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":647,"lock":null}
14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
