14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":689,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery weather. Wind S W. Took a cab into the city and afterwards walked to the docks. Found the people employed hauling the ship out, intending to take her down to Dukes shore. Received from Stephenson &pound;89.7.6 for the lathwood. <span class=underline_double>With Maryann</span>.  Attended chambers. H Harry never made his appearance. Did nothing. Went by a Paddington stage to Nottingham Place where Bob Marsh &amp; I dined with William &amp; enjoyed ourselves much.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":647,"lock":null}
14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/11/2325
14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2325,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... since I had the pleasure of seeing him. We afterwards took a Greenwich boat &amp; went down to the Hope upon Dowslands way where we dined off cold mutton. At low water looked at her bottom &amp; gave orders for her to go into the dock to be caulked. Turned out an exceptionally wet evening. Had our tea on board &amp; afterwards took a <span class=highlight_yellow>Mackware</span> stage to Leadenhall Street &amp; then walked to New Inn. Bob Marsh at the theatre.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2265,"lock":null}
14:36:38.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
