14:36:38.784 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":692,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning wind. Feeling exceptionally annoyed &amp; hurt by Bob Marsh's conduct, I got up early &amp; left his chambers. Indeed had it not been so late I should have done so last night. Breakfasted with William in Nottingham Place. We afterwards went to <span class=highlight_yellow>vere</span> St Chapel. In the afternoon we walked to Sloan Street &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>we</span> called at Mrs Locks to see Mary &amp; Emma. On our way home had a <span class=highlight_yellow>stroll</span> in Hyde Park. Very few people there. Vincent <span class=highlight_yellow>Fitz</span><span class=highlight_yellow>manian</span> &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us. We intended to have given the latter a hint that his company could be dispensed with, but did not, as it might have caused much unpleasantness. I determined however to tell him what I thought of his conduct, but had not an opportunity. He shall yet hear more about it. A very wet night</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":650,"lock":null}
14:36:38.784 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/2326
14:36:38.784 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2326,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Rather showery. Called at the New Inn. Put my <font color=#222222>portmanteau</font>  &amp; bag into a cab &amp; drove up to Nottingham Place. Spent the evening quietly at home.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2266,"lock":null}
14:36:38.784 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/2326
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2326,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Rather showery. Called at the New Inn. Put my <font color=#222222>portmanteau</font>  &amp; bag into a cab &amp; drove up to Nottingham Place. Spent the evening quietly at home.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2266,"lock":null}
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/693
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":693,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning. Wind WSW. Went into the city upon a Paddington stage coach rather early, to pack a hamper of <span class=highlight_yellow>special madeira</span> up for Mr Chapman of Elseineur. J Galbraith &amp; I thence walked down to Dowson's dock to the Hope, where we dined. The people busy caulking &amp; repairing some soft places where she has been leaking. Left the ship between 4 &amp; 5 o'clock. Brought new <span class=highlight_yellow>umbrella</span></p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":651,"lock":null}
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/14/693
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":693,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning. Wind WSW. Went into the city upon a Paddington stage coach rather early, to pack a hamper of <span class=highlight_yellow>special madeira</span> up for Mr Chapman of Elseineur. J Galbraith &amp; I thence walked down to Dowson's dock to the Hope, where we dined. The people busy caulking &amp; repairing some soft places where she has been leaking. Left the ship between 4 &amp; 5 o'clock. Brought new <span class=highlight_yellow>umbrella</span></p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":651,"lock":null}
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/15/694
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":694,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull showery day. Wind W by N. Went by a Paddington dray into the city. Stephenson called at the office having got his dispatches. Surprised to find that Chapmans had given him a copy of a charter which did not agree with that I signed, having <span class=highlight_yellow>Stavers</span> introduced. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Color's</span> office &amp; saw the original charter &amp; found it <span class=highlight_yellow>outlined</span>. Exceedingly surprised &amp; angry that such a thing should be done without my knowledge or sanction &amp; the more surprised that Chapmans should permit it. A most unjustifiable act, nay worse. Walked down to the ship, the people getting on very well or it seem to be giving her a good caulking. Dined on board. J Galbraith &amp; I walked home by Fleet Street, Regent Street etc...</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":652,"lock":null}
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/15/694
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":694,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull showery day. Wind W by N. Went by a Paddington dray into the city. Stephenson called at the office having got his dispatches. Surprised to find that Chapmans had given him a copy of a charter which did not agree with that I signed, having <span class=highlight_yellow>Stavers</span> introduced. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Color's</span> office &amp; saw the original charter &amp; found it <span class=highlight_yellow>outlined</span>. Exceedingly surprised &amp; angry that such a thing should be done without my knowledge or sanction &amp; the more surprised that Chapmans should permit it. A most unjustifiable act, nay worse. Walked down to the ship, the people getting on very well or it seem to be giving her a good caulking. Dined on board. J Galbraith &amp; I walked home by Fleet Street, Regent Street etc...</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":652,"lock":null}
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/695
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":695,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day &amp; been raining heavy all night. Wind NE. Took a Paddington dray to the city. Called at Chapmans &amp; agreed to take 500 staves and not more unless the master wished. The agent giving me a letter pledging himself to that effect. On the Coal Exchange nothing particular there. Did not find a ship to take me to Shields. Took a coach &amp; carried all J G's cloths down to the ship. Found her just hauled out of dock. Had some <span class=highlight_yellow>beef</span>.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":653,"lock":null}
14:36:38.785 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/695
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":695,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day &amp; been raining heavy all night. Wind NE. Took a Paddington dray to the city. Called at Chapmans &amp; agreed to take 500 staves and not more unless the master wished. The agent giving me a letter pledging himself to that effect. On the Coal Exchange nothing particular there. Did not find a ship to take me to Shields. Took a coach &amp; carried all J G's cloths down to the ship. Found her just hauled out of dock. Had some <span class=highlight_yellow>beef</span>.</p>","pageId":774,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":653,"lock":null}
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/696
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":696,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Packed my clothes up ready to tranship. William, J.G. &amp; I walked up home calling at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Carfs</span> &amp; at the Cock in the Fleet Street where we had some oysters &amp; brandy &amp; water. Stephenson gave me his accounts.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":654,"lock":null}
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/16/696
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":696,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Packed my clothes up ready to tranship. William, J.G. &amp; I walked up home calling at Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Carfs</span> &amp; at the Cock in the Fleet Street where we had some oysters &amp; brandy &amp; water. Stephenson gave me his accounts.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":654,"lock":null}
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/17/697
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":697,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NE. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Stephenson up, but not cleared for want of papers relative to the sum, from the West India docks. J Galbraith &amp; I walked down to the ship. Dined on board. Got our ballast alongside. Put all my cloths etc. on board the Peggy, captain Hunter, intending to take my passage to Shields in her. She hauled out of the Regents Canal &amp; proceeded down the river to Purfleet to ballast. William &amp; I walked up to the city, calling at Chapmans respecting the clearing papers.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":655,"lock":null}
14:36:38.786 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.787 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/17/697
14:36:38.787 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":697,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NE. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Stephenson up, but not cleared for want of papers relative to the sum, from the West India docks. J Galbraith &amp; I walked down to the ship. Dined on board. Got our ballast alongside. Put all my cloths etc. on board the Peggy, captain Hunter, intending to take my passage to Shields in her. She hauled out of the Regents Canal &amp; proceeded down the river to Purfleet to ballast. William &amp; I walked up to the city, calling at Chapmans respecting the clearing papers.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":655,"lock":null}
14:36:38.787 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/18/2327
14:36:38.787 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2327,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... Peggy laying at the wharf at Purfleet. Young White of Wordland near Durham, a 4<sup>th</sup> mate in the company's service also joined us. Blew a cloud or two &amp; turned in.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2267,"lock":null}
