14:36:38.787 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2327,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... Peggy laying at the wharf at Purfleet. Young White of Wordland near Durham, a 4<sup>th</sup> mate in the company's service also joined us. Blew a cloud or two &amp; turned in.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2267,"lock":null}
14:36:38.787 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/18/698
14:36:38.787 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":698,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been raining very heavy all night. Weather thick. Wind NE. Packed my cloths up. Took a packing coach &amp; went down to the office. Paid &pound;4.12. for 23 gallons of rum at 4/ per gallon. William paid it out of &pound;30 I gave him to place to my <span class=highlight_yellow>Chapmans account</span>. William &amp; I got on board the Pearl Gravesend boat. He accompanied me as far as Woolwich where he landed &amp; I proceeded to the ...</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":656,"lock":null}
