14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":700,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind about NNE. Got under way about 6 o'clock &amp; ran down to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Warp</span> where we brought up about &frac12; past 9 o'clock am.  Turned out an uncommonly fine day &amp; warm. About 12 o'clock the wind got to the NNW then NW &amp; after dinner to W by S &amp; WSW. When we got our anchor up, but being little wind, did not make much way. At about 8 o'clock being dark &amp; not able to see the buoy of the middle, we brought up for the night. Several ships in company.</p>\r\n<p>At 9 o'clock smoked a pipe, wet both eyes &amp; turned in. A good deal annoyed at not being able to proceed, there being a fine breeze.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":658,"lock":null}
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/21/701
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":701,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been blowing fresh all night &amp; still continues at SE with small rain. The ship remaining down river with a strong ebb tide at the rate of about 10 knots, having got underway at day light between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock. At 10 o'clock am abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Ald</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>b</span><span class=highlight_yellow>urgh</span>. Clearer weather. Top mast &amp; lower studding sails set. Passed through the <span class=highlight_yellow>Br</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oads</span> about 1 o'clock with a fine breeze. At about 8 o'clock pm abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>H</span><span class=highlight_yellow>appisburg</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span>. Took our pipe &amp; nip &amp; turned in at 9 o'clock. A beautiful star light night. Wind about W by S</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":659,"lock":null}
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/21/701
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":701,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been blowing fresh all night &amp; still continues at SE with small rain. The ship remaining down river with a strong ebb tide at the rate of about 10 knots, having got underway at day light between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock. At 10 o'clock am abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>Ald</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>b</span><span class=highlight_yellow>urgh</span>. Clearer weather. Top mast &amp; lower studding sails set. Passed through the <span class=highlight_yellow>Br</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oads</span> about 1 o'clock with a fine breeze. At about 8 o'clock pm abreast of <span class=highlight_yellow>H</span><span class=highlight_yellow>appisburg</span><span class=highlight_yellow>h</span>. Took our pipe &amp; nip &amp; turned in at 9 o'clock. A beautiful star light night. Wind about W by S</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":659,"lock":null}
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/22/702
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":702,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock ship abreast of Darlington, having had a fine run all night. Wind W by S &amp; W SW &amp; beautiful weather at noon got round Flamborough Head close in shore. A delightful sail. Passed Scarborough about 2 o'clock &amp; at 3 o'clock where off the south cheek of Robin Hoods Bay, had a small shower of rain, but soon cleared up &amp; we had fine weather again &amp; being close in shore enjoyed a most beautiful view of the coast &amp; country. Passed Huntcliff Foot before dusk with a continuance of the breeze at about W. At 11 o'clock brought up off Tynemouth Bar, being past high water, we could only attempt to go in.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":660,"lock":null}
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/22/702
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":702,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock ship abreast of Darlington, having had a fine run all night. Wind W by S &amp; W SW &amp; beautiful weather at noon got round Flamborough Head close in shore. A delightful sail. Passed Scarborough about 2 o'clock &amp; at 3 o'clock where off the south cheek of Robin Hoods Bay, had a small shower of rain, but soon cleared up &amp; we had fine weather again &amp; being close in shore enjoyed a most beautiful view of the coast &amp; country. Passed Huntcliff Foot before dusk with a continuance of the breeze at about W. At 11 o'clock brought up off Tynemouth Bar, being past high water, we could only attempt to go in.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":660,"lock":null}
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/23/703
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":703,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by N. At 7 o'clock a steam boat came alongside &amp; afterwards towed us into the harbour, where Mr White &amp; I landed &amp; went up to Dockwray Square to breakfast. Found Mrs Scott much better than I expected &amp; able to get into the drawing room. Took an early dinner with Mr Tinley. Sat with <span class=highlight_yellow>neuf</span> for some time in the evening &amp; took tea with Mr Tinley.</p>\r\n<p>Much mortified and unhappy at being informed by <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font><font color=#0070C0> </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>of her being with child to me. What the end of it be, I cannot divine, but it makes me miserable that I should have been such a fool &amp; madman to have committed such an act. Such a break of hospitality, such shaming &amp; disgraceful conduct. I am ashamed of myself.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":661,"lock":null}
14:36:38.790 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/23/703
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":703,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by N. At 7 o'clock a steam boat came alongside &amp; afterwards towed us into the harbour, where Mr White &amp; I landed &amp; went up to Dockwray Square to breakfast. Found Mrs Scott much better than I expected &amp; able to get into the drawing room. Took an early dinner with Mr Tinley. Sat with <span class=highlight_yellow>neuf</span> for some time in the evening &amp; took tea with Mr Tinley.</p>\r\n<p>Much mortified and unhappy at being informed by <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font><font color=#0070C0> </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>of her being with child to me. What the end of it be, I cannot divine, but it makes me miserable that I should have been such a fool &amp; madman to have committed such an act. Such a break of hospitality, such shaming &amp; disgraceful conduct. I am ashamed of myself.</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":661,"lock":null}
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/24/704
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":704,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind North. Engaged writing nearly all the morning. Mrs Dixon unexpectedly came down, dined &amp; left us in the evening. Much confusion in the house.</p>\r\n<p>Poor <font color=#0000FF>Ann </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being obliged to acknowledge herself in a family way. Consequently Mrs Scott discharged her &amp; she left the house. A strong suspicion I believe, but not known that I am the father. This day passed over without any further discovery &amp; I hope I shall be able to keep it a secret in all events from Mrs Scott. In a devil of a stew.</p>\r\n<p>Settled with Robert for payment of <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>ly</span></sup><span class=highlight_yellow> recovery</span>. Wrote to William at Windsor. <font color=#0000FE>Mr French died suddenly</font></p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":662,"lock":null}
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/24/704
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":704,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind North. Engaged writing nearly all the morning. Mrs Dixon unexpectedly came down, dined &amp; left us in the evening. Much confusion in the house.</p>\r\n<p>Poor <font color=#0000FF>Ann </font><font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being obliged to acknowledge herself in a family way. Consequently Mrs Scott discharged her &amp; she left the house. A strong suspicion I believe, but not known that I am the father. This day passed over without any further discovery &amp; I hope I shall be able to keep it a secret in all events from Mrs Scott. In a devil of a stew.</p>\r\n<p>Settled with Robert for payment of <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>ly</span></sup><span class=highlight_yellow> recovery</span>. Wrote to William at Windsor. <font color=#0000FE>Mr French died suddenly</font></p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":662,"lock":null}
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/25/705
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":705,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind ESE &amp; SE. Nothing further transpired respecting this unfortunate business with <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell</font>. Mrs Scott has not spoken to me about, though I believe &lsquo;tis her intention. I gave her every opportunity by dining at home &amp; sitting with her, for I'm anxious it was over, for this suspense is unpleasant.</p>\r\n<p>Saw <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>in the evening &amp; gave her a sovereign</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":663,"lock":null}
14:36:38.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/25/705
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":705,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind ESE &amp; SE. Nothing further transpired respecting this unfortunate business with <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell</font>. Mrs Scott has not spoken to me about, though I believe &lsquo;tis her intention. I gave her every opportunity by dining at home &amp; sitting with her, for I'm anxious it was over, for this suspense is unpleasant.</p>\r\n<p>Saw <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>in the evening &amp; gave her a sovereign</p>","pageId":776,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":663,"lock":null}
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/26/706
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":706,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Afterwards turned to rain. Wind SW &amp; WSW blowing strong. Engaged all the morning in the office making up the Hope's Petersburg voyage. Dined at home. Mrs S<font color=#BFBFBF>cott</font> put the question to me whether I was the cause of <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being with child, which on her (Mrs Scott's ) account being in so precarious a state of health, I denied.  Therefor if she hears of it through some kind officious friend &amp; anything happens, be the blame upon their shoulders. I shall not be the cause.</p>\r\n<p>With Ann Stokes this evening</p>\r\n<p>The Childers, Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Moriay</span> came into harbour</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":664,"lock":null}
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/26/706
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":706,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Afterwards turned to rain. Wind SW &amp; WSW blowing strong. Engaged all the morning in the office making up the Hope's Petersburg voyage. Dined at home. Mrs S<font color=#BFBFBF>cott</font> put the question to me whether I was the cause of <font color=#0000FF>Ann</font> <font color=#BFBFBF>Maxwell </font>being with child, which on her (Mrs Scott's ) account being in so precarious a state of health, I denied.  Therefor if she hears of it through some kind officious friend &amp; anything happens, be the blame upon their shoulders. I shall not be the cause.</p>\r\n<p>With Ann Stokes this evening</p>\r\n<p>The Childers, Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Moriay</span> came into harbour</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":664,"lock":null}
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/27/707
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":707,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW blowing fresh during the day. Sent a letter by Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>J </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Haker's</span>  ship, the Ajax, to Elsineus, directed to Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Brown, Copenhagen, that I forgot to deliver when there. Attended church in the morning. Walked with Mr Allen to Tynemouth in the afternoon &amp; afterward dined with him</p>","pageId":777,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":665,"lock":null}
14:36:38.792 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
