14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":686,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery. Wind SW. William &amp; Lea called at new Inn &amp; we went into the city together in a coach. Called at Chapmans but did not freight the Hope, thinking to send her to Shields. Walked down to the ship. William took J Galbraith to Nottingham Place with him. I &amp; J Hodgson ...</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":644,"lock":null}
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/8/687
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":687,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>.. got into a stage at 6 o'clock &amp; went down to Greenwich &amp; dined with G Watt, it being his wife's birthday. Returned to town in the evening.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":645,"lock":null}
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/8/687
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":687,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>.. got into a stage at 6 o'clock &amp; went down to Greenwich &amp; dined with G Watt, it being his wife's birthday. Returned to town in the evening.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":645,"lock":null}
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1829/9/9/688
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":688,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about SW. Nothing particular occurred today. Attended chambers. Sam Harry offered me 21/- <span class=highlight_yellow>pload</span> for Hull, having had a letter from Henry, that such freights could be obtained. Agreed to wait till tomorrow when Henry would be in town. Walked to the Blue Ports in Cork Square where we all met &amp; dined.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":646,"lock":null}
14:36:38.799 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
