14:36:38.810 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/28/835
14:36:38.810 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":835,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful winter's morning &amp; a sharp frost. Wind NW. On board the new ship &quot;William Green&quot; built by Mr Smith at St Peters of 600 tons as from a vessel as fine a vessel as was ever built, to sail this evening. Walked to Tynemouth. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott. Dined at home &amp; in the evening attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":791,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":787,"lock":null}
