14:36:38.811 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":835,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful winter's morning &amp; a sharp frost. Wind NW. On board the new ship &quot;William Green&quot; built by Mr Smith at St Peters of 600 tons as from a vessel as fine a vessel as was ever built, to sail this evening. Walked to Tynemouth. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott. Dined at home &amp; in the evening attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":791,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":787,"lock":null}
14:36:38.811 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/1/29/836
14:36:38.811 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":836,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning &amp; a very intense frost. Wind about west. Walked with H Nicholson to the Ridges at High Cherton. Had a little scaling, soon tired. Walked round by Tynemouth. Returned to dinner at 3 o'clock. In the evening walked again to Tynemouth &amp; took wine, played a rubber &amp; suppered with Mr Brown &amp; a party at the Star &amp; Garter. Not my favourite. Got home at 1 o'clock. Frost again &amp; a very wet night.</p>","pageId":791,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":788,"lock":null}
14:36:38.811 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
