14:36:38.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1140,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showering morning &amp; blowing hard from SE. Stephenson called, could not prevail on Mr Walker to send us coal down tomorrow to ensure us an earlier <span class=highlight_yellow>turey</span>. Dined at home. Got &pound;5 of chapman Took wine with I A Richardson at the Albion</p>","pageId":862,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1088,"lock":null}
14:36:38.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/11/27/1141
14:36:38.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1141,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Wintery weather and blowing strong from SE. On board the Hope people engaged with the wind <span class=highlight_yellow>lafe</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>preparing</span> for new barrel &amp; paul bits. On breaking the old barrel off, found the wind <span class=highlight_yellow>lefs</span> sprung &amp; rotten. Obliged to condemn it. Dined at home. In the billiard room afternoon &amp; at the whist club. In the evening  at the Duke.</p>","pageId":862,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1089,"lock":null}
14:36:38.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
