14:36:38.852 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1166,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, rather Cold. Wind W by N.  Sea fallen. Walked up to the Point to dine with Sadler. Spent a pleasant day</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1114,"lock":null}
14:36:38.852 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/22/1167
14:36:38.852 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1167,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine clear weather but blowing extremely hard at W by N &amp; has been since last evening. The account of the Hope having got to London, she ought to have been there, ship that sailed the day after her having got up. Dined with <span class=highlight_yellow>Warl</span> Wright on board the Merlin. Mrs Stephenson had a letter from her husband at Gravesend. The had very blowing weather. In the evening at the theatre &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1115,"lock":null}
