14:36:38.855 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1171,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frosty weather. A good deal of snow fallen in the night. Wind WNW. Did not go to church. Wrote to B B Galbraith. Received an account these H Harry, A Clark &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Berges</span> of the sale of 84 more than Hope coals at 35/-. Dined with J Tealey. The officers of HMS Samarang &amp; Childers there &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Goshing</span> RA</p>","pageId":870,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1119,"lock":null}
14:36:38.856 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/12/27/1172
14:36:38.856 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1172,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine winters morning. Frost still continues. Wind wavering variable between SSW &amp; SSE.  Received a letter from WBS. HMS Childers sailed out in beautiful style. Dined at home. At Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Received &pound;1.15. for WBS. Herald <span class=highlight_yellow>hewop</span> open</p>","pageId":871,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1120,"lock":null}
