14:36:38.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":853,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning &amp; quite mild wind about north. On board the Hope only got J Kuls down Today. Dined at home. Mrs Dixon down to See Mrs Scott. Drank tea at home &amp; in The evening at the George with H Harry &amp; Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":805,"lock":null}
14:36:38.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/16/854
14:36:38.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":854,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful morning &amp; frosty. Wind mild. On board the Hope When she finished her loading leffering in 16 Kule &amp; 5 Char. Attended the annual meeting of the eligible &amp; afterwards and dined with Placaad &amp; spend a pleasant day. In the evening with Bell Jervis</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":806,"lock":null}
14:36:38.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/16/854
14:36:38.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":854,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful morning &amp; frosty. Wind mild. On board the Hope When she finished her loading leffering in 16 Kule &amp; 5 Char. Attended the annual meeting of the eligible &amp; afterwards and dined with Placaad &amp; spend a pleasant day. In the evening with Bell Jervis</p>","pageId":798,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":806,"lock":null}
14:36:38.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/17/855
14:36:38.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":855,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Rather frosty wind fresh at NW. Got up at 7 o'clock and went on board the Hope. The pilot on board but decided to not venture to take her out, it being in bad tide &amp; threw feet sea upon the bar. Received a letter from WBS &amp; one from Tom Lee. Answered Tom Lees. Dined at home &amp; spent the afternoon at the billiard table. In the evening, heavy rain &amp; wind to NNE. At the Duke of York with H Harry &amp; Nicholson</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":807,"lock":null}
14:36:38.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
