14:36:38.868 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":857,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A course frost. Wind NNW &amp; blowing fresh &amp; although the sea was breaking upon the bar, several small ships ventured out &amp; some were literally smothered in the surf, but all got out safe. Dined with I Readhead on board the Nautalus At the billiard room in the afternoon. Drank tea at home &amp; in the evening With Bode Jerois &amp; afterwards at the Duke Of York</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":809,"lock":null}
14:36:38.868 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/2/840
14:36:38.868 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":840,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A countenance of winter weather, very cold. Been blowing a gale all night with snow showers A heavy sea upon the bar. Wind E.S.E Dined at home. At 3 o'clock at the billiard room in the afternoon. In the evening called and sat an hour or two with Mark, he having had a severe loin attack</p>","pageId":795,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":792,"lock":null}
