14:36:38.874 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":841,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still very cold and frosty and A good deal of snow on the ground Wind about East blowing fresh. Received from Robert and paid into Chapmans &pound;86 rents. Gave Mrs Scott a draft for her quarter annuity &pound;75. Mrs Dixon down I returned with her in the carriage to Barton. Dined &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":795,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":793,"lock":null}
