14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":846,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The thaw continues &amp; the  snow has disappeared. Blowing a gale of wind at WNW. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle Fixed the Hope for the Bursaton Walls to be loaded on Monday. Gave Stephenson orders to lay her the shore line. Dined at home at 3 then took wine with I Craig &amp; afterwards spent the evening At Tynemouth Castle with Captain French of The 80<sup>th</sup>. A large Hulk sailed today. Ann Maxwell delivered of a fine boy</p>","pageId":797,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":798,"lock":null}
14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/2/9/847
14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":847,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning and Mild weather.  Wind SW. A great deal Of ice in the river. Walked up to the Ship. &amp; dine at the annual dinner of the Great Premium Club. Reduced my insurance in at to &pound;500 &amp; paid &pound;500 into the eligibles. Mrs Scott very ill</p>","pageId":797,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":799,"lock":null}
14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
