14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":847,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning and Mild weather.  Wind SW. A great deal Of ice in the river. Walked up to the Ship. &amp; dine at the annual dinner of the Great Premium Club. Reduced my insurance in at to &pound;500 &amp; paid &pound;500 into the eligibles. Mrs Scott very ill</p>","pageId":797,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":799,"lock":null}
14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/1/867
14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":867,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning Wind SSW. Took physic &amp; stayed in the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon &amp; Tom Smith down to see Mrs Scott On board the Brodnick with R Peach &amp; in the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":819,"lock":null}
14:36:38.877 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.878 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/1/867
14:36:38.878 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":867,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull thick morning Wind SSW. Took physic &amp; stayed in the house all the morning. Mrs Dixon &amp; Tom Smith down to see Mrs Scott On board the Brodnick with R Peach &amp; in the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":819,"lock":null}
14:36:38.878 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/10/876
14:36:38.878 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":876,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dull &amp; thick weather &amp; rather cold. Blowing fresh at NSW. Mr &amp; Mrs Dixon &amp; I Smith came down today for the purpose of having Mrs Scott's will read &amp; which not a little surprised all of us, a more extraordinary one perhaps never was: By it I am left the very handsome legacy of &pound;10 !!! the same to my brother, plainly proving &amp; confirming what her feelings towards us throughout life must have been, inveterately bad, &amp; carried to the grave with her. Peace go with her. I forgive her For all the mischief &amp; misery she Has caused in our family. The party left us in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":828,"lock":null}
14:36:38.878 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/10/876
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":876,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dull &amp; thick weather &amp; rather cold. Blowing fresh at NSW. Mr &amp; Mrs Dixon &amp; I Smith came down today for the purpose of having Mrs Scott's will read &amp; which not a little surprised all of us, a more extraordinary one perhaps never was: By it I am left the very handsome legacy of &pound;10 !!! the same to my brother, plainly proving &amp; confirming what her feelings towards us throughout life must have been, inveterately bad, &amp; carried to the grave with her. Peace go with her. I forgive her For all the mischief &amp; misery she Has caused in our family. The party left us in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":828,"lock":null}
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/11/877
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":877,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but blowing hard from about west. Received at the bank for Salmon's debt &pound;88.9.3 for WBS &amp; deducted from it 20/- for my trouble &amp; &pound;11.6 money lent to Bob Marsh &amp; sec by WBS in London. Dined with I Finley, being less Of the confinement to the house. Received a letter from WBS </p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":829,"lock":null}
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/11/877
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":877,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but blowing hard from about west. Received at the bank for Salmon's debt &pound;88.9.3 for WBS &amp; deducted from it 20/- for my trouble &amp; &pound;11.6 money lent to Bob Marsh &amp; sec by WBS in London. Dined with I Finley, being less Of the confinement to the house. Received a letter from WBS </p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":829,"lock":null}
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/12/878
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":878,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather, but very windy at West. Received a letter from ABS in reply to their informing him of Mrs Scott's death, saying he cannot leave London before tonight or tomorrow morning Dined at home. Wes &amp; Fanny Smith excessively angry that we should claim the amount of taxes upon the house paid by us in error &amp; which ought to have been paid by Mrs Scott. Fanny inclined to be very violent, her conduct disgusting &amp; very insulting; displaying more regard for the money than for the aunt. Blew a perfect hurricane with heavy rain the afternoon</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":830,"lock":null}
14:36:38.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/12/878
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":878,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather, but very windy at West. Received a letter from ABS in reply to their informing him of Mrs Scott's death, saying he cannot leave London before tonight or tomorrow morning Dined at home. Wes &amp; Fanny Smith excessively angry that we should claim the amount of taxes upon the house paid by us in error &amp; which ought to have been paid by Mrs Scott. Fanny inclined to be very violent, her conduct disgusting &amp; very insulting; displaying more regard for the money than for the aunt. Blew a perfect hurricane with heavy rain the afternoon</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":830,"lock":null}
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/13/879
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":879,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but still Blowing very hard at NW. In the house All day</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":831,"lock":null}
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/13/879
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":879,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but still Blowing very hard at NW. In the house All day</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":831,"lock":null}
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/14/880
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":880,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cool morning &amp; blown very hard all day at west. Of course in the house. Fanny Smith again exceedingly violent today. More so than before &amp; insulting. Than I was obliged to speak to her in a way that had the effect of making her silent. Wonder ? Be at opposite William BS did not arrive until after 11 o'clock having called &amp; stopped a short time in Westgate Street. Went to bed from after his arrival.</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":832,"lock":null}
14:36:38.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
