14:36:38.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":871,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning, rather Frosty. Wind SW. Sent an answer to Mr Anderson's letter. Hope Club stating the Hope being laid up between 20 Dec &amp; 20 Feb Went with H Harry &amp; the H Pemberton of Quebec to Sunderland. Called upon Capt Bunbury of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment &amp; returned to dine with H Harry at 5 o'clock A small party to <span class=highlight_yellow>mubt</span> Mrs Pemberton. attended Mrs Heddill's evening party. Received a letter from WBS confirming the of the sale of the Hope's cargo at 29/6 A miserable price, about 6/6 <span class=highlight_yellow>pecght</span> Shall lose I dare say between &pound;30 &amp; &pound;40</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":823,"lock":null}
14:36:38.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/6/872
14:36:38.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":872,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A duller foggy morning. Wind SW.  <del>Afterwards got to the L&amp;E</del> <del>Cold accompanied</del> Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Dined with Nicholson a party spent a very Pleasant day &amp; in the evening Attended the Whist Club at I Dales</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":824,"lock":null}
14:36:38.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
