14:36:38.893 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":873,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy morning. Wind NE. Afterwards changed to SE &amp; fine clear weather. Went to Church in the morning. Mr Pemberton accompanied me. I was engaged to dine with I Tealey today but on my return from Church. I found that Mrs Scott was so much poorer &amp; her death expected every moment. I sent an apology. She expired precisely at 9 o'clock without a struggle</p>","pageId":802,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":825,"lock":null}
14:36:38.893 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/3/8/874
14:36:38.893 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":874,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather Frosty. Wind  SSW. Emma G came From school. Mrs Dixon down &amp; Took Emma to N Coatts with her. Wrote to WBS: BBG: &amp; A <span class=highlight_yellow>Deighera</span> of Mrs Scotts death. Kept the house all day.</p>","pageId":803,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":826,"lock":null}
