14:36:38.903 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":923,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another dull morning with rain. Wind SE. Walked with Captain Webb to Tynmouth &amp; called upon Mr &amp; Mrs Ilderton at the Star &amp; Garter. Dined at house &amp; attended the whist club in the evening at the A Fenwicks. Rained very heavy  all the afternoon with the wind changed to N by W</p>","pageId":814,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":875,"lock":null}
14:36:38.903 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/25/924
14:36:38.903 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":924,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather again &amp; glafs risen considerably since yesterday evening about 1 &frac12;  inch &amp; up to fair. Wind NNW. Attended morning wives. Dined with I Tealeg, Mrs Cumliff &amp; keifs of the These. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon; At the S <span class=highlight_yellow>Cellegator</span> off several ships went to sea, bound foreign, the Broderweck, 3 Brothers, Dalsymple, Hannah, Equity les. Spent the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Tealegs</span> A heavy rain at night.</p>","pageId":814,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":876,"lock":null}
