14:36:38.906 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":929,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Wind ESE. Went by Steamer to Newcastle could get nothing for the Hope. Dined with D Dixon, a party Tom Smith, Mr Busqter; they all went to the theater to see Liston, I looked in but did not remain long, the house very full for his benefit. Got into a gig &amp; returned to Shields</p>","pageId":815,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":881,"lock":null}
14:36:38.906 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/4/4/902
14:36:38.906 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":902,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning wind NW. Emma Mary Carfs &amp; went to church. Heard a funeral sermon from Mr Mark who held the service. The Vicars father being dead &amp; also young Mrs Read he died in London of the gout in the head &amp; after two days illness. Dined at home &amp; afternoon walked with H Henry to Tynemouth. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ews</span><span class=highlight_yellow> r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>oo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>m</span> &amp; H Harry's</p>","pageId":809,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":854,"lock":null}
