14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":939,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>at &frac12; past 8 o'clock. Got the Alnwick coach at Newcastle at 10 o'clock and reached Alnwick at 3. Mr &amp; Mrs Ilderstow there in the carriage &amp; took me out to Leamington to dinner</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":891,"lock":null}
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/11/940
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":940,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still blowing fresh from the NE &amp; cold. Robert &amp; Tom I Ldestow &amp; I started after breakfast to fish in the Alm, but had bad sport &amp; river busy sheet &amp; cold weather</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":892,"lock":null}
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/11/940
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":940,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still blowing fresh from the NE &amp; cold. Robert &amp; Tom I Ldestow &amp; I started after breakfast to fish in the Alm, but had bad sport &amp; river busy sheet &amp; cold weather</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":892,"lock":null}
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/12/941
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":941,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fairer and warmer weather. Robert Ilderstow &amp; I had an early breakfast &amp; rode over the river till below Hedghey, where we fished until it began to rain when we took shelter at a mill &amp; then walked up to Rosea an estate of the Ildestonn's.  Had tea &amp; eggs &amp; rode home in the evening, when we found Mrs Crosby &amp; Mrs Strothard had arrived from Newcastle on a visit. Had better sport today, brought home a few good trout</p>","pageId":818,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":893,"lock":null}
14:36:38.911 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
