14:36:38.920 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":958,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but still rather cool &amp; wind about SE. Left Lemmington after having spent a very pleasant time. Rode Bob Ildercoade home onto Alnwick &amp; got them onto place, left at 1/s past 10 o'clock. The day got cloudy &amp; cold &amp; before we left Morpeth it began to rain. ...</p>","pageId":821,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":910,"lock":null}
14:36:38.920 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/29/959
14:36:38.920 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":959,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... &amp; continued showering all day. Got upon Dunns coach at 4 o'clock &amp; arrived at home a little after 5 o'clock to dinner. Received a letter from <span class=highlight_yellow>l</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ss</span>. That my friend A Harry &amp; A Nicholson the latter the first time since his parried <span class=highlight_yellow>extect</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>es</span> captain his ship the Tenacity having foundered in the North Sea &amp; he &amp; the crew taken aboard on <span class=highlight_yellow>gallcot</span> that <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuekerly</span> hove in sights before dark. Spent the evening together with Mr Com <span class=highlight_yellow>Hewesion</span> at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":822,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":911,"lock":null}
