14:36:38.921 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":932,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind about West. By Steam to Newcastle but did not find the Hope to load coal for Dublin as intended as they could not load her before they did of much works. Returned to Dinner on board the Choice in the afternoon. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":884,"lock":null}
14:36:38.921 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/5/30/960
14:36:38.921 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":960,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about West. Icy cold having flown to the locns suffering some pain. Got Robert to sub the park with <span class=highlight_yellow>opadildoc</span>, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>scidlily</span> &amp; did not go to church. Wrote a long letter to ABP Emma G: came over to see us. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon A Harry &amp; I walked up to North Sheilds to take wine</p>","pageId":822,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":912,"lock":null}
