14:36:38.933 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":987,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; like more rain again blowing fresh at WNW. Received a letter from B B Gallbraith &amp; answered it. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":938,"lock":null}
14:36:38.933 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/3/965
14:36:38.933 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":965,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with rain. Wind SSE About 11o'clock the weather cleared up, Harry, Nicholson &amp; I walked with I Richardson in his cable up to Mr Sadlers at the Point &amp; then to Jarrow Slake where we had two hours fishing, but very poor sport, we afterwards landed &amp; dined with Sadler &amp; spent a very pleasant day. It turned out a rainy evening &amp; we had a wet &amp; unpleasant walk home</p>","pageId":824,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":917,"lock":null}
14:36:38.933 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/3/965
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":965,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with rain. Wind SSE About 11o'clock the weather cleared up, Harry, Nicholson &amp; I walked with I Richardson in his cable up to Mr Sadlers at the Point &amp; then to Jarrow Slake where we had two hours fishing, but very poor sport, we afterwards landed &amp; dined with Sadler &amp; spent a very pleasant day. It turned out a rainy evening &amp; we had a wet &amp; unpleasant walk home</p>","pageId":824,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":917,"lock":null}
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/30/988
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":988,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning something like summer weather at last. Wind WNW afterwards the heat brought is round to SE. Walked out to Whitley Park &amp; called upon I Wright &amp; returned by  Cullercoats to dinner.Webb came in &amp; took part of a bottle of port with me. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. King William the 4th proclaimed at Newcastle today &amp; the guns fired at Tynemouth castle</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":939,"lock":null}
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/30/988
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":988,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning something like summer weather at last. Wind WNW afterwards the heat brought is round to SE. Walked out to Whitley Park &amp; called upon I Wright &amp; returned by  Cullercoats to dinner.Webb came in &amp; took part of a bottle of port with me. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. King William the 4th proclaimed at Newcastle today &amp; the guns fired at Tynemouth castle</p>","pageId":829,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":939,"lock":null}
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/6/4/966
14:36:38.934 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":966,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning. Wind N by W. Accepted Baleracus bill at 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>mos</span> for the archangel <span class=highlight_yellow>prrorraccon</span> for &pound;12.13.8 down 22<sup>nd</sup> but from the great fall of rain last night a heavy fresh in the season, take <span class=highlight_yellow>ch</span> with the wind drove two sloops upon the headland &amp; a brig over the points of the sand where the rode very heavy for 2 or 3 hours, but the life boat pulling some hands on board the got a offering upon his cable &amp; thus succeeded in taking her to sea. Turned out a fine afternoon. Walked in the evening to Tynemouth to near the band of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment</p>","pageId":824,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":918,"lock":null}
