14:36:38.940 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1002,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning blowing fresh at SW. Walked up to Tynemouth, met Harry Nicholson &amp; Richardson who had been over the bar with the Harvey bound to <span class=highlight_yellow>Ascksaget</span>. Dined at home. Took wine with Richardson &amp; spent a very pleasant afternoon &amp; in the evening again walked to Tynemouth</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":953,"lock":null}
14:36:38.940 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/7/16/1003
14:36:38.940 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1003,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning But again blowing hard at WSW It large concussion of people with A professional gentleman with <span class=highlight_yellow>Baudr</span>, flags to went to Chester Whence they met the Bale &amp; brought him through the upper part of town to the George Tavern after which low sat down to an excellent &amp; well arranged discussion nearly 200 freehold all went off well. The latter part of the evening a glorious scene of drunk cuffs and confusion amongst the lower set of freeholders.</p>","pageId":834,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":954,"lock":null}
