14:36:38.948 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1017,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful morning. Wind SE. bathed again. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. In the afternoon went to sea in the coble &amp; got home at &frac12; past 9 o'clock. Caught only one mackerel.</p>","pageId":837,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":968,"lock":null}
14:36:38.948 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/7/3/991
14:36:38.948 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":991,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. Walked to Tynemouth. Much to my surprise met with Mrs Lumley and Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Bcagdon</span> who had arrived by sea. The long <span class=highlight_yellow>gifore</span>. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon Webb Hopkins the boy &amp; I went in a boat to fish but had no sport, weather unpleasant &amp; thick.</p>","pageId":830,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":942,"lock":null}
