14:36:38.960 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1043,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"images/img2398-image-archangel-map.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n  <figcaption>Archangel</figcaption>\r\n</figure>","pageId":null,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":null,"lock":null}
14:36:38.960 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/22/1044
14:36:38.960 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1044,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind NE. Went to church in the morning. Mr Mark preached. Received a letter from Stephenson dated Archangel the 15<sup>th</sup> July of his boxing load &amp; that he had brought 57 barrels of tar on ship account, <font color=#BFBFBF>but </font>the merchant refusing to give him deck freight. The amount of the bill drawn &pound;120.1.1. Wrote to J Chapman to sell the tar.</p>\r\n<p>Walked to Tynemouth. A great many people there. Dined with J Huntly at 5 o'clock &amp; walked again to Tynemouth in the evening when it unfortunately began to rain &amp; dispersed the people.</p>","pageId":843,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":992,"lock":null}
