14:36:38.964 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1053,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. William &amp; I took our guns &amp; walked with Mrs Tealey &amp; his wife.  Robersons to Marsden where the committee for the preservation for ship wrecks met &amp; tried several experiments. We afterwards returned by steam to Shields. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum at night</p>","pageId":845,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1001,"lock":null}
14:36:38.964 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/4/1023
14:36:38.964 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1023,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind variable during the day W &amp; SSE with rain in the afternoon. After hard fighting between the Parisians &amp; the military where about 8 or 10000 were killed, the former drove the military out of the city &amp; established pro: term: a provisional government &amp; appointing the Duke of Orleans retired general of the kingdom which he accepted. Charles the X &amp; his minions flown. The Lord Khoas where the French with much credit to themselves have effected the revolution without those outrages which characterized the former. Dined with Doctor Drourg. He &amp; Richardson afterwards came &amp; took wine with me.</p>","pageId":839,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":974,"lock":null}
14:36:38.964 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/4/1023
14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1023,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind variable during the day W &amp; SSE with rain in the afternoon. After hard fighting between the Parisians &amp; the military where about 8 or 10000 were killed, the former drove the military out of the city &amp; established pro: term: a provisional government &amp; appointing the Duke of Orleans retired general of the kingdom which he accepted. Charles the X &amp; his minions flown. The Lord Khoas where the French with much credit to themselves have effected the revolution without those outrages which characterized the former. Dined with Doctor Drourg. He &amp; Richardson afterwards came &amp; took wine with me.</p>","pageId":839,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":974,"lock":null}
14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/5/1024
14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1024,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning wind NW. Walked to Tynemouth with Allen &amp; balled wine at houses. Remained in the town all the afternoon expecting Williams's arrival in the steam boat from London. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. The boat arrived off the bar at &frac12; past 9 o'clock but being thick could not see her. The Shields Pafseeyer landed in the Haven &amp; WBS got home about 11 o'clock. Received the rents &amp; paid &pound;70 cats chapmans on account of the Exors</p>","pageId":839,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":975,"lock":null}
14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
