14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1024,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning wind NW. Walked to Tynemouth with Allen &amp; balled wine at houses. Remained in the town all the afternoon expecting Williams's arrival in the steam boat from London. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. The boat arrived off the bar at &frac12; past 9 o'clock but being thick could not see her. The Shields Pafseeyer landed in the Haven &amp; WBS got home about 11 o'clock. Received the rents &amp; paid &pound;70 cats chapmans on account of the Exors</p>","pageId":839,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":975,"lock":null}
14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1830/8/6/1025
14:36:38.965 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1025,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been rain during the night. Wind N by E &amp; the sea having risen put a stop to our fishery excursion. Dined at home. Hewes &amp; Robert Harry came in &amp; took wine with us. In the evening walked to Tynemouth. Suppered with H Harry</p>","pageId":840,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":976,"lock":null}
