14:36:38.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1188,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning, blowing fresh from NNE. Went by steam to Newcastle. Fixed the Hope to load <span class=highlight_yellow>ords</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Redheught</span> to be upheld 11/- freight go to WBS as factor, &amp; all profit above 11/- to be divided. Returned by coach. Attended the annual meeting of the Eligible and United clubs to alter &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>receive</span> the rules etc. Sat down a large party to dinner afterwards. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":876,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1134,"lock":null}
14:36:38.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/11/1189
14:36:38.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1189,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another damp morning but likely to be finer weather. Wind NW. At the George tavern a great part of the morning. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ilderton</span> there, with whom &amp; a small party, I afterwards dined. Bob <span class=highlight_yellow>Ilderton</span> &amp; I called at the Mulstrum.</p>\r\n<p>Hope got 3 keels down.</p>","pageId":876,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1135,"lock":null}
