14:36:38.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1189,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another damp morning but likely to be finer weather. Wind NW. At the George tavern a great part of the morning. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ilderton</span> there, with whom &amp; a small party, I afterwards dined. Bob <span class=highlight_yellow>Ilderton</span> &amp; I called at the Mulstrum.</p>\r\n<p>Hope got 3 keels down.</p>","pageId":876,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1135,"lock":null}
14:36:38.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/12/1190
14:36:38.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1190,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant foggy damp morning. A little wind <span class=highlight_yellow>lope at</span> appears to be W.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to WBS giving him a copy of Chapmans <span class=highlight_yellow>book on</span>. In the afternoon at the billiard room. Wrote to Tom Smith &amp; sent him some <span class=highlight_yellow>tripe</span>. Harry, Nicholas, Drury &amp; Cunningham came home with me in the evening &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":876,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1136,"lock":null}
