14:36:38.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1190,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant foggy damp morning. A little wind <span class=highlight_yellow>lope at</span> appears to be W.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to WBS giving him a copy of Chapmans <span class=highlight_yellow>book on</span>. In the afternoon at the billiard room. Wrote to Tom Smith &amp; sent him some <span class=highlight_yellow>tripe</span>. Harry, Nicholas, Drury &amp; Cunningham came home with me in the evening &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":876,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1136,"lock":null}
14:36:38.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/13/1191
14:36:38.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1191,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An unpleasant foggy morning. Wind NW. Shanks called &amp; I gave him a draft on Chapmans for &pound;18.18 his bill for new windless repairs to the Hope. Gave Stephenson a draft on Chapmans for &pound;30. Dined at home. Attended the whist club in the evening. 5 keels came down. None yesterday.</p>","pageId":876,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1137,"lock":null}
14:36:38.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
