14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1196,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very damp foggy morning. Wind fresh at SE &amp; a good deal of sea. Dined at 5 o'clock with the Gastling RA Tynemouth Place. A very pleasant party. Got home before1 o'clock in the morning. Gave notes to the Premium &amp; Hope clubs of the Hope being loaded. Leadbetter went to Newcastle</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1142,"lock":null}
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/19/1197
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/19/1197
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/2/1179
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1179,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and unpleasant damp morning.  Wind SW.  Walked down to Shields.  Dined with H Harry in the evening. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1126,"lock":null}
14:36:38.987 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/2/1179
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1179,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and unpleasant damp morning.  Wind SW.  Walked down to Shields.  Dined with H Harry in the evening. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1126,"lock":null}
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/20/1198
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/20/1198
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/21/1199
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
14:36:38.988 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.989 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/21/1199
14:36:38.989 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
14:36:38.989 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/22/1200
14:36:38.989 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1200,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain this morning. Wind about East with a heavy sea. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle. Dined &amp; stayed all night at D Dixons. Mentioned to him my having applied to the Duke for a commission in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> militia of which he approved</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1146,"lock":null}
14:36:38.989 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/22/1200
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1200,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain this morning. Wind about East with a heavy sea. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle. Dined &amp; stayed all night at D Dixons. Mentioned to him my having applied to the Duke for a commission in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> militia of which he approved</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1146,"lock":null}
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/23/1201
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1201,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. For the first time for many days we have seen the sun. Wind ENE &amp; cold with showers. Left Dixon's after breakfast took the steam boat &amp; returned to Shields to dinner. Emma Galbraith looking much better. No letter from WBS, disappointed. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1147,"lock":null}
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/23/1201
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1201,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. For the first time for many days we have seen the sun. Wind ENE &amp; cold with showers. Left Dixon's after breakfast took the steam boat &amp; returned to Shields to dinner. Emma Galbraith looking much better. No letter from WBS, disappointed. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1147,"lock":null}
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/24/1202
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1202,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been a slight frost with a little snow during the night. Wind NW. Sea much fallen, so that I think many ships will get to sea.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with copies of letters written to the Duke &amp; Lord Beverley applying for a commission for me in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> Militia. Answered his letter.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Bevor's</span> brother to come down to Shields to make some arrangements with regard to the <span class=highlight_yellow>fasern</span> after seeing J Tinley upon the subject.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with H Harry.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1148,"lock":null}
14:36:38.990 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/24/1202
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1202,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been a slight frost with a little snow during the night. Wind NW. Sea much fallen, so that I think many ships will get to sea.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with copies of letters written to the Duke &amp; Lord Beverley applying for a commission for me in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> Militia. Answered his letter.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Bevor's</span> brother to come down to Shields to make some arrangements with regard to the <span class=highlight_yellow>fasern</span> after seeing J Tinley upon the subject.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with H Harry.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1148,"lock":null}
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/25/1203
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1203,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine wintery morning having been a very heavy fall of snow during the night. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from B B Galbraith. A bill for &pound;6.0.10 drawn by <span class=highlight_yellow>Stodter</span> of the Eligible club presented for payment, but I did not take it up having no notice. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Dale &amp; in the evening attended the ball at the George which was the best we have had for a long time. Got home at &frac14; past 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1149,"lock":null}
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/25/1203
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1203,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine wintery morning having been a very heavy fall of snow during the night. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from B B Galbraith. A bill for &pound;6.0.10 drawn by <span class=highlight_yellow>Stodter</span> of the Eligible club presented for payment, but I did not take it up having no notice. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Dale &amp; in the evening attended the ball at the George which was the best we have had for a long time. Got home at &frac14; past 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1149,"lock":null}
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/26/1204
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1204,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of sharp frost. Wind NNW. Very little additional snow fallen in the night. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle, there being a meeting of the <span class=highlight_yellow>leiabenantcy</span> &amp; saw Dixon who promised to speak to Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlson</span> respecting a commission for me in the military. <span class=highlight_yellow>Had</span> some dinner with Emma Galbraith &amp; returned by Duna in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>Eat a couple of mutton chops at 6 o'clock &amp; finished in the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1150,"lock":null}
14:36:38.991 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/26/1204
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1204,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of sharp frost. Wind NNW. Very little additional snow fallen in the night. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle, there being a meeting of the <span class=highlight_yellow>leiabenantcy</span> &amp; saw Dixon who promised to speak to Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlson</span> respecting a commission for me in the military. <span class=highlight_yellow>Had</span> some dinner with Emma Galbraith &amp; returned by Duna in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>Eat a couple of mutton chops at 6 o'clock &amp; finished in the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1150,"lock":null}
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/27/1205
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1205,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; every appearance of snow or sleet &amp; looking as if it would thaw. Wind about west. The ship preparing for sea. Received a note from D Dixon stating he had seen Colonel Coulson &amp; that there are several commissions vacant &amp; I must apply through Colonel Coulson.</p>\r\n<p>Accepted a bill for &pound;8.17 the <span class=highlight_yellow>prccuccia</span> for the present voyage: due 27<sup>th</sup> April dated 18 Jan at 9 months.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Mr Brown of the George Tavern a <span class=highlight_yellow>signature</span> written notice to quit on the 1<sup>st</sup> Aug next.</p>\r\n<p>On board the Hope. Got a steam boat which towed her to sea with fine NW wind.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club I the evening. The wind got round &amp; blew hard from the NE &amp; brought on a heavy sea &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>remained</span> thaw during the whole of the day.</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1151,"lock":null}
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/27/1205
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1205,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; every appearance of snow or sleet &amp; looking as if it would thaw. Wind about west. The ship preparing for sea. Received a note from D Dixon stating he had seen Colonel Coulson &amp; that there are several commissions vacant &amp; I must apply through Colonel Coulson.</p>\r\n<p>Accepted a bill for &pound;8.17 the <span class=highlight_yellow>prccuccia</span> for the present voyage: due 27<sup>th</sup> April dated 18 Jan at 9 months.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Mr Brown of the George Tavern a <span class=highlight_yellow>signature</span> written notice to quit on the 1<sup>st</sup> Aug next.</p>\r\n<p>On board the Hope. Got a steam boat which towed her to sea with fine NW wind.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club I the evening. The wind got round &amp; blew hard from the NE &amp; brought on a heavy sea &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>remained</span> thaw during the whole of the day.</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1151,"lock":null}
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/28/1206
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1206,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Wrote to Colonel Coalson applying for a commission. Took a walk round by Tynemouth. Dined at home. At billiard room latter in the afternoon &amp; abbey in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1152,"lock":null}
14:36:38.992 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/28/1206
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1206,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Wrote to Colonel Coalson applying for a commission. Took a walk round by Tynemouth. Dined at home. At billiard room latter in the afternoon &amp; abbey in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1152,"lock":null}
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/29/1207
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1207,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine winter's morning. Slight frost &amp; been a great deal of snow during the night &amp; appearance of more. Wind NW.</p> <p></p> <p>Went by Durrer's coach to Newcastle &amp; took Robert with me. Tom, Ann &amp; Bell Smith at D Dixons. Tom Dixon &amp; I called at Leadbetters The attorneys &amp; I settled with them as Mrs Scott's executor giving them a draft on Chapmans on WBS &amp; JRS executors account for &pound;108.19.5 which with other payments we have made, leaves only &pound;702 due from us, of the &pound;1000 left under Mrs Scott's will. Robert &amp; Leadbetters received their legacies. Called twice on Colonel Coulson, not at home. Met him afterwards in the street &amp; had some conversation with him as to my application for a commission.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined with Mrs Dixon. The whole party excepting myself went to a concert. I called &amp; saw Mr Weatherly &amp; by his advice afterwards called upon Mr Turnbull, deputy clerk of the Peace, but he was not at home.</p> <p></p> <p>Suppered at Dixons &amp; slept at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Jessop</span> Hotel</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1153,"lock":null}
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/29/1207
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1207,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine winter's morning. Slight frost &amp; been a great deal of snow during the night &amp; appearance of more. Wind NW.</p> <p></p> <p>Went by Durrer's coach to Newcastle &amp; took Robert with me. Tom, Ann &amp; Bell Smith at D Dixons. Tom Dixon &amp; I called at Leadbetters The attorneys &amp; I settled with them as Mrs Scott's executor giving them a draft on Chapmans on WBS &amp; JRS executors account for &pound;108.19.5 which with other payments we have made, leaves only &pound;702 due from us, of the &pound;1000 left under Mrs Scott's will. Robert &amp; Leadbetters received their legacies. Called twice on Colonel Coulson, not at home. Met him afterwards in the street &amp; had some conversation with him as to my application for a commission.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined with Mrs Dixon. The whole party excepting myself went to a concert. I called &amp; saw Mr Weatherly &amp; by his advice afterwards called upon Mr Turnbull, deputy clerk of the Peace, but he was not at home.</p> <p></p> <p>Suppered at Dixons &amp; slept at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Jessop</span> Hotel</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1153,"lock":null}
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/3/1180
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1180,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most unpleasant weather, damp &amp; uncomfortable. Wind SW. Received a letter yesterday from Stephenson of the ship being out on Thursday delivering 282 char &amp; expecting to get his ballast on Saturday. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>afsales</span> with a balance note for &pound;93.7. which I paid into Chapmans &amp; drew for &pound;50 with which I paid the bells for the Archangel voyage viz: swan &pound;___ sharp &pound;___ &amp; spares &pound;___. At the theatre in the evening, Michaels benefit. A good house.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1127,"lock":null}
14:36:38.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/3/1180
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1180,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most unpleasant weather, damp &amp; uncomfortable. Wind SW. Received a letter yesterday from Stephenson of the ship being out on Thursday delivering 282 char &amp; expecting to get his ballast on Saturday. Received the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>afsales</span> with a balance note for &pound;93.7. which I paid into Chapmans &amp; drew for &pound;50 with which I paid the bells for the Archangel voyage viz: swan &pound;___ sharp &pound;___ &amp; spares &pound;___. At the theatre in the evening, Michaels benefit. A good house.</p>","pageId":873,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1127,"lock":null}
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/30/1208
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1208,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Breakfasted at Dixons.</p> <p></p> <p>Afterwards called &amp; saw Mr Turnball who wrote out my declaration of qualifications which I signed &amp; which he will deliver to Mr Thorp the clerk of the Peace tomorrow.</p> <p></p> <p>Called upon &amp; saw Colonel Coulson who was with Captain Bigg &amp; told him what I had done &amp; had some conversation with them. He of course will immediately apply for a captain's course for me which will most likely come down in the course of the work, as the military is to go into training immediately.</p> <p></p> <p>Returned to Shields by steam &amp; dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; Nicholson took wine with me in the afternoon &amp; in the evening I walked to the Mulstrum. Received a letter from WBS</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1154,"lock":null}
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/30/1208
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1208,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Breakfasted at Dixons.</p> <p></p> <p>Afterwards called &amp; saw Mr Turnball who wrote out my declaration of qualifications which I signed &amp; which he will deliver to Mr Thorp the clerk of the Peace tomorrow.</p> <p></p> <p>Called upon &amp; saw Colonel Coulson who was with Captain Bigg &amp; told him what I had done &amp; had some conversation with them. He of course will immediately apply for a captain's course for me which will most likely come down in the course of the work, as the military is to go into training immediately.</p> <p></p> <p>Returned to Shields by steam &amp; dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; Nicholson took wine with me in the afternoon &amp; in the evening I walked to the Mulstrum. Received a letter from WBS</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1154,"lock":null}
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/31/1209
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1209,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A frosty morning. Rather <span class=highlight_yellow>damp</span> with a fall of snow. Wind NW. Dined at home. Received a letter from B B Galbraith &amp; answered it &amp; also WBS's. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; Albion in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>During the afternoon the wind got round to SW, S by W. At night blew fresh at S by E &amp; still frosty.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1155,"lock":null}
14:36:38.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:38.995 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/31/1209
14:36:38.995 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1209,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A frosty morning. Rather <span class=highlight_yellow>damp</span> with a fall of snow. Wind NW. Dined at home. Received a letter from B B Galbraith &amp; answered it &amp; also WBS's. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; Albion in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>During the afternoon the wind got round to SW, S by W. At night blew fresh at S by E &amp; still frosty.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1155,"lock":null}
14:36:38.995 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/1/4/1181
14:36:38.995 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1181,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp day. Wind ___. Dined at home. The Saturday night whist club with me in the evening. Kept it up till &frac12; past 2 o'clock in the morning</p>","pageId":874,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1128,"lock":null}
