14:36:39.000 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1481,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind W by S. Dined with H Nicholson on board the Crisis. J Wight, J Redhead &amp; Lockwood there. With Bess at night</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1427,"lock":null}
14:36:39.000 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/12/1482
14:36:39.000 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1482,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind WSW. Went up in a gig to Newcastle. Called &amp; saw Emma Galbraith who was looking well. Payed Mrs Noakes for Emma G's board and education up to June &pound;39.10/-. Afterwards walked out to Benton where I dined &amp; stayed all night. Dixon Clark there, he slept in Newcastle to take the coach in the morning for Oxford. Tom Smith left them in the morning for Togston</p>","pageId":953,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1428,"lock":null}
14:36:39.000 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
