14:36:39.010 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.010 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/29/1499
14:36:39.010 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1499,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind SW. Took a long walk with Mark to Tynemouth, Cullercoat Sands &amp; dined with Joblings at the George at 4 o'clock</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1445,"lock":null}
14:36:39.010 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/3/1473
14:36:39.010 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1473,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned the hands up about 5 o'clock being low water &amp; the wind at SSW I got up before 6 o'clock. The people busy getting the anchor &amp; setting sails. Had a fine run during the day down <span class=highlight_yellow>swin</span>, studding sails set but not much wind which varied between <span class=highlight_yellow>SE</span> &amp; S by W. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock at night off Aldeburgh &amp; beautiful clear weather but a strong flood tide against us. Turned in about 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1419,"lock":null}
14:36:39.010 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
