14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/30/1500
14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1500,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast took a walk to Tynemouth &amp; went to church in the afternoon, again walked to Tynemouth. Jobling dined with me at 5 o'clock. Reconciled with <font color=#BFBFBF>Bess</font></p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1446,"lock":null}
14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/30/1500
14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1500,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of mild weather. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast took a walk to Tynemouth &amp; went to church in the afternoon, again walked to Tynemouth. Jobling dined with me at 5 o'clock. Reconciled with <font color=#BFBFBF>Bess</font></p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1446,"lock":null}
14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/31/1501
14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1501,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind West. After breakfast walked to Tynemouth &amp; with others. Amused ourselves on Cullercoat Sands practicing ball firing. Dined at home at 5 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to Mr Archer last night the owner of the planter to meet me at 11 o'clock on Tuesday morning to survey the damage.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess at night.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1447,"lock":null}
14:36:39.012 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/31/1501
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1501,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind West. After breakfast walked to Tynemouth &amp; with others. Amused ourselves on Cullercoat Sands practicing ball firing. Dined at home at 5 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to Mr Archer last night the owner of the planter to meet me at 11 o'clock on Tuesday morning to survey the damage.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess at night.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1447,"lock":null}
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/4/1474
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/4/1474
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/5/1475
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
14:36:39.013 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/5/1475
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/6/1476
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
