14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/7/1477
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1477,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still blowing hard from the SSW. Several light ships got down &amp; must have had a good run. Lockwood &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth. H Nicholson &amp; Mark dined with me at 3 o'clock. In the evening attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Aldertons</span> Committee room &amp; afterwards with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1423,"lock":null}
14:36:39.014 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
