14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/8/1478
14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1478,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind SW &amp; still looks like more rain. Walked to Preston to see Moor's brother who had not come down. Dined on board the Crisis with A Nicholson. In the evening we walked to Tynemouth at night with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1424,"lock":null}
14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/8/1478
14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1478,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind SW &amp; still looks like more rain. Walked to Preston to see Moor's brother who had not come down. Dined on board the Crisis with A Nicholson. In the evening we walked to Tynemouth at night with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1424,"lock":null}
14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/9/1479
14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1479,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind during the day varying between SE &amp; SE. At church in the morning. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Spencer</span> yesterday who agreed to renew our bill upon our rubbing off &pound;100 or &pound;150. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Called at Cunningham's Dr Drury there &amp; had some excellent glenlivet with them. Called afterwards at the castle, sat with the Marines &amp; at night again with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1425,"lock":null}
14:36:39.015 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/10/9/1479
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1479,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind during the day varying between SE &amp; SE. At church in the morning. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Spencer</span> yesterday who agreed to renew our bill upon our rubbing off &pound;100 or &pound;150. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Called at Cunningham's Dr Drury there &amp; had some excellent glenlivet with them. Called afterwards at the castle, sat with the Marines &amp; at night again with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1425,"lock":null}
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/1/1502
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1502,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning blowing &amp; has been all night hard from the SW. Ob board the Hope. Mr Archer did not come to survey the damage but sent a letter with an estimate, offering me &pound;1.10 &amp; the old boom etc. Walked up &amp; saw him but did not agree, however afterwards determined to take it with an 18 inch plank.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1448,"lock":null}
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/1/1502
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1502,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning blowing &amp; has been all night hard from the SW. Ob board the Hope. Mr Archer did not come to survey the damage but sent a letter with an estimate, offering me &pound;1.10 &amp; the old boom etc. Walked up &amp; saw him but did not agree, however afterwards determined to take it with an 18 inch plank.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home.</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1448,"lock":null}
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/10/1511
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1511,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw damp &amp; cold morning. Wind WSW. Two ships got upon the herd in coming into the harbour. Received a letter from Harry &amp;  G of Yarmouth informing me that the Hope had sprung a leak on Sunday night off Orford &amp; got a boat with 14 men to assist in pumping &amp; could scarcely keep her with both pumps going. They however had got her to Yarmouth close to the bar where they were lightening her to get her into the harbour. Laid the letter before the club who sent instructions to Messrs Hurry. I wrote to Stephenson &amp; WBS &amp; also sent a copy of the letter to the Hope Club at Newcastle.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at 2 o'clock. At the whist club in the evening &amp; suppered with Bess. Jobling with me</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1457,"lock":null}
14:36:39.016 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/10/1511
14:36:39.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1511,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A raw damp &amp; cold morning. Wind WSW. Two ships got upon the herd in coming into the harbour. Received a letter from Harry &amp;  G of Yarmouth informing me that the Hope had sprung a leak on Sunday night off Orford &amp; got a boat with 14 men to assist in pumping &amp; could scarcely keep her with both pumps going. They however had got her to Yarmouth close to the bar where they were lightening her to get her into the harbour. Laid the letter before the club who sent instructions to Messrs Hurry. I wrote to Stephenson &amp; WBS &amp; also sent a copy of the letter to the Hope Club at Newcastle.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at 2 o'clock. At the whist club in the evening &amp; suppered with Bess. Jobling with me</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1457,"lock":null}
14:36:39.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/11/1512
14:36:39.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1512,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW.</p>\r\n<p>The two ships got off the herd.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with our note to Chapman for &pound;200 dated the 9<sup>th</sup> Nov. Jobling left for Seghill. Tom Smith arrived from Togston. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1458,"lock":null}
14:36:39.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/11/1512
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1512,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW.</p>\r\n<p>The two ships got off the herd.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with our note to Chapman for &pound;200 dated the 9<sup>th</sup> Nov. Jobling left for Seghill. Tom Smith arrived from Togston. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1458,"lock":null}
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/12/1513
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1513,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from Messrs Hurry &amp; Co &amp; Stephenson of the ship having struck upon the bar in going into Yarmouth. Wrote to them to deliver &amp; sell the coals, get the leak stopped &amp; return to Shields. Wrote also to WBS. Went across the water &amp; saw Mr Potts who is to send me a copy of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Harmongs</span> protest on Monday. Tom Smith &amp; I dined at home at 5 o'clock &amp; had the whist club in the evening. A pleasant party. Jobling returned late</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1459,"lock":null}
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/12/1513
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1513,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Received a letter from Messrs Hurry &amp; Co &amp; Stephenson of the ship having struck upon the bar in going into Yarmouth. Wrote to them to deliver &amp; sell the coals, get the leak stopped &amp; return to Shields. Wrote also to WBS. Went across the water &amp; saw Mr Potts who is to send me a copy of the <span class=highlight_yellow>Harmongs</span> protest on Monday. Tom Smith &amp; I dined at home at 5 o'clock &amp; had the whist club in the evening. A pleasant party. Jobling returned late</p>","pageId":960,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1459,"lock":null}
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/13/1514
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1514,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold morning blowing hard from the NW &amp; NNW.</p>\r\n<p>Tom Smith &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; he afterwards drove up to Benton. Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 4 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>At night with Bess</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1460,"lock":null}
14:36:39.018 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.019 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/13/1514
14:36:39.019 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1514,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold morning blowing hard from the NW &amp; NNW.</p>\r\n<p>Tom Smith &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; he afterwards drove up to Benton. Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 4 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>At night with Bess</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1460,"lock":null}
14:36:39.019 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/14/1515
14:36:39.019 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1515,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold raw damp morning. Frosty during the night. Wind W &amp; W by S.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Spencer our note for &pound;200 at 6 months dated 9<sup>th</sup> Nov to be placed to the credit of the executors &amp; paid &pound;85 rents to their credit also Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 2 o'clock. I refused an invitation to dinner at Mr Reeds. At the billiard</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1461,"lock":null}
14:36:39.019 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/14/1515
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1515,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold raw damp morning. Frosty during the night. Wind W &amp; W by S.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Spencer our note for &pound;200 at 6 months dated 9<sup>th</sup> Nov to be placed to the credit of the executors &amp; paid &pound;85 rents to their credit also Jobling &amp; I dined at home at 2 o'clock. I refused an invitation to dinner at Mr Reeds. At the billiard</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1461,"lock":null}
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/15/1516
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1516,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind W by N. Received two letters, one from Hurry &amp; Co, the other from Stephenson stating the ship to be still very leaky requiring 6 extra men to pumps. They had got her about &frac14; of a mile up the way up to the quay. Laid the letters before the club. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1462,"lock":null}
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/15/1516
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1516,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind W by N. Received two letters, one from Hurry &amp; Co, the other from Stephenson stating the ship to be still very leaky requiring 6 extra men to pumps. They had got her about &frac14; of a mile up the way up to the quay. Laid the letters before the club. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1462,"lock":null}
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/16/1517
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1517,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Received a letter from WBS</p>\r\n<p>A comfortable winter's morning. Been a heavy fall of snow during the night. The country covered. Wind NNW. Thawing.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. With Bess at night.</p>\r\n<p>Sent Robert over the water to Mr Potts who let me have the Harmony Protest in the evening for which I paid &pound;1.11-6</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1463,"lock":null}
14:36:39.020 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.021 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/16/1517
14:36:39.021 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1517,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Received a letter from WBS</p>\r\n<p>A comfortable winter's morning. Been a heavy fall of snow during the night. The country covered. Wind NNW. Thawing.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. With Bess at night.</p>\r\n<p>Sent Robert over the water to Mr Potts who let me have the Harmony Protest in the evening for which I paid &pound;1.11-6</p>","pageId":961,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1463,"lock":null}
14:36:39.021 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/17/1518
14:36:39.021 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1518,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A sharp frost in the night having been a thaw yesterday. The streets this morning a sheet of ice &amp; dangerous walking. Wind WNW. The clubs received a letter from Messrs Hurry's stating they had sold the remainder of the coals to be taken out of the ship in two days. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent the Hairmongers protest with a copy of Chapman's book &amp; an account of rents. Attended the whist club. Boswell came home with us in the evening to join us in a glass of toddy. Took physic</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1464,"lock":null}
14:36:39.021 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/17/1518
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1518,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A sharp frost in the night having been a thaw yesterday. The streets this morning a sheet of ice &amp; dangerous walking. Wind WNW. The clubs received a letter from Messrs Hurry's stating they had sold the remainder of the coals to be taken out of the ship in two days. Wrote to WBS &amp; sent the Hairmongers protest with a copy of Chapman's book &amp; an account of rents. Attended the whist club. Boswell came home with us in the evening to join us in a glass of toddy. Took physic</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1464,"lock":null}
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/18/1519
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1519,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Having from cold I suppose, the back of my neck &amp; head much affected &amp; sore. I this morning took a black draught &amp; lay in bed till 1 o'clock. Charles Redley called from Hartley. Dined &amp; spent the afternoon with us. He left us at &frac14; past 9 o'clock to walk back being a fine moonlight night. I went along &amp; slept with Bess. Robert yesterday paid Philipson Mason his bill &pound;37 &amp; today paid into Chapman's &pound;15 more rents</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1465,"lock":null}
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/18/1519
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1519,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind WNW. Having from cold I suppose, the back of my neck &amp; head much affected &amp; sore. I this morning took a black draught &amp; lay in bed till 1 o'clock. Charles Redley called from Hartley. Dined &amp; spent the afternoon with us. He left us at &frac14; past 9 o'clock to walk back being a fine moonlight night. I went along &amp; slept with Bess. Robert yesterday paid Philipson Mason his bill &pound;37 &amp; today paid into Chapman's &pound;15 more rents</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1465,"lock":null}
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/19/1520
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1520,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A heavy fall of snow last night again. A complete thaw with sleet. Wind E by N. Paid average Eligible Club &pound;12. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; at night with Bess</p>","pageId":962,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1466,"lock":null}
14:36:39.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
