14:36:39.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1524,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Mild weather &amp; fresh breezes from WNW. Wrote to WBS with a list of ships that sailed before &amp; after the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room &amp; at night at Bess's. Jobling, H Hurry &amp; Boswell <font color=#BFBFBF>there</font>.</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1470,"lock":null}
14:36:39.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/24/1525
14:36:39.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1525,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuation of mild weather. Wind WSW. Received a letter from Stephenson of his having got the leak stopped. The ballast alongside &amp; expecting to get away the next day. Gave a draft on Ch<font color=#BFBFBF>apmans</font> for &pound;5 <span class=highlight_yellow>account</span> for self. Dined with Mr Harrison the brewer at 3 o'clock. At the whist club &amp; at night with Bess. Jobling went to South Shields</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1471,"lock":null}
14:36:39.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
