14:36:39.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1526,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Wind SW. gave a draft on Ch<font color=#BFBFBF>apmans</font> for &pound;9.10 average Hope Club. Wind changed to SE. A great many ships got down. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. With Bess at night. Lockwood there</p>","pageId":963,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1472,"lock":null}
14:36:39.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/11/26/1527
14:36:39.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1527,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather but cold and wind SE. A great many light ships arrived <span class=highlight_yellow>ravenjot</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>this</span>. The Hope from Yarmouth quite light. Went to Newcastle &amp; fixed her to load Bell&amp; Brown again to be loaded in 3 weeks,. Returned home to dinner. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; attended the club. At night at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garthays</span></p>","pageId":964,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1473,"lock":null}
