14:36:39.037 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1546,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; frosty. Wind WSW. Accepted a bill for balance of premium (182). Great Premium Clun &pound;7.6.6 due 14 March. On board the Stokes, the remainder of her coals (4 keels) came down &amp; she finished her loading. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. The whist club in the evening. Called in at the widows at night &amp; saw the Hope go to sea at 1 o'clock in the morning.</p>\r\n<p>Wind WNW</p>","pageId":968,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1492,"lock":null}
14:36:39.037 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/12/16/1547
14:36:39.037 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1547,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Paid the Hope's piolet &pound;1.16 &amp; to 3 men for getting the ship chain hawser which she was obliged to ship &amp; leave behind &amp; for placing it on shore 7/6.</p>\r\n<p>Gave a draft on C<font color=#BFBFBF>hapman</font>'s &amp; Co for self &pound;5</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Joblings brothers with us.</p>\r\n<p>At the theatre &amp; with Bess at night.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening blew a gale at SSE</p>","pageId":968,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1493,"lock":null}
14:36:39.037 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
