14:36:39.037 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1547,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Paid the Hope's piolet &pound;1.16 &amp; to 3 men for getting the ship chain hawser which she was obliged to ship &amp; leave behind &amp; for placing it on shore 7/6.</p>\r\n<p>Gave a draft on C<font color=#BFBFBF>hapman</font>'s &amp; Co for self &pound;5</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Joblings brothers with us.</p>\r\n<p>At the theatre &amp; with Bess at night.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening blew a gale at SSE</p>","pageId":968,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1493,"lock":null}
14:36:39.037 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/12/17/1548
14:36:39.037 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1548,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning, but fine weather. A fresh breeze from WSW &amp; SW. Went by steam to Newcastle. Signed the Hope's cargo bill &pound;216.10.6 at 60 days from the 14 Dec.</p>\r\n<p>Saw Dixon Dixon. Returned by steam. Wrote to WBS. Lockwood dined with me at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. At the whist club with me at Ben Wrights</p>","pageId":968,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1494,"lock":null}
