14:36:39.081 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1242,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind fresh at W by N. paid Robert &pound;2.4/ Walton the brewer bills 3<sup>rd</sup> &amp; 4<sup>th</sup> coal voyage which will be given credit for as sent, be being in <span class=highlight_yellow>asseasy</span>. Engaged today making up ships books. Dined at home. At the Abbey in the evening. The Hope arrived</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1188,"lock":null}
14:36:39.081 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/20/1260
14:36:39.081 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1260,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine mild weather. Wind West. Attended church parade the whole of the officers &amp; men. Went to church. Paraded at 5 o'clock in the afternoon. Dined at the mess. Captain Biggs finished <span class=highlight_yellow>withing</span> his <span class=highlight_yellow>com</span><font color=#BFBFBF><span class=highlight_yellow>pany</span></font>. Kept it up very late. Did not get to bed till 4 o'clock in the morning. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":894,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1206,"lock":null}
14:36:39.081 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
