14:36:39.084 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1266,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Exceptionally cold. East wind with showers. Attended 10 o'clock drill, but did not go to the pasture. Received a letter from WBS of the safe arrival of the Hop at London, but not able to sell her coals, the <span class=highlight_yellow>proves</span> quite light. Lunched with W Torston. At 2 o'clock parade marched to the pasture &amp; went through the manoeuvres. Returned earlier than usual in consequence of the rain. Dined at the mess. A stranger day, but a small party. The band had a concert at the Town hall. I took a ticket but <font color=#BFBFBF>did </font>not go.</p>","pageId":895,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1212,"lock":null}
14:36:39.084 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/3/26/1267
14:36:39.084 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1267,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning. Wind E but with heavy showers of rain &amp; sleet. Continued raining very heavy all day, so that we could not have any parade. Dined at the mess</p>","pageId":896,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1213,"lock":null}
