14:36:39.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1291,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. The Hope arrived at 5 o'clock am. Went by Duma coach to Newcastle &amp; fixed her to load Bell &amp; Brown being the readiest time &amp; all other collieries being off work excepting Wellington, <span class=highlight_yellow>Pontop</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Jaasects</span>. Wrote to WBS. Dined at the Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> Tavern being the annual dinner of the whist club.</p>","pageId":901,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1237,"lock":null}
14:36:39.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/4/15/1292
14:36:39.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1292,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Received the Hopes accounts &amp; balance note &pound;97.9/ = { balance accounts 47.9 : on account 50 } Received also a letter from Leadbottom, the <span class=highlight_yellow>introduction</span> Newcastle w entry a statement of the account between us &amp; Mrs Scott executors which I sent him.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. On board the Harvy in the afternoon &amp; went over the bar <span class=highlight_yellow>with:</span> bound to Quebec. Finished off at the Albion &amp; called at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":902,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1238,"lock":null}
14:36:39.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
