14:36:39.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1277,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":2,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but very cold. Lockerand breakfasted with me &amp; we went up to Newcastle together by Duma coach. Called at Westgate Street, saw the Dixons and Emma Galbraith who was looking very well &amp; is spending her Easter holidays there. Wrote to WBS. Dined with D Dixon at Tom Fenwick in Charlotte Square. Met a party there. Slept at Miss <span class=highlight_yellow>Willi</span> with <span class=highlight_yellow>Bess</span></p>","pageId":898,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1223,"lock":null}
14:36:39.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/4/20/1298
14:36:39.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1298,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but rather damp morning. Wind ESE. The charter for the Hope arrived by the post from Hull. The Merchants Messrs Wade Sons &amp; Forster Wybury &amp; Hull. 70/ for <span class=highlight_yellow>deals</span> &amp; buttons. The latter not to exceed 6/8. Ordered 3 casks or pork of Bradshaws &amp; 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>loaves</span> of bread of Walkerley &amp; a new main topgallantsail. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon H Harry gave the Doctor &amp; me some wine at the Northumberland Alms. Afterwards at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1244,"lock":null}
14:36:39.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
