14:36:39.099 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1298,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but rather damp morning. Wind ESE. The charter for the Hope arrived by the post from Hull. The Merchants Messrs Wade Sons &amp; Forster Wybury &amp; Hull. 70/ for <span class=highlight_yellow>deals</span> &amp; buttons. The latter not to exceed 6/8. Ordered 3 casks or pork of Bradshaws &amp; 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>loaves</span> of bread of Walkerley &amp; a new main topgallantsail. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon H Harry gave the Doctor &amp; me some wine at the Northumberland Alms. Afterwards at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1244,"lock":null}
14:36:39.099 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/4/21/1299
14:36:39.099 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1299,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold morning. Wind NE. Paid into Chapmans the <span class=highlight_yellow>hote</span> for &pound;97.9. Gave Stephenson &pound;50. Got the pork, bread etc on board. Had a few friends to dine with me at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>veg</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Te</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nley's</span> Rudyard 15<sup>th</sup> Regiment Dick artillery J Wright &amp; Boswell.</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1245,"lock":null}
