14:36:39.104 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1308,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy day. Wind continues from SE. The election for Newcastle took place. I went to the Guild Hall but I could not get near enough to the hustings to hear any part of the speeches. For Mr Ridley &amp; Mr Hodgson returned without opposition. Lucky fellows. Saw them chained. Had a lunch at the Turf &amp; returned to Shields by Dunn. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1254,"lock":null}
