14:36:39.106 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1281,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Turned out rather showery. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined with Jibbs &amp; afterwards went to the Sands to see the races. Lockerwood and Charlton gave us wine in the evening &amp; finished off at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":899,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1227,"lock":null}
14:36:39.106 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/4/6/1282
14:36:39.106 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1282,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; every appearance of rain. Wind changeable being <span class=highlight_yellow>raily</span> in the morning from the west &amp; afterwards NE. Received a letter from WBS. Called on Mr Robinson but got no money. The W<font color=#BFBFBF>illia</font><sup>m</sup> Shand, Boswell arrived from Rotterdam. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth nut nothing doing. In the evening at the Albion &amp; called at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":899,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1228,"lock":null}
