14:36:39.114 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1327,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Wind S by E. H Harry Cunningham &amp; I took a long walk round by Burdon &amp; Percy Main collieries. The <span class=highlight_yellow>pitmen</span> in a very disturbed state. Dined with Dr Drury &amp; in the afternoon walked to Billy Mill to play a quoits &amp; took wine with Charlton. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":910,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1273,"lock":null}
14:36:39.114 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/18/1328
14:36:39.114 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1328,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful morning. Wind SE. Captain <font color=#BFBFBF>William Fanshawe</font> Martin of the Samarang having hired a steamer I accompanied him &amp; a party to Seaham with which we were much pleased and surprised at so vast an undertaking  for one individual. Having taken one <span class=highlight_yellow>prog</span><span class=highlight_yellow>:</span> etc with us we dined at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Prince</span> &amp; embarked again at &frac12; past 6 o'clock &amp; reached Shields between 10 &amp; 11 o'clock after having spent an uncommonly   pleasant day. At the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":910,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1274,"lock":null}
