14:36:39.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1338,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another dull morning. The wind still from the old quarter NE. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; saw the troops fire a salute at 12 o'clock in honour of the King's birthday. Returned &amp; also saw the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Orestes gun brig do the same &amp; man her yards. Dined at 4 o'clock with Mr Bradshaw in celebration of his wife's birthday, a very pleasant party &amp; most splendid dinner &amp; wines.</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1284,"lock":null}
14:36:39.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/29/1339
14:36:39.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1339,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning rather dull wind S by E. Attended morning service. Dined at home. Lockwood took dinner with me. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Took wine with Tibbs &amp; spent the evening in the castle yard &amp; Lockwood</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1285,"lock":null}
14:36:39.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
