14:36:39.122 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1311,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull orning &amp; damp heavy been a good deal of rain in the night. Wind SE. Lord Howielt &amp; Mr Beaumont came into the town conducted by an immense crowd of people with bands &amp; colours, whom they addressed from a hustings erected in front on the Commercial. Turned out a very rainy afternoon. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum. In the evening gave Jonny Smith &pound;28.1.6 <span class=highlight_yellow>Int</span> for his mother.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1257,"lock":null}
14:36:39.122 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/5/30/1340
14:36:39.122 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1340,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind ESE. Received a letter from WBS. At Tynemouth all the morning. Dined with Griffiths, RM &amp; Dick RA at the castle. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":913,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1286,"lock":null}
14:36:39.122 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
