14:36:39.130 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1355,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Very unwell last night &amp; all the day suffered from eating some salmon. Walked into Newcastle with D Dixon. Saw Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font> &amp; took the steam boat to Shields. Dined with Doctor &amp; afterwards walked up to his garden. Very unwell this evening. Took some tincture of rhubarb a couple of pills &amp; went early to bed.</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1301,"lock":null}
14:36:39.130 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/15/1356
14:36:39.130 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1356,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh at SW by S. Received a letter from Stephenson of his safe arrival at Hull after a fine passage of sixteen days from Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>burg <font color=#BFBFBF>(Cape Town)</font>. He has to lay 8 days quarantine.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font>d average Hope Club &pound;9.17.6 &amp; Mrs Brown sail-making etc. &pound;5.15.6. Wrote to Stephenson. Dined at home. Went on board W<font color=#BFBFBF>illia</font>m C Wright's ship the Mulgrave Castle with H Harry, bound to Archangel. At the Albion &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1302,"lock":null}
14:36:39.130 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/15/1356
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1356,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh at SW by S. Received a letter from Stephenson of his safe arrival at Hull after a fine passage of sixteen days from Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>burg <font color=#BFBFBF>(Cape Town)</font>. He has to lay 8 days quarantine.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font>d average Hope Club &pound;9.17.6 &amp; Mrs Brown sail-making etc. &pound;5.15.6. Wrote to Stephenson. Dined at home. Went on board W<font color=#BFBFBF>illia</font>m C Wright's ship the Mulgrave Castle with H Harry, bound to Archangel. At the Albion &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":917,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1302,"lock":null}
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/16/1357
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1357,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine growing morning. Been a shower &amp; the appearance of more rain. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Received a letter (post paid) from Harenan &amp; Co, London, enclosing Stephenson's WyBurg bills of &pound;50.5/ for acceptance. Accepted at by leave of Chapman's payable at Barketts &amp; Co, dated 29<sup>th</sup> Aug &amp; returned it by post. Lockwood dined with me. Walked round in the afternoon by the Doctor's garden to Tynemouth. At Tynemouth also in the morning. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1303,"lock":null}
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/16/1357
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1357,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine growing morning. Been a shower &amp; the appearance of more rain. Wind SW.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Received a letter (post paid) from Harenan &amp; Co, London, enclosing Stephenson's WyBurg bills of &pound;50.5/ for acceptance. Accepted at by leave of Chapman's payable at Barketts &amp; Co, dated 29<sup>th</sup> Aug &amp; returned it by post. Lockwood dined with me. Walked round in the afternoon by the Doctor's garden to Tynemouth. At Tynemouth also in the morning. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1303,"lock":null}
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/17/1358
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1358,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about West. Received a letter from WBS from Carlow &amp; clear Stephenson's letter from Wyburg of his being loaded. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon with H Harry. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1304,"lock":null}
14:36:39.131 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
