14:36:39.139 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1369,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; very sultry close morning. Wind N by W &amp; NNW. Called upon Martin Orr at the Garrison. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>utt</span> but declined fixing a foreign mail being expected &amp; the chance of freights being better. H French dined with me on board after having a long walk about the town. The ship out &amp; cleared this afternoon. Wrote to Bess B. Martin Orr &amp; his wife called upon me at the ship. Set H French <span class=highlight_yellow>part</span> of the way home &amp; amused myself the remainder of the evening by strolling round the town. Turned out a very rainy day.</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1315,"lock":null}
14:36:39.139 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/29/1370
14:36:39.139 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1370,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy morning. Wind NW. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbu</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tt'</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Stephenson busy paying dock dues etc. &amp; getting ships provisions on board. The rain &amp; wind prevented the lighters working &amp; we got no ballast today. Dined at 4 o'clock with J Bell. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ward</span> dined with us. In the evening walked to H French's house &amp; spent it with <span class=highlight_yellow>nens</span> &amp; Fanny</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1316,"lock":null}
14:36:39.139 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
