14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1370,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy morning. Wind NW. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbu</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tt'</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Stephenson busy paying dock dues etc. &amp; getting ships provisions on board. The rain &amp; wind prevented the lighters working &amp; we got no ballast today. Dined at 4 o'clock with J Bell. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ward</span> dined with us. In the evening walked to H French's house &amp; spent it with <span class=highlight_yellow>nens</span> &amp; Fanny</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1316,"lock":null}
14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/3/1344
14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1344,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day, rather foggy at sea. Wind NNE. Walked to Tynemouth with Webb. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; I together in the afternoon. Played at Quoits in the evening at the Doctor's garden. Called at the Mulstrum on our way home.</p>","pageId":914,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1290,"lock":null}
14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/3/1344
14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1344,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day, rather foggy at sea. Wind NNE. Walked to Tynemouth with Webb. Dined at home. H Harry &amp; I together in the afternoon. Played at Quoits in the evening at the Doctor's garden. Called at the Mulstrum on our way home.</p>","pageId":914,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1290,"lock":null}
14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/6/30/1371
14:36:39.140 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1371,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind NNW. Breakfasted with Orr &amp; his wife at the Garrison. Saw the armoury containing the arms of all the local militias etc of the district, about 20000. Walked up to the ship, a <span class=highlight_yellow>lighter</span> up with 40 tons of ballast. At Garbutt's, Wade not having got the deal <span class=highlight_yellow>counted</span> are unable to settle the freight. Dined on board. Walked about the town &amp; docks in the afternoon &amp; spent the evening with Orr. Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":922,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1317,"lock":null}
