14:36:39.160 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1408,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuation of most delightful weather. Wind from the S &amp; E. At church in the morning. Dined at home. Lockerwood dined with me. H Harry came in &amp; took wine. At Tynemouth &amp; Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1354,"lock":null}
14:36:39.160 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/4/1377
14:36:39.160 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1377,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind with the heat got to ENE. Arrived at Shields at 7 o'clock. Crossed the water &amp; got home in time to go to the Low Lights &amp; bath before breakfast. Dined at home. Being excessively sleepy, turned into bed for three hours. Walked after tea up to Preston through the fields to examine them &amp; see <span class=highlight_yellow>moors</span>. Went to the theatre in the evening &amp; afterwards called at the Mulstrum to see Bess</p>","pageId":923,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1323,"lock":null}
14:36:39.160 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
