14:36:39.162 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1379,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind E by S. paid into Chapmans a bill at 4 months, <span class=highlight_yellow>Weider</span> accepted on <span class=highlight_yellow>Hoarses</span> for &pound;175. Took a walk round by the rocks to Tynemouth. Dined at 5 o'clock With Mr J Metcalf &amp; went to the theatre in the evening being thebespeak of the officers of the marines. At the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":923,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1325,"lock":null}
14:36:39.162 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/7/1380
14:36:39.162 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1380,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most delightful morning. Wind SE. paid Walnsley baker &pound;9.3, Morris butcher &pound;9, Bradshaws Irish pork 3 casks &pound;9. J Tinley dined with us at 5 o'clock. Ben Galbraith &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening.</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1326,"lock":null}
