14:36:39.163 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1381,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Beautiful weather. Wind SE. Went with WBS on board the City of Edinburgh to take his birth to London.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Bathed at 1 o'clock. Accompanied a party of officers to Wallsend and dined with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hotts</span> a large party &amp; spent a very pleasant day. He was so kind as to send his carriage for us. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1327,"lock":null}
14:36:39.163 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/7/9/1382
14:36:39.163 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1382,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind SE. Moor &amp; his brothers with J Tinley with us. Foster Moor signed a document making over to us all his stack &amp; crop etc &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>resigning</span> the farm which we have allowed Mr Moor to take as <span class=highlight_yellow>tinanl</span>. Walked up to Preston. People busy with the potatoes &amp; turnips &amp; clearing the hedges.  Gave in a draft on Chapmans for &pound;20 for WBS. <span class=highlight_yellow>Dined</span> at 2 o'clock. Went on board the City of Edinburgh steamer with WBS &amp; saw him sail for London. Ben &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening. A heavy rain about &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1328,"lock":null}
