14:36:39.164 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1410,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW &amp; ESE. Walked to Tynemouth. Ben G<font color=#BFBFBF>ailbraith</font> went to Newcastle to see Emma. At Tynemouth again in the afternoon. Had a most delightful bath at the end of Cullercoats Sands &amp; dined with L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Mitchel &amp; Lockerwood at the castle. Bess met me on the mound, gave her a long lecture but <span class=highlight_yellow>query</span> it has any good effect. Heavy shower of rain</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1356,"lock":null}
14:36:39.164 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/12/1411
14:36:39.164 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1411,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Bathed before breakfast. Engaged at home writing. Dined at home. Called and took a glass of wine with the Doctor. Walked up to Tynemouth. Called &amp; spent the evening at the Castle. At the Mulstrum at night. P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font><sup>d</sup> Brown <span class=highlight_yellow>Tarters</span> 17/-</p>","pageId":930,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1357,"lock":null}
