14:36:39.169 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/19/1421
14:36:39.169 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1421,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been rain in the night. Wind fresh at WNW. In endeavouring to throw my portmanteau upon my shoulder, it being very heavy, I strained the muscles of my back very severely &amp; I fear I shall not soon recover from it. Pain very acute. Got on the coach at the White Horse <span class=highlight_yellow>ally</span> at 8 o'clock with WBS &amp; BBG &amp; started for Southampton where we arrived at &frac12; past 4 o'clock having had very fine weather &amp; a pleasant journey, the dust being laid by the rain. My back very painful &amp; with some difficulty got down to my lodgings &amp; to bed. We got Mrs Sands lodgings, the same as when at Southampton before.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1367,"lock":null}
14:36:39.169 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/19/1421
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1421,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been rain in the night. Wind fresh at WNW. In endeavouring to throw my portmanteau upon my shoulder, it being very heavy, I strained the muscles of my back very severely &amp; I fear I shall not soon recover from it. Pain very acute. Got on the coach at the White Horse <span class=highlight_yellow>ally</span> at 8 o'clock with WBS &amp; BBG &amp; started for Southampton where we arrived at &frac12; past 4 o'clock having had very fine weather &amp; a pleasant journey, the dust being laid by the rain. My back very painful &amp; with some difficulty got down to my lodgings &amp; to bed. We got Mrs Sands lodgings, the same as when at Southampton before.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1367,"lock":null}
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/20/1422
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1422,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. I made an attempt to get out of bed this morning but my back was so bad I was obliged to lay down again. Breakfasted in bed. About 1 o'clock determined to make another attempt to get up &amp; dress myself &amp; with much difficulty &amp; pain &amp; the assistance of Ben I succeeded. After being up &amp; walking a short time, found myself much easier. Walked down to the Pier &amp; baths. Had a warm bath &amp; Mr Lee afterwards drove me home in his gig. The remainder of the afternoon &amp; evening found myself much relieved. About dinner time we had a very heavy squall with rain.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1368,"lock":null}
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/20/1422
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1422,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; blowing fresh from the WNW. I made an attempt to get out of bed this morning but my back was so bad I was obliged to lay down again. Breakfasted in bed. About 1 o'clock determined to make another attempt to get up &amp; dress myself &amp; with much difficulty &amp; pain &amp; the assistance of Ben I succeeded. After being up &amp; walking a short time, found myself much easier. Walked down to the Pier &amp; baths. Had a warm bath &amp; Mr Lee afterwards drove me home in his gig. The remainder of the afternoon &amp; evening found myself much relieved. About dinner time we had a very heavy squall with rain.</p>","pageId":932,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1368,"lock":null}
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/21/1423
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1423,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing hard from the N by E. got up &amp; walked to Mr Lee's to breakfast. Walked down to the post office &amp; pier. Mr Lee drove me down to Shirley to call upon the Lewis. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1369,"lock":null}
14:36:39.170 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.171 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/21/1423
14:36:39.171 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1423,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but blowing hard from the N by E. got up &amp; walked to Mr Lee's to breakfast. Walked down to the post office &amp; pier. Mr Lee drove me down to Shirley to call upon the Lewis. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1369,"lock":null}
14:36:39.171 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/22/1424
14:36:39.171 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1424,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning . Wind fresh from N by E. Played at billiards. The Lewis's came in &amp; dined at Mr Lees. Messrs Horsford &amp; Hawksley came in the evening. My back much better.</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1370,"lock":null}
14:36:39.171 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/22/1424
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1424,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning . Wind fresh from N by E. Played at billiards. The Lewis's came in &amp; dined at Mr Lees. Messrs Horsford &amp; Hawksley came in the evening. My back much better.</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1370,"lock":null}
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/23/1425
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1425,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine morning. Wind SW. Wrote to Garbull &amp; son of Hull to inform him when the Hope arrived etc. Dined at 2 o'clock at Mr lee's. The Lewis there &amp; embarked at &frac12; past 5 o'clock on board the Ariadne steam boat at 6 o'clock. Sailed for Guernsey with a good many passengers on board. A most beautiful evening. Moon light &amp; not a cloud to be seen. I walked the deck until we had passed the Needles &amp; went to bed at 12 o'clock. R Marsh with us</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1371,"lock":null}
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/23/1425
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1425,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine morning. Wind SW. Wrote to Garbull &amp; son of Hull to inform him when the Hope arrived etc. Dined at 2 o'clock at Mr lee's. The Lewis there &amp; embarked at &frac12; past 5 o'clock on board the Ariadne steam boat at 6 o'clock. Sailed for Guernsey with a good many passengers on board. A most beautiful evening. Moon light &amp; not a cloud to be seen. I walked the deck until we had passed the Needles &amp; went to bed at 12 o'clock. R Marsh with us</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1371,"lock":null}
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1426
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1426,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Got up at 6 o'clock at which time we were abreast of the ____ with Alderney, Sark &amp; Guernsey or S<sup>t</sup> Peters <font color=#BFBFBF>Port </font>in sight. Came to an anchor in Guernsey Sands about 8 o'clock &amp; landed after a most delightful passage. The town of St Peter port is beautifully situated above the bay upon a rising hill &amp; consists of a great many very excellent houses. It is of considerable extent but the streets are narrow. It however is rapidly improving and contains a great many beautiful private houses as well as public institutions, the collage the most striking ...</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1372,"lock":null}
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.172 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1426
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1426,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind SW. Got up at 6 o'clock at which time we were abreast of the ____ with Alderney, Sark &amp; Guernsey or S<sup>t</sup> Peters <font color=#BFBFBF>Port </font>in sight. Came to an anchor in Guernsey Sands about 8 o'clock &amp; landed after a most delightful passage. The town of St Peter port is beautifully situated above the bay upon a rising hill &amp; consists of a great many very excellent houses. It is of considerable extent but the streets are narrow. It however is rapidly improving and contains a great many beautiful private houses as well as public institutions, the collage the most striking ...</p>","pageId":933,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1372,"lock":null}
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1427
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1427,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We put up at Mousehole Hotel which is near the harbour &amp; the back bed room window commanded an exceedingly fine view of the sea adjacent islands. This hotel I recommend to all travellers both for the activity &amp; attention of the landlady &amp; her daughter Mrs ____ &amp; their reasonable charges. There is a small harbour formed by piers which is dry at low water. The rise and fall is very considerable being I should think thirty feet.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Having changed our cloths &amp; made ourselves comfortable we had breakfast. Much to our surprise met James Basher in the coffee room who agreed to join our party at dinner. After breakfast strolled out to see the town. Much pleased with the new market. Fish &amp; butchers etc. It is the best &amp; most perfect thing of the kind I ever saw or heard of.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Afterwards called upon Dr Proctor who was not at home. Went over &amp; saw the interior of the collage, a very fine institution &amp; apparently well placed &amp; of it were not for the low heavy square towers in the centre would be a handsome building.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>During the afternoon saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>presence</span> feast of the town &amp; walked up to the garrison which stands very high upon the south point of the bay which <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> the town, it &amp; fort completely commands. In our rambles we met with old Charlton late of the firm of Scott &amp; Charlton, who came &amp; dined with us at 6 o'clock. He has lived about a year here. Saw Dr Proctor this afternoon. Much pleased with him.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>","pageId":934,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1373,"lock":null}
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/24/1427
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1427,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":24,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>We put up at Mousehole Hotel which is near the harbour &amp; the back bed room window commanded an exceedingly fine view of the sea adjacent islands. This hotel I recommend to all travellers both for the activity &amp; attention of the landlady &amp; her daughter Mrs ____ &amp; their reasonable charges. There is a small harbour formed by piers which is dry at low water. The rise and fall is very considerable being I should think thirty feet.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Having changed our cloths &amp; made ourselves comfortable we had breakfast. Much to our surprise met James Basher in the coffee room who agreed to join our party at dinner. After breakfast strolled out to see the town. Much pleased with the new market. Fish &amp; butchers etc. It is the best &amp; most perfect thing of the kind I ever saw or heard of.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Afterwards called upon Dr Proctor who was not at home. Went over &amp; saw the interior of the collage, a very fine institution &amp; apparently well placed &amp; of it were not for the low heavy square towers in the centre would be a handsome building.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>During the afternoon saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>presence</span> feast of the town &amp; walked up to the garrison which stands very high upon the south point of the bay which <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> the town, it &amp; fort completely commands. In our rambles we met with old Charlton late of the firm of Scott &amp; Charlton, who came &amp; dined with us at 6 o'clock. He has lived about a year here. Saw Dr Proctor this afternoon. Much pleased with him.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>","pageId":934,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1373,"lock":null}
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/25/1428
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1428,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most delightful weather. Wind SW. Had a warm bath this morning. At 12 o'clock we all got into a four wheeled vehicle. Drove round the greater part of the island, excepting the north angles, but there is nothing very picturesque or beautiful to be seen. Got home to dinner at 6 o'clock. Ian Basnes dines out</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1374,"lock":null}
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/25/1428
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1428,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most delightful weather. Wind SW. Had a warm bath this morning. At 12 o'clock we all got into a four wheeled vehicle. Drove round the greater part of the island, excepting the north angles, but there is nothing very picturesque or beautiful to be seen. Got home to dinner at 6 o'clock. Ian Basnes dines out</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1374,"lock":null}
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/26/1429
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1429,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Amused ourselves by strolling about the markets etc. William went &amp; saw Dr Proctor again, but I being tired did not go. Having settled our bill, at 2 o'clock we again embarked on board the <font color=#000000>Ariadne</font><font size=3.4pt color=#000000>&nbsp;</font>&amp; sailed about 9 o'clock. The vessel most uncomfortably crowded, being about 155 passengers on board. We could not get berths. Passed close by the Island of Alderney. A fine sight.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1375,"lock":null}
14:36:39.173 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/26/1429
14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1429,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Amused ourselves by strolling about the markets etc. William went &amp; saw Dr Proctor again, but I being tired did not go. Having settled our bill, at 2 o'clock we again embarked on board the <font color=#000000>Ariadne</font><font size=3.4pt color=#000000>&nbsp;</font>&amp; sailed about 9 o'clock. The vessel most uncomfortably crowded, being about 155 passengers on board. We could not get berths. Passed close by the Island of Alderney. A fine sight.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1375,"lock":null}
14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/27/1430
14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1430,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. We arrived at Southampton at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, very much fatigued having been waiting to sleep or lay on deck all night. After waiting two hours &amp; a half at the custom house, we were obliged to go home to breakfast without our luggage. Dined at the Lewises at Shirley. Colonel Ogilvie &amp; Captain Cobb there.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1376,"lock":null}
14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
