14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1430,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. We arrived at Southampton at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, very much fatigued having been waiting to sleep or lay on deck all night. After waiting two hours &amp; a half at the custom house, we were obliged to go home to breakfast without our luggage. Dined at the Lewises at Shirley. Colonel Ogilvie &amp; Captain Cobb there.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1376,"lock":null}
14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/28/1431
14:36:39.174 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1431,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NW. Did not go to church. After lunch took a walk round by the Pier, the baths to the Itchen &amp; crossed the ferry to see PearTree Green. Returned to dinner</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1377,"lock":null}
