14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1433,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW. Again engaged much the same as yesterday. Received a letter from Stephenson as which both Roads dated the 24<sup>th</sup> all well. The Lewis' &amp; Mr Carry dined with us. Major Falls of the 93<sup>rd</sup> &amp; Colonel Ogilvie came in the evening.</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1379,"lock":null}
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/31/1434
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/8/31/1434
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/1/1435
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
14:36:39.176 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/1/1435
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/10/1446
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1446,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still damp unpleasant weather &amp; appearance of more rain. Wind NW. Called a little earlier upon Lord Beverley who had again gone out. Returned to Nottingham Place. At 2 o'clock walked down to Charring Cross &amp; there got upon a stage &amp; went to the Elephant &amp; castle &amp; thence walked to George Harry Apollo Buildings, Walworth &amp; saw Henry H. who I found laid up, being much bruised &amp; injured by the upsetting of a Blackwell Stage. Returned by stage &amp; dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Richmond. Walked home early in the evening.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1392,"lock":null}
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/10/1446
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1446,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still damp unpleasant weather &amp; appearance of more rain. Wind NW. Called a little earlier upon Lord Beverley who had again gone out. Returned to Nottingham Place. At 2 o'clock walked down to Charring Cross &amp; there got upon a stage &amp; went to the Elephant &amp; castle &amp; thence walked to George Harry Apollo Buildings, Walworth &amp; saw Henry H. who I found laid up, being much bruised &amp; injured by the upsetting of a Blackwell Stage. Returned by stage &amp; dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Richmond. Walked home early in the evening.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1392,"lock":null}
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/11/1447
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1447,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of dull cloudy weather, wind NNW &amp; every appearance of more rain. William, Emma &amp; Lee went to church. I did not go being obliged to take some <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuberts</span>. At 3 o'clock walked through the Regents Park to the Zoological Gardens with which &amp; the collection of wild beasts. I was much pleased. Returned home &amp; dressed &amp; went to dine with Mr Leaskill at 7 o'clock, a small party, only Captain Greg &amp; myself there</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1393,"lock":null}
14:36:39.177 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/11/1447
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1447,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of dull cloudy weather, wind NNW &amp; every appearance of more rain. William, Emma &amp; Lee went to church. I did not go being obliged to take some <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuberts</span>. At 3 o'clock walked through the Regents Park to the Zoological Gardens with which &amp; the collection of wild beasts. I was much pleased. Returned home &amp; dressed &amp; went to dine with Mr Leaskill at 7 o'clock, a small party, only Captain Greg &amp; myself there</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1393,"lock":null}
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/12/1448
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1448,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but rather cloudy. Wind NW &amp; NNW. After lunch walked down to St James street &amp; saw the nobility etc. go to court. Her Majesty holding a drawing room.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with C <span class=highlight_yellow>Reibarud</span>. J Griffith &amp; WBS there.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Mary Scott <font color=#BFBFBF>(daughter of WBS) </font>went to school</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1394,"lock":null}
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/12/1448
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1448,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but rather cloudy. Wind NW &amp; NNW. After lunch walked down to St James street &amp; saw the nobility etc. go to court. Her Majesty holding a drawing room.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with C <span class=highlight_yellow>Reibarud</span>. J Griffith &amp; WBS there.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Mary Scott <font color=#BFBFBF>(daughter of WBS) </font>went to school</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1394,"lock":null}
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/13/1449
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1449,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind N by W. Wrote to Robert Snowdon. Lee Scott went to School. Walked down to St James Street. His Majesty holding a Levee went along the Strand &amp; called on Bob Marsh. Returned &amp; saw the company come from the Levee. Walked with WBS in Regent Street at 6 o'clock dined alone at the Blue Ports &amp; afterwards went home.</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1395,"lock":null}
14:36:39.178 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/13/1449
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1449,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind N by W. Wrote to Robert Snowdon. Lee Scott went to School. Walked down to St James Street. His Majesty holding a Levee went along the Strand &amp; called on Bob Marsh. Returned &amp; saw the company come from the Levee. Walked with WBS in Regent Street at 6 o'clock dined alone at the Blue Ports &amp; afterwards went home.</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1395,"lock":null}
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/14/1450
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1450,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind from the N &amp; E. Wrote a letter to Lord Beverley &amp; afterwards called upon him &amp; found him at home, very graciously received. Entered into a long account &amp; related to him all the inconsistencies respecting any complaint about being <span class=highlight_yellow>regazzetted</span> etc, but he could not interfere at the same. Explained himself as not surprised at my feelings &amp; regret that it should have happened, but that he thought no further change could be made. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Called at the <span class=highlight_yellow>courting</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> &amp; thence walked down to Mrs Carr's. Saw Boswell the <span class=highlight_yellow>Decgttonte</span> and dined there. Spent the evening &amp; returned by stage at night.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1396,"lock":null}
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/14/1450
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1450,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind from the N &amp; E. Wrote a letter to Lord Beverley &amp; afterwards called upon him &amp; found him at home, very graciously received. Entered into a long account &amp; related to him all the inconsistencies respecting any complaint about being <span class=highlight_yellow>regazzetted</span> etc, but he could not interfere at the same. Explained himself as not surprised at my feelings &amp; regret that it should have happened, but that he thought no further change could be made. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Called at the <span class=highlight_yellow>courting</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> &amp; thence walked down to Mrs Carr's. Saw Boswell the <span class=highlight_yellow>Decgttonte</span> and dined there. Spent the evening &amp; returned by stage at night.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1396,"lock":null}
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/15/1451
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1451,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind N by E. Remained in the house till after 1 o'clock expecting Boswell, but he did not come. Walked round the inner circle of the Regents Park &amp; thence to Bob Marsh's  &amp; WBS &amp; I afterwards walked up by Regents Street home to dinner. Found that Boswell had called after I had left home.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1397,"lock":null}
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/15/1451
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1451,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind N by E. Remained in the house till after 1 o'clock expecting Boswell, but he did not come. Walked round the inner circle of the Regents Park &amp; thence to Bob Marsh's  &amp; WBS &amp; I afterwards walked up by Regents Street home to dinner. Found that Boswell had called after I had left home.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1397,"lock":null}
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/16/1452
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1452,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the north. Wrote to Lord Beverley requesting him to present one to His Majesty at the Levee on Wednesday next &amp; left the letter at his house. Thence walked down Regents Street. St James's Street round the park &amp; there to Richmond's. Walked again up Regents Street &amp; dined with Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1398,"lock":null}
14:36:39.179 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/16/1452
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1452,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the north. Wrote to Lord Beverley requesting him to present one to His Majesty at the Levee on Wednesday next &amp; left the letter at his house. Thence walked down Regents Street. St James's Street round the park &amp; there to Richmond's. Walked again up Regents Street &amp; dined with Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1398,"lock":null}
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/17/1453
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1453,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another delightful autumnal morning. Wind north. Received a note from H Harry to say they called upon me this morning. A little after 1 o'clock, he, Miss G Hurry &amp; Miss Fenwick called &amp; we drove to the Zoological Gardens. Afterwards to the Coliseum with which we were much delighted &amp; astonished &amp; most particularly with the Swiss Cottage &amp; arcade. Thence we drove to Walworth &amp; I dined with them. Walked home in the evening where I found a note from Lord Beverley saying he will have much pleasure in presenting me to His Majesty on Wednesday next.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1399,"lock":null}
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/17/1453
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1453,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another delightful autumnal morning. Wind north. Received a note from H Harry to say they called upon me this morning. A little after 1 o'clock, he, Miss G Hurry &amp; Miss Fenwick called &amp; we drove to the Zoological Gardens. Afterwards to the Coliseum with which we were much delighted &amp; astonished &amp; most particularly with the Swiss Cottage &amp; arcade. Thence we drove to Walworth &amp; I dined with them. Walked home in the evening where I found a note from Lord Beverley saying he will have much pleasure in presenting me to His Majesty on Wednesday next.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1399,"lock":null}
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/18/1454
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1454,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Slept in the house all the morning. Richmond called at 3 o'clock &amp; drove me out in his gig. Went round by Highgate &amp; Hampstead &amp; returned by Regent &amp; Hyde Park Home to dinner. Bob marsh also dined with us.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1400,"lock":null}
14:36:39.180 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
