14:36:39.183 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1436,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning. Wind NW but cool. After breakfasting with Mr Lee, got upon the Red Robin coach driven by Pearce at 10 o'clock &amp; started for Town where we arrived at &frac14; before 7 o'clock travelling a new &amp; by far the more beautiful road, over the Hog Back. Here we had a drenching shower of rain &amp; hail, through Guilford to town. Got to Nottingham Place at 7 o'clock. Had a cup of tea &amp; went to bed at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1382,"lock":null}
14:36:39.183 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/20/1457
14:36:39.183 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
14:36:39.183 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
