14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/21/1458
14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/21/1458
14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/21/1459
14:36:39.184 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1459,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... decorated with all their orders, it was a very splendid &amp; magnificent sight. I thought I should have been very nervous, but was not at all so. I was nominally presented by the Earl of Beverley, but in fact by the Lord in waiting who was I believe was Lord ____  <font color=#BFBFBF>Earl of Gosford</font>   I had the honour of kissing the Kings hand. Lord Beverley found me out in the ante room &amp; was particularly polite &amp; attentive. After leaving the Levee, WBS &amp; Bob Marsh were waiting for me &amp; we walked along Pall Mall &amp; I got a coach &amp; drove home where I exchanged my dress &amp; returned to Richmond where I dined</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1405,"lock":null}
