14:36:39.186 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1462,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":22,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. After breakfast WBS &amp; I went into the city &amp; at 11 o'clock embarked on board the Brocklebank steamer with an immense crowd of people &amp; preceded to Woolwich to see the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Thunderer 74 a round ship launched. An immense concourse of people present. The King &amp; Queen arrived about 2 o'clock &amp; soon afterwards the Thunderer slid into the river in most beautiful style, the best launch I ever saw. Afterwards it was a grand &amp; imposing sight. Returned to town &amp; dined at the Blue Ports at 6 o'clock</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1408,"lock":null}
14:36:39.186 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/23/1463
14:36:39.186 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1463,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<style>\r\n#t01_18310923 {\r\n  border-collapse: collapse;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(3) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(4) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(5) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#c01_18310923 {\r\n  border-top: 1px solid black; \r\n  border-bottom: 1px solid black;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by S. After breakfast walked into the city. At the office, received a letter from Bess B &amp; one from Rob Stephenson by mistake, instead of Stephenson, Wyburn bill enclosing the merchant's bill and notes for the freight.</p>\r\n<table id=\"t01_18310923\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"width:50px\">viz.</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:400px\">A country Bank note cash</br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;Pbls at Musluman</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&pound;10</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:15px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Little & Co on Smith Payne etc</td>\r\n    <td>12</td>\r\n    <td>18</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>S J Wright on Wheatley & Riots at due</td>\r\n    <td>21</td>\r\n    <td>13</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>J Kin Ward & Co on Glyman</td>\r\n    <td>35</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Bill Garbalt to JRS on Wades 2nd half payment</td>\r\n    <td>199</td>\r\n    <td>10</td>\r\n    <td>9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >279</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >1</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Kitchenmein</span> for repairing fishing rods &pound;1.0.6.</p>\r\n<p>Met H Harry &amp; walked with him down to the Catherine docks to see Hy Nicholson who we found on board &amp; had a lunch with him. His ship out <span class=highlight_yellow>exupting</span> lathwood. He expects to get away about Wednesday &amp; offered me a passage which I think I shall accept. Saw Messrs Harrison &amp; explained Rolt's mistake in sending the freight bill instead of the Wyburn bill. Wrote to Bess. Walked back to Nottingham Place to dinner. Met WBS &amp; Bob Marsh in Regent Street. The latter dined with us.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1409,"lock":null}
14:36:39.186 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/23/1463
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1463,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<style>\r\n#t01_18310923 {\r\n  border-collapse: collapse;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(3) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(4) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#t01_18310923 td:nth-child(5) {\r\n  text-align: right;\r\n}\r\n#c01_18310923 {\r\n  border-top: 1px solid black; \r\n  border-bottom: 1px solid black;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about W by S. After breakfast walked into the city. At the office, received a letter from Bess B &amp; one from Rob Stephenson by mistake, instead of Stephenson, Wyburn bill enclosing the merchant's bill and notes for the freight.</p>\r\n<table id=\"t01_18310923\">\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"width:50px\">viz.</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:400px\">A country Bank note cash</br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;Pbls at Musluman</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&pound;10</br>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:20px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td style=\"width:15px\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Little & Co on Smith Payne etc</td>\r\n    <td>12</td>\r\n    <td>18</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>S J Wright on Wheatley & Riots at due</td>\r\n    <td>21</td>\r\n    <td>13</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>J Kin Ward & Co on Glyman</td>\r\n    <td>35</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>Bill Garbalt to JRS on Wades 2nd half payment</td>\r\n    <td>199</td>\r\n    <td>10</td>\r\n    <td>9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >279</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >1</td>\r\n    <td id=\"c01_18310923\" >9</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Kitchenmein</span> for repairing fishing rods &pound;1.0.6.</p>\r\n<p>Met H Harry &amp; walked with him down to the Catherine docks to see Hy Nicholson who we found on board &amp; had a lunch with him. His ship out <span class=highlight_yellow>exupting</span> lathwood. He expects to get away about Wednesday &amp; offered me a passage which I think I shall accept. Saw Messrs Harrison &amp; explained Rolt's mistake in sending the freight bill instead of the Wyburn bill. Wrote to Bess. Walked back to Nottingham Place to dinner. Met WBS &amp; Bob Marsh in Regent Street. The latter dined with us.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1409,"lock":null}
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/24/1464
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1464,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind WSW. H<sup>y</sup> Harry called upon me about 12 o'clock. After lunch we went to the Baker Street Bazaar to look for a gig for Sadler, but did not purchase. Got into a cab in Oxford Street &amp; drove to the Pantechnicon  in Belgrave square, a very splendid large building lately erected for the sale of Carriages etc. etc. An immense number of vehicles of all sorts. One of which a new dennilt we brought for Sadler for &pound;30, a very cheap bargain all that it will want will be two or three coats of varnish in a few months. Returned to Nottingham Place to dinner. H Harry left us a little after 8 o'clock in an omnibus.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>I took suddenly unwell &amp; at bed time took a couple of camomile pills.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1410,"lock":null}
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/24/1464
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1464,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind WSW. H<sup>y</sup> Harry called upon me about 12 o'clock. After lunch we went to the Baker Street Bazaar to look for a gig for Sadler, but did not purchase. Got into a cab in Oxford Street &amp; drove to the Pantechnicon  in Belgrave square, a very splendid large building lately erected for the sale of Carriages etc. etc. An immense number of vehicles of all sorts. One of which a new dennilt we brought for Sadler for &pound;30, a very cheap bargain all that it will want will be two or three coats of varnish in a few months. Returned to Nottingham Place to dinner. H Harry left us a little after 8 o'clock in an omnibus.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>I took suddenly unwell &amp; at bed time took a couple of camomile pills.</p>","pageId":946,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1410,"lock":null}
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/25/1465
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1465,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of beautiful weather. Wind SW. Swallowed a black draught before breakfast which, with the pills, have had the desired effect.</p>\r\n<p>Did not move out until near 3 o'clock. Then took a walk to the Zoological Gardens &amp; thence to Hyde Park &amp; home to dinner, where I found Richmond had come to feed with us</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1411,"lock":null}
14:36:39.187 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
