14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1465,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of beautiful weather. Wind SW. Swallowed a black draught before breakfast which, with the pills, have had the desired effect.</p>\r\n<p>Did not move out until near 3 o'clock. Then took a walk to the Zoological Gardens &amp; thence to Hyde Park &amp; home to dinner, where I found Richmond had come to feed with us</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1411,"lock":null}
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/26/1466
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1466,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been a little rain. Wind difficult to make out, appears to have got from the east. Took an omnibus <span class=highlight_yellow>to</span> the city. Called at the office. The Hope sailed from Shields on Friday. Walked down to Whitechapel to Stirling's the chemists for a bottle of the essence of cubebs. Thence to the St Catherine docks &amp; dined with H Nicholson on board the Crises, H<font color=#BFBFBF>enr</font><sup>y</sup><sup> </sup>&amp; Sam Hurry there. Left the docks at 6 o'clock &amp; walked to Nottingham Place.</p>\r\n<p>WBS received  letter from Colonel <span class=highlight_yellow>Farwole</span></p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1412,"lock":null}
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/26/1466
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1466,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning having been a little rain. Wind difficult to make out, appears to have got from the east. Took an omnibus <span class=highlight_yellow>to</span> the city. Called at the office. The Hope sailed from Shields on Friday. Walked down to Whitechapel to Stirling's the chemists for a bottle of the essence of cubebs. Thence to the St Catherine docks &amp; dined with H Nicholson on board the Crises, H<font color=#BFBFBF>enr</font><sup>y</sup><sup> </sup>&amp; Sam Hurry there. Left the docks at 6 o'clock &amp; walked to Nottingham Place.</p>\r\n<p>WBS received  letter from Colonel <span class=highlight_yellow>Farwole</span></p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1412,"lock":null}
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/27/1467
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1467,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind SE. Did not go out till late. Walked down by Regents Street &amp; called at Richmond's, thence to the Temple &amp; left my card at <span class=highlight_yellow>wwards</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>chainpers</span>,. Returned to Regent Street at 6 o'clock with Richmond. G Taylor, Bob Marsh, WBS &amp; self there</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1413,"lock":null}
14:36:39.188 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/27/1467
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1467,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind SE. Did not go out till late. Walked down by Regents Street &amp; called at Richmond's, thence to the Temple &amp; left my card at <span class=highlight_yellow>wwards</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>chainpers</span>,. Returned to Regent Street at 6 o'clock with Richmond. G Taylor, Bob Marsh, WBS &amp; self there</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1413,"lock":null}
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/28/1468
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1468,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been some rain this morning. Rather dull &amp; excessively close &amp; sultry. Wind for the ESE. Took an omnibus into the city. Called at the office. Accepted Stephenson's Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>berg bill for &pound;44.5/- due 8 Nov payable with WBS &amp; left it at Messrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Halmgons</span>. Went down to the St Catherine dock &amp; dined on board the Crisis. Tea at <span class=highlight_yellow>Lodlins</span>. A heavy fall of rain with lightning at night.</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1414,"lock":null}
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/28/1468
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1468,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been some rain this morning. Rather dull &amp; excessively close &amp; sultry. Wind for the ESE. Took an omnibus into the city. Called at the office. Accepted Stephenson's Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>berg bill for &pound;44.5/- due 8 Nov payable with WBS &amp; left it at Messrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Halmgons</span>. Went down to the St Catherine dock &amp; dined on board the Crisis. Tea at <span class=highlight_yellow>Lodlins</span>. A heavy fall of rain with lightning at night.</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1414,"lock":null}
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/29/1469
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1469,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; cooler weather after heavy rain last night. Wind SE. Sat in the house until after 1 o'clock. Called &amp; had a lunch at Miles Forsters offices in Wimpole Street &amp; sat some time with him. Walked in Regent Street till dinner time. Richmond dined with us</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1415,"lock":null}
14:36:39.189 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/29/1469
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1469,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; cooler weather after heavy rain last night. Wind SE. Sat in the house until after 1 o'clock. Called &amp; had a lunch at Miles Forsters offices in Wimpole Street &amp; sat some time with him. Walked in Regent Street till dinner time. Richmond dined with us</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1415,"lock":null}
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/3/1437
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1437,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Walked into the city by Regents Street called at Oliphant's &amp; got a new hat. Passed along the Strand &amp; returned from the city &amp; dined with C Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1383,"lock":null}
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/3/1437
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1437,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Walked into the city by Regents Street called at Oliphant's &amp; got a new hat. Passed along the Strand &amp; returned from the city &amp; dined with C Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1383,"lock":null}
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/30/1470
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1470,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning dull &amp; thick, afterwards cleared away &amp; turned out a fine day. Wind SSE. Got all my luggage into a Hackney coach &amp; down to Philpot lane (there saw Stephenson, the Hope being at Greenwich <del>got up to stone stairs</del>) down on St Catherine dock &amp; the Crises having got out, I <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> &amp; left all my luggage at Lodlings. Walked up again to Phillpotts Lane, accompanied WBS to Guildhall and having got a Beef Steak at Jewps on WBS, Lee &amp; I walked down to Mr Carr's &amp; drank tea. Called at Codlings &amp; saw H Nicholson who had got the ship down to Duke Shore &amp; expecting to get away in the morning. I determined to accept Mr Carr's offer of a bed. Set WBS part of the way up the Commercial Road. Returned with Nicholson to Lodlings &amp; got to Mr Carr's a little after 10 o'clock. Rained very heavy with a great deal of lightning. Part of the Hope sold today.</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1416,"lock":null}
14:36:39.190 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
