14:36:39.192 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1439,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Breakfasted with C Richmond. He drove me in the afternoon around &amp; called upon Mrs Fletcher alias Hoffman then through the park by Pimlico &amp; Westminster to Greenwich. Called &amp; saw Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> Watt and his wife, dined off whitebait etc. at the Crown &amp; Sceptre &amp; returned to town at 7 o'clock to tea. Got home in good time</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1385,"lock":null}
14:36:39.192 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/5/1440
14:36:39.192 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1440,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW &amp; warm. Took the Paddington Stage into the city. Went to the office, nothing there, at the Coal Exchange. Saw there Brown &amp; Fenwick. Walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh, strolled round by Pall Mall, St James's Street &amp; Piccadilly to Richmond's to dinner.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Got to Nottingham place at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; found WBS Mary &amp; Lee had arrived.</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1386,"lock":null}
14:36:39.192 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/5/1440
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1440,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW &amp; warm. Took the Paddington Stage into the city. Went to the office, nothing there, at the Coal Exchange. Saw there Brown &amp; Fenwick. Walked out of the city. Called upon Bob Marsh, strolled round by Pall Mall, St James's Street &amp; Piccadilly to Richmond's to dinner.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Got to Nottingham place at &frac12; past 10 o'clock &amp; found WBS Mary &amp; Lee had arrived.</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1386,"lock":null}
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/6/1441
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1441,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather close. WBS went out the city. Arrived myself in the West End of the town all the morning. Dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Junior Wright at Blackfriars, a small party <span class=highlight_yellow>there. </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Crg</span> Richmond, G Walters, Mr Gordon, G Kain &amp; two Miss Jobling's of Austlery</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1387,"lock":null}
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/6/1441
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1441,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather close. WBS went out the city. Arrived myself in the West End of the town all the morning. Dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Junior Wright at Blackfriars, a small party <span class=highlight_yellow>there. </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Crg</span> Richmond, G Walters, Mr Gordon, G Kain &amp; two Miss Jobling's of Austlery</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1387,"lock":null}
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/7/1442
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1442,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull unpleasant morning. Heavy showers all day. Wind SW. Took a walk &amp; called upon Mr Lenskill &amp; Mr Ward. Met Captain Shepherd in the Burley Tea Arcade who has got appointed to the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Melville 74 &amp; going out to the East Indies with <font color=#BFBFBF>admiral </font>Sir J<font color=#BFBFBF>ohn</font> Gore. Dined with Richmond at 6 o'clock to meet Mr &amp; Mrs Hoffman alias Mary Fletcher, his sister &amp; J Wrights</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1388,"lock":null}
14:36:39.193 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
