14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1442,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull unpleasant morning. Heavy showers all day. Wind SW. Took a walk &amp; called upon Mr Lenskill &amp; Mr Ward. Met Captain Shepherd in the Burley Tea Arcade who has got appointed to the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Melville 74 &amp; going out to the East Indies with <font color=#BFBFBF>admiral </font>Sir J<font color=#BFBFBF>ohn</font> Gore. Dined with Richmond at 6 o'clock to meet Mr &amp; Mrs Hoffman alias Mary Fletcher, his sister &amp; J Wrights</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1388,"lock":null}
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1443
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1443,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation_of_William_IV_and_Adelaide\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2799-coronation-william-4th.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Coronation of William IV</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":939,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1389,"lock":null}
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1443
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1443,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation_of_William_IV_and_Adelaide\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2799-coronation-william-4th.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Coronation of William IV</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":939,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1389,"lock":null}
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1444
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1444,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. The town all alive &amp; on the move towards Charring Cross, Pall Mall etc. to see Coronation Procession. After breakfast I went out but could not see the procession, so great was the crowd.  It appearing however to be near the United Services Club House after it had passed I saw major Falls who asked me in &amp; upon I had a very fine view of the whole of it on its return. A most splendid &amp; magnificent sight it was. Saw there Majesties very distinctly. Unfortunately there was a great deal of rain which they were in the Abbey which made the streets very dirty &amp; dampt the pleasure of the people no doubt very much. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; in the evening saw the illuminations which passed good</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1390,"lock":null}
14:36:39.194 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.195 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/8/1444
14:36:39.195 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1444,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. The town all alive &amp; on the move towards Charring Cross, Pall Mall etc. to see Coronation Procession. After breakfast I went out but could not see the procession, so great was the crowd.  It appearing however to be near the United Services Club House after it had passed I saw major Falls who asked me in &amp; upon I had a very fine view of the whole of it on its return. A most splendid &amp; magnificent sight it was. Saw there Majesties very distinctly. Unfortunately there was a great deal of rain which they were in the Abbey which made the streets very dirty &amp; dampt the pleasure of the people no doubt very much. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; in the evening saw the illuminations which passed good</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1390,"lock":null}
14:36:39.195 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/9/1445
14:36:39.195 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1445,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant day. Rained incessantly. Wind NW. Did not go out until 2 o'clock. Called upon Beverley who was not at home. Left my card. Walked down to Bob Marsh and Richmond's. Got a letter from Stephenson who will not be cleared so soon as expected. Answered it &amp; told him I should not be at Hull &amp; of my intention to leave town on Tuesday by the city of Edinburgh steamer. Called at Hawtry the dentists &amp; got my teeth cleaned. Dined at 6 o'clock at Nottingham Place. Richmond &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1391,"lock":null}
14:36:39.195 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:39.195 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/dates/1831/9/9/1445
14:36:39.195 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1445,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant day. Rained incessantly. Wind NW. Did not go out until 2 o'clock. Called upon Beverley who was not at home. Left my card. Walked down to Bob Marsh and Richmond's. Got a letter from Stephenson who will not be cleared so soon as expected. Answered it &amp; told him I should not be at Hull &amp; of my intention to leave town on Tuesday by the city of Edinburgh steamer. Called at Hawtry the dentists &amp; got my teeth cleaned. Dined at 6 o'clock at Nottingham Place. Richmond &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1391,"lock":null}
