14:36:39.209 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1569,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":1,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Engaged to dine with Charlton at Billy Mill at 2 o'clock. Thick foggy morning &amp; frosty. Wind WSW. Did not go to Charlton being unwell. Received from Eligible Club &pound;____ in notes at 2 months date 30 December which with Hurry &amp; Co's bill of &pound;59.9 making &pound;228.5/- I paid into Chapmans. Dined at home. <span class=highlight_yellow>Rec</span><font color=#BFBFBF><span class=highlight_yellow>eived</span></font> an <span class=highlight_yellow>Brt</span> Andersons acceptance at 2 months from 4. I am on account of average for &pound;50. I am on account of average for &pound;50</p>\r\n<p>With Bess in the evening</p>","pageId":981,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1513,"lock":null}
14:36:39.209 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1832/1/5/1570
14:36:39.209 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1570,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":1,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A hard frost &amp; foggy. Wind SSW but I should think from the e<font color=#BFBFBF>ast</font> of sea. Wrote to Mr Anderson acknowledging the receipt of the &pound;50 bill</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the evening attended the whist club, With Bess at night who had submitted to be examined by Dr Horsley who pronounced her quite well &amp; therefore I must be free from disease</p>","pageId":981,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1514,"lock":null}
