14:36:39.478 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2049,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy damp morning. Wind ESE. Mr Thompson of South Shields &amp; another examined the Hope. Dined with C Charlton at the Northumberland Alms. At H Hurry in the evening. He has got a slight attack of gout. Met Bess</p>","pageId":1077,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1990,"lock":null}
14:36:39.478 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/dates/1834/5/20/2068
14:36:39.478 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2068,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":5,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind W by N. Received a letter from Mr Watson offering me &pound;1005. Called upon him &amp; agreed to take it. R Ilderton &amp; yound Fenwick came down &amp; dined with me &amp; afterwards went to South Shields races which were pretty good. Finished at the Albion</p>","pageId":1079,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2008,"lock":null}
