14:36:40.870 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1000,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WNW Captain Webb &amp; I with the boys went on a boat down to the rocks to fish but had no sport. Whilst there a part of the cliff gave way &amp; falling upon a poor girl who happened to be sitting underneath completely buried. She was soon dug out but dreadfully crushed &amp; quite dead. Her sister was close to her &amp; saw the accident. Returned home &amp; had some dinner at 5 o'clock. Spent the latter part of the evening at H Harry's</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":951,"lock":null}
14:36:40.870 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1001
14:36:40.870 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1001,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather dull. Wind SSW &amp; blowing hard. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Again in the evening walked with Mark to Tynemouth. Heard this evening of Leddill having resigned! Consequently there is no possibility of a contest for the county</p>","pageId":833,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":952,"lock":null}
14:36:40.870 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
