14:36:40.871 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1003,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning But again blowing hard at WSW It large concussion of people with A professional gentleman with <span class=highlight_yellow>Baudr</span>, flags to went to Chester Whence they met the Bale &amp; brought him through the upper part of town to the George Tavern after which low sat down to an excellent &amp; well arranged discussion nearly 200 freehold all went off well. The latter part of the evening a glorious scene of drunk cuffs and confusion amongst the lower set of freeholders.</p>","pageId":834,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":954,"lock":null}
14:36:40.871 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1004
14:36:40.871 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1004,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Wind SW. Walked to Tynemouth Had a little rain. In the afternoon Henry Mark Nicklinson had a little Wiskey todd at Koddams. Walked to Tynemouth again in the evening and finished off at the Duke of York (paid the <span class=highlight_yellow>su</span><span class=highlight_yellow>shious</span> wives the amount of &pound;16-10)</p>","pageId":834,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":955,"lock":null}
