14:36:40.872 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1006,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, wind W by S and WNW. Walked  to Tynemouth and shuffled home to <span class=highlight_yellow>denby</span> for M W Kedley cause afraid N  South Shields Then took <span class=highlight_yellow>Wenes</span> walk at Nicklinson at the <span class=highlight_yellow>G</span><span class=highlight_yellow>eor</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ge</span></p>","pageId":834,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":957,"lock":null}
14:36:40.872 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1007
14:36:40.872 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1007,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; blowing fresh ay WSW. Took a walk to Dr Drurgs garden where we played at quoits. An immense number of people went out to Chistow to meet Mr Hodgson where they took the horses out of the carriage &amp; drew him into town in procession to the George tavern where he  addressed the people in a short speech. I afterwards dined with him. We sat down about 85 to dinner  &amp; spent a very pleasant evening. Mr Ildeston slept at our house</p>","pageId":835,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":958,"lock":null}
14:36:40.872 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.873 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1007
14:36:40.873 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1007,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; blowing fresh ay WSW. Took a walk to Dr Drurgs garden where we played at quoits. An immense number of people went out to Chistow to meet Mr Hodgson where they took the horses out of the carriage &amp; drew him into town in procession to the George tavern where he  addressed the people in a short speech. I afterwards dined with him. We sat down about 85 to dinner  &amp; spent a very pleasant evening. Mr Ildeston slept at our house</p>","pageId":835,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":958,"lock":null}
14:36:40.873 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1008
14:36:40.873 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1008,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Wind NNW &amp; NW. A most beautiful Day. Breakfasted at the George with Rec Hodgson who afterwards with his friends set off for Blyth where they were to decide with the Premium.  At &frac12; past 1 o'clock, Harry, Drury &amp; I took a boat &amp; rowed up to Sadless to dinner. I Dale also there. We spent a very pleasant day it being his birthday. Took a glass of wine &amp; water with Dale on our return. Received a letter from Fanny Soneth informing us of Emma being rather unwell &amp; requesting if I would allow to stay with them a little longer, which I agreed to.</p>","pageId":835,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":959,"lock":null}
14:36:40.873 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
