14:36:40.896 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":105,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair day, but very cold &amp; blowing strong from SSE &amp; the dust very unpleasant. Took an early dinner &amp; attended the races, better sport but not many people. Took tea at Tibbs</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":100,"lock":null}
14:36:40.896 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1050
14:36:40.896 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1050,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning having been a deluge of rain in the night &amp; blowing hard from NE. Wind changed to NW &amp; nearly calm. After breakfast turned out a very fair day. Emma came from school. WBS went to Newcastle to see D Dixon. Moor &amp; his brother called, after a great deal of conversation, agreed to let him continue on the farm should he exert himself to pay off the arrears. His brother promised his <span class=highlight_yellow>abstinence</span> &amp; to continue his security. Emma &amp; I walked round by the wells to Tynemouth. Dined at home at 5 o'clock. At the Duke in the evening.</p>","pageId":845,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":998,"lock":null}
