14:36:40.898 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1053,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. William &amp; I took our guns &amp; walked with Mrs Tealey &amp; his wife.  Robersons to Marsden where the committee for the preservation for ship wrecks met &amp; tried several experiments. We afterwards returned by steam to Shields. H Harry dined with us at the Mulstrum at night</p>","pageId":845,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1001,"lock":null}
