14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1066
14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1066,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. Got up early &amp; went by steam to Newcastle. Fixed the Hope with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hindhaegh</span> at 10/3 freight. Got home to dinner. Took wine at the George with French &amp; Harry. Drank tea at H Harry's &amp; in the evening at the Duke.</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1014,"lock":null}
14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1066
14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1066,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. Got up early &amp; went by steam to Newcastle. Fixed the Hope with <span class=highlight_yellow>Hindhaegh</span> at 10/3 freight. Got home to dinner. Took wine at the George with French &amp; Harry. Drank tea at H Harry's &amp; in the evening at the Duke.</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1014,"lock":null}
14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1067
14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1067,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been rain in the night &amp; has the appearance of more wind SW. Went up to the ship. Walked to Tynemouth. Ordered a new square mainsail. Got the canvas of Bradshaw &amp; to be made by Mrs Brown Polly of Wallsend. J Carr, H Harry &amp; French dined with me. Spent a very pleasant day. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1015,"lock":null}
14:36:40.904 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1067
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1067,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been rain in the night &amp; has the appearance of more wind SW. Went up to the ship. Walked to Tynemouth. Ordered a new square mainsail. Got the canvas of Bradshaw &amp; to be made by Mrs Brown Polly of Wallsend. J Carr, H Harry &amp; French dined with me. Spent a very pleasant day. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":848,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1015,"lock":null}
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1068
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1068,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Walked up to the Hope alongside <span class=highlight_yellow>gran</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span> getting ballast out. Got her down up the shore at Metcalf dock to sink her to find out the peak. Walked to Tynemouth, saw Potts, who returned with me to Shields. He, Harry, French &amp; I  went to the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1016,"lock":null}
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1068
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1068,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Walked up to the Hope alongside <span class=highlight_yellow>gran</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span> getting ballast out. Got her down up the shore at Metcalf dock to sink her to find out the peak. Walked to Tynemouth, saw Potts, who returned with me to Shields. He, Harry, French &amp; I  went to the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1016,"lock":null}
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1069
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1069,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. A fresh breeze from the West. The Hope upon the shore having been sank did not find any bad places of consequence. The buts ends bolts been in a great many places corroded &amp; heavily worn was the principal cause of her making so much water. Employed getting new bolts put in &amp; the buts ends caulked. Dined at Home. Spent the afternoon at Dr Drury's garden playing at quoits &amp; the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1017,"lock":null}
14:36:40.905 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
