14:36:40.907 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1071,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind NW. Onboard the Hope. Got two keels of <span class=highlight_yellow>wqlaure</span> down. Pain G Slop &pound;3.11.3 wages up to today. Dined at home. H Henry &amp; I on board the Hope to taste some brandy. In the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1019,"lock":null}
14:36:40.907 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1072
14:36:40.907 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1072,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with a little rain. Wind SW, increased in the afternoon to a gale. Attended morning service. The vicar did duty &amp; preached. Dined at home. Took wine with H Harry &amp; tea in the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":849,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1020,"lock":null}
