14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1092,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine morning. Wind WNW. Walked to the new quay &amp; round by Preston Lane. Dined at 3  o'clock with H Harry Miss R Fenwick, Metcalf &amp; Drury there. Spent a pleasant day. Got &pound;5 of Chapman</p>","pageId":853,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1040,"lock":null}
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1093
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1093,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull foggy morning Wind WNW but little of it. Received a letter from WBS. The Hope was out on Friday &amp; going to the chalk wharfs. Went to church. The vicar's brother preached. Gave a most excellent sermon for the benefit of the inadequate society. He a beautiful preacher</p>","pageId":853,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1041,"lock":null}
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1093
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1093,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull foggy morning Wind WNW but little of it. Received a letter from WBS. The Hope was out on Friday &amp; going to the chalk wharfs. Went to church. The vicar's brother preached. Gave a most excellent sermon for the benefit of the inadequate society. He a beautiful preacher</p>","pageId":853,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1041,"lock":null}
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1094
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1094,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind little at SE. Got up early &amp; walked round by Tynemouth &amp; Cullercoats, called upon Mr Hewetson &amp; returned to breakfast. Received a letter from WBS with the Hopes coal freight account enclosing Metcalfrs &amp; Drury's note for &pound;79.18.2 Which I paid into chapmans. Took another long walk with H Harry &amp; Peart round by the head of the town, Burdon Main, height Charton, Belly Hill &amp; Preston &amp; got home to dinner. Spent the latter part of the evening at Alderneys.</p>","pageId":854,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1042,"lock":null}
14:36:40.919 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
