14:36:40.920 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1094,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":10,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning Wind little at SE. Got up early &amp; walked round by Tynemouth &amp; Cullercoats, called upon Mr Hewetson &amp; returned to breakfast. Received a letter from WBS with the Hopes coal freight account enclosing Metcalfrs &amp; Drury's note for &pound;79.18.2 Which I paid into chapmans. Took another long walk with H Harry &amp; Peart round by the head of the town, Burdon Main, height Charton, Belly Hill &amp; Preston &amp; got home to dinner. Spent the latter part of the evening at Alderneys.</p>","pageId":854,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1042,"lock":null}
