14:36:40.932 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1119,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Wind SW. Been a little rain in the night. Walked as far as Vrilly Mill &amp; saw Pott's harriers. Returned home to dinner In the afternoon on board the Crises with A Nicholson &amp; Webb. Afterwards at the fair &amp; Malstrum Turned out a very wet evening</p>","pageId":860,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1067,"lock":null}
14:36:40.932 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.932 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1119
14:36:40.932 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1119,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning Wind SW. Been a little rain in the night. Walked as far as Vrilly Mill &amp; saw Pott's harriers. Returned home to dinner In the afternoon on board the Crises with A Nicholson &amp; Webb. Afterwards at the fair &amp; Malstrum Turned out a very wet evening</p>","pageId":860,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1067,"lock":null}
14:36:40.932 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/112
14:36:40.932 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":112,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Much annoyed at finding I should not get to Liverpool in time to catch the Post Office packit for Dublin. Deceived by the people at the coach office. Left Leeds by coach at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Outside a cloudy morning, soon began to rain &amp; continued very heavy all day. Reached Huddersfield at 10 o'clock. I think where I had to wait an hour &amp; change coach. Got to Manchester at 1 o'clock &amp; found to my surprise &amp; vexation the coach would not proceed until 5 o'clock. Kicked up a row at the office, got part of any money returned &amp; fortunately caught a coach about to start for Liverpool where I arrived at 6 o'clock &amp; immediately embarked on board the &quot;Bereuenyham&quot;  steam boat which as luck would have it, was that evening going to start for Dublin. Wind WSW</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":107,"lock":null}
14:36:40.932 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
