14:36:40.937 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1129,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine cold morning Wind WSW. Received a letter from WBS with Hope's archangel account but not <span class=highlight_yellow>reliance</span> the delivered very little more than <span class=highlight_yellow>good</span> deals Paid Robert &amp; Leadbetter their &frac14; year wages &pound;10.11/- draft on chapmans exor account Dined at home. Called on J Young Paid Mrs Wright for E<font color=#BFBFBF>mma</font> Galbraiths education &pound;13.3.9 at the theatre &amp; Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":861,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1077,"lock":null}
14:36:40.937 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/113
14:36:40.937 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":113,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>During the whole of last night we had a heavy sea &amp; foul wind blowing WSW very hard, to contend with but fortunately a fine boat under us. As it was low water when we started, we overtook to steam Office packit at anchor, at the Rock not able to proceed for want of water, having left 2 &frac12;  hours before us so that after all, I lost no time, no thanks to the rascally clerks at the coach office. We kept company all night &amp; after a tedious passage arrived at the custom House quay, Dublin at 3 o'clock PM. Took my luggage to Mackens Hotel, Dawson Street where I stayed all night</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":108,"lock":null}
14:36:40.937 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
