14:36:40.945 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1144,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":11,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The wind still present from ESE but both it &amp; the sea much fallen. Gave <span class=highlight_yellow>g</span><span class=highlight_yellow>esheding</span> a draft on chapmans for &pound;8.6.8 an average Premium Club. Walked up to Coble dean, carpenters busy with wind cap. Got 7 Keels more down, making 14. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; in the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":863,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1092,"lock":null}
14:36:40.945 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1145
14:36:40.945 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1145,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of SE wind but weather more moderate. On board the Hope. Finished her loading of Adairs Main <span class=highlight_yellow>pa</span><span class=highlight_yellow>in us bad </span><span class=highlight_yellow>oneaseere</span> having taken in 17 Keels &amp; still have room for 3 ches more. Dined with Mr Wright on board the Mulgrave Castle &amp; in the evening went to Bill Hill &amp; suppered with <span class=highlight_yellow>Holroid</span>.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to Mr Walker Adams Main for an allowance</p>","pageId":864,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1093,"lock":null}
