14:36:40.953 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1159,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet raw unpleasant morning. Wind W by N. The Hope got to sea in the afternoon without touching the bar, there being a great deal of sea on. Some had accounts of the ships that sailed on Saturday many struck very heavily on the bar &amp; some in consequence the crew not being able to <span class=highlight_yellow>Kup</span> them, foundered &amp; all the people drowned. At least we had an account of one &amp; another having run on shore. Dined at the Albion, a bed dance &amp; a very good one, spent a pleasant day. In visiting Bradshaw &amp; H Harry, chain &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>vi</span><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>c</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span>. 12 percent</p>","pageId":866,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1107,"lock":null}
