14:36:40.957 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1167,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine clear weather but blowing extremely hard at W by N &amp; has been since last evening. The account of the Hope having got to London, she ought to have been there, ship that sailed the day after her having got up. Dined with <span class=highlight_yellow>Warl</span> Wright on board the Merlin. Mrs Stephenson had a letter from her husband at Gravesend. The had very blowing weather. In the evening at the theatre &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1115,"lock":null}
14:36:40.957 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1168
14:36:40.957 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1168,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning, blowing hard from NNW. It must have been &amp; no doubt no is at sea, from NNE. Such a human disaster sea, been upon the bar. Heavy showers of snow. Dined at home At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; in the evening at the whist club</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1116,"lock":null}
