14:36:40.957 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1168,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning, blowing hard from NNW. It must have been &amp; no doubt no is at sea, from NNE. Such a human disaster sea, been upon the bar. Heavy showers of snow. Dined at home At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; in the evening at the whist club</p>","pageId":869,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1116,"lock":null}
14:36:40.957 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1169
14:36:40.957 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1169,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful winter's morning. Most intense frost &amp; NW wind, sea high. Received a letter from WBS of the arrival &amp; sale of 126 chars of the Hope cargo at Wednesday day mackerel  at 34/-. Mr C Wright &amp; Mr L Loyd a <span class=highlight_yellow>dined</span> on board the Lamaracy came &amp; took dinner today. Attended the whist club in the evening at Fenwicks. A most intense frost</p>","pageId":870,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1117,"lock":null}
