14:36:40.958 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1170,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><u>Xmas day</u> After a most intense frost during the night, we have a heavy fall of snow. Wind NW. At the newsroom. Paris in a fearful state of excitement. The most fearing the decision of the peers well be in favour of the later. Herewith to WBS giving him an account of the weather here. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; dined with J Cunningham, family party. Spent a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":870,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1118,"lock":null}
14:36:40.958 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1171
14:36:40.958 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1171,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":12,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frosty weather. A good deal of snow fallen in the night. Wind WNW. Did not go to church. Wrote to B B Galbraith. Received an account these H Harry, A Clark &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Berges</span> of the sale of 84 more than Hope coals at 35/-. Dined with J Tealey. The officers of HMS Samarang &amp; Childers there &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Goshing</span> RA</p>","pageId":870,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1119,"lock":null}
14:36:40.958 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
