14:36:40.968 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":119,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":6.0000,"text":"<p>Left Dublin outside the Carlow coach at 9 o'clock AM. When I arrived at 4 o'clock in a state of anxiety impossible for me to describe, misery was in store for me &amp; on enquiring of the servant &quot;how my sister was?&quot; to my insufferable horror I learned she was dead. The fever was so malignant nature could not struggle with it &amp; and on Sunday last at 10 o'clock I lost one of the kindest &amp; most affectionate of sisters &amp; the town one of the best &amp; most benevolent of human beings. I was doomed not even one last parting look at her cold remains for such was the rapidity with which decomposition took place that her remains were obliged to be deposited in the select tomb next to her dear husband yesterday. However upon ...</p>","pageId":694,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":109,"lock":null}
14:36:40.968 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1190
14:36:40.968 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1190,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant foggy damp morning. A little wind <span class=highlight_yellow>lope at</span> appears to be W.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to WBS giving him a copy of Chapmans <span class=highlight_yellow>book on</span>. In the afternoon at the billiard room. Wrote to Tom Smith &amp; sent him some <span class=highlight_yellow>tripe</span>. Harry, Nicholas, Drury &amp; Cunningham came home with me in the evening &amp; played a rubber.</p>","pageId":876,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1136,"lock":null}
14:36:40.968 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
