14:36:40.971 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1196,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very damp foggy morning. Wind fresh at SE &amp; a good deal of sea. Dined at 5 o'clock with the Gastling RA Tynemouth Place. A very pleasant party. Got home before1 o'clock in the morning. Gave notes to the Premium &amp; Hope clubs of the Hope being loaded. Leadbetter went to Newcastle</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1142,"lock":null}
14:36:40.971 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1197
14:36:40.971 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
14:36:40.971 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1197
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1197,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp &amp; foggy weather. Still continuing with a SE wind. <span class=highlight_yellow>Signed</span> the <span class=highlight_yellow>book</span> for the Hope's <span class=highlight_yellow>cassign</span> of <span class=highlight_yellow>oxd</span>. <span class=highlight_yellow>Redheangh</span> for &pound;153.18.8 date 14<sup>th</sup> Jan at 60 days on WBS. Leadbetter not having returned from Newcastle. Robert &amp; I dined on board the Hope. At the Albion in the evening. Leadbetter got home in the evening.</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1143,"lock":null}
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1198
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1198
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1198,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy &amp; foggy day &amp; blowing strong from SE &amp; high sea. Sent the bill for the Hope's cargo by Dunn the <span class=highlight_yellow>coach</span><span class=highlight_yellow>man</span> to Mr Heindhaigh. Received a letter from Margaret Scott of Crathorn, I having forgot to send her 20/- her quarters allowance. Sent it by return of post. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club in the evening. Drew upon Chapman for &pound;5</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1144,"lock":null}
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1199
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
14:36:40.972 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1199
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1199,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing hard &amp; has been all night from the E by S &amp; ESE with a heavy sea. On board the Hope. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening. Gave Bess a turn, <u>first time</u><span class=underline_double> since</span></p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1145,"lock":null}
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/12
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":12,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at home. Wind &amp; weather the same as yesterday</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":9,"lock":null}
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/12
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":12,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at home. Wind &amp; weather the same as yesterday</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":9,"lock":null}
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/120
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":120,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":7.0000,"text":"<p>... upon reflection, I am resigned and convinced that I have been spared a great deal of painful feeling distress &amp; misery by not having witnessed her suffering &amp; tis a consolation to find that she has had so many kind &amp; attentive friends about her, particularly one Mr Vernon, whose conduct both to my poor sister &amp; myself I shall I trust never forget or be ungrateful for. He insists upon my staying at his house &amp; his great anxiety id to console &amp; make me comfortable. Poor little Emma has fortunately been at Captain Butlins at Broomville &amp; the boys at school. Poor children, they are too young to be sensible of the irreparable loss they have sustained. But I trust that god the father of all will spare &amp; enable me to supply the place of their dear parents they have lost. John J Baker came up to see me in the evening</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":110,"lock":null}
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/120
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":120,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":17,"sequence":7.0000,"text":"<p>... upon reflection, I am resigned and convinced that I have been spared a great deal of painful feeling distress &amp; misery by not having witnessed her suffering &amp; tis a consolation to find that she has had so many kind &amp; attentive friends about her, particularly one Mr Vernon, whose conduct both to my poor sister &amp; myself I shall I trust never forget or be ungrateful for. He insists upon my staying at his house &amp; his great anxiety id to console &amp; make me comfortable. Poor little Emma has fortunately been at Captain Butlins at Broomville &amp; the boys at school. Poor children, they are too young to be sensible of the irreparable loss they have sustained. But I trust that god the father of all will spare &amp; enable me to supply the place of their dear parents they have lost. John J Baker came up to see me in the evening</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":110,"lock":null}
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1200
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1200,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain this morning. Wind about East with a heavy sea. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle. Dined &amp; stayed all night at D Dixons. Mentioned to him my having applied to the Duke for a commission in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> militia of which he approved</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1146,"lock":null}
14:36:40.973 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1200
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1200,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A deluge of rain this morning. Wind about East with a heavy sea. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle. Dined &amp; stayed all night at D Dixons. Mentioned to him my having applied to the Duke for a commission in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> militia of which he approved</p>","pageId":878,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1146,"lock":null}
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1201
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1201,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. For the first time for many days we have seen the sun. Wind ENE &amp; cold with showers. Left Dixon's after breakfast took the steam boat &amp; returned to Shields to dinner. Emma Galbraith looking much better. No letter from WBS, disappointed. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1147,"lock":null}
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1201
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1201,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. For the first time for many days we have seen the sun. Wind ENE &amp; cold with showers. Left Dixon's after breakfast took the steam boat &amp; returned to Shields to dinner. Emma Galbraith looking much better. No letter from WBS, disappointed. At the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1147,"lock":null}
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1202
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1202,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been a slight frost with a little snow during the night. Wind NW. Sea much fallen, so that I think many ships will get to sea.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with copies of letters written to the Duke &amp; Lord Beverley applying for a commission for me in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> Militia. Answered his letter.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Bevor's</span> brother to come down to Shields to make some arrangements with regard to the <span class=highlight_yellow>fasern</span> after seeing J Tinley upon the subject.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with H Harry.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1148,"lock":null}
14:36:40.974 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1202
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1202,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Been a slight frost with a little snow during the night. Wind NW. Sea much fallen, so that I think many ships will get to sea.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from WBS with copies of letters written to the Duke &amp; Lord Beverley applying for a commission for me in the North<font color=#BFBFBF>umbria</font> Militia. Answered his letter.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to <span class=highlight_yellow>Bevor's</span> brother to come down to Shields to make some arrangements with regard to the <span class=highlight_yellow>fasern</span> after seeing J Tinley upon the subject.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Spent the evening &amp; suppered with H Harry.</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1148,"lock":null}
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1203
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1203,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine wintery morning having been a very heavy fall of snow during the night. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from B B Galbraith. A bill for &pound;6.0.10 drawn by <span class=highlight_yellow>Stodter</span> of the Eligible club presented for payment, but I did not take it up having no notice. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Dale &amp; in the evening attended the ball at the George which was the best we have had for a long time. Got home at &frac14; past 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1149,"lock":null}
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1203
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1203,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine wintery morning having been a very heavy fall of snow during the night. Wind WNW.</p>\r\n<p>Received a letter from B B Galbraith. A bill for &pound;6.0.10 drawn by <span class=highlight_yellow>Stodter</span> of the Eligible club presented for payment, but I did not take it up having no notice. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Dale &amp; in the evening attended the ball at the George which was the best we have had for a long time. Got home at &frac14; past 3 o'clock</p>","pageId":879,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1149,"lock":null}
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1204
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1204,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of sharp frost. Wind NNW. Very little additional snow fallen in the night. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle, there being a meeting of the <span class=highlight_yellow>leiabenantcy</span> &amp; saw Dixon who promised to speak to Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlson</span> respecting a commission for me in the military. <span class=highlight_yellow>Had</span> some dinner with Emma Galbraith &amp; returned by Duna in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>Eat a couple of mutton chops at 6 o'clock &amp; finished in the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1150,"lock":null}
14:36:40.975 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1204
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1204,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of sharp frost. Wind NNW. Very little additional snow fallen in the night. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle, there being a meeting of the <span class=highlight_yellow>leiabenantcy</span> &amp; saw Dixon who promised to speak to Captain <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlson</span> respecting a commission for me in the military. <span class=highlight_yellow>Had</span> some dinner with Emma Galbraith &amp; returned by Duna in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>Eat a couple of mutton chops at 6 o'clock &amp; finished in the evening at the Albion</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1150,"lock":null}
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1205
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1205,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; every appearance of snow or sleet &amp; looking as if it would thaw. Wind about west. The ship preparing for sea. Received a note from D Dixon stating he had seen Colonel Coulson &amp; that there are several commissions vacant &amp; I must apply through Colonel Coulson.</p>\r\n<p>Accepted a bill for &pound;8.17 the <span class=highlight_yellow>prccuccia</span> for the present voyage: due 27<sup>th</sup> April dated 18 Jan at 9 months.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Mr Brown of the George Tavern a <span class=highlight_yellow>signature</span> written notice to quit on the 1<sup>st</sup> Aug next.</p>\r\n<p>On board the Hope. Got a steam boat which towed her to sea with fine NW wind.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club I the evening. The wind got round &amp; blew hard from the NE &amp; brought on a heavy sea &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>remained</span> thaw during the whole of the day.</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1151,"lock":null}
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1205
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1205,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; every appearance of snow or sleet &amp; looking as if it would thaw. Wind about west. The ship preparing for sea. Received a note from D Dixon stating he had seen Colonel Coulson &amp; that there are several commissions vacant &amp; I must apply through Colonel Coulson.</p>\r\n<p>Accepted a bill for &pound;8.17 the <span class=highlight_yellow>prccuccia</span> for the present voyage: due 27<sup>th</sup> April dated 18 Jan at 9 months.</p>\r\n<p>Gave Mr Brown of the George Tavern a <span class=highlight_yellow>signature</span> written notice to quit on the 1<sup>st</sup> Aug next.</p>\r\n<p>On board the Hope. Got a steam boat which towed her to sea with fine NW wind.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; the whist club I the evening. The wind got round &amp; blew hard from the NE &amp; brought on a heavy sea &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>remained</span> thaw during the whole of the day.</p>","pageId":880,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1151,"lock":null}
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1206
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1206,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Wrote to Colonel Coalson applying for a commission. Took a walk round by Tynemouth. Dined at home. At billiard room latter in the afternoon &amp; abbey in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1152,"lock":null}
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1206
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1206,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine frosty morning. Wind NW. Wrote to Colonel Coalson applying for a commission. Took a walk round by Tynemouth. Dined at home. At billiard room latter in the afternoon &amp; abbey in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1152,"lock":null}
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1207
14:36:40.976 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1207,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine winter's morning. Slight frost &amp; been a great deal of snow during the night &amp; appearance of more. Wind NW.</p> <p></p> <p>Went by Durrer's coach to Newcastle &amp; took Robert with me. Tom, Ann &amp; Bell Smith at D Dixons. Tom Dixon &amp; I called at Leadbetters The attorneys &amp; I settled with them as Mrs Scott's executor giving them a draft on Chapmans on WBS &amp; JRS executors account for &pound;108.19.5 which with other payments we have made, leaves only &pound;702 due from us, of the &pound;1000 left under Mrs Scott's will. Robert &amp; Leadbetters received their legacies. Called twice on Colonel Coulson, not at home. Met him afterwards in the street &amp; had some conversation with him as to my application for a commission.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined with Mrs Dixon. The whole party excepting myself went to a concert. I called &amp; saw Mr Weatherly &amp; by his advice afterwards called upon Mr Turnbull, deputy clerk of the Peace, but he was not at home.</p> <p></p> <p>Suppered at Dixons &amp; slept at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Jessop</span> Hotel</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1153,"lock":null}
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1207
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1207,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine winter's morning. Slight frost &amp; been a great deal of snow during the night &amp; appearance of more. Wind NW.</p> <p></p> <p>Went by Durrer's coach to Newcastle &amp; took Robert with me. Tom, Ann &amp; Bell Smith at D Dixons. Tom Dixon &amp; I called at Leadbetters The attorneys &amp; I settled with them as Mrs Scott's executor giving them a draft on Chapmans on WBS &amp; JRS executors account for &pound;108.19.5 which with other payments we have made, leaves only &pound;702 due from us, of the &pound;1000 left under Mrs Scott's will. Robert &amp; Leadbetters received their legacies. Called twice on Colonel Coulson, not at home. Met him afterwards in the street &amp; had some conversation with him as to my application for a commission.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined with Mrs Dixon. The whole party excepting myself went to a concert. I called &amp; saw Mr Weatherly &amp; by his advice afterwards called upon Mr Turnbull, deputy clerk of the Peace, but he was not at home.</p> <p></p> <p>Suppered at Dixons &amp; slept at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Jessop</span> Hotel</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":881,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1153,"lock":null}
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1208
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1208,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Breakfasted at Dixons.</p> <p></p> <p>Afterwards called &amp; saw Mr Turnball who wrote out my declaration of qualifications which I signed &amp; which he will deliver to Mr Thorp the clerk of the Peace tomorrow.</p> <p></p> <p>Called upon &amp; saw Colonel Coulson who was with Captain Bigg &amp; told him what I had done &amp; had some conversation with them. He of course will immediately apply for a captain's course for me which will most likely come down in the course of the work, as the military is to go into training immediately.</p> <p></p> <p>Returned to Shields by steam &amp; dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; Nicholson took wine with me in the afternoon &amp; in the evening I walked to the Mulstrum. Received a letter from WBS</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1154,"lock":null}
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1208
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1208,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Breakfasted at Dixons.</p> <p></p> <p>Afterwards called &amp; saw Mr Turnball who wrote out my declaration of qualifications which I signed &amp; which he will deliver to Mr Thorp the clerk of the Peace tomorrow.</p> <p></p> <p>Called upon &amp; saw Colonel Coulson who was with Captain Bigg &amp; told him what I had done &amp; had some conversation with them. He of course will immediately apply for a captain's course for me which will most likely come down in the course of the work, as the military is to go into training immediately.</p> <p></p> <p>Returned to Shields by steam &amp; dined at home at 2 o'clock. H Harry &amp; Nicholson took wine with me in the afternoon &amp; in the evening I walked to the Mulstrum. Received a letter from WBS</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1154,"lock":null}
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1209
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1209,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A frosty morning. Rather <span class=highlight_yellow>damp</span> with a fall of snow. Wind NW. Dined at home. Received a letter from B B Galbraith &amp; answered it &amp; also WBS's. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; Albion in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>During the afternoon the wind got round to SW, S by W. At night blew fresh at S by E &amp; still frosty.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1155,"lock":null}
14:36:40.977 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1209
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1209,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A frosty morning. Rather <span class=highlight_yellow>damp</span> with a fall of snow. Wind NW. Dined at home. Received a letter from B B Galbraith &amp; answered it &amp; also WBS's. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; Albion in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>During the afternoon the wind got round to SW, S by W. At night blew fresh at S by E &amp; still frosty.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":882,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1155,"lock":null}
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/121
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":121,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind about North. Much refreshed by a good night's rest. Received a letter from William. Wrote to Mrs Scott. F Falknes &amp; Mr J Fitzmaurice called upon me. Took a long &amp; retired walk upon the banks of the river Barrow with Mr Vernon, returned to dine. John J Baker dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":111,"lock":null}
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/121
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":121,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind about North. Much refreshed by a good night's rest. Received a letter from William. Wrote to Mrs Scott. F Falknes &amp; Mr J Fitzmaurice called upon me. Took a long &amp; retired walk upon the banks of the river Barrow with Mr Vernon, returned to dine. John J Baker dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":111,"lock":null}
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1210
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1210,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Such a winters day. Blowing very hard at ESE and frosty. Wind increased to a perfect hurricane with one continuous shower of snow all day. I fear we shall have bad accounts of the shipping, many vessels being upon the coast. Dined at home and in the evening at the Mulstrum</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":883,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1156,"lock":null}
14:36:40.978 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.979 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1210
14:36:40.979 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1210,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Such a winters day. Blowing very hard at ESE and frosty. Wind increased to a perfect hurricane with one continuous shower of snow all day. I fear we shall have bad accounts of the shipping, many vessels being upon the coast. Dined at home and in the evening at the Mulstrum</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":883,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1156,"lock":null}
14:36:40.979 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1211
14:36:40.979 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1211,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Storm abated &amp; finer weather. Wind SE and a rapid thaw.</p> <p></p> <p>Many ships on shore. Two on the Herd Sand &amp; one a wreck, two on the rocks <span class=highlight_yellow>and</span> broken to pieces, three under the castle light house <span class=highlight_yellow>too</span> scattered to pieces <span class=highlight_yellow>mesher</span> &amp; boy of one drowned a smack at Cullercoats, all hands drowned. Three or four near Whitley, two broke to pieces immediately on coming on shore at night &amp; crews drowned. Walked round by the rock &amp; Tynemouth. Dreadful destruction.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; <font color=#BFBFBF>in the </font>evening Mr Lockword came home with me &amp; drank a glass of punch. Paid an average bill Eligible Club by draft for &pound;6.0.10. Came on to blow almost as hard as ever. Many ships got in today.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":883,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1157,"lock":null}
14:36:40.979 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1211
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1211,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>Storm abated &amp; finer weather. Wind SE and a rapid thaw.</p> <p></p> <p>Many ships on shore. Two on the Herd Sand &amp; one a wreck, two on the rocks <span class=highlight_yellow>and</span> broken to pieces, three under the castle light house <span class=highlight_yellow>too</span> scattered to pieces <span class=highlight_yellow>mesher</span> &amp; boy of one drowned a smack at Cullercoats, all hands drowned. Three or four near Whitley, two broke to pieces immediately on coming on shore at night &amp; crews drowned. Walked round by the rock &amp; Tynemouth. Dreadful destruction.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room all the afternoon &amp; <font color=#BFBFBF>in the </font>evening Mr Lockword came home with me &amp; drank a glass of punch. Paid an average bill Eligible Club by draft for &pound;6.0.10. Came on to blow almost as hard as ever. Many ships got in today.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":883,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1157,"lock":null}
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1212
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1212,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A calm morning. Very foggy. Wind S by W &amp; a frost.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting of the Eligible Club &amp; the members agreed to resist Mr Kings of South Shields claim as being unjust.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; whist club in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS of the safe arrival of the Hope &amp; a copy of a letter received from the Duke of Northumbria in answer to his application for a commission in the military for me; very polite.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1158,"lock":null}
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1212
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1212,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A calm morning. Very foggy. Wind S by W &amp; a frost.</p> <p></p> <p>Attended a meeting of the Eligible Club &amp; the members agreed to resist Mr Kings of South Shields claim as being unjust.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; whist club in the evening.</p> <p></p> <p>Received a letter from WBS of the safe arrival of the Hope &amp; a copy of a letter received from the Duke of Northumbria in answer to his application for a commission in the military for me; very polite.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1158,"lock":null}
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1213
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1213,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very stormy morning. Blew a gale of wind all night from ENE with heavy sleet &amp; rain.</p> <p></p> <p>Two ships have got upon the Herd <span class=highlight_yellow>Sand</span>. One from America, the other from ____</p> <p></p> <p>Settled with Robert &amp; paid into Chapmans on executors account &pound;65 of rents &amp; drew for &pound;18.11.6 to pay Mrs Noakes, late Miss Robinson for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ilbraith</font> boards etc.</p> <p></p> <p>Another small light vessel got upon the Herd.</p> <p></p> <p>At the news &amp; billiard rooms all the morning. No moving out such stormy weather. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Tinley, a party. Attended an evening party at the Messes Frenches'</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1159,"lock":null}
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1213
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1213,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very stormy morning. Blew a gale of wind all night from ENE with heavy sleet &amp; rain.</p> <p></p> <p>Two ships have got upon the Herd <span class=highlight_yellow>Sand</span>. One from America, the other from ____</p> <p></p> <p>Settled with Robert &amp; paid into Chapmans on executors account &pound;65 of rents &amp; drew for &pound;18.11.6 to pay Mrs Noakes, late Miss Robinson for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ilbraith</font> boards etc.</p> <p></p> <p>Another small light vessel got upon the Herd.</p> <p></p> <p>At the news &amp; billiard rooms all the morning. No moving out such stormy weather. Dined at 5 o'clock with J Tinley, a party. Attended an evening party at the Messes Frenches'</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1159,"lock":null}
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1214
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1214,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>It has been very stormy all night with showers of sleet &amp; snow. Wind this morning got round to NW. Sea very high. One of the ships that got upon the Herd Sand ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1160,"lock":null}
14:36:40.980 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1214
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1214,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>It has been very stormy all night with showers of sleet &amp; snow. Wind this morning got round to NW. Sea very high. One of the ships that got upon the Herd Sand ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":884,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1160,"lock":null}
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1215
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1215,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... yesterday gone to pieces.</p> <p></p> <p>The Magpie cutter being embayed was obliged yesterday to run for the harbour &amp; providentially got in safe, losing before she took the bar, one of her boats &amp; being obliged to cut away her square-sail, a sea having filled it and they could not take it in.</p> <p></p> <p>Sent Mr Leadbetter by Dunn this morning <span class=highlight_yellow>Rawling's</span> valuation of wines etc &amp; also Leadbitter the cook's receipt for her legacy. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; attended the whist club at H Dales in the evening. Turned rather frosty. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1161,"lock":null}
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1215
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1215,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... yesterday gone to pieces.</p> <p></p> <p>The Magpie cutter being embayed was obliged yesterday to run for the harbour &amp; providentially got in safe, losing before she took the bar, one of her boats &amp; being obliged to cut away her square-sail, a sea having filled it and they could not take it in.</p> <p></p> <p>Sent Mr Leadbetter by Dunn this morning <span class=highlight_yellow>Rawling's</span> valuation of wines etc &amp; also Leadbitter the cook's receipt for her legacy. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; attended the whist club at H Dales in the evening. Turned rather frosty. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1161,"lock":null}
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1216
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1216,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Did not go to church. Took a walk to Tynemouth after seeing the newspapers. Some light ships got in today from Leith Roads &amp; also some laden ones passed for London.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the Mulstrum in the evening. A heavy gale of snow &amp; blowing hard, 12 pm</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1162,"lock":null}
14:36:40.981 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1216
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1216,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine morning &amp; hard frost. Wind NW. Did not go to church. Took a walk to Tynemouth after seeing the newspapers. Some light ships got in today from Leith Roads &amp; also some laden ones passed for London.</p> <p></p> <p>Dined at home. At the Mulstrum in the evening. A heavy gale of snow &amp; blowing hard, 12 pm</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1162,"lock":null}
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1217
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1217,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind S by W &amp; SSW. Such unpleasant weather prevented going to Newcastle as I intended. The same course kept me at home on Saturday. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered &amp; spent the evening with a party at Dr Drury's</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1163,"lock":null}
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1217
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1217,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A dull rainy morning. Wind S by W &amp; SSW. Such unpleasant weather prevented going to Newcastle as I intended. The same course kept me at home on Saturday. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon. Suppered &amp; spent the evening with a party at Dr Drury's</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1163,"lock":null}
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1218
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1218,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A mild morning but rather dull; Wind SW. Afterwards turning out a fine day. J Cunningham breakfasted with me &amp; we went up to Newcastle together by steam. Mr Gorthing RA ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1164,"lock":null}
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1218
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1218,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A mild morning but rather dull; Wind SW. Afterwards turning out a fine day. J Cunningham breakfasted with me &amp; we went up to Newcastle together by steam. Mr Gorthing RA ...</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":885,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1164,"lock":null}
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1219
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1219,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... accompanied us. J Cunningham left me to see captain Maun of the north, wishing to obtain a commission. I called at D Dixon &amp; then went to Mrs Noaks &amp; paid her &pound;18.11.6 for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ailbraith</font>'s &frac14; year board etc. and also &pound;2.2 entrance for training dancing &amp; drawing. Gostling &amp; I lunched at D Dixons afterwards played at billiards at the rooms &amp; at 5 o'clock returned in a gig to Shields. The ice above <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>bridge having come away in immense quantities with the ebb tide prevented the steam boats plying.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1165,"lock":null}
14:36:40.982 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1219
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1219,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p><p>... accompanied us. J Cunningham left me to see captain Maun of the north, wishing to obtain a commission. I called at D Dixon &amp; then went to Mrs Noaks &amp; paid her &pound;18.11.6 for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>ailbraith</font>'s &frac14; year board etc. and also &pound;2.2 entrance for training dancing &amp; drawing. Gostling &amp; I lunched at D Dixons afterwards played at billiards at the rooms &amp; at 5 o'clock returned in a gig to Shields. The ice above <font color=#BFBFBF>the </font>bridge having come away in immense quantities with the ebb tide prevented the steam boats plying.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1165,"lock":null}
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/122
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":122,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind N. Wrote to William. J Harry &amp; Mr Jamison called upon Mr I Called upon &amp; saw poor old Miss Falkman who seemed much affected &amp; grieved at dear Bopy's death. Took a walk to Clogrennane, coll Rockforts seat with Mr Vernon &amp; the boys. Caught in heavy shower of rain on our way home got wet through. The boys dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":112,"lock":null}
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/122
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":122,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind N. Wrote to William. J Harry &amp; Mr Jamison called upon Mr I Called upon &amp; saw poor old Miss Falkman who seemed much affected &amp; grieved at dear Bopy's death. Took a walk to Clogrennane, coll Rockforts seat with Mr Vernon &amp; the boys. Caught in heavy shower of rain on our way home got wet through. The boys dined with us</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":112,"lock":null}
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1220
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1220,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine mild morning. Wind WSW. Several light ships got down. Went to Milburn Place to see Mr Stephenson respecting <span class=highlight_yellow>remitting</span> &pound;13.10 to London. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At a party in the evening at Mr W Hewson's</p> <p></p> <p>Great confusion &amp; I fear damage in the harbour tonight, the heavy fresh <font color=#BFBFBF>wind </font>having driven the ships adrift.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1166,"lock":null}
14:36:40.983 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1220
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1220,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A very fine mild morning. Wind WSW. Several light ships got down. Went to Milburn Place to see Mr Stephenson respecting <span class=highlight_yellow>remitting</span> &pound;13.10 to London. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At a party in the evening at Mr W Hewson's</p> <p></p> <p>Great confusion &amp; I fear damage in the harbour tonight, the heavy fresh <font color=#BFBFBF>wind </font>having driven the ships adrift.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1166,"lock":null}
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1221
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1221,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful mild spring morning. Wind fresh at about W by S. A great deal of damage done last night amongst the shipping.</p> <p></p> <p>Lunched on board the Choice. Dined at home at 5 o'clock, being my birthday, had a party of friends consisting of J &amp; H Dale, H Harry, Mark, H Nicholas &amp; Drury &amp; spent a very pleasant day.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1167,"lock":null}
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1221
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1221,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful mild spring morning. Wind fresh at about W by S. A great deal of damage done last night amongst the shipping.</p> <p></p> <p>Lunched on board the Choice. Dined at home at 5 o'clock, being my birthday, had a party of friends consisting of J &amp; H Dale, H Harry, Mark, H Nicholas &amp; Drury &amp; spent a very pleasant day.</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1167,"lock":null}
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1222
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1222,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful day. Quite spring weather. Wind WNW.</p> <p></p> <p>In consequence of late <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> etc last night &amp; did not breakfast &lsquo;<span class=highlight_yellow>till</span> 12 o'clock. Took a walk round by Tynemouth &amp; dined at home at 5 o'clock.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1168,"lock":null}
14:36:40.984 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.985 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1222
14:36:40.985 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1222,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A beautiful day. Quite spring weather. Wind WNW.</p> <p></p> <p>In consequence of late <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> etc last night &amp; did not breakfast &lsquo;<span class=highlight_yellow>till</span> 12 o'clock. Took a walk round by Tynemouth &amp; dined at home at 5 o'clock.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":886,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1168,"lock":null}
14:36:40.985 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1223
14:36:40.985 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1223,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A delightful morning. Quite spring, mild weather. A light air from about W.  Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at H Harry's in the evening</p> <p></p></p>","pageId":887,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1169,"lock":null}
