14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1239,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A thick damp morning. Wind SW. Did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrums</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":890,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1185,"lock":null}
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/124
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":124,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind still from the North. Engaged all the morning in examining Dear Betsy's books &amp; papers. In the afternoon Mr Vernon, the boys &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh to see the Herrings &amp; also called upon F Falkener, went round by Old derrgy &amp; home to dinner</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":114,"lock":null}
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/124
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":124,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind still from the North. Engaged all the morning in examining Dear Betsy's books &amp; papers. In the afternoon Mr Vernon, the boys &amp; I walked out to Crossleigh to see the Herrings &amp; also called upon F Falkener, went round by Old derrgy &amp; home to dinner</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":114,"lock":null}
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1240
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1240,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine but cold morning having been a frost in the night. Wind NW. My name not in the Gazette. Received a letter from WBS stating the season that Lord Melbourn had not made up his mind as to filling up the vacancies. Gave Robert a draft for &pound;5 executor's account for the house. Drew also for &pound;6.9 to pay Mrs Dixon for sundries got for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Paid into Chapman on my own account WBS's note for &pound;95.10 &amp; &pound;36.0.9 received of Hindhaugh = 131.16.9. Called upon Dr Drury &amp; gave him a draft on C&amp;C for his bills &pound;11.4/- afterwards walked up to Craigs &amp; took wine at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1186,"lock":null}
14:36:40.993 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1240
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1240,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":2,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p><p>A fine but cold morning having been a frost in the night. Wind NW. My name not in the Gazette. Received a letter from WBS stating the season that Lord Melbourn had not made up his mind as to filling up the vacancies. Gave Robert a draft for &pound;5 executor's account for the house. Drew also for &pound;6.9 to pay Mrs Dixon for sundries got for Emma G<font color=#BFBFBF>albraith</font>. Paid into Chapman on my own account WBS's note for &pound;95.10 &amp; &pound;36.0.9 received of Hindhaugh = 131.16.9. Called upon Dr Drury &amp; gave him a draft on C&amp;C for his bills &pound;11.4/- afterwards walked up to Craigs &amp; took wine at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p></p>\r\n<p><p></p></p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1186,"lock":null}
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1241
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1241,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Frosty &amp; wind at NW blowing fresh. Called upon Captain Webb. He &amp; I walked round by the high end of the town, Plett's Yard &amp; Chesterton, home to dinner. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; at the Duke of York in the evening.</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1187,"lock":null}
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1241
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1241,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Frosty &amp; wind at NW blowing fresh. Called upon Captain Webb. He &amp; I walked round by the high end of the town, Plett's Yard &amp; Chesterton, home to dinner. In the afternoon at the billiard room &amp; at the Duke of York in the evening.</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1187,"lock":null}
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1242
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1242,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind fresh at W by N. paid Robert &pound;2.4/ Walton the brewer bills 3<sup>rd</sup> &amp; 4<sup>th</sup> coal voyage which will be given credit for as sent, be being in <span class=highlight_yellow>asseasy</span>. Engaged today making up ships books. Dined at home. At the Abbey in the evening. The Hope arrived</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1188,"lock":null}
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1242
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1242,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind fresh at W by N. paid Robert &pound;2.4/ Walton the brewer bills 3<sup>rd</sup> &amp; 4<sup>th</sup> coal voyage which will be given credit for as sent, be being in <span class=highlight_yellow>asseasy</span>. Engaged today making up ships books. Dined at home. At the Abbey in the evening. The Hope arrived</p>","pageId":891,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1188,"lock":null}
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1243
14:36:40.994 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1243,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning &amp; light air at SE. Did not go to church. Dr Drury dined with me &amp; H Harry came in after dinner &amp; took wine. At the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1189,"lock":null}
