14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1245,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind S by W. Received a letter from Captain Crisp adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> of the regiment stating the Col<font color=#BFBFBF>onel</font> Coul<font color=#BFBFBF>son</font> having received a notification from the Duke of N<font color=#BFBFBF>orthamptonshire</font>  that my commission was preparing  &amp; that I must order my uniform etc &amp; hold myself in readiness to join. Attended a meeting at the North <span class=highlight_yellow>aems</span>, the room full, to petition both houses of parliament to pass the reform bill &amp; setting forth our approval of the measure. Went up to the ship. Dined at home. Wrote to WBS giving him a copy of the above mentioned letter. At the Albion in the evening.</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1191,"lock":null}
14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1246
14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1246,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind NNW. Walked out to Whitley &amp; called upon Mr J Wright &amp; returned home by Cullercoats &amp; Tynemouth to dinner. Dr Drury, Charlton &amp; I had wine at Sears &amp; finished the evening at the Mulstrum</p>","pageId":892,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1192,"lock":null}
14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
