14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1247,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful day. Wind SW. Went to Newcastle by steam &amp; ordered coals down on Monday. Enrolled <span class=highlight_yellow>H A </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Bealls</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>interviews</span> at the Custom House. Returned home to dinner. Dr Drewry &amp; Chartson dined with me. At the club in the evening.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1193,"lock":null}
14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1248
14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1248,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet unpleasant day. Wind between SW &amp; WNW. Could not get to the ship. Received a letter from WBS informing me of my name being in the Gazette, which I see in this days papers. Dined at home. H harry, Cunningham &amp; and I took wine at the Albion &amp; in the evening finished at the Duke <font color=#BFBFBF>of York</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font></p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1194,"lock":null}
14:36:40.996 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1248
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1248,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet unpleasant day. Wind between SW &amp; WNW. Could not get to the ship. Received a letter from WBS informing me of my name being in the Gazette, which I see in this days papers. Dined at home. H harry, Cunningham &amp; and I took wine at the Albion &amp; in the evening finished at the Duke <font color=#BFBFBF>of York</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font></p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1194,"lock":null}
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1249
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1249,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning and wind SW. Received a letter from Alnwick from the adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> Crisp ordering me to join the Regiment. Walked to Tynemouth with the intention of taking a warm bath, but they are not yet open for the season. Returned &amp; went up to the Hope. <span class=highlight_yellow>Repairs</span> nearly finished. At high water they hauled her off the shore &amp; dropped her down to Custom House Quay. Toward the afternoon it began to blow very hard varying between SSW &amp; SSE &amp; increased to a gale which continued all night. Spent the evening at home writing etc.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1195,"lock":null}
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1249
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1249,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":3,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning and wind SW. Received a letter from Alnwick from the adj<font color=#BFBFBF>utant</font> Crisp ordering me to join the Regiment. Walked to Tynemouth with the intention of taking a warm bath, but they are not yet open for the season. Returned &amp; went up to the Hope. <span class=highlight_yellow>Repairs</span> nearly finished. At high water they hauled her off the shore &amp; dropped her down to Custom House Quay. Toward the afternoon it began to blow very hard varying between SSW &amp; SSE &amp; increased to a gale which continued all night. Spent the evening at home writing etc.</p>","pageId":893,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1195,"lock":null}
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/125
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":125,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of the same sort of weather with the cool wind. Engaged all the morning with Mr Turner in examining &amp; entering rents. In the afternoon Mr Vernon &amp; I took a walk along the Kilkenny Road, returned home to drefs &amp; took a family dinner with Mr W<sup>en</sup> Fishburn who was exceedingly kind, but yet I should have preferred dining quietly at Mr Vernon's. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":695,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":115,"lock":null}
14:36:40.997 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
