14:36:41.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1288,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/maps/place/55%C2%B027'18.9%22N+1%C2%B054'44.6%22W/@55.4551396,-1.9123251,383m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x0:0x0!7e2!8m2!3d55.4552398!4d-1.9123944?hl=en\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2761-brandon-white-house.png\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Brandon, White House</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":901,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1234,"lock":null}
14:36:41.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1289
14:36:41.017 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1289,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":12,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful &amp; mild morning. Quite a summer's day, not a cloud to be seen. C Redley having stopped all night with me, left after breakfast for Newcastle. Wrote to Robert Reed Brandon White House to say I would pay him a visit in a few days. J Cunningham &amp; I again walked by the Sands to Cullercoats . On our return Bess B was waiting on the sands for me. J C went home &amp; I joined &amp; remained with Bess all the afternoon until &frac12; past 4 o'clock when I came home to dinner, after which I had another walk &amp; finished at the Albion</p>","pageId":901,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1235,"lock":null}
