14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1297,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind ESE. Walked up to the ship with H Harry &amp; round by Percy Main the turnpike, home to dinner. Spent the afternoon on board the Tom Shand &amp; the evening at the Mulstrum. Wrote to WBS</p>","pageId":902,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1243,"lock":null}
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1298
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1298,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but rather damp morning. Wind ESE. The charter for the Hope arrived by the post from Hull. The Merchants Messrs Wade Sons &amp; Forster Wybury &amp; Hull. 70/ for <span class=highlight_yellow>deals</span> &amp; buttons. The latter not to exceed 6/8. Ordered 3 casks or pork of Bradshaws &amp; 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>loaves</span> of bread of Walkerley &amp; a new main topgallantsail. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon H Harry gave the Doctor &amp; me some wine at the Northumberland Alms. Afterwards at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1244,"lock":null}
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1298
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1298,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but rather damp morning. Wind ESE. The charter for the Hope arrived by the post from Hull. The Merchants Messrs Wade Sons &amp; Forster Wybury &amp; Hull. 70/ for <span class=highlight_yellow>deals</span> &amp; buttons. The latter not to exceed 6/8. Ordered 3 casks or pork of Bradshaws &amp; 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>loaves</span> of bread of Walkerley &amp; a new main topgallantsail. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon H Harry gave the Doctor &amp; me some wine at the Northumberland Alms. Afterwards at the Abbey &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1244,"lock":null}
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1299
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1299,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold morning. Wind NE. Paid into Chapmans the <span class=highlight_yellow>hote</span> for &pound;97.9. Gave Stephenson &pound;50. Got the pork, bread etc on board. Had a few friends to dine with me at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>veg</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Te</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nley's</span> Rudyard 15<sup>th</sup> Regiment Dick artillery J Wright &amp; Boswell.</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1245,"lock":null}
14:36:41.022 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1299
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1299,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold morning. Wind NE. Paid into Chapmans the <span class=highlight_yellow>hote</span> for &pound;97.9. Gave Stephenson &pound;50. Got the pork, bread etc on board. Had a few friends to dine with me at 5 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>veg</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Te</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nley's</span> Rudyard 15<sup>th</sup> Regiment Dick artillery J Wright &amp; Boswell.</p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1245,"lock":null}
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/13
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":13,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got captain Hallam to moor the Hope securely by carrying an anchor out astern. Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at Mrs Greenhours, met a large party, a regular squeeze; quadrille &amp; broke up at 12 o'clock. It was cold with snow in the evening</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":10,"lock":null}
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/13
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":13,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got captain Hallam to moor the Hope securely by carrying an anchor out astern. Dined with Mrs Scott &amp; spent the evening at Mrs Greenhours, met a large party, a regular squeeze; quadrille &amp; broke up at 12 o'clock. It was cold with snow in the evening</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":10,"lock":null}
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/130
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":130,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind WSW. Captain Butler read the morning service. We afterwards took a drive between showers &amp; returned to dinner</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":120,"lock":null}
14:36:41.023 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/130
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":130,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet day. Wind WSW. Captain Butler read the morning service. We afterwards took a drive between showers &amp; returned to dinner</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":120,"lock":null}
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1300
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1300,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but cool with a NE wind. Got a cask of rum on board the Hope. Ordered the men on shore as they refused to sign articles for less than &pound;3 per month. Stephenson at Newcastle clearing.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Ministries in a minority of eight upon Gen<font color=#BFBFBF>era</font>l  Gascoyne's amendment on the reform bill respecting English members. Attended a meeting at the George tavern called in consequence of the minister being in the minority for the purpose of explaining their determination to support them in their proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>grievances</span> &amp; not to give any candidate a vote until he promises to support reform.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Finished at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum.</p>\r\n<p><u> </u></p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1246,"lock":null}
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1300
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1300,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning but cool with a NE wind. Got a cask of rum on board the Hope. Ordered the men on shore as they refused to sign articles for less than &pound;3 per month. Stephenson at Newcastle clearing.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Ministries in a minority of eight upon Gen<font color=#BFBFBF>era</font>l  Gascoyne's amendment on the reform bill respecting English members. Attended a meeting at the George tavern called in consequence of the minister being in the minority for the purpose of explaining their determination to support them in their proposed <span class=highlight_yellow>grievances</span> &amp; not to give any candidate a vote until he promises to support reform.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Finished at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum.</p>\r\n<p><u> </u></p>","pageId":903,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1246,"lock":null}
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1301
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1301,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold day &amp; blowing fresh from NNE &amp; sea coming on. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it. Called at Chapmans, Mr Spence declines answering our note, but proposes continuing the <span class=highlight_yellow>loan</span> on my giving a bill upon WBS to have his acceptance, the <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span> to be afterward agreed upon when I secure WBS's answer. Walked up to the ship, all ready for sea, excepting <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span>. Towed her down to the low end of the town. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand in the afternoon &amp; at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1247,"lock":null}
14:36:41.024 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1301
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1301,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cold day &amp; blowing fresh from NNE &amp; sea coming on. Received a letter from WBS &amp; answered it. Called at Chapmans, Mr Spence declines answering our note, but proposes continuing the <span class=highlight_yellow>loan</span> on my giving a bill upon WBS to have his acceptance, the <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span> to be afterward agreed upon when I secure WBS's answer. Walked up to the ship, all ready for sea, excepting <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span>. Towed her down to the low end of the town. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand in the afternoon &amp; at the Mulstrum in the evening.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1247,"lock":null}
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1302
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1302,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind NNE &amp; much sea. A good deal of rain during the day. An account this morning of there being having prorogued parliament in person.  Dined at home. Took wine with the doctor &amp; finished at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1248,"lock":null}
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1302
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1302,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind NNE &amp; much sea. A good deal of rain during the day. An account this morning of there being having prorogued parliament in person.  Dined at home. Took wine with the doctor &amp; finished at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1248,"lock":null}
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1303
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1303,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NNE. Paid by draft on executors account &frac12; years taxes &pound;14.7.11 &amp; on my own account {premium &pound;8.17, own account &pound;10.15, WBS &pound;5} &pound;24.12. Dined on board the Hope, H Harry &amp; Webb with me. Finished off at the Albion.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1249,"lock":null}
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1303
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1303,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NNE. Paid by draft on executors account &frac12; years taxes &pound;14.7.11 &amp; on my own account {premium &pound;8.17, own account &pound;10.15, WBS &pound;5} &pound;24.12. Dined on board the Hope, H Harry &amp; Webb with me. Finished off at the Albion.</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1249,"lock":null}
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1304
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1304,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy rainy day. Wind SE &amp; SSE. Some ships went to sea amongst them the Geronimi. We could not get men &amp; were therefore obliged to lay. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand. Spent the evening at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1250,"lock":null}
14:36:41.025 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
