14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1304,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy rainy day. Wind SE &amp; SSE. Some ships went to sea amongst them the Geronimi. We could not get men &amp; were therefore obliged to lay. Dined at home. On board the Mr Shand. Spent the evening at the Albion &amp; Mulstrum</p>","pageId":904,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1250,"lock":null}
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1305
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1305,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another foggy &amp; rainy morning &amp; but little wind at SSW. Got our men this morning for &pound;2.17.6 per month &amp; have the ship out. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon the Hope sailed with a fresh breeze at SSE. Finished at the Albion. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1251,"lock":null}
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1305
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1305,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another foggy &amp; rainy morning &amp; but little wind at SSW. Got our men this morning for &pound;2.17.6 per month &amp; have the ship out. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon the Hope sailed with a fresh breeze at SSE. Finished at the Albion. Received a letter from WBS</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1251,"lock":null}
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1306
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1306,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still dull &amp; looks like more rain. Called and saw Mr Spear who agreed to take out joint note payable at <span class=highlight_yellow>neis</span>. Leis for the loan of &pound;300 at 4 or 6 months. Wrote to WBS to that effect. Dined with the Committees of the Eligible &amp; United clubs. In the evening at the Malstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1252,"lock":null}
14:36:41.026 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1306
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1306,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still dull &amp; looks like more rain. Called and saw Mr Spear who agreed to take out joint note payable at <span class=highlight_yellow>neis</span>. Leis for the loan of &pound;300 at 4 or 6 months. Wrote to WBS to that effect. Dined with the Committees of the Eligible &amp; United clubs. In the evening at the Malstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1252,"lock":null}
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1307
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1307,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Went with Lockwood by Dunn's coach to Newcastle &amp; put up at the Turf Hotel where we also dined at the Wallsend Hunt dinner &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1253,"lock":null}
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1307
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1307,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Went with Lockwood by Dunn's coach to Newcastle &amp; put up at the Turf Hotel where we also dined at the Wallsend Hunt dinner &amp; stayed all night.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1253,"lock":null}
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1308
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1308,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy day. Wind continues from SE. The election for Newcastle took place. I went to the Guild Hall but I could not get near enough to the hustings to hear any part of the speeches. For Mr Ridley &amp; Mr Hodgson returned without opposition. Lucky fellows. Saw them chained. Had a lunch at the Turf &amp; returned to Shields by Dunn. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1254,"lock":null}
14:36:41.027 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1308
14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1308,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy day. Wind continues from SE. The election for Newcastle took place. I went to the Guild Hall but I could not get near enough to the hustings to hear any part of the speeches. For Mr Ridley &amp; Mr Hodgson returned without opposition. Lucky fellows. Saw them chained. Had a lunch at the Turf &amp; returned to Shields by Dunn. At the Duke of York &amp; Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":905,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1254,"lock":null}
14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1309
14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1309,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; all the appearance of more rain. Afterwards turned out a fine warm spring day. Walked to Cullercoats Sands. Ed Charlton dined with me. H Harry &amp; Sadler came in afterwards &amp; took wine. Sadler brought the account from the committee room of the Bell having retired. Finished off at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1255,"lock":null}
14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
