14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1309,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning &amp; all the appearance of more rain. Afterwards turned out a fine warm spring day. Walked to Cullercoats Sands. Ed Charlton dined with me. H Harry &amp; Sadler came in afterwards &amp; took wine. Sadler brought the account from the committee room of the Bell having retired. Finished off at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":906,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1255,"lock":null}
14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/131
14:36:41.028 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":131,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull and damp morning. Wind the same. Left Broomville &amp; reached Carlow without rain. Received a letter from William. Dined with Mr Vernon</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":121,"lock":null}
