14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1345,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still fine weather. Wind NE. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; Cullercoat Sands with Bess. Dined at home. Walked again in the evening on the Sands with Bess</p>","pageId":914,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1291,"lock":null}
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1346
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1346,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NNE. Went to church. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined with J Tinley. At 5 o'clock met Cap<sup>t</sup><font color=#BFBFBF>ain</font> Glasscost &amp; L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Drickey of the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS</font> Orestes, Major Mitchell &amp; Rudyard at the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":914,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1292,"lock":null}
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1346
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1346,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NNE. Went to church. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined with J Tinley. At 5 o'clock met Cap<sup>t</sup><font color=#BFBFBF>ain</font> Glasscost &amp; L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Drickey of the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS</font> Orestes, Major Mitchell &amp; Rudyard at the Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":914,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1292,"lock":null}
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1347
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1347,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning with slight rain &amp; blowing fresh from N by E &amp; good deal of sea on. Received a letter from WBS. Attended a meeting for the relief of the seamen out of employment, whose families are in great distress, subscribed a Guinea. Dined at home. Called at the Doctor's &amp; walked up to his garden &amp; spent the evening playing at quoits. At the Albion</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1293,"lock":null}
14:36:41.046 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1347
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1347,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning with slight rain &amp; blowing fresh from N by E &amp; good deal of sea on. Received a letter from WBS. Attended a meeting for the relief of the seamen out of employment, whose families are in great distress, subscribed a Guinea. Dined at home. Called at the Doctor's &amp; walked up to his garden &amp; spent the evening playing at quoits. At the Albion</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1293,"lock":null}
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1348
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1348,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NW. Afterwards turned out a most delightful day &amp; the wind again from the old quarter NE. Walked up to High Cheston &amp; called upon Mr Robson as bridegroom. Dined at home. At Tynemouth in the evening.. Took coffee with J Tinley.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1294,"lock":null}
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1348
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1348,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NW. Afterwards turned out a most delightful day &amp; the wind again from the old quarter NE. Walked up to High Cheston &amp; called upon Mr Robson as bridegroom. Dined at home. At Tynemouth in the evening.. Took coffee with J Tinley.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1294,"lock":null}
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1349
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1349,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind NW. Glass fallen &amp; more the appearance of rain. Received a letter from Emma Galbraith informing me of the holy days commencing on the 17<sup>th</sup>. <span class=highlight_yellow>But</span> glad to see her so much improved in her writing. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At Tynemouth again &amp; Cullercoat Sands in the afternoon &amp; evening. At the Albion.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Towards noon the wind got into the old quarter NE again &amp; turned out a most beautiful day.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1295,"lock":null}
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1349
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1349,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind NW. Glass fallen &amp; more the appearance of rain. Received a letter from Emma Galbraith informing me of the holy days commencing on the 17<sup>th</sup>. <span class=highlight_yellow>But</span> glad to see her so much improved in her writing. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At Tynemouth again &amp; Cullercoat Sands in the afternoon &amp; evening. At the Albion.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Towards noon the wind got into the old quarter NE again &amp; turned out a most beautiful day.</p>","pageId":915,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1295,"lock":null}
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/135
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":135,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring day with a shower of rain in the morning. Wind SW. Mr Vernon &amp; I walked out to_____ &amp; dined with J Fitzmaurice. The house stands about halfway up the mountain &amp; commands a most extensive &amp; beautiful view of the surrounding country for many miles, bounded by the Wiklow &amp; other mountains, taking in Carlow in north 10 miles or more off &amp; other towns. We spent a very pleasant day. Received from &amp; wrote a letter to William</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":125,"lock":null}
14:36:41.047 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/135
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":135,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring day with a shower of rain in the morning. Wind SW. Mr Vernon &amp; I walked out to_____ &amp; dined with J Fitzmaurice. The house stands about halfway up the mountain &amp; commands a most extensive &amp; beautiful view of the surrounding country for many miles, bounded by the Wiklow &amp; other mountains, taking in Carlow in north 10 miles or more off &amp; other towns. We spent a very pleasant day. Received from &amp; wrote a letter to William</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":125,"lock":null}
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1350
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1350,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind W by N. Afterwards NE. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Went again to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Saw Bess became friends again &amp; had a long walk with her. Got to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mont</span>, <span class=highlight_yellow>trcien</span> about 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1296,"lock":null}
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1350
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1350,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cloudy. Wind W by N. Afterwards NE. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. Went again to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Saw Bess became friends again &amp; had a long walk with her. Got to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mont</span>, <span class=highlight_yellow>trcien</span> about 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1296,"lock":null}
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1351
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1351,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At last a change in the weather, having rain, but wild &amp; wind WSW. A fine <span class=highlight_yellow>growing</span> day. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon with Bess at Mrs Woodham's. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Called on our return at the Duke of York &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1297,"lock":null}
14:36:41.048 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
