14:36:41.049 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1351,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At last a change in the weather, having rain, but wild &amp; wind WSW. A fine <span class=highlight_yellow>growing</span> day. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon with Bess at Mrs Woodham's. H Harry &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Called on our return at the Duke of York &amp; afterwards at the Mulstrum.</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1297,"lock":null}
14:36:41.049 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1352
14:36:41.049 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1352,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. The rain will do great good. The country being much in want of it. Wind E by S. Dined at home. Spent the afternoon on board the Telemachus, with Mr Bradshaw. At the Albion &amp; Mulstrum in the evening</p>","pageId":916,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1298,"lock":null}
