14:36:41.052 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1359,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SSW. A shower of rain about 1 o'clock. L<font color=#BFBFBF>ieutenan</font><sup>t</sup> Griffin RM took his dinner with me &amp; Webb came along afterwards. Walked to Tynemouth in the evening. P<font color=#BFBFBF>ai</font><sup>d</sup> E Reid's mother &pound;2.6.9 balance of <span class=highlight_yellow>gegarayers</span> wages</p>","pageId":918,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1305,"lock":null}
14:36:41.052 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/136
14:36:41.052 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":136,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine spring day, very warm, with a few gentle showers. Wind SW. Engaged in the morning packing then called upon Mr W Fishbeam. Dined at Mr Vernon. The two Mr Cureys dined with us. Spent a very pleasant evening</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":126,"lock":null}
