14:36:41.056 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1367,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fair. Wind fresh at N by E &amp; NNE. Crossed the water &amp; got on the coach for York westside at 8 o'clock where we arrived at 6 o'clock to dinner after a very pleasant drive without rain. Got an <span class=highlight_yellow>inside</span> in the march at &frac12; past 7 o'clock &amp; arrived at Hull at &frac12; past 12 o'clock. A beautiful moonlight night. Drank a glass of whiskey Toddy &amp; went to bed.</p>","pageId":920,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1313,"lock":null}
14:36:41.056 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1368
14:36:41.056 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1368,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. After breakfast went &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbertts</span>, met Stephenson on the road. Afterwards walked to the ship &amp; saw the merchant but would not freight until the ship is out. Dined on board. A heavy thunder storm in the afternoon &amp; continued to rain all day. Stephenson &amp; I in the evening walked round the docks etc &amp; finished with a glass of toddy at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Ina</span></p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1314,"lock":null}
