14:36:41.057 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1368,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by E. After breakfast went &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbertts</span>, met Stephenson on the road. Afterwards walked to the ship &amp; saw the merchant but would not freight until the ship is out. Dined on board. A heavy thunder storm in the afternoon &amp; continued to rain all day. Stephenson &amp; I in the evening walked round the docks etc &amp; finished with a glass of toddy at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Ina</span></p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1314,"lock":null}
14:36:41.057 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1369
14:36:41.057 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1369,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull &amp; very sultry close morning. Wind N by W &amp; NNW. Called upon Martin Orr at the Garrison. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Garb</span><span class=highlight_yellow>utt</span> but declined fixing a foreign mail being expected &amp; the chance of freights being better. H French dined with me on board after having a long walk about the town. The ship out &amp; cleared this afternoon. Wrote to Bess B. Martin Orr &amp; his wife called upon me at the ship. Set H French <span class=highlight_yellow>part</span> of the way home &amp; amused myself the remainder of the evening by strolling round the town. Turned out a very rainy day.</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1315,"lock":null}
