14:36:41.057 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":137,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but cold wind NW. Went to church in the morning &amp; heard a very good discourse from Mr Vernon. Wrote a letter to Mrs Scott. Dined at the Mr Careys &amp; spent an extremely pleasant day. Present Mr Vernon, Captain Warren (65<sup>th</sup> regiment), 2 Careys, Ed Butler &amp; Mr Ballerely. Came into wine</p>","pageId":696,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":127,"lock":null}
14:36:41.057 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1370
14:36:41.057 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1370,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very rainy morning. Wind NW. Called at <span class=highlight_yellow>Garbu</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tt'</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span>. Stephenson busy paying dock dues etc. &amp; getting ships provisions on board. The rain &amp; wind prevented the lighters working &amp; we got no ballast today. Dined at 4 o'clock with J Bell. Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Ward</span> dined with us. In the evening walked to H French's house &amp; spent it with <span class=highlight_yellow>nens</span> &amp; Fanny</p>","pageId":921,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1316,"lock":null}
14:36:41.057 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
