14:36:41.064 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1383,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning after the rain, having been a good deal in the night 7 the appearance yet of more wind E by N &amp; ENE. At church in the morning. D Dixon called but we were out. Dined at home. Took tea with Messrs Harry, walked to Tynemouth in the evening. Very foggy &amp; damp. Finished at H Harry's with a glass of whiskey</p>","pageId":924,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1329,"lock":null}
14:36:41.064 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1384
14:36:41.064 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1384,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":7,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind ESE. Very foggy. Ben &amp; I got on board a steamer &amp; went to Newcastle. Saw D Dixon. I walked with him out to Benton, dined &amp; in the evening walked through the country to Shields. Called at the Mustrum</p>","pageId":925,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1330,"lock":null}
14:36:41.064 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
