14:36:41.086 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1429,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Amused ourselves by strolling about the markets etc. William went &amp; saw Dr Proctor again, but I being tired did not go. Having settled our bill, at 2 o'clock we again embarked on board the <font color=#000000>Ariadne</font><font size=3.4pt color=#000000>&nbsp;</font>&amp; sailed about 9 o'clock. The vessel most uncomfortably crowded, being about 155 passengers on board. We could not get berths. Passed close by the Island of Alderney. A fine sight.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1375,"lock":null}
14:36:41.086 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/143
14:36:41.086 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":143,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with fine spring showers. Left Captain Butlers &amp; returned to Carlow. Mr Vernon &amp; I dined at Mr Butlins &amp; met a very pleasant party</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":133,"lock":null}
