14:36:41.087 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1430,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. We arrived at Southampton at &frac12; past 5 o'clock, very much fatigued having been waiting to sleep or lay on deck all night. After waiting two hours &amp; a half at the custom house, we were obliged to go home to breakfast without our luggage. Dined at the Lewises at Shirley. Colonel Ogilvie &amp; Captain Cobb there.</p>","pageId":935,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1376,"lock":null}
14:36:41.087 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1431
14:36:41.087 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1431,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NW. Did not go to church. After lunch took a walk round by the Pier, the baths to the Itchen &amp; crossed the ferry to see PearTree Green. Returned to dinner</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1377,"lock":null}
14:36:41.087 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1431
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1431,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NW. Did not go to church. After lunch took a walk round by the Pier, the baths to the Itchen &amp; crossed the ferry to see PearTree Green. Returned to dinner</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1377,"lock":null}
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1432
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1432,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of delightful weather. Wind SW. Passed the morning in walking about, playing at billiards etc. Wrote to the Duke of Northumberland at court requesting him to grant me an interview &amp; complaining of my having been a second time passed for the purpose of Captains Loraiac &amp;  being placed over my head. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1378,"lock":null}
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1432
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1432,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of delightful weather. Wind SW. Passed the morning in walking about, playing at billiards etc. Wrote to the Duke of Northumberland at court requesting him to grant me an interview &amp; complaining of my having been a second time passed for the purpose of Captains Loraiac &amp;  being placed over my head. Dined at Mr Lees</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1378,"lock":null}
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1433
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1433,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW. Again engaged much the same as yesterday. Received a letter from Stephenson as which both Roads dated the 24<sup>th</sup> all well. The Lewis' &amp; Mr Carry dined with us. Major Falls of the 93<sup>rd</sup> &amp; Colonel Ogilvie came in the evening.</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1379,"lock":null}
14:36:41.088 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.089 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1433
14:36:41.089 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1433,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day. Wind SW. Again engaged much the same as yesterday. Received a letter from Stephenson as which both Roads dated the 24<sup>th</sup> all well. The Lewis' &amp; Mr Carry dined with us. Major Falls of the 93<sup>rd</sup> &amp; Colonel Ogilvie came in the evening.</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1379,"lock":null}
14:36:41.089 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1434
14:36:41.089 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
14:36:41.089 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.089 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1434
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1434,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind SW. Bob Marsh left for London. Received an answer from the Duke referring me to Colonel Coulson. The Duke tied up with the gout &amp; not able to see me. Wrote to Stephenson, Major Falls, Colonel Ogilvie, William &amp; I went to Shirley to dine. Amused ourselves in rifle shooting</p>","pageId":936,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1380,"lock":null}
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1435
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1435
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1435,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A miserable cold morning. Wind NE. rained continuously all day. After breakfast packed up my cloths &amp; spent the remainder of the day till dinner playing at billiards until Colonel Ogilvie, captain Lewis &amp; Harry RM. The former of whom with Major Falls dined with us.</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1381,"lock":null}
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1436
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1436,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning. Wind NW but cool. After breakfasting with Mr Lee, got upon the Red Robin coach driven by Pearce at 10 o'clock &amp; started for Town where we arrived at &frac14; before 7 o'clock travelling a new &amp; by far the more beautiful road, over the Hog Back. Here we had a drenching shower of rain &amp; hail, through Guilford to town. Got to Nottingham Place at 7 o'clock. Had a cup of tea &amp; went to bed at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1382,"lock":null}
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1436
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1436,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning. Wind NW but cool. After breakfasting with Mr Lee, got upon the Red Robin coach driven by Pearce at 10 o'clock &amp; started for Town where we arrived at &frac14; before 7 o'clock travelling a new &amp; by far the more beautiful road, over the Hog Back. Here we had a drenching shower of rain &amp; hail, through Guilford to town. Got to Nottingham Place at 7 o'clock. Had a cup of tea &amp; went to bed at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":937,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1382,"lock":null}
14:36:41.090 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1437
