14:36:41.092 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1439,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind WSW. Breakfasted with C Richmond. He drove me in the afternoon around &amp; called upon Mrs Fletcher alias Hoffman then through the park by Pimlico &amp; Westminster to Greenwich. Called &amp; saw Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> Watt and his wife, dined off whitebait etc. at the Crown &amp; Sceptre &amp; returned to town at 7 o'clock to tea. Got home in good time</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1385,"lock":null}
