14:36:41.093 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1441,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Rather close. WBS went out the city. Arrived myself in the West End of the town all the morning. Dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Junior Wright at Blackfriars, a small party <span class=highlight_yellow>there. </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Crg</span> Richmond, G Walters, Mr Gordon, G Kain &amp; two Miss Jobling's of Austlery</p>","pageId":938,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1387,"lock":null}
14:36:41.093 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1442
14:36:41.093 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1442,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull unpleasant morning. Heavy showers all day. Wind SW. Took a walk &amp; called upon Mr Lenskill &amp; Mr Ward. Met Captain Shepherd in the Burley Tea Arcade who has got appointed to the <font color=#BFBFBF>HMS </font>Melville 74 &amp; going out to the East Indies with <font color=#BFBFBF>admiral </font>Sir J<font color=#BFBFBF>ohn</font> Gore. Dined with Richmond at 6 o'clock to meet Mr &amp; Mrs Hoffman alias Mary Fletcher, his sister &amp; J Wrights</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1388,"lock":null}
14:36:41.093 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
