14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1443,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<figure>\r\n  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation_of_William_IV_and_Adelaide\" >\r\n    <img src=\"images/img2799-coronation-william-4th.jpg\" width=\"600px\" />\r\n    <figcaption>Coronation of William IV</figcaption>\r\n  </a>\r\n</figure>","pageId":939,"type":null,"imageId":null,"marqueeId":1389,"lock":null}
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1444
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1444,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. The town all alive &amp; on the move towards Charring Cross, Pall Mall etc. to see Coronation Procession. After breakfast I went out but could not see the procession, so great was the crowd.  It appearing however to be near the United Services Club House after it had passed I saw major Falls who asked me in &amp; upon I had a very fine view of the whole of it on its return. A most splendid &amp; magnificent sight it was. Saw there Majesties very distinctly. Unfortunately there was a great deal of rain which they were in the Abbey which made the streets very dirty &amp; dampt the pleasure of the people no doubt very much. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; in the evening saw the illuminations which passed good</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1390,"lock":null}
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1444
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1444,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SW. The town all alive &amp; on the move towards Charring Cross, Pall Mall etc. to see Coronation Procession. After breakfast I went out but could not see the procession, so great was the crowd.  It appearing however to be near the United Services Club House after it had passed I saw major Falls who asked me in &amp; upon I had a very fine view of the whole of it on its return. A most splendid &amp; magnificent sight it was. Saw there Majesties very distinctly. Unfortunately there was a great deal of rain which they were in the Abbey which made the streets very dirty &amp; dampt the pleasure of the people no doubt very much. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; in the evening saw the illuminations which passed good</p>","pageId":939,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1390,"lock":null}
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1445
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1445,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant day. Rained incessantly. Wind NW. Did not go out until 2 o'clock. Called upon Beverley who was not at home. Left my card. Walked down to Bob Marsh and Richmond's. Got a letter from Stephenson who will not be cleared so soon as expected. Answered it &amp; told him I should not be at Hull &amp; of my intention to leave town on Tuesday by the city of Edinburgh steamer. Called at Hawtry the dentists &amp; got my teeth cleaned. Dined at 6 o'clock at Nottingham Place. Richmond &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1391,"lock":null}
14:36:41.094 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1445
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1445,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant day. Rained incessantly. Wind NW. Did not go out until 2 o'clock. Called upon Beverley who was not at home. Left my card. Walked down to Bob Marsh and Richmond's. Got a letter from Stephenson who will not be cleared so soon as expected. Answered it &amp; told him I should not be at Hull &amp; of my intention to leave town on Tuesday by the city of Edinburgh steamer. Called at Hawtry the dentists &amp; got my teeth cleaned. Dined at 6 o'clock at Nottingham Place. Richmond &amp; Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1391,"lock":null}
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1446
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1446,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still damp unpleasant weather &amp; appearance of more rain. Wind NW. Called a little earlier upon Lord Beverley who had again gone out. Returned to Nottingham Place. At 2 o'clock walked down to Charring Cross &amp; there got upon a stage &amp; went to the Elephant &amp; castle &amp; thence walked to George Harry Apollo Buildings, Walworth &amp; saw Henry H. who I found laid up, being much bruised &amp; injured by the upsetting of a Blackwell Stage. Returned by stage &amp; dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Richmond. Walked home early in the evening.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1392,"lock":null}
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1446
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1446,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still damp unpleasant weather &amp; appearance of more rain. Wind NW. Called a little earlier upon Lord Beverley who had again gone out. Returned to Nottingham Place. At 2 o'clock walked down to Charring Cross &amp; there got upon a stage &amp; went to the Elephant &amp; castle &amp; thence walked to George Harry Apollo Buildings, Walworth &amp; saw Henry H. who I found laid up, being much bruised &amp; injured by the upsetting of a Blackwell Stage. Returned by stage &amp; dined at &frac12; past 5 o'clock with Richmond. Walked home early in the evening.</p>","pageId":940,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1392,"lock":null}
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1447
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1447,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of dull cloudy weather, wind NNW &amp; every appearance of more rain. William, Emma &amp; Lee went to church. I did not go being obliged to take some <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuberts</span>. At 3 o'clock walked through the Regents Park to the Zoological Gardens with which &amp; the collection of wild beasts. I was much pleased. Returned home &amp; dressed &amp; went to dine with Mr Leaskill at 7 o'clock, a small party, only Captain Greg &amp; myself there</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1393,"lock":null}
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1447
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1447,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of dull cloudy weather, wind NNW &amp; every appearance of more rain. William, Emma &amp; Lee went to church. I did not go being obliged to take some <span class=highlight_yellow>Cuberts</span>. At 3 o'clock walked through the Regents Park to the Zoological Gardens with which &amp; the collection of wild beasts. I was much pleased. Returned home &amp; dressed &amp; went to dine with Mr Leaskill at 7 o'clock, a small party, only Captain Greg &amp; myself there</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1393,"lock":null}
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1448
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1448,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but rather cloudy. Wind NW &amp; NNW. After lunch walked down to St James street &amp; saw the nobility etc. go to court. Her Majesty holding a drawing room.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with C <span class=highlight_yellow>Reibarud</span>. J Griffith &amp; WBS there.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Mary Scott <font color=#BFBFBF>(daughter of WBS) </font>went to school</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1394,"lock":null}
14:36:41.095 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1448
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1448,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day but rather cloudy. Wind NW &amp; NNW. After lunch walked down to St James street &amp; saw the nobility etc. go to court. Her Majesty holding a drawing room.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Dined with C <span class=highlight_yellow>Reibarud</span>. J Griffith &amp; WBS there.</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p>Mary Scott <font color=#BFBFBF>(daughter of WBS) </font>went to school</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1394,"lock":null}
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1449
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1449,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind N by W. Wrote to Robert Snowdon. Lee Scott went to School. Walked down to St James Street. His Majesty holding a Levee went along the Strand &amp; called on Bob Marsh. Returned &amp; saw the company come from the Levee. Walked with WBS in Regent Street at 6 o'clock dined alone at the Blue Ports &amp; afterwards went home.</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1395,"lock":null}
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
