14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1449,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind N by W. Wrote to Robert Snowdon. Lee Scott went to School. Walked down to St James Street. His Majesty holding a Levee went along the Strand &amp; called on Bob Marsh. Returned &amp; saw the company come from the Levee. Walked with WBS in Regent Street at 6 o'clock dined alone at the Blue Ports &amp; afterwards went home.</p>","pageId":941,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1395,"lock":null}
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/145
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":145,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day engaged all the morning in preparing for the sale. Dined quietly at home, wrote to A Fitzmaurice</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":135,"lock":null}
14:36:41.096 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/145
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":145,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day engaged all the morning in preparing for the sale. Dined quietly at home, wrote to A Fitzmaurice</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":135,"lock":null}
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1450
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1450,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind from the N &amp; E. Wrote a letter to Lord Beverley &amp; afterwards called upon him &amp; found him at home, very graciously received. Entered into a long account &amp; related to him all the inconsistencies respecting any complaint about being <span class=highlight_yellow>regazzetted</span> etc, but he could not interfere at the same. Explained himself as not surprised at my feelings &amp; regret that it should have happened, but that he thought no further change could be made. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Called at the <span class=highlight_yellow>courting</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> &amp; thence walked down to Mrs Carr's. Saw Boswell the <span class=highlight_yellow>Decgttonte</span> and dined there. Spent the evening &amp; returned by stage at night.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1396,"lock":null}
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1450
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1450,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind from the N &amp; E. Wrote a letter to Lord Beverley &amp; afterwards called upon him &amp; found him at home, very graciously received. Entered into a long account &amp; related to him all the inconsistencies respecting any complaint about being <span class=highlight_yellow>regazzetted</span> etc, but he could not interfere at the same. Explained himself as not surprised at my feelings &amp; regret that it should have happened, but that he thought no further change could be made. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Called at the <span class=highlight_yellow>courting</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>homes</span> &amp; thence walked down to Mrs Carr's. Saw Boswell the <span class=highlight_yellow>Decgttonte</span> and dined there. Spent the evening &amp; returned by stage at night.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1396,"lock":null}
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1451
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1451,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind N by E. Remained in the house till after 1 o'clock expecting Boswell, but he did not come. Walked round the inner circle of the Regents Park &amp; thence to Bob Marsh's  &amp; WBS &amp; I afterwards walked up by Regents Street home to dinner. Found that Boswell had called after I had left home.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1397,"lock":null}
14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
