14:36:41.097 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1451,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind N by E. Remained in the house till after 1 o'clock expecting Boswell, but he did not come. Walked round the inner circle of the Regents Park &amp; thence to Bob Marsh's  &amp; WBS &amp; I afterwards walked up by Regents Street home to dinner. Found that Boswell had called after I had left home.</p>","pageId":942,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1397,"lock":null}
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1452
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1452,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the north. Wrote to Lord Beverley requesting him to present one to His Majesty at the Levee on Wednesday next &amp; left the letter at his house. Thence walked down Regents Street. St James's Street round the park &amp; there to Richmond's. Walked again up Regents Street &amp; dined with Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1398,"lock":null}
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1452
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1452,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind from the north. Wrote to Lord Beverley requesting him to present one to His Majesty at the Levee on Wednesday next &amp; left the letter at his house. Thence walked down Regents Street. St James's Street round the park &amp; there to Richmond's. Walked again up Regents Street &amp; dined with Richmond at &frac12; past 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1398,"lock":null}
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1453
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1453,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another delightful autumnal morning. Wind north. Received a note from H Harry to say they called upon me this morning. A little after 1 o'clock, he, Miss G Hurry &amp; Miss Fenwick called &amp; we drove to the Zoological Gardens. Afterwards to the Coliseum with which we were much delighted &amp; astonished &amp; most particularly with the Swiss Cottage &amp; arcade. Thence we drove to Walworth &amp; I dined with them. Walked home in the evening where I found a note from Lord Beverley saying he will have much pleasure in presenting me to His Majesty on Wednesday next.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1399,"lock":null}
14:36:41.098 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
