14:36:41.099 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1453,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another delightful autumnal morning. Wind north. Received a note from H Harry to say they called upon me this morning. A little after 1 o'clock, he, Miss G Hurry &amp; Miss Fenwick called &amp; we drove to the Zoological Gardens. Afterwards to the Coliseum with which we were much delighted &amp; astonished &amp; most particularly with the Swiss Cottage &amp; arcade. Thence we drove to Walworth &amp; I dined with them. Walked home in the evening where I found a note from Lord Beverley saying he will have much pleasure in presenting me to His Majesty on Wednesday next.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1399,"lock":null}
14:36:41.099 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1454
14:36:41.099 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1454,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Slept in the house all the morning. Richmond called at 3 o'clock &amp; drove me out in his gig. Went round by Highgate &amp; Hampstead &amp; returned by Regent &amp; Hyde Park Home to dinner. Bob marsh also dined with us.</p>","pageId":943,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1400,"lock":null}
