14:36:41.100 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1456,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":19,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to the office. Received a short letter from Bess, very angry for not writing to her. Called at Harman's about the Hope's Wyburn bill which has been lagging at the docks agent for my acceptance. Wrote to Rob<font color=#BFBFBF>er</font><sup>t</sup> S<font color=#BFBFBF>tephenson</font> to send it up. Called at J Chapman. Took a cab &amp; drove direct to St James. Called at the Lord Chamberlains office. Saw Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Master</span> who was very polite &amp; introduced me as to how I am to act at the Levee. Left a card with him. Walked home &amp; wrote to Bess blowing her up for her saucy letter. Dined at home</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1402,"lock":null}
14:36:41.100 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1457
14:36:41.100 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
