14:36:41.101 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1457,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine autumnal morning. Wind WNW. Been a little rain in the night. Took an omnibus  into the city. At the offices. <del>Called upon Messrs Harman's statement they had sent the Hope's Wyburn bill to Shields for above</del>. Walked down to Miss Carr. Boswell gone down to Maldon this morning to the ship, which it appears, arrived there a fortnight ago, but he had not heard of it. Returned to the office &amp; WBS &amp; I walked out of the city together. Called at Bob Marsh's who afterwards joined is in Regents Street &amp; went to Nottingham Place to dinner</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1403,"lock":null}
14:36:41.101 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1458
14:36:41.101 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
