14:36:41.101 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1458,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Wind SSW very unfortunate, having to go to the Levee but hope it will clear up. WBS returned from the city at 1 o'clock. When I dressed myself in full fig &amp; drove in a hackney coach to St James Palace &amp; was presented to the King. The Levee was not numerously attended, being nearly all naval &amp; military ...</p>","pageId":944,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1404,"lock":null}
14:36:41.101 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1459
14:36:41.101 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1459,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... decorated with all their orders, it was a very splendid &amp; magnificent sight. I thought I should have been very nervous, but was not at all so. I was nominally presented by the Earl of Beverley, but in fact by the Lord in waiting who was I believe was Lord ____  <font color=#BFBFBF>Earl of Gosford</font>   I had the honour of kissing the Kings hand. Lord Beverley found me out in the ante room &amp; was particularly polite &amp; attentive. After leaving the Levee, WBS &amp; Bob Marsh were waiting for me &amp; we walked along Pall Mall &amp; I got a coach &amp; drove home where I exchanged my dress &amp; returned to Richmond where I dined</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1405,"lock":null}
14:36:41.101 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.102 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1459
14:36:41.102 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1459,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":21,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... decorated with all their orders, it was a very splendid &amp; magnificent sight. I thought I should have been very nervous, but was not at all so. I was nominally presented by the Earl of Beverley, but in fact by the Lord in waiting who was I believe was Lord ____  <font color=#BFBFBF>Earl of Gosford</font>   I had the honour of kissing the Kings hand. Lord Beverley found me out in the ante room &amp; was particularly polite &amp; attentive. After leaving the Levee, WBS &amp; Bob Marsh were waiting for me &amp; we walked along Pall Mall &amp; I got a coach &amp; drove home where I exchanged my dress &amp; returned to Richmond where I dined</p>","pageId":945,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1405,"lock":null}
14:36:41.102 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/146
14:36:41.102 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":146,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful and hot summers day. Received two letters from Mrs &amp; Miss Scott. The sale commenced &amp; good prices said to be obtained. Mr Vernon with his unreal kindness &amp; consideration asked a party to dine with us consisting of the two Careys, E Butler, Fishebourne, O'Connor &amp; Captain Ballesby. Spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":136,"lock":null}
14:36:41.102 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
