14:36:41.106 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1467,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull damp morning. Wind SE. Did not go out till late. Walked down by Regents Street &amp; called at Richmond's, thence to the Temple &amp; left my card at <span class=highlight_yellow>wwards</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>chainpers</span>,. Returned to Regent Street at 6 o'clock with Richmond. G Taylor, Bob Marsh, WBS &amp; self there</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1413,"lock":null}
14:36:41.106 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1468
14:36:41.106 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1468,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been some rain this morning. Rather dull &amp; excessively close &amp; sultry. Wind for the ESE. Took an omnibus into the city. Called at the office. Accepted Stephenson's Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>berg bill for &pound;44.5/- due 8 Nov payable with WBS &amp; left it at Messrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Halmgons</span>. Went down to the St Catherine dock &amp; dined on board the Crisis. Tea at <span class=highlight_yellow>Lodlins</span>. A heavy fall of rain with lightning at night.</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1414,"lock":null}
14:36:41.106 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1468
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1468,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been some rain this morning. Rather dull &amp; excessively close &amp; sultry. Wind for the ESE. Took an omnibus into the city. Called at the office. Accepted Stephenson's Wy<font color=#BFBFBF>n</font>berg bill for &pound;44.5/- due 8 Nov payable with WBS &amp; left it at Messrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Halmgons</span>. Went down to the St Catherine dock &amp; dined on board the Crisis. Tea at <span class=highlight_yellow>Lodlins</span>. A heavy fall of rain with lightning at night.</p>","pageId":947,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1414,"lock":null}
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1469
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1469,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; cooler weather after heavy rain last night. Wind SE. Sat in the house until after 1 o'clock. Called &amp; had a lunch at Miles Forsters offices in Wimpole Street &amp; sat some time with him. Walked in Regent Street till dinner time. Richmond dined with us</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1415,"lock":null}
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1469
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1469,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; cooler weather after heavy rain last night. Wind SE. Sat in the house until after 1 o'clock. Called &amp; had a lunch at Miles Forsters offices in Wimpole Street &amp; sat some time with him. Walked in Regent Street till dinner time. Richmond dined with us</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1415,"lock":null}
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/147
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":147,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. The sale still going on. Wrote to Mr I Robert about a chain cable for the Hope. Dined early. John &amp; I took a long walk to fish but had no sport</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":137,"lock":null}
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/147
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":147,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. The sale still going on. Wrote to Mr I Robert about a chain cable for the Hope. Dined early. John &amp; I took a long walk to fish but had no sport</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":137,"lock":null}
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1470
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1470,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning dull &amp; thick, afterwards cleared away &amp; turned out a fine day. Wind SSE. Got all my luggage into a Hackney coach &amp; down to Philpot lane (there saw Stephenson, the Hope being at Greenwich <del>got up to stone stairs</del>) down on St Catherine dock &amp; the Crises having got out, I <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> &amp; left all my luggage at Lodlings. Walked up again to Phillpotts Lane, accompanied WBS to Guildhall and having got a Beef Steak at Jewps on WBS, Lee &amp; I walked down to Mr Carr's &amp; drank tea. Called at Codlings &amp; saw H Nicholson who had got the ship down to Duke Shore &amp; expecting to get away in the morning. I determined to accept Mr Carr's offer of a bed. Set WBS part of the way up the Commercial Road. Returned with Nicholson to Lodlings &amp; got to Mr Carr's a little after 10 o'clock. Rained very heavy with a great deal of lightning. Part of the Hope sold today.</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1416,"lock":null}
14:36:41.107 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.108 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1470
14:36:41.108 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1470,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":9,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The early part of the morning dull &amp; thick, afterwards cleared away &amp; turned out a fine day. Wind SSE. Got all my luggage into a Hackney coach &amp; down to Philpot lane (there saw Stephenson, the Hope being at Greenwich <del>got up to stone stairs</del>) down on St Catherine dock &amp; the Crises having got out, I <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> &amp; left all my luggage at Lodlings. Walked up again to Phillpotts Lane, accompanied WBS to Guildhall and having got a Beef Steak at Jewps on WBS, Lee &amp; I walked down to Mr Carr's &amp; drank tea. Called at Codlings &amp; saw H Nicholson who had got the ship down to Duke Shore &amp; expecting to get away in the morning. I determined to accept Mr Carr's offer of a bed. Set WBS part of the way up the Commercial Road. Returned with Nicholson to Lodlings &amp; got to Mr Carr's a little after 10 o'clock. Rained very heavy with a great deal of lightning. Part of the Hope sold today.</p>","pageId":948,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1416,"lock":null}
14:36:41.108 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1471
14:36:41.108 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1471,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning after a very heavy fall of rain during the night. Wind SSW. Afterwards changeable between <span class=highlight_yellow>N</span> &amp; S by E. After breakfast went to Codlings, Stephenson met me there &amp; we got all my luggage on board the Crisis &amp; about 12 o'clock having got all her ballast in, she weighed anchor &amp; dropped down to Greenwich where we were enabled to sail down the reach &amp; we got to Woolwich between 2 &amp; 3 o'clock. The tide here low we took the ground &amp; there remained until 10 o'clock at which time I had gone to bed but the ship got under way &amp; beat down to earth &amp; brought up between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock in the morning</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1417,"lock":null}
14:36:41.108 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.109 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1471
14:36:41.109 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1471,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning after a very heavy fall of rain during the night. Wind SSW. Afterwards changeable between <span class=highlight_yellow>N</span> &amp; S by E. After breakfast went to Codlings, Stephenson met me there &amp; we got all my luggage on board the Crisis &amp; about 12 o'clock having got all her ballast in, she weighed anchor &amp; dropped down to Greenwich where we were enabled to sail down the reach &amp; we got to Woolwich between 2 &amp; 3 o'clock. The tide here low we took the ground &amp; there remained until 10 o'clock at which time I had gone to bed but the ship got under way &amp; beat down to earth &amp; brought up between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock in the morning</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1417,"lock":null}
14:36:41.109 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1472
14:36:41.109 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1472,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At anchor off Erith. A cloudy morning with showers. Wind fresh from SSW after washing the decks &amp; trimming ballast, the ship having been by the stern, we got under way at about 11 o'clock &amp; beat down to the <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span> light where we brought up at 6 o'clock. The wind having changed during the day to S by W: S: &amp; S by E blowing fresh. Turned after a glass of grog between 8 &amp; 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1418,"lock":null}
14:36:41.109 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1472
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1472,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At anchor off Erith. A cloudy morning with showers. Wind fresh from SSW after washing the decks &amp; trimming ballast, the ship having been by the stern, we got under way at about 11 o'clock &amp; beat down to the <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span> light where we brought up at 6 o'clock. The wind having changed during the day to S by W: S: &amp; S by E blowing fresh. Turned after a glass of grog between 8 &amp; 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1418,"lock":null}
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1473
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1473,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned the hands up about 5 o'clock being low water &amp; the wind at SSW I got up before 6 o'clock. The people busy getting the anchor &amp; setting sails. Had a fine run during the day down <span class=highlight_yellow>swin</span>, studding sails set but not much wind which varied between <span class=highlight_yellow>SE</span> &amp; S by W. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock at night off Aldeburgh &amp; beautiful clear weather but a strong flood tide against us. Turned in about 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1419,"lock":null}
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1473
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1473,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned the hands up about 5 o'clock being low water &amp; the wind at SSW I got up before 6 o'clock. The people busy getting the anchor &amp; setting sails. Had a fine run during the day down <span class=highlight_yellow>swin</span>, studding sails set but not much wind which varied between <span class=highlight_yellow>SE</span> &amp; S by W. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock at night off Aldeburgh &amp; beautiful clear weather but a strong flood tide against us. Turned in about 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":949,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1419,"lock":null}
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1474
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
14:36:41.110 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1474
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1474,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 12 o'clock am. The ship then running with a fresh breeze at SW for the <span class=highlight_yellow>Newrope</span> light which we passed about 1 o'clock &amp; ran through Hasbrough Gateway. Turned into my crib again before 2 o'clock I awoke or rather disturbed at 5 o'clock by a tremendous squall at SW a little to the south w of Cromer with heavy rise. It took us suddenly &amp; without any warning &amp; therefore with all sails standing that they had great difficulty in taking them in. However they succeeded at last in taking them without losing anything, which considering the violence of the squall was fortunate. When they had double reefed the topsails &amp; made all snug I again went to bed. Got up at 8 o'clock still blowing hard from the WSW. We were then abreast of the Dadgrow floating light. It continued to blow fresh all the morning varying between WSW &amp; W by N. After dinner Nicholson &amp; I turned in &amp; had a good snooze until &frac12; past 4 o'clock where we found Flamborough in sight distant probably about 15 miles. Wind &amp; sea very much fallen, but still a fine light breeze from about WSW. All reefs out, top gallant <del>sails set</del> &amp; fore topmast studding sails set. Passed Flamborough Head at 8 o'clock, a most beautiful night. At 9 o'clock we had a glass of grog &amp; I afterwards walked the deck with Nicholson till 12 o'clock when we turned in.</p>","pageId":950,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1420,"lock":null}
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1475
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1475
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1475,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>We were disturbed again this morning at about 3 o'clock by a heavy squall with rain from the SSW which increased. I &amp; Nicholson immediately turned out, the ship being off the Tees by the time we got upon deck, they had got the top sail &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>missen</span> stowed &amp; top sail reefed,  <span class=highlight_yellow>lay</span> the ship too soon afterwards left with the head to the land, between Seaham &amp; Hartlepool, the squall gradually subsided &amp; at day light 5 o'clock fine weather again. Ran the ship in for the land &amp; between 7 &amp; 8 o'clock got a piolet on board. Lay off the harbour until the tide flowed sufficiently for us to run the bar, which we did at 11 o'clock, working up to the narrows &amp; then dropping up to the <span class=highlight_yellow>Lenickeln</span> shore where I landed &amp; came home. Robert got my things on shore.</p>\r\n<p>I dined with J Tinley &amp; in the evening called &amp; saw Bess, got home before 11 o'clock</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1421,"lock":null}
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1476
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.111 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1476
14:36:41.112 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1476,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning having been a great deal of rain at an early hour, blowing fresh at SSW. Paid Robert. Borrowed of him &pound;3 for child 8 weeks &pound;1.16 &amp; settled his book in passages etc. &pound;3.5.3</p>\r\n<p>Dined at the Northumberland Alms being the Dukes court day, the <span class=highlight_yellow>cooks on recorder</span> of Newcastle <span class=highlight_yellow>proceeded</span> there for the first time. At the <span class=highlight_yellow>nefs</span> room ...</p>","pageId":951,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1422,"lock":null}
14:36:41.112 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1477
14:36:41.112 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1477,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning but still blowing hard from the SSW. Several light ships got down &amp; must have had a good run. Lockwood &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth. H Nicholson &amp; Mark dined with me at 3 o'clock. In the evening attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Aldertons</span> Committee room &amp; afterwards with Bess</p>","pageId":952,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1423,"lock":null}
14:36:41.112 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
