14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1487,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning blowing fresh at WNW. Went across the water to Shortridge's Glass works to order some claret glasses for Mr Lee according to patterns</p>","pageId":955,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1433,"lock":null}
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1488
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1488,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind WNW. Went again to South Shields &amp; ordered 2 doz<font color=#BFBFBF>en</font> claret glasses. Played at billiards. Made up the Hope's Wyburg voyage. Dined at home &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":955,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1434,"lock":null}
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1488
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1488,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind WNW. Went again to South Shields &amp; ordered 2 doz<font color=#BFBFBF>en</font> claret glasses. Played at billiards. Made up the Hope's Wyburg voyage. Dined at home &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":955,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1434,"lock":null}
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1489
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1489,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fair morning. Wind from SW. Got up early &amp; took Dunn's gig to Newcastle. Took a place in the Alnwick coach at 10 o'clock. Got there before 3 o'clock where most of the officers who intended dining at the mess had arrived. Sat down to dinner at 6 o'clock. Spent a very pleasant &amp; jovial evening &amp; kept it up until 4 o'clock in the morning.</p>","pageId":955,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1435,"lock":null}
14:36:41.117 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1489
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1489,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fair morning. Wind from SW. Got up early &amp; took Dunn's gig to Newcastle. Took a place in the Alnwick coach at 10 o'clock. Got there before 3 o'clock where most of the officers who intended dining at the mess had arrived. Sat down to dinner at 6 o'clock. Spent a very pleasant &amp; jovial evening &amp; kept it up until 4 o'clock in the morning.</p>","pageId":955,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1435,"lock":null}
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/149
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":149,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but turned out exceptionally hot. Called upon Messrs Ryan &amp; Parkinson respecting Nuv<sup>n</sup> Fitzmaurice bond who said they were wise endeavouring to raise money to pay off all his debts. To my great surprise I met Cha<sup>r</sup> Hurry who I found had been residing in Dublin for 18 months. Dined at Mackens. Went today to see the Rotunda</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":139,"lock":null}
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/149
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":149,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":5,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but turned out exceptionally hot. Called upon Messrs Ryan &amp; Parkinson respecting Nuv<sup>n</sup> Fitzmaurice bond who said they were wise endeavouring to raise money to pay off all his debts. To my great surprise I met Cha<sup>r</sup> Hurry who I found had been residing in Dublin for 18 months. Dined at Mackens. Went today to see the Rotunda</p>","pageId":697,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":139,"lock":null}
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1490
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1490,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Did not rain till late. A fine morning. A fine morning. Walked about Alnwick. Left my card at Sir D Smith's. The <span class=highlight_yellow>Jefson</span> held the day. The <span class=highlight_yellow>heapesteutes</span> dined together. I dined with W<font color=#BFBFBF>illia</font><sup>m</sup> Forstes. A party there consisting of <span class=highlight_yellow>Chat</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span> MP, cap<font color=#BFBFBF>tain</font> Forster &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Justies</span> Hodgson MP etc. They all in the eve<font color=#BFBFBF>ning</font>s event to the Ball &amp; I dressed in my uniform having no other cloths with me with the intention of going but finding at the door that all the officers, even those who had promised to be in uniform were in plain cloths. I returned to the Inn, had a glass of brandy &amp; water &amp; went to bed</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1436,"lock":null}
14:36:41.118 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1490
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1490,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Did not rain till late. A fine morning. A fine morning. Walked about Alnwick. Left my card at Sir D Smith's. The <span class=highlight_yellow>Jefson</span> held the day. The <span class=highlight_yellow>heapesteutes</span> dined together. I dined with W<font color=#BFBFBF>illia</font><sup>m</sup> Forstes. A party there consisting of <span class=highlight_yellow>Chat</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span> MP, cap<font color=#BFBFBF>tain</font> Forster &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Justies</span> Hodgson MP etc. They all in the eve<font color=#BFBFBF>ning</font>s event to the Ball &amp; I dressed in my uniform having no other cloths with me with the intention of going but finding at the door that all the officers, even those who had promised to be in uniform were in plain cloths. I returned to the Inn, had a glass of brandy &amp; water &amp; went to bed</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1436,"lock":null}
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1491
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1491,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. The air rather frosty. Wind NSW. Left Alnwick by the Wonder coach at 10 o'clock, got to Newcastle before 3 o'clock, took a Shields gig &amp; got home in time to order dinner at 6 o'clock when Cha<font color=#BFBFBF>rle</font>s Redley came &amp; stayed all night. I spoke to Col<font color=#BFBFBF>onel  </font>Colson yesterday respecting the second gazetteer stating that I still considered myself very unhandsomely treated. <font color=#BFBFBF>I</font> showed him the Dukes letter but could get nothing out of him</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1437,"lock":null}
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1491
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1491,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. The air rather frosty. Wind NSW. Left Alnwick by the Wonder coach at 10 o'clock, got to Newcastle before 3 o'clock, took a Shields gig &amp; got home in time to order dinner at 6 o'clock when Cha<font color=#BFBFBF>rle</font>s Redley came &amp; stayed all night. I spoke to Col<font color=#BFBFBF>onel  </font>Colson yesterday respecting the second gazetteer stating that I still considered myself very unhandsomely treated. <font color=#BFBFBF>I</font> showed him the Dukes letter but could get nothing out of him</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1437,"lock":null}
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1492
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1492,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning blowing hard from the SW.</p>\r\n<p>Redley &amp; I walked to the newsroom, thence to Preston where we parted, he going on to Hartley. Saw Moore &amp; urged him to thrash &amp; sell everything. Dined at 5 o'clock alone. Stephenson called &amp; informed me the Eligible Committee had been on board surveyed the stores etc. &amp; reported the ship complete. Had got the dung out, the ship upon the shore to look at &amp; clean her bottom. Found her in good order, only a <span class=highlight_yellow>butts and or</span> two wanting caulking.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess in the evening</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1438,"lock":null}
14:36:41.119 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.120 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1492
14:36:41.120 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1492,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning blowing hard from the SW.</p>\r\n<p>Redley &amp; I walked to the newsroom, thence to Preston where we parted, he going on to Hartley. Saw Moore &amp; urged him to thrash &amp; sell everything. Dined at 5 o'clock alone. Stephenson called &amp; informed me the Eligible Committee had been on board surveyed the stores etc. &amp; reported the ship complete. Had got the dung out, the ship upon the shore to look at &amp; clean her bottom. Found her in good order, only a <span class=highlight_yellow>butts and or</span> two wanting caulking.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess in the evening</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1438,"lock":null}
14:36:41.120 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1493
14:36:41.120 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1493,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with showers &amp; SW wind. Did not go to church. At the newsroom all the morning. Dined at &frac12; past 6 o'clock. Ed Chesterton dined with me. Lockerwood came in in the afternoon.</p>\r\n<p>With Bess at night</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1439,"lock":null}
14:36:41.120 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
