14:36:41.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1494,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather blowing fresh from the SW. Lockerwood &amp; I walked up to Wallsend &amp; breakfasted with Potts. The hounds after breakfast were taken out. Charlton offered me his horse but I declined it. Laid the hounds on a <span class=highlight_yellow>bag</span> fox. Returned home. Dined with Readhead &amp; at night with Bess</p>","pageId":956,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1440,"lock":null}
14:36:41.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1495
14:36:41.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1495,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":10,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Heavy SW wind. Called at Chapman's &amp; settled for WBS to take up the &pound;300 note in London. They to give the executors account credit for &pound;200 &amp; take our note at 6 months for it. Wrote to WBS in answer to his letter received yesterday about it. Dined at home at 2 o'clock &amp; Lockwood &amp; I walked up afterwards to Billy Mill &amp; took wine with Charlton.</p>\r\n<p>At Bess in the evening</p>\r\n<p>Got &pound;5 of GH</p>","pageId":957,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1441,"lock":null}
14:36:41.121 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
