14:36:41.141 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1532,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp unpleasant morning. Wind WNW. The Hope got down to the dock gate. Took a walk &amp; Tynemouth. Got the Hope into dock at 2 o'clock, high tide.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at Home. At billiard room &amp; in the evening attended the whist club</p>","pageId":965,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1478,"lock":null}
14:36:41.141 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1533
14:36:41.141 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1533,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Thick cold weather wind WNW. The committee of the Eligible &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Whcatley</span> as a member of the Hope Club committee, went on board the Hope &amp; surveyed her &amp; found her much strained &amp; they readily agreed to give her a caulking, if I were willing to accept it &amp; not strip her etc. two warps a <span class=highlight_yellow>trwlinge</span> &amp; studding sail continued. Set the men on to work after dinner.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to Messrs Hurry &amp; Co. <font color=#BFBFBF>of </font>Yarmouth acknowledging the receipt of these accounts &amp; vouchers.</p>\r\n<p>Dined with a party at Gordons at Tynemouth Place at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":965,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1479,"lock":null}
14:36:41.141 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.142 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/1533
14:36:41.142 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1533,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Thick cold weather wind WNW. The committee of the Eligible &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Whcatley</span> as a member of the Hope Club committee, went on board the Hope &amp; surveyed her &amp; found her much strained &amp; they readily agreed to give her a caulking, if I were willing to accept it &amp; not strip her etc. two warps a <span class=highlight_yellow>trwlinge</span> &amp; studding sail continued. Set the men on to work after dinner.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote to Messrs Hurry &amp; Co. <font color=#BFBFBF>of </font>Yarmouth acknowledging the receipt of these accounts &amp; vouchers.</p>\r\n<p>Dined with a party at Gordons at Tynemouth Place at 5 o'clock</p>","pageId":965,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1479,"lock":null}
14:36:41.142 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1534
14:36:41.142 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1534,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very foggy unpleasant morning. Wind WNW. At the dock the men 21 busy caulking. Stephenson &amp; the carpenter found the ship in good order &amp; not at all broken. Wrote to WBS. Dined at home. At the billiard room. Called to see Bess &amp; at night at the club at Drury</p>","pageId":965,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1480,"lock":null}
