14:36:41.144 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1537,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, after rain &amp; blowing very heavy from WSW. Went to Newcastle by Dunns coach, called on bell &amp; Brown to let them know when the Hope would be out of dock. Saw Emma Galbraith who was quite well. Returned to Shields by steam. At the ship. Dined with Dr Drury.  At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night.</p>","pageId":966,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1483,"lock":null}
14:36:41.144 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/1538
14:36:41.144 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":1538,"version":0,"year":1831,"month":12,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning. Been a great deal of rain during the night &amp; blowing hard from SSE. Delivered Hurry's account &amp; vouchers onto the Eligible Club. Down at the ship, the caulking to be finished &amp; ship out of dock in the evening. Dined at home. At the billiard room in the afternoon &amp; with Bess at night</p>","pageId":966,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1484,"lock":null}
