14:36:41.226 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":1699,"version":0,"year":1832,"month":5,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind still from the N by E. Walked to Tynemouth. Dined at home. At Tynemouth again in the afternoon. Took wine &amp; spent the evening at Tibbs. Called at Bess</p>","pageId":999,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":1643,"lock":null}
14:36:41.226 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/17
14:36:41.226 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":17,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After a blowy and rainy night, on rising this morning, found the snow nearly dissolved. Wind E to ESE &amp; very heavy sea upon the bar, a few ships arrived. Another disappointment! Received a letter from Sir D Smith stating the Dukes inability to comply with my request for a loan. Every person poor when you want assistance! Adversities the time for trying friendship, in prosperity you have professions enough. I've oft been told, but I have now ascertained it's a d-d selfish world we live in; every one for himself. &lsquo;tis almost a crime to be liberal &amp; kind hearted</p>","pageId":687,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":14,"lock":null}
14:36:41.226 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
