14:36:41.316 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/188
14:36:41.316 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":188,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":6,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. This being a holy day at the Court of Chancery, we could do nothing. I therefor went in the steam boat to Kingstown &amp; dined with J Thompson on board the Royal Charlotte. The Mayor of Anglesey came down &amp; took a sail in his yacht the Pearl. Lieutenant M  Paget came on too and the Royal Charlotte to whom I was introduced. No great honor as it is not likely he will know me again.</p>","pageId":701,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":178,"lock":null}
