14:36:41.408 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":207,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":7,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>It began very early in the morning to rain &amp; blow hard &amp; it increased to a heavy gale. Nearly all on board sick. Obliged about 12 o'clock to lay to not being able to see land or make the floating light. The weather so thick. Between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock made the light &amp; got into Liverpool at 3 o'clock after a very stormy passage across of 20 hours and landed very wet. Got Emma to bed, much exhausted from the fatigues &amp; sickness. We stopped at the Angel Inn</p>","pageId":702,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":197,"lock":null}
14:36:41.408 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2070
14:36:41.408 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2070,"version":0,"year":1834,"month":5,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather &amp; wind SE. Received a letter from WBS. Answered it with the Kent &amp; Gth account &amp; informing him of the the sale of the Hope. R Ilderton came down &amp; we &amp; H Hurry dined with Mr Tibbs</p>","pageId":1079,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2010,"lock":null}
