14:36:41.514 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":23,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning. On going out, found the harbour in dreadful state of confusion &amp; much damage done in consequence of the immense land floods driving the ships adrift. Rode to Newcastle with J Tinley, saw W Chapman. He offered to take my bill at 6 months with another approved name to it, for 1000 or 1200. Refused &amp; dined with J Tinley. Wrote to William. Wind SW. Many ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":20,"lock":null}
14:36:41.514 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/230
14:36:41.514 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":230,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 4 o'clock this morning Went to the spout. Brought a lot of beef on my way up at 40/- Returned to breakfast &amp; went by steam to Newcastle where I learned  that the act gave them the power of loading any ship under 6 keels before larger vessels. Dined with J Tinley. Mrs Scott got from Toyston</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":219,"lock":null}
