ock went to the Hotel D'Angleterre &amp; had our breakfast &amp; afterwards proceeded, accompanied by a clerk of Mr Ryan, a very intelligent young Dame who talked English fluently. Arrived <span class=highlight_yellow>at</span> the town by the ramparts. As our time would not allow us to see much more than the town itself, but with it we were as touched &amp; delighted without exception. Taking it all together, it is the most beautiful city I ever saw. Most of cities have their S<sup>t</sup> Gales Bellengales &amp; but here there does not appear to be anything of the sort. &lsquo;tis all alike most ...</p>","pageId":742,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2245,"lock":null}
14:36:41.517 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2306
14:36:41.517 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2306,"version":7,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock &amp; most delightful morning, with a fine breeze from NW. been going 5 &amp; 6 knots all night. After breakfast going 6 knots &amp; steering an ENE course. At few of our companions, the dragon flies still with us. At 12 o'clock took observation &amp; by it, <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> in lat:56.36. long: 18.41</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2246,"lock":null}
14:36:41.517 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/2306
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2306,"version":7,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock &amp; most delightful morning, with a fine breeze from NW. been going 5 &amp; 6 knots all night. After breakfast going 6 knots &amp; steering an ENE course. At few of our companions, the dragon flies still with us. At 12 o'clock took observation &amp; by it, <span class=highlight_yellow>with</span> in lat:56.36. long: 18.41</p>","pageId":744,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2246,"lock":null}
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2307
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2307,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... debt. I should also mention that before the ship got to the mole, party of customs house officers came on board &amp; immediately scaled down all the hatches&amp; everything on board in the shape of a trunk or parcel belonging to us as passengers. The masters &amp; crew's trunks &amp; cabin lockers &amp; draws being <span class=highlight_yellow>examined</span>, the seals to <span class=highlight_yellow>re</span><span class=highlight_yellow>m</span><span class=highlight_yellow>a</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ce</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span> upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>karabis</span> until the collector came on board to search the ship.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening we walked about the town which is perfectly good for the plaice &amp; the fort exceedingly strong being covered with cannons &amp; having a garrison. I know not of how many men. I should think not numerous. The mole where the merchants vessels lay is a fine reservoir or wet dock capable of containing several hundred ships &amp; water enough for them to take in the whole of their cargos. There is also another mole for the men-of-war. We strolled about the town the whole of the evening &amp; when we looked at our watches much to our astonishment we found at nearly 12 o'clock  &amp; quite day light. In fact it is light all night here in summer. We returned to the ship, had our glass of spirit &amp; water &amp; turned in.</p>","pageId":746,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2247,"lock":null}
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/2307
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2307,"version":2,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":29,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... debt. I should also mention that before the ship got to the mole, party of customs house officers came on board &amp; immediately scaled down all the hatches&amp; everything on board in the shape of a trunk or parcel belonging to us as passengers. The masters &amp; crew's trunks &amp; cabin lockers &amp; draws being <span class=highlight_yellow>examined</span>, the seals to <span class=highlight_yellow>re</span><span class=highlight_yellow>m</span><span class=highlight_yellow>a</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ce</span><span class=highlight_yellow>r</span> upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>karabis</span> until the collector came on board to search the ship.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening we walked about the town which is perfectly good for the plaice &amp; the fort exceedingly strong being covered with cannons &amp; having a garrison. I know not of how many men. I should think not numerous. The mole where the merchants vessels lay is a fine reservoir or wet dock capable of containing several hundred ships &amp; water enough for them to take in the whole of their cargos. There is also another mole for the men-of-war. We strolled about the town the whole of the evening &amp; when we looked at our watches much to our astonishment we found at nearly 12 o'clock  &amp; quite day light. In fact it is light all night here in summer. We returned to the ship, had our glass of spirit &amp; water &amp; turned in.</p>","pageId":746,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2247,"lock":null}
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2308
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2308,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":30,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>... some prayer. Returned to the ship about 11 o'clock. Had a glass of cool brandy &amp; water &amp; went to bed</p>","pageId":747,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2248,"lock":null}
14:36:41.518 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
