14:36:41.520 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2310,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":4.0000,"text":"<p>... took a long stroll down the New <span class=highlight_yellow>Ky</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Prosped</span>, the fashionable &amp; finest street in Pitusby. It is about 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>wests</span> in length &amp; having <span class=highlight_yellow>trus</span> on each side between the froth pavement &amp; road which adds much to its beauty. Returned to our lodgings about 11 o'clock completely knocked up &amp; foot sore.</p>","pageId":749,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2250,"lock":null}
14:36:41.520 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2311
14:36:41.520 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2311,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... long there as it threatened another storm, we therefor got into our boat, but  had not been long on board before the rain came down in torrents with most awful  thunder &amp; lightning. It however cleared up again before we reached our landing place. These gardens are about two miles or more from Petersburg &amp; where the people flocked to in thousands on a Sunday. The walks upon this &amp; neighbouring islands are beautiful. We fortunately had a boat with an awning over it.</p>\r\n<p>On our return took a glass of grog &amp; went to bed</p>","pageId":751,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2251,"lock":null}
