14:36:41.520 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2311,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... long there as it threatened another storm, we therefor got into our boat, but  had not been long on board before the rain came down in torrents with most awful  thunder &amp; lightning. It however cleared up again before we reached our landing place. These gardens are about two miles or more from Petersburg &amp; where the people flocked to in thousands on a Sunday. The walks upon this &amp; neighbouring islands are beautiful. We fortunately had a boat with an awning over it.</p>\r\n<p>On our return took a glass of grog &amp; went to bed</p>","pageId":751,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2251,"lock":null}
14:36:41.520 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2312
14:36:41.520 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2312,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":7,"sequence":6.0000,"text":"<p>... city of Petersburg, it contains only three very small rooms, something after this plan <font color=#00B0F0>[See figure]</font>  Here is also to be see the boat which he built himself. How it is <span class=highlight_yellow>made</span> known he was an excellent carpenter &amp; used to row in. In the Citadel church there are some beautiful things in ivory of his turning &amp; workmanship.</p>\r\n<p>Dined with Mr Gillibrand only his wife &amp; Mr Lindsey there. Spent a very quiet day &amp; left early being foreign port day, which over the water &amp; took tea with a friend of Mr Lumleys &amp; Bob &amp; I afterwards had a stroll down the Mews by Prospect to see the people &amp; illuminations for the Emperors birthday. They don't as with us place candle &amp; light in the windows etc, but <span class=highlight_yellow>feet</span> what they call <span class=highlight_yellow>fat pots</span> along the street upon the edge of the pavement &amp; most horrible <span class=highlight_yellow>effluence</span> they send forth. We got to bed about 12 o'clock</p>","pageId":752,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2252,"lock":null}
14:36:41.520 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.521 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/2312
