14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2318,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... humour to go on shore. Obliged to go to bed. The pain &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>opium</span> making me exceptionally drowsy. Bought some flannel &amp; hartshorn in the evening which I put upon my face when I went to bed</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2258,"lock":null}
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2319
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2319,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... not inhabited. They are all within a stone's throw of each other. After passing Ertholmene, we had a most delightful sail under the Island of Bornholm &amp; a good view of it. This is one of the richest and most beautiful islands that can be imagined. It is in fact a perfect garden &amp; to us had all the appearance of a gentleman's park. The soil is good &amp; exceedingly productive yielding as much in one season as would keep the inhabitants several years. A boat came out to us from the shore &amp; we purchased of them four ducks &frac34; score of eggs &amp; 2 pounds of butter for which we gave only 6/6</p>\r\n<p>When we reached the west end of the island then wind took us all at a <span class=highlight_yellow>lk</span>, but soon favoured us again. In the evening it became quite calm. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock the captain, Bob &amp; I as usual had our grog &amp; being in the humour, <span class=highlight_yellow>had</span> some supper &amp; had a regular jollification, blew a cloud &amp; got to roost between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2259,"lock":null}
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/2319
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2319,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":5,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... not inhabited. They are all within a stone's throw of each other. After passing Ertholmene, we had a most delightful sail under the Island of Bornholm &amp; a good view of it. This is one of the richest and most beautiful islands that can be imagined. It is in fact a perfect garden &amp; to us had all the appearance of a gentleman's park. The soil is good &amp; exceedingly productive yielding as much in one season as would keep the inhabitants several years. A boat came out to us from the shore &amp; we purchased of them four ducks &frac34; score of eggs &amp; 2 pounds of butter for which we gave only 6/6</p>\r\n<p>When we reached the west end of the island then wind took us all at a <span class=highlight_yellow>lk</span>, but soon favoured us again. In the evening it became quite calm. At &frac12; past 8 o'clock the captain, Bob &amp; I as usual had our grog &amp; being in the humour, <span class=highlight_yellow>had</span> some supper &amp; had a regular jollification, blew a cloud &amp; got to roost between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2259,"lock":null}
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/232
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":232,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind SE Engaged in the office with Robert. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; took a warm bath. Dined with Mrs Scott. Walked in the evening to Carr's Wall Spout The Hope got under it in the morning &amp; to come off at night with 13 or 14 Keels. The remainder to follow</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":221,"lock":null}
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/232
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":232,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine day. Wind SE Engaged in the office with Robert. Walked to Tynemouth &amp; took a warm bath. Dined with Mrs Scott. Walked in the evening to Carr's Wall Spout The Hope got under it in the morning &amp; to come off at night with 13 or 14 Keels. The remainder to follow</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":221,"lock":null}
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2320
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2320,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>.. glass of wine with him &amp; I don't know how to account for it, excepting it was drinking upon an empty stomach but I really got muzzy of which I was sensible enough to feel heartily ashamed when I had to appear in the presence of Mr ships Chapmans. Got on board a little after 12 o'clock after one or two adventured before we left the town H French's ship, the 3 Brothers &amp; several other vessels passed us upward bound between Copenhagen &amp; Elsinore</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2260,"lock":null}
14:36:41.524 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/2320
14:36:41.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2320,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>.. glass of wine with him &amp; I don't know how to account for it, excepting it was drinking upon an empty stomach but I really got muzzy of which I was sensible enough to feel heartily ashamed when I had to appear in the presence of Mr ships Chapmans. Got on board a little after 12 o'clock after one or two adventured before we left the town H French's ship, the 3 Brothers &amp; several other vessels passed us upward bound between Copenhagen &amp; Elsinore</p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2260,"lock":null}
14:36:41.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2321
14:36:41.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2321,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the stateroom scuttle light, wet my bed &amp; I did not expect to have had one to sleep in tonight, indeed had the gale continued I should not have cared about it, but I contrived by placing canvas between the bed and sides of the vessel to fortify it pretty well from the wet &amp; thus gained a better nights rest than I anticipated.</p>\r\n<p>My face beginning to swell again, but no pain.</p>","pageId":766,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2261,"lock":null}
14:36:41.525 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
