14:36:41.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":2324,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":28,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... were compelled to give the ship the whole chain. Wind WNW &amp; cloudy. Dismal weather with rain. A light ship close by us drove &amp; another broke his chain &amp; sun down the river. Continued blowing hard all day with heavy showers of rain &amp; squalls &amp; towards evening the wind got to about N by W but the tide not answering. <span class=highlight_yellow>Till</span> near dark, we lay still, indeed it blew too hard to think of getting under way &amp; one or two vessels that weighed were soon obliged to bring up again</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2264,"lock":null}
14:36:41.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/2325
14:36:41.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":2325,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... since I had the pleasure of seeing him. We afterwards took a Greenwich boat &amp; went down to the Hope upon Dowslands way where we dined off cold mutton. At low water looked at her bottom &amp; gave orders for her to go into the dock to be caulked. Turned out an exceptionally wet evening. Had our tea on board &amp; afterwards took a <span class=highlight_yellow>Mackware</span> stage to Leadenhall Street &amp; then walked to New Inn. Bob Marsh at the theatre.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":2265,"lock":null}
14:36:41.527 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
