14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":234,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. The Hope got safe down from the spout having taken in 13 keels &amp; 6 char. The remainder followed her down &amp; we got to sea about &frac12; past 1 o'clock PM wind about NE but very little of it so that we did not get much beyond Sunderland before dark. Gave Richardson &amp; Davidson notice of appeal against the land tax for the property in Shields &amp; Preston. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":222,"lock":null}
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/235
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":235,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Quite calm during the whole of the night Got up at 8 o'clock &amp; found we were only off Hartlepool A heavy rain early in the morning &amp; a change of wind to about S. A large steam boat passed us for Leith at 9 o'clock. The weather fine but still little wind &amp; continued moderate all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":223,"lock":null}
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/235
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":235,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Quite calm during the whole of the night Got up at 8 o'clock &amp; found we were only off Hartlepool A heavy rain early in the morning &amp; a change of wind to about S. A large steam boat passed us for Leith at 9 o'clock. The weather fine but still little wind &amp; continued moderate all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":223,"lock":null}
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/236
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":236,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am off Whitby. Wind about SE by S &amp; SSE during the day heavy squalls with rain &amp; a little thunder &amp; lightning. Obliged to take in sail until at last we only carried two close reefed topsails, reefed trysail &amp; fore topmast staysail before dark the wind got to W by S &amp; WSW when off Robin Hood's bay &amp; increased to a heavy gale &amp; tremendous sea which lasted all night, continued on the starboard tack until 6 o'clock Sunday morning. Still blowing a gale with heavy sea. Up all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":224,"lock":null}
14:36:41.530 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/236
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":236,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am off Whitby. Wind about SE by S &amp; SSE during the day heavy squalls with rain &amp; a little thunder &amp; lightning. Obliged to take in sail until at last we only carried two close reefed topsails, reefed trysail &amp; fore topmast staysail before dark the wind got to W by S &amp; WSW when off Robin Hood's bay &amp; increased to a heavy gale &amp; tremendous sea which lasted all night, continued on the starboard tack until 6 o'clock Sunday morning. Still blowing a gale with heavy sea. Up all night</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":224,"lock":null}
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/237
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":237,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am rose. Ship a little to the north of Flamborough Head &amp; stood in on the eastbound tack. Wind about W &amp; W by N. Made Robin Hood's bay at 11 o'clock am tacked &amp; stood to the southward again wind &amp; weather now moderate, set main staysail. At 12 o'clock let a reef out of top sails at 1 o'clock set main sail. Turned out a beautiful summers afternoon with a fine breeze, about 6 o'clock lay too under Flamborough head, unbent &amp; repaired foresail at 8 o'clock, again got underway with a fine westerly breeze to cross the Dups. Drank a glass of porter, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":225,"lock":null}
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/237
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":237,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 6 o'clock am rose. Ship a little to the north of Flamborough Head &amp; stood in on the eastbound tack. Wind about W &amp; W by N. Made Robin Hood's bay at 11 o'clock am tacked &amp; stood to the southward again wind &amp; weather now moderate, set main staysail. At 12 o'clock let a reef out of top sails at 1 o'clock set main sail. Turned out a beautiful summers afternoon with a fine breeze, about 6 o'clock lay too under Flamborough head, unbent &amp; repaired foresail at 8 o'clock, again got underway with a fine westerly breeze to cross the Dups. Drank a glass of porter, smoked a pipe &amp; turned in between 9 &amp; 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":704,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":225,"lock":null}
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/238
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":238,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock. Found the ship off Dunlengton Church with a fine leading wind from W by S about two points worse than last night. A fine morning, towards evening began to blow fresh. Found the fore topmast backstay spring, secured it with a tackle &amp; took in a reef being rather squally Turned in about &frac12; past 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":226,"lock":null}
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/238
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":238,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock. Found the ship off Dunlengton Church with a fine leading wind from W by S about two points worse than last night. A fine morning, towards evening began to blow fresh. Found the fore topmast backstay spring, secured it with a tackle &amp; took in a reef being rather squally Turned in about &frac12; past 9 o'clock</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":226,"lock":null}
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/239
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":239,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Looked out a little after 4 o'clock am. Found we had got a change of wind about 2 o'clock from about WNW. An agreeable change for us, making all sail. The ship passed the floating light at 3 o'clock, reached Cromer at ____. Passed through Yarmouth Roads at 11 o'clock &amp; brought up being high water, at &frac12; past. Off Golaton, the <span class=highlight_yellow>Dalryaple</span> &amp; Nancy in company. Wind about W &amp; by S. The latter ship from Archangel Captain Stormont came on board to dinner. At 5 pm being low-water got underway with a light breeze from the W by S &amp; sailed out of St Nicholas Gateway &amp; beat to the southern water highwater between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock, when we brought up for the tide between the reefs points about 4 miles to the south of Southwold, between 1 &amp; 2 o'clock am. After supper, turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":705,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":227,"lock":null}
14:36:41.531 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
