14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/261
14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":261,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<p>Rather cloudy in the morning. Wind NE but afterwards turned out an exceedingly fine day. Started at &frac12; past 10 o'clock am with the following party in two sociables &amp; a gig upon a tour round the island viz: Mr Rebecca &amp; Laura Lee, Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS, self &amp; two servants. Stopped &amp; saw Shanklin Chine, called &amp; left our luggage at Ventnor. Drove on to &amp; saw Appuldurcombe the seat of Lord Yarborough containing several fine paintings &amp; finely situated. Returned to Ventnor to dinner &amp; slept. A very pleasant &amp; agreeable party</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":245,"lock":null}
14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/261
14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":261,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":30,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<p>Rather cloudy in the morning. Wind NE but afterwards turned out an exceedingly fine day. Started at &frac12; past 10 o'clock am with the following party in two sociables &amp; a gig upon a tour round the island viz: Mr Rebecca &amp; Laura Lee, Captain &amp; Mrs Lewis, F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS, self &amp; two servants. Stopped &amp; saw Shanklin Chine, called &amp; left our luggage at Ventnor. Drove on to &amp; saw Appuldurcombe the seat of Lord Yarborough containing several fine paintings &amp; finely situated. Returned to Ventnor to dinner &amp; slept. A very pleasant &amp; agreeable party</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":245,"lock":null}
14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/262
14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":262,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather cloudy. Wind NE. F Barclay &amp; I got up early &amp; bathed. Started after breakfast &amp; travelled along undercliff &amp; saw the difficult gentlemans seats. Most beautiful &amp; romantic well wooded &amp; cliffs very grand. Stopped at Blackgang Chine, immense high cliffs with waterfall, continued our journey through a beautiful &amp; well cultivated country to Freshwater Bay, where we had lunch about 4 o'clock. Captain Lewis &amp; the ladies went by land to see the Needles. F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS and self &amp; two servants went by water &amp; got very well to the Needles which with the cave &amp; majestic chalk cliffs, were very grand. But our return was attended with much unpleasantness to say the least, having an ebb tide &amp; strong wind against us &amp; being in a bad and cranky sea boat, we all got most uncomfortably wet by the spray of the sea. With much difficulty got back to Freshwater Bay to an 8 o'clock dinner. This is a very retired &amp; pretty place</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":246,"lock":null}
14:36:41.542 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/262
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":262,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":8,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning but rather cloudy. Wind NE. F Barclay &amp; I got up early &amp; bathed. Started after breakfast &amp; travelled along undercliff &amp; saw the difficult gentlemans seats. Most beautiful &amp; romantic well wooded &amp; cliffs very grand. Stopped at Blackgang Chine, immense high cliffs with waterfall, continued our journey through a beautiful &amp; well cultivated country to Freshwater Bay, where we had lunch about 4 o'clock. Captain Lewis &amp; the ladies went by land to see the Needles. F Barclay, Bob Marsh, WBS and self &amp; two servants went by water &amp; got very well to the Needles which with the cave &amp; majestic chalk cliffs, were very grand. But our return was attended with much unpleasantness to say the least, having an ebb tide &amp; strong wind against us &amp; being in a bad and cranky sea boat, we all got most uncomfortably wet by the spray of the sea. With much difficulty got back to Freshwater Bay to an 8 o'clock dinner. This is a very retired &amp; pretty place</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":246,"lock":null}
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/263
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":263,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind still from the NE. F Barclay, WBS &amp; I bathed &amp; after breakfast started for Newport where after passing through a pretty country, we arrived about 2 o'clock, stopping to see Carisbrooke Castle on the way. After lunch continued our journey to East Cows, where we dined. <del>For</del> Previously crossing the water to see West Cowes &amp; in the evening, after a most delightful tour &amp; favored with most beautiful weather. We all returned safe to Navarino House much pleased &amp; satisfied. Expenses of the tour &pound;3.10.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":247,"lock":null}
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/263
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":263,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind still from the NE. F Barclay, WBS &amp; I bathed &amp; after breakfast started for Newport where after passing through a pretty country, we arrived about 2 o'clock, stopping to see Carisbrooke Castle on the way. After lunch continued our journey to East Cows, where we dined. <del>For</del> Previously crossing the water to see West Cowes &amp; in the evening, after a most delightful tour &amp; favored with most beautiful weather. We all returned safe to Navarino House much pleased &amp; satisfied. Expenses of the tour &pound;3.10.</p>","pageId":707,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":247,"lock":null}
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/264
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":264,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind fresh from the NE. After taking an early breakfast F Barclay, Bob Marsh &amp; I embarked in the Geo<font color=#BFBFBF>rge</font> IV steam boat &amp; went to see Southampton, stopping &frac12; home at Cowes on the way, &amp; after spending a very pleasant day returned to Ryde to dinner. William left for Town</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":248,"lock":null}
14:36:41.543 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
