14:36:41.545 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":265,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still delightful weather. Wind variable between NE &amp; NW but returned to the old quarter NE in the afternoon again. Strolled about the town &amp; pier all day. Dined at Navarino</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":249,"lock":null}
14:36:41.545 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/266
14:36:41.545 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":266,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind NE. Changed to NW &amp; N with thunder &amp; lightning &amp; apparently heavy rain in Hampshire, but returned to the old quarter at night. F Barclay left us this morning for London. Sorry to loose him, a pleasant fellow. Mr Lee &amp; Laura in the chaise &amp; the rest walked to Binstead to see the abbey of which there is little remaining, after lunching on the grass with difficulty &amp; getting our feet covered with mud. We returned home by the beach.</p>","pageId":708,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":250,"lock":null}
14:36:41.545 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
