14:36:41.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":287,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A glorious day. Not a cloud to be seen. Wind SW. After breakfast Lewis, Fanny, Bob Marsh took a boat &amp; sailed round to Brading Harbour. Much pleased with the views of the country &amp; coast &amp; delighted with our sail. Got back at &frac12; past 3 pm. Received a letter from William of the arrival of the Hope but too late for yesterdays market.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":271,"lock":null}
14:36:41.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/288
14:36:41.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":288,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":9,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind SW to W. After breakfast walked to Binstead parsonage, about 1 mile, from Naravinos. In my opinion the prettiest &amp; most picturesque place in the island. The grounds laid out with great taste &amp; kept in the highest order. The views from them very fine. Wrote to William of my intention to be in town on Sunday.</p>","pageId":709,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":272,"lock":null}
14:36:41.554 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
