14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":297,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind South. Got underway from off _____ at 11 o'clock am with a fresh breeze, landed William at Gravesend. At 1 o'clock pm. At 4 o'clock passed through Shoe Hole 8 o'clock abreast of Harwich &amp; 10 o'clock off the Lowestoft Light &amp; turned in for the night. Blowing fresh.</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":281,"lock":null}
14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/298
14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/298
14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":298,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing hard all night with rain towards morning. Got up at 8 o'clock am. Wind just changed to WNW, rather squally. Ship off Cromer. At 11 o'clock abreast of the floating light. Blowing hard from West. Ship under foresail &amp; reefed topsail, mainsail &amp; double reefed main topsail &amp; reefed trysail. At 2 o'clock pm double reefed fore-top-sail. At 3 o'clock made the Spurn <font color=#BFBFBF>[Point]</font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font> being off the floating light. Still blowing strong from the West</p>","pageId":710,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":282,"lock":null}
14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/299
14:36:41.559 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":299,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":6,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>About 7 o'clock got bound. Flamborough Head at 10 o'clock. Off Robin Hoods bay blowing hard with squalls at 11 o'clock between the bay &amp; Whitby met a fleet of London vessels. Blowing hard. Nearly run down one vessel owing to his own obstinacy or keeping a bad lookout. Stowed trysail &amp; main sail &amp; took in jib. Very dark ahead. At 12 o'clock or little after it, clear weather but continued to blow off Hunt Cliff Foot. Turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":283,"lock":null}
