14:36:41.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":30,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. The air rather cool. Wind NW. Went over the water &amp; called upon Mr Heatley . Dined at Mr Tibbs, Tynemouth</p>","pageId":688,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":27,"lock":null}
14:36:41.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/300
14:36:41.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":300,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 5 o'clock am off Sunderland with fine weather. Wind about WSW. Got a pilot on board. At 6 o'clock brought up off Shields Bar, turned out dressed &amp; landed in Tynemouth Haven. Breakfasted in Dockwray Square. Mrs Scott not up being rather unwell. Went up to Newcastle but the Carrs busy from a fortnight to three weeks, returned to Shields by steam &amp; fixed the Hope to take Burdon main to be load up under the spout on Friday. The ship towed safe into the harbour by a steam boat. Blowing a gale of wind from about WSW. Dined with Mrs Scott. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":284,"lock":null}
14:36:41.560 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/300
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":300,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 5 o'clock am off Sunderland with fine weather. Wind about WSW. Got a pilot on board. At 6 o'clock brought up off Shields Bar, turned out dressed &amp; landed in Tynemouth Haven. Breakfasted in Dockwray Square. Mrs Scott not up being rather unwell. Went up to Newcastle but the Carrs busy from a fortnight to three weeks, returned to Shields by steam &amp; fixed the Hope to take Burdon main to be load up under the spout on Friday. The ship towed safe into the harbour by a steam boat. Blowing a gale of wind from about WSW. Dined with Mrs Scott. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":284,"lock":null}
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/301
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":301,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Received a letter from William with the Hope's Balance Note for &pound;63.18/-  Engaged all the morning on board ship. Got the ballast out. Dined at home. Mrs Scott not well. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. W Temple there. Won 10/- at whist. Several ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":285,"lock":null}
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/301
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":301,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Received a letter from William with the Hope's Balance Note for &pound;63.18/-  Engaged all the morning on board ship. Got the ballast out. Dined at home. Mrs Scott not well. Spent the evening at J Tinleys. W Temple there. Won 10/- at whist. Several ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":285,"lock":null}
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/302
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":302,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Made the Hope's book up. On board the ship under the spout. Got some keels in. Set the new for-topmast backstays. The Lady Jane arrived from Greenland with 15 fish, a full ship. Gave Stephenson &pound;30. Made an agreement with the washerwoman for the quarter at 1 &frac12; guinea. Dined with J Tindley. Won at whist 4/-</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":286,"lock":null}
14:36:41.561 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/302
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":302,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Made the Hope's book up. On board the ship under the spout. Got some keels in. Set the new for-topmast backstays. The Lady Jane arrived from Greenland with 15 fish, a full ship. Gave Stephenson &pound;30. Made an agreement with the washerwoman for the quarter at 1 &frac12; guinea. Dined with J Tindley. Won at whist 4/-</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":286,"lock":null}
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/303
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":303,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind WSW with a shower of rain at 1 o'clock. Mr Mark went on board the Hope with me &amp; had some soup at 4 o'clock pm. The Hope load up &amp; at 5 o'clock got to sea with a fine leading wind &amp; beautiful weather &amp; prospect of making a quick passage. Burdon Main loaded her for 15 keels &amp; 6 char. Dined with J Tinley, J Dale, mark &amp; Temple there. Won at whist 16/6 Gave Stephenson 35 to pay pilotage etc. with.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":287,"lock":null}
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/303
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":303,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind WSW with a shower of rain at 1 o'clock. Mr Mark went on board the Hope with me &amp; had some soup at 4 o'clock pm. The Hope load up &amp; at 5 o'clock got to sea with a fine leading wind &amp; beautiful weather &amp; prospect of making a quick passage. Burdon Main loaded her for 15 keels &amp; 6 char. Dined with J Tinley, J Dale, mark &amp; Temple there. Won at whist 16/6 Gave Stephenson 35 to pay pilotage etc. with.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":287,"lock":null}
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/304
14:36:41.562 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":304,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":10,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind about WNW. Went to Newcastle &amp; saw the Dixons, Smith of Joyston &amp; returned with J Tinley to dinner. Wrote to William of the sailing of the Hope. A few ships got to sea.</p>","pageId":711,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":288,"lock":null}
