14:36:41.572 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":326,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Wind NW. Out shooting, no sport, the dog being tired by having been at Warkworth &amp; the birds wild. Dined at Mr A Moises. <span class=highlight_yellow>Amble</span> &amp; spent a very pleasant day. The party consisting of Major Mr &amp; Miss Clatterburn, Mr &amp; Mrs Moises, Mr Elliott, Tom &amp; Fanny Smith, self &amp; Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>I Ord</span>. Received a letter from master of the Hope being to sail on Thursday from London</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":309,"lock":null}
14:36:41.572 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/327
14:36:41.572 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":327,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day. Wind NNW. Went to Warkworth Church in the morning. Called upon Mr &amp; Miss Watons. Drove Fanny &amp; Bell Smith &amp; Emma Galbraith in the afternoon. Robert Brown walked down from Brinkburn, dined &amp; stayed all night. Spent a jolly evening.</p>","pageId":713,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":310,"lock":null}
14:36:41.572 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
