14:36:41.583 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":35,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":1,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine day &amp; mild. Wind SSW to WSW. Engaged in the morning in examining my father's old papers &amp; accounts in search of the Ariel's vouchers and burning such papers as were out of date &amp; useless. Dined at home &amp; at the whist club in the evening.</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":32,"lock":null}
14:36:41.583 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/350
14:36:41.583 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":350,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly pleasant day. Wind W by S. Employed all the morning in unpacking the <span class=highlight_yellow>tenure</span> books we brought from Ireland. Dined at Mr Craiges, a large party.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":333,"lock":null}
14:36:41.583 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/350
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":350,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly pleasant day. Wind W by S. Employed all the morning in unpacking the <span class=highlight_yellow>tenure</span> books we brought from Ireland. Dined at Mr Craiges, a large party.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":333,"lock":null}
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/351
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":351,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair day. Wind W. Received a letter this morning from William of Frys &amp; Chapmans failure which surprised me much, the consequence was a run upon Chapmans <span class=highlight_yellow>House</span> here, but which I believe ended towards the evening. The bank are otherwise not affected by Frys failure having known for a fortnight it was to happen &amp; consequently preparing for a run, they suffer no losses. At the theatre in the evening. Much amused.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":334,"lock":null}
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/351
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":351,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fair day. Wind W. Received a letter this morning from William of Frys &amp; Chapmans failure which surprised me much, the consequence was a run upon Chapmans <span class=highlight_yellow>House</span> here, but which I believe ended towards the evening. The bank are otherwise not affected by Frys failure having known for a fortnight it was to happen &amp; consequently preparing for a run, they suffer no losses. At the theatre in the evening. Much amused.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":334,"lock":null}
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/352
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":352,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind NW to W &amp; WSW towards the evening. Took a walk with Emma &amp; called upon Mrs Paul &amp; Sharp. Wrote to William but forgot to put the letter into the post. At the whist club in the evening. No run upon Chapmans today. All quiet &amp; business going as usual.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":335,"lock":null}
14:36:41.584 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/352
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":352,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold morning. Wind NW to W &amp; WSW towards the evening. Took a walk with Emma &amp; called upon Mrs Paul &amp; Sharp. Wrote to William but forgot to put the letter into the post. At the whist club in the evening. No run upon Chapmans today. All quiet &amp; business going as usual.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":335,"lock":null}
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/353
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":353,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind about West. Attended a meeting of the Commissioners under the new act to appeal against the rate of the House in Dockwray Square &amp; got it reduced from &pound;50 to &pound;45. Took a walk with Emma &amp; showed her the glass exhibition. Received a letter from William. No account of the Hope. Drew upon Chapmans for &pound;5 for self.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":336,"lock":null}
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/353
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":353,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day. Wind about West. Attended a meeting of the Commissioners under the new act to appeal against the rate of the House in Dockwray Square &amp; got it reduced from &pound;50 to &pound;45. Took a walk with Emma &amp; showed her the glass exhibition. Received a letter from William. No account of the Hope. Drew upon Chapmans for &pound;5 for self.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":336,"lock":null}
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/354
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":354,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day. Wind ESE. A few light ships got in. Finished a long letter to William a continuation to that which I forgot to put into the post on Thursday &amp; enclosing Turner's letter from Carlow, sent them off. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at Mr Allens. A very wet afternoon &amp; night.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":337,"lock":null}
14:36:41.585 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/354
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":354,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day. Wind ESE. A few light ships got in. Finished a long letter to William a continuation to that which I forgot to put into the post on Thursday &amp; enclosing Turner's letter from Carlow, sent them off. Dined at home. Attended the whist club at Mr Allens. A very wet afternoon &amp; night.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":337,"lock":null}
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/355
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":355,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very stormy &amp; rainy morning with a gale of wind from ESE to E by N. &amp; high sea upon the bar. I went to church in the morning. A continuation of rain &amp; much heavier. Dined with J Tinley. Received a letter from William of the Hope's arrival. Old Mr Metcalf of Tynemouth died very suddenly this morning during church time.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":338,"lock":null}
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/355
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":355,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":11,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very stormy &amp; rainy morning with a gale of wind from ESE to E by N. &amp; high sea upon the bar. I went to church in the morning. A continuation of rain &amp; much heavier. Dined with J Tinley. Received a letter from William of the Hope's arrival. Old Mr Metcalf of Tynemouth died very suddenly this morning during church time.</p>","pageId":715,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":338,"lock":null}
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/356
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":356,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Early this morning it blew a very heavy gale of wind from the NE &amp; ENE with showers of rain &amp; heavy sea. Towards afternoon the wind abated but continued from the east. Engaged in the office the principal part of the morning. Wrote to William. Dined at home. Mr Wheatley buried a son &amp; daughter Mr Gun today. They died of consumption.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":339,"lock":null}
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/356
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":356,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Early this morning it blew a very heavy gale of wind from the NE &amp; ENE with showers of rain &amp; heavy sea. Towards afternoon the wind abated but continued from the east. Engaged in the office the principal part of the morning. Wrote to William. Dined at home. Mr Wheatley buried a son &amp; daughter Mr Gun today. They died of consumption.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":339,"lock":null}
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/357
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":357,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by S towards evening the wind got up &amp; increased to a perfect gale from the S by W &amp; excessively cold. Understand that several ships, all on shore, some near Sunderland. Walked with Mr Mark &amp; called upon Captain Bunbury &amp; Mr Hopkins. Dined at home. In the evening went to the Commercial to see Mr Ildeston who was waiting there for Mr Tibbs. Received an invitation &amp; suppered with the committee of Association for prosecuting felons. Sat rather late.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":340,"lock":null}
14:36:41.586 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.587 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/357
14:36:41.587 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":357,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind N by S towards evening the wind got up &amp; increased to a perfect gale from the S by W &amp; excessively cold. Understand that several ships, all on shore, some near Sunderland. Walked with Mr Mark &amp; called upon Captain Bunbury &amp; Mr Hopkins. Dined at home. In the evening went to the Commercial to see Mr Ildeston who was waiting there for Mr Tibbs. Received an invitation &amp; suppered with the committee of Association for prosecuting felons. Sat rather late.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":340,"lock":null}
14:36:41.587 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/358
14:36:41.587 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":358,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild day and wind about W by N. Walked to Tynemouth called at Tibbs upon Mr Ildeston who returned to Shields with me. Dined at home &amp; in the evening met Mr Ildeston at Mr Baskers to take wine. Mr Mark there.</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":341,"lock":null}
