14:36:41.589 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":363,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant winters morning. Wind NNW which changed in the afternoon to about WSW. Got &pound;5 from the bank for own use. Dined with J Tinley. Went to the theatre at <span class=highlight_yellow>the Prince</span>. Mrs Metcalf of Tynemouth buried today</p>","pageId":716,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":346,"lock":null}
14:36:41.589 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/364
14:36:41.589 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":364,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Milder wind WSW. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":347,"lock":null}
14:36:41.589 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/364
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":364,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant day. Milder wind WSW. Dined at home.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":347,"lock":null}
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/365
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":365,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold frosty day. Wind WNW. Went to Benton by the coach in the morning. Walked there from the turnpike &amp; afterwards onto Newcastle where I wrote to William to sell the Hope. Missed Dixons, walked out to Benton again to dinner. Mr Colonel Dixon staying there. Mr Allinson dined with us</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":348,"lock":null}
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/365
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":365,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine but cold frosty day. Wind WNW. Went to Benton by the coach in the morning. Walked there from the turnpike &amp; afterwards onto Newcastle where I wrote to William to sell the Hope. Missed Dixons, walked out to Benton again to dinner. Mr Colonel Dixon staying there. Mr Allinson dined with us</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":348,"lock":null}
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/366
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":366,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a stormy day &amp; cold. Wind WNW. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. A great day at Gosforth guns firing etc etc. Mr Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Bell married one the Miss Brandlengs. Returned to Benton to Dinner.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":349,"lock":null}
14:36:41.590 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/366
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":366,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":11,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Rather a stormy day &amp; cold. Wind WNW. Walked into Newcastle with Dixon. A great day at Gosforth guns firing etc etc. Mr Char<font color=#BFBFBF>les</font> Bell married one the Miss Brandlengs. Returned to Benton to Dinner.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":349,"lock":null}
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/367
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":367,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild day. Wind WNN. Out greyhound coursing. Ran 8 or 9 hares &amp; killed none. The dogs out of wind not having had any exercise lately. But had some pretty running.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":350,"lock":null}
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/367
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":367,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful mild day. Wind WNN. Out greyhound coursing. Ran 8 or 9 hares &amp; killed none. The dogs out of wind not having had any exercise lately. But had some pretty running.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":350,"lock":null}
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/368
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":368,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Exceedingly fine mild. More like summer than December. Walked with Dixon to Newcastle. Spent the morning there, took the steamer boat &amp; got to Shields at 3 o'clock. Dined with J Tinley in the evening at Mr Harry's. Then whist club. At night the wind got round to the east.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":351,"lock":null}
14:36:41.591 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/368
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":368,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Exceedingly fine mild. More like summer than December. Walked with Dixon to Newcastle. Spent the morning there, took the steamer boat &amp; got to Shields at 3 o'clock. Dined with J Tinley in the evening at Mr Harry's. Then whist club. At night the wind got round to the east.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":351,"lock":null}
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/369
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":369,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very foggy day &amp; unpleasant day. Wind about S by E. At church in the morning. Tinley, Mr Brereton of Liverpool &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined at Tinley's. Met Mr Brereton &amp; a Mr Smith of Oporto.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":352,"lock":null}
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/369
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":369,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very foggy day &amp; unpleasant day. Wind about S by E. At church in the morning. Tinley, Mr Brereton of Liverpool &amp; I walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon. Dined at Tinley's. Met Mr Brereton &amp; a Mr Smith of Oporto.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":352,"lock":null}
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/37
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":37,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, Wind WNW &amp; a slight frost. Dined at Mr Reeds, a large party. Received a letter from William with gratifying intelligence that Lees &amp; co had agreed to let me take the Hope upon mortgage the price &pound;1250 to pay all expenses incurred in the last two years making her stand me in about &pound;1350. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":34,"lock":null}
14:36:41.592 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/37
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":37,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day, Wind WNW &amp; a slight frost. Dined at Mr Reeds, a large party. Received a letter from William with gratifying intelligence that Lees &amp; co had agreed to let me take the Hope upon mortgage the price &pound;1250 to pay all expenses incurred in the last two years making her stand me in about &pound;1350. Wrote to William</p>","pageId":689,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":34,"lock":null}
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/370
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":370,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day but dry. Wind about S. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 34/6, a miserable price = 8/6 freight. After laying a fortnight at London. Dined at home. Wind changed to about SW in the evening.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":353,"lock":null}
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/370
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":370,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull day but dry. Wind about S. Received a letter from William of the sale of the Hope at 34/6, a miserable price = 8/6 freight. After laying a fortnight at London. Dined at home. Wind changed to about SW in the evening.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":353,"lock":null}
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/371
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":371,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind S &amp; SW. Went at Williams request to look for Baxter Arthur of the amety, but he had gone to sea. Called upon J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>io</font><sup>r</sup> Carr &amp; gave him William's letter to pay me the balance of the Hope's freight account. Dinned at home. Wrote to William. Payed into Chapmans &pound;15 rents on account of ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":354,"lock":null}
14:36:41.593 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/371
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":371,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind S &amp; SW. Went at Williams request to look for Baxter Arthur of the amety, but he had gone to sea. Called upon J<font color=#BFBFBF>u</font>n<font color=#BFBFBF>io</font><sup>r</sup> Carr &amp; gave him William's letter to pay me the balance of the Hope's freight account. Dinned at home. Wrote to William. Payed into Chapmans &pound;15 rents on account of ex<font color=#BFBFBF>ecut</font>ors</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":354,"lock":null}
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/372
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":372,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A little rain in the morning. Wind W &amp; SW. A pleasant afternoon. Dined on board the Combatant, Captain Barnes. A ship of the Tinleys, an agreeable party consisting of J Tinley, A Harry, Mr Boswell, Captain Webb, W Barnes, Mr Richardson &amp; self, went to the play at &frac12; price to pass an hour but returned home at 10 o'clock at which hour Mrs Scott had made up her mind I should be in. Her conduct towards me so pointed &amp; bad that I have determined to go to lodgings as I neither have nor do I wish to give her any annoyance at the same time. I don't choose to submit to it myself, for it seems her temper &amp; disposition neither to be happy &amp; comfortable herself or to let others be so.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":355,"lock":null}
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/372
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":372,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":12,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A little rain in the morning. Wind W &amp; SW. A pleasant afternoon. Dined on board the Combatant, Captain Barnes. A ship of the Tinleys, an agreeable party consisting of J Tinley, A Harry, Mr Boswell, Captain Webb, W Barnes, Mr Richardson &amp; self, went to the play at &frac12; price to pass an hour but returned home at 10 o'clock at which hour Mrs Scott had made up her mind I should be in. Her conduct towards me so pointed &amp; bad that I have determined to go to lodgings as I neither have nor do I wish to give her any annoyance at the same time. I don't choose to submit to it myself, for it seems her temper &amp; disposition neither to be happy &amp; comfortable herself or to let others be so.</p>","pageId":717,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":355,"lock":null}
14:36:41.594 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/373
