14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":392,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine winters day. Wind NE. Cols &amp; sea high at night, a little snow &amp; frost. Dined at home. Received a letter from William. Engaged most of the morning in the office writing. Mrs Dixon brought Emma home.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":374,"lock":null}
14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/393
14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":393,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold day with frost. Wind NE &amp; sea high. Walked to Preston with Robert &amp; Emma to talk to Moor about arrears of rent. Went on board the Hope. All safe. Dined at home. Mrs Marr called  in the evening with whom we agreed to send Emma to school the next morning. Suppered and smoked a few <span class=highlight_yellow>segar</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> with A Harry. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":375,"lock":null}
14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
