14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":393,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold day with frost. Wind NE &amp; sea high. Walked to Preston with Robert &amp; Emma to talk to Moor about arrears of rent. Went on board the Hope. All safe. Dined at home. Mrs Marr called  in the evening with whom we agreed to send Emma to school the next morning. Suppered and smoked a few <span class=highlight_yellow>segar</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> with A Harry. Wrote to William.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":375,"lock":null}
14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/394
14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":394,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":1,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day &amp; cold. Wind ENE &amp; E by N. Attended a general meeting of the ship owners &amp; entered into resolutions relative to the rate of timber freights for the <span class=highlight_yellow>ensuring</span> years &amp; agreed not to take less than 45/- for <span class=highlight_yellow>Quebec</span>, other ports in proportion. The meeting from the conflicting interests could come to no resolution with regard to the coal trade. Dined at home in the evening. Took wine &amp; suppered with A Harry, A French &amp; A Nicolson at the Albion. Called at the Mulstream.</p>","pageId":720,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":376,"lock":null}
14:36:41.604 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
