14:36:41.618 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":421,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning &amp; hard frost. Wind W &amp; W by S. A French &amp; I walked round the town with Mr Chapman of <span class=highlight_yellow>Elseneur</span> to call upon his friends. Dined at 2 o'clock with A Harry. On board the Choise, A French, A Nicholson, <span class=highlight_yellow>Drewing</span>, Cunningham, Mark ____, self &amp; Captain ____ Mr Bradshaw came on board. After dinner we spent a very pleasant day.</p>","pageId":722,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":403,"lock":null}
14:36:41.618 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/422
14:36:41.618 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":422,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":2,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind West. Passed part of the morning in drawing &amp; writing to William with Robert's account of <span class=highlight_yellow>seats</span>. Attended a meeting of shipowners &amp; masters for the purpose of establishing a asylum for aged &amp; infirm master mariners, an excellent institution &amp; long wasted the meeting most respectfully &amp; numerous attended &amp; then business well conducted &amp; a most liberal feeling persuading every person as the donation &amp; subscriptions best testified. Read a letter from Geo Dunn to know if I intended loading the Hope. Answered in the negative unless <span class=highlight_yellow>fieghted</span> or upheld. Dined at home. Mrs Scott  very unwell, but downstairs. Saw <span class=highlight_yellow>arr</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>&gamma;&alpha;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&lambda;&lambda;&omicron;</span><span class=highlight_yellow>&pi;</span></p>","pageId":723,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":404,"lock":null}
