14:36:41.630 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":448,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine frosty morning. Wind SE &amp; E by S. Went to Newcastle by steam. Could do nothing for the Hope. Walked up to Westgate Street &amp; the billiard rooms. Returned to Shields to dinner. Spent the latter part of the evening at J Tinleys</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":430,"lock":null}
14:36:41.630 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/449
14:36:41.630 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":449,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":3,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind NW. Went by steam to Newcastle. Nothing to be done for the Hope. Dined with Dixon Dixon. In the evening went to the theatre. Met the  <span class=highlight_yellow>Ildestons</span> there. A very thin house. The high sheriffs benefit. The Dixons &amp; Tom &amp; Bell Smith went to a ball given by the offices of the dragoon quarter at Newcastle.</p>","pageId":726,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":431,"lock":null}
