14:36:41.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":508,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW walked about the town with Tom Smith the principle part of the morning. Dined at home &amp; took a walk to Tynemouth after dinner. Accepted <span class=highlight_yellow>In</span> Hearn's bill for &pound;34.7/- at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>mo</span><span class=highlight_yellow>nth</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> dated 27 April, due 30 July, for repairing Hope's sails. A most extraordinary bill.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":490,"lock":null}
14:36:41.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/509
14:36:41.660 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":509,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant morning blowing rather fresh from NW by W. Walked with Tom Smith down to Low Town &amp; afterwards to Alec Sadlers at Whitle Point. Dined at home &amp; after tea again walked to Whitle Point but the sloop had not come down.</p>","pageId":732,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":491,"lock":null}
