14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":512,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning with showers. Wind SSW. Several light ships arrived. Tom &amp; Mrs Smith left us this morning for Benton. Dined at home. Accepted a bill at 3 <span class=highlight_yellow>months</span> dated 16 April for polices &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Insurance</span> 1 &amp; 2 coal voyages in general Premium Club &pound;13.7.10. With Bell Jervis in the evening</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":494,"lock":null}
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/513
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":513,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Called upon &amp; spent an hour with Fergusson the artist. Dined at home. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth with Fergusson to sketch the ruins. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Davies</span> Rooms at the Castle</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":495,"lock":null}
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/513
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":513,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SW. Called upon &amp; spent an hour with Fergusson the artist. Dined at home. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth with Fergusson to sketch the ruins. In the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Davies</span> Rooms at the Castle</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":495,"lock":null}
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/514
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":514,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant spring morning. Wind NNW. Changed during the day to NE &amp; again at night to W. Took a walk round by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. A beautiful summers day. Dined with Jackson 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment at the Castle. H Dale, Dacres, RA. Newton &amp; a Lieutenant Hamilton Brown there. (with 1<sup>st</sup> term)</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":496,"lock":null}
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/514
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":514,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A pleasant spring morning. Wind NNW. Changed during the day to NE &amp; again at night to W. Took a walk round by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. A beautiful summers day. Dined with Jackson 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment at the Castle. H Dale, Dacres, RA. Newton &amp; a Lieutenant Hamilton Brown there. (with 1<sup>st</sup> term)</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":496,"lock":null}
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/515
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":515,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning . A fine mild rain. Wind W by N. Called upon Fergusson Dined at home. The Hope arrived this evening after a fine passage. Left Gravesend on Wednesday morning.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":497,"lock":null}
14:36:41.662 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/515
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":515,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning . A fine mild rain. Wind W by N. Called upon Fergusson Dined at home. The Hope arrived this evening after a fine passage. Left Gravesend on Wednesday morning.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":497,"lock":null}
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/516
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":516,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning. Some showers during the night. Warmer growing weather at last. Wind W by N. Mr Fergusson &amp; I went to Newcastle by steam on the quay, but could do nothing for the Hope. Called upon Inspector Hodgson &amp; dined with him at his brothers. Returned to Shields in the evening. With Bell Jarvis, remained with her until 4 o'clock in the morning. Received from Geo Dunn &amp; sons &pound;27 being the difference between the freight made &amp; that upheld <span class=highlight_yellow>=rig</span>: 8/6</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":498,"lock":null}
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/516
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":516,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine spring morning. Some showers during the night. Warmer growing weather at last. Wind W by N. Mr Fergusson &amp; I went to Newcastle by steam on the quay, but could do nothing for the Hope. Called upon Inspector Hodgson &amp; dined with him at his brothers. Returned to Shields in the evening. With Bell Jarvis, remained with her until 4 o'clock in the morning. Received from Geo Dunn &amp; sons &pound;27 being the difference between the freight made &amp; that upheld <span class=highlight_yellow>=rig</span>: 8/6</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":498,"lock":null}
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/517
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":517,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning &amp; summers weather SE. Went with Emma to church. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry. Walked to Tynemouth in the  evening.</p>","pageId":733,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":499,"lock":null}
14:36:41.663 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
