14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/528
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":528,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock am been a fresh breeze all night from NE. Got round the Head at 5 o'clock am. A fine morning but rather dull. Had a good sun. About 9 o'clock Cromer. At 10 o'clock turned in being <span class=highlight_yellow>marhasborough</span>. Ann Stokes 1<sup>st</sup> <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span>.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":510,"lock":null}
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/528
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":528,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at 8 o'clock am been a fresh breeze all night from NE. Got round the Head at 5 o'clock am. A fine morning but rather dull. Had a good sun. About 9 o'clock Cromer. At 10 o'clock turned in being <span class=highlight_yellow>marhasborough</span>. Ann Stokes 1<sup>st</sup> <span class=highlight_yellow>time</span>.</p>","pageId":734,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":510,"lock":null}
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/529
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":529,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock am. Very thick weather, but a fine breeze at NE, then appeared to be off Yarmouth behind the sands. We ran until about 1 o'clock pm when we took in studding sails &amp; stood in for the land, which we made a little to the northward of Aldeburgh. The weather clearer from thence. We took our departure to run down <span class=highlight_yellow>raren</span> . About 4 o'clock it turned out a beautiful clear day. At 6 o'clock pm abreast of Orford. At 10 pm being dark, brought up abreast of the Hook of the middle. At a little after 12 o'clock went to bed. A fine moonlit night. With Ann Stokes again!!</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":511,"lock":null}
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/529
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":529,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up at 8 o'clock am. Very thick weather, but a fine breeze at NE, then appeared to be off Yarmouth behind the sands. We ran until about 1 o'clock pm when we took in studding sails &amp; stood in for the land, which we made a little to the northward of Aldeburgh. The weather clearer from thence. We took our departure to run down <span class=highlight_yellow>raren</span> . About 4 o'clock it turned out a beautiful clear day. At 6 o'clock pm abreast of Orford. At 10 pm being dark, brought up abreast of the Hook of the middle. At a little after 12 o'clock went to bed. A fine moonlit night. With Ann Stokes again!!</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":511,"lock":null}
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/53
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":53,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day and frosty, Wind WNW. Got the fore rigging over the mast head &amp; the main mast out &amp; found it much decayed both foot and head &amp; fear we shall be obliged to have a new one. Ordered a new bowsprit of Morton &amp; Thompson. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening with N Bird</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":50,"lock":null}
14:36:41.669 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
