14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":53,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day and frosty, Wind WNW. Got the fore rigging over the mast head &amp; the main mast out &amp; found it much decayed both foot and head &amp; fear we shall be obliged to have a new one. Ordered a new bowsprit of Morton &amp; Thompson. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening with N Bird</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":50,"lock":null}
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/530
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":530,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock <font color=#BFBFBF>[in]</font> the morning they got the ship under way, with a light breeze from the NE. At 7 o'clock I got up &amp; went upon deck, past through a large fleet of light ships. At 8 o'clock got the flood with a little more wind. Again passed a great number of light ships. Between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock brought up a little blow Gravesend. The crew went to bed early. Ann &amp; I walked the deck until after 10 o'clock. Sat up until 12 o'clock. Went to bed to Ann</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":512,"lock":null}
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/530
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":530,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>At 3 o'clock <font color=#BFBFBF>[in]</font> the morning they got the ship under way, with a light breeze from the NE. At 7 o'clock I got up &amp; went upon deck, past through a large fleet of light ships. At 8 o'clock got the flood with a little more wind. Again passed a great number of light ships. Between 5 &amp; 6 o'clock brought up a little blow Gravesend. The crew went to bed early. Ann &amp; I walked the deck until after 10 o'clock. Sat up until 12 o'clock. Went to bed to Ann</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":512,"lock":null}
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/531
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":531,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up about 7 o'clock. A most delightful morning. Wind unfortunately changed to W so that at the early morning tide, we could not move, There also being very little of it. After breakfast dressed myself &amp; landed at Gravesend about 11 o'clock, waited until <span class=highlight_yellow>about</span> 1 o'clock before I could get a coach. Got to town at 4 o'clock pm. Left the ships papers at the office &amp; got to Nottingham Place at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Found them all well &amp; glad to see me. Bob Marsh &amp; his father dined with us. Heavy rain in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":513,"lock":null}
14:36:41.670 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/531
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":531,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Got up about 7 o'clock. A most delightful morning. Wind unfortunately changed to W so that at the early morning tide, we could not move, There also being very little of it. After breakfast dressed myself &amp; landed at Gravesend about 11 o'clock, waited until <span class=highlight_yellow>about</span> 1 o'clock before I could get a coach. Got to town at 4 o'clock pm. Left the ships papers at the office &amp; got to Nottingham Place at &frac12; past 5 o'clock. Found them all well &amp; glad to see me. Bob Marsh &amp; his father dined with us. Heavy rain in the afternoon.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":513,"lock":null}
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/532
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":532,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but blowing hard from the N by E. William &amp; I walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh only a short time at the office, when Stephenson brought Ann up. I walked with her to Grays Inn, showed her St Pants, went round by Oxford &amp; Regents street &amp; Ann feet being very sore we after buying a pair of easy shoes, took a coach &amp; drove to  new inn. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; afterwards we all went to the pit at Covent garden Theatre. Ann much astonished at the size &amp; splendour of the houses. We saw Romeo &amp; Juliet performed by C Kenneth &amp; Mrs Smithson. Then afterwards the Devils Elixir, not worth seeing. Ann &amp; I slept at the Fountain in Catherine Street</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":514,"lock":null}
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/532
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":532,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning, but blowing hard from the N by E. William &amp; I walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh only a short time at the office, when Stephenson brought Ann up. I walked with her to Grays Inn, showed her St Pants, went round by Oxford &amp; Regents street &amp; Ann feet being very sore we after buying a pair of easy shoes, took a coach &amp; drove to  new inn. Dined with Bob Marsh &amp; afterwards we all went to the pit at Covent garden Theatre. Ann much astonished at the size &amp; splendour of the houses. We saw Romeo &amp; Juliet performed by C Kenneth &amp; Mrs Smithson. Then afterwards the Devils Elixir, not worth seeing. Ann &amp; I slept at the Fountain in Catherine Street</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":514,"lock":null}
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/533
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":533,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind still fresh from the N by E. We got breakfast at 11 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked into the Green park round by the Kings Place by Pall Mall to Somerset House &amp; saw the exhibition. Ann much pleased with her mornings <span class=highlight_yellow>amusements</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>took</span> &amp;  left in Grays Inn. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Changes</span>, did nothing with the ship &amp; walked to Nottingham Place to dinner. The Hope could not be sold today.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":515,"lock":null}
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/533
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":533,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful day. Wind still fresh from the N by E. We got breakfast at 11 o'clock &amp; afterwards walked into the Green park round by the Kings Place by Pall Mall to Somerset House &amp; saw the exhibition. Ann much pleased with her mornings <span class=highlight_yellow>amusements</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>took</span> &amp;  left in Grays Inn. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>Changes</span>, did nothing with the ship &amp; walked to Nottingham Place to dinner. The Hope could not be sold today.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":515,"lock":null}
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/534
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":534,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind blowing fresh at N by E. Called upon Mr ward. Walked into the city. On my way saw Ann. Attended the coal market with much difficulty they sold <span class=highlight_yellow>58/2</span> of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city. Saw Ann again. Called upon Richmond found him looking well, though still lame. Returned by Regents <span class=highlight_yellow>He</span> to Mr Lee to dinner. Bob marsh with us.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":516,"lock":null}
14:36:41.671 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/534
14:36:41.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":534,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind blowing fresh at N by E. Called upon Mr ward. Walked into the city. On my way saw Ann. Attended the coal market with much difficulty they sold <span class=highlight_yellow>58/2</span> of the Hope's cargo. Walked out of the city. Saw Ann again. Called upon Richmond found him looking well, though still lame. Returned by Regents <span class=highlight_yellow>He</span> to Mr Lee to dinner. Bob marsh with us.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":516,"lock":null}
14:36:41.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/535
14:36:41.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":535,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fine weather. Wind NE. Wrote to Mr Vernon to send <span class=highlight_yellow>Inspector</span> Galbraith to London. Walked into the city. Attended <span class=highlight_yellow>changers</span>. Did nothing. Dined with Richmond.</p>","pageId":735,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":517,"lock":null}
14:36:41.672 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
