14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":536,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning but fine weather. Wind still NE &amp; ENE. Mr Lee drove me into the city. Attended the local exchange. Sold 63 more of the Hope's coals. Went to the Royal Ex. Could not fix. Walked out of the city. Dined at Mr Lees. Mr &amp; Bob Marsh &amp; F Barclay there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":518,"lock":null}
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/537
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":537,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cloudy morning. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. He &amp; his father walked with me down to the Hope. Saw the St Catherine Docks in our way &amp; the most perfect &amp; comfortable perhaps of thing of the sort all the warehouses &amp; upon so good a place. Had lunch on board &amp; I afterwards attended changes but did nothing for the ship. Walked out of the city with Inspector Chapman &amp; dined with him. His brothers the captain, Thomas, Ben, Mr Graham &amp; a Mr Day there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":519,"lock":null}
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
