14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":537,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another cloudy morning. Wind NE. Walked into the city. Called upon Bob Marsh. He &amp; his father walked with me down to the Hope. Saw the St Catherine Docks in our way &amp; the most perfect &amp; comfortable perhaps of thing of the sort all the warehouses &amp; upon so good a place. Had lunch on board &amp; I afterwards attended changes but did nothing for the ship. Walked out of the city with Inspector Chapman &amp; dined with him. His brothers the captain, Thomas, Ben, Mr Graham &amp; a Mr Day there.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":519,"lock":null}
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/538
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":538,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind about N. Went with the Miss Lees to the chapel in Vern Street. Afterwards called upon Mr &amp; Mrs Lumley in Gower Street. Mr Lee very unwell, consumption, going to leave this <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span>. Called upon Mr Linskill. Went to see Mary &amp; Emma in Sloan Street &amp; then to the park. Dined with Mr ward &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":520,"lock":null}
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
