14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":538,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":5,"day":31,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull cloudy morning. Wind about N. Went with the Miss Lees to the chapel in Vern Street. Afterwards called upon Mr &amp; Mrs Lumley in Gower Street. Mr Lee very unwell, consumption, going to leave this <span class=highlight_yellow>home</span>. Called upon Mr Linskill. Went to see Mary &amp; Emma in Sloan Street &amp; then to the park. Dined with Mr ward &amp; spent a pleasant day.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":520,"lock":null}
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/539
14:36:41.673 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":539,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very dull morning &amp; light rain. Wind NW. Walked into the city. At the coal exchange the remainder of the Hope sold. Attended the Royal Exchange but could not fix the Hope. Walked to Mr Lees to dinner. Bob Marsh dined with us.</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":521,"lock":null}
