14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":540,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. Walked into the city. Saw Ann. Fixed the Hope for Petersburg with Mr Hubbard ar 26/-. <span class=highlight_yellow>&amp; </span><span class=highlight_yellow>iow</span><span class=highlight_yellow> for fellow</span>. Walked to Mr Lees to dinner. Bob Marsh there, he &amp; the guests having been to Kensington gardens</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":522,"lock":null}
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/541
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":541,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; very hot. Wind NW. Rode into the city. Went to the Bull at Alegate &amp; saw Ann Stokes set off for <span class=highlight_yellow>Hford</span>. Went to the ship with William, Bob Marsh &amp; Vincent , dined on board. Returned to Aldgate to meet Ann. Took her to Astleys theatre &amp; afterwards slept at the Fountain</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":523,"lock":null}
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/541
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":541,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; very hot. Wind NW. Rode into the city. Went to the Bull at Alegate &amp; saw Ann Stokes set off for <span class=highlight_yellow>Hford</span>. Went to the ship with William, Bob Marsh &amp; Vincent , dined on board. Returned to Aldgate to meet Ann. Took her to Astleys theatre &amp; afterwards slept at the Fountain</p>","pageId":736,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":523,"lock":null}
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/542
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":542,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... upon one of which, <span class=highlight_yellow>Yelagin</span>. We landed &amp; walked through the plantations, the walk of which are beautiful, in good order &amp; under the management of an English <span class=highlight_yellow>Lumana</span> &amp; and attached to a very fine palace of the Emperor that stands close to the water. Near it is a bridge which we crossed to the opposite Island of <span class=highlight_yellow>Kam</span><span class=highlight_yellow>enny</span>, at the end is a handsome theatre, placed there to be near this summer retreat of the Emperor's. This is a very fashionable theatre &amp; attended principally by the court, but I believe open to all. Here they perform French, Italian &amp; German operas. These islands are the property of the Emperor &amp; noblemen. The grounds most beautifully laid out &amp; always open to the public. The Russians being much more <span class=highlight_yellow>ce</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ri</span><span class=highlight_yellow>bal</span> in this respect than John Bull. They delight in seeing the people strolling about the grounds &amp; have seats placed in all directions for their accommodation. We then proceeded through these fairy grounds to the island of <span class=highlight_yellow>Kres</span><span class=highlight_yellow>tovsky</span> Island where Mr Dye has a cottage for the summer. Here we took tea with his family &amp; late in the evening returned to Petersburg which we did not reach till after 1 o'clock in the morning exceptionally tired with our walk</p>","pageId":750,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":524,"lock":null}
14:36:41.675 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
