14:36:41.678 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":548,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":5,"sequence":5.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance  of fine weather. Wind NW. Mr Lee drove me into the city. Walked down to the ship upon Dowland's Ways. The painters finished painting the cabin &amp; busy with the sides. Made a port hole into the state room. Moored the ship down in Duke Shore &amp; got ballast. Took boat to the tower &amp; walked from thence to  Mr Lees to dinner</p>","pageId":737,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":526,"lock":null}
14:36:41.678 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/549
14:36:41.678 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":549,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning &amp; a fresh breeze from NW. Walked into the city with William. Got a new hat at Olipharts. Called for Bob Marsh &amp; we afterwards went by water to the Hope. Walked home to dinner</p>","pageId":737,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":527,"lock":null}
14:36:41.678 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
