14:36:41.684 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":558,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out at &frac12; past 6 o'clock. Found that J Galbraith had kept his watch last night for the first time. Have had a fair breeze all night from the SW. Continuing our course NE with steering sail set at the rate of 6 knots. Got fishing line out but could not catch nothing. The ship going too fast through the water.</p>\r\n<p>Bob &amp; I employed ourselves in painting the skiff &amp; making her decent to go to shore in at <span class=highlight_yellow>Elsinecra</span>.</p>\r\n<p>At 12 o'clock the Captain took his observation lat 55.1 long: 4.15 having been 112 miles since 12<sup>th</sup>  yesterday &amp; 123 from our departure.</p>\r\n<p>After dinner Bob &amp; I took a single glass of grog &amp; again set to work to finish painting the skiff. In the evening the wind changed to South. Got trysail set &amp; main tack down. At 9 o'clock had a glass of brandy &amp; water &amp; turned in</p>","pageId":739,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":536,"lock":null}
