14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":56,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp day. A little rain in the morning. Wind SE. A few ships arrived. Carpenters at work caulking the upper works. Dined at home. In the evening at whist club. Mr Macarthy called to say he was going to send the <span class=highlight_yellow>Brolog</span> Loves, to my brother</p>","pageId":690,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":53,"lock":null}
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/560
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":560,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... SE &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>us</span>. The wind getting to SSE took in studding sails &amp; stood <span class=highlight_yellow>aft</span> of to Norway coast which we saw between 4 &amp; 5 o'clock. Had our fishing lines out all this morning but only caught two gurnets.</p>\r\n<p>A little before 5 o'clock seeing it very black to windward &amp; a squall coming, stowed <span class=highlight_yellow>t</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>p</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>galla</span><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>d</span> sails &amp; lowered topsails upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>Cep</span> just as the squall took us, very heavy, but little rain. It lasted about &frac14; of an hour. Got topsails hoisted again single reefed. Wind seemed much inclined to change. At one time we had it to our great delight from the westward where we squared our yards, but to our inexpressible annoyance had scarcely done when it returned to the old quarter.</p>\r\n<p>During this evening a large fleet of loaded vessels upwards of 80 sail from the Baltic passed us as we let out both reefs. Walked the deck until 10 o'clock when we had our glass of comfort &amp; turned in. Little wind from about the south</p>","pageId":740,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":538,"lock":null}
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/560
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":560,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":16,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... SE &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>us</span>. The wind getting to SSE took in studding sails &amp; stood <span class=highlight_yellow>aft</span> of to Norway coast which we saw between 4 &amp; 5 o'clock. Had our fishing lines out all this morning but only caught two gurnets.</p>\r\n<p>A little before 5 o'clock seeing it very black to windward &amp; a squall coming, stowed <span class=highlight_yellow>t</span><span class=highlight_yellow>o</span><span class=highlight_yellow>p</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>galla</span><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span><span class=highlight_yellow>d</span> sails &amp; lowered topsails upon the <span class=highlight_yellow>Cep</span> just as the squall took us, very heavy, but little rain. It lasted about &frac14; of an hour. Got topsails hoisted again single reefed. Wind seemed much inclined to change. At one time we had it to our great delight from the westward where we squared our yards, but to our inexpressible annoyance had scarcely done when it returned to the old quarter.</p>\r\n<p>During this evening a large fleet of loaded vessels upwards of 80 sail from the Baltic passed us as we let out both reefs. Walked the deck until 10 o'clock when we had our glass of comfort &amp; turned in. Little wind from about the south</p>","pageId":740,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":538,"lock":null}
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/561
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":561,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":6,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After a regular good &amp; sound snooze, turned out at &frac12; past 7 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>During the night slight shower with very little wind. To our great joy when we looked up through the cabin sky light, we saw the yards square &amp; studding sails set. Wind WNW. After breakfast &amp; commenced a heavy rain, which continued until 12 o'clock. Saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>Shaw</span> light at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Employed myself in painting the ship's name upon the skiff &amp; the carpenter finishing painting the underside. Bob Marsh being too lazy to complete his work.</p>\r\n<p>Wind continuing favourable &amp; a fine fresh breeze going 5 or 6 knots. At 9 o'clock saw the <span class=highlight_yellow>Trindlew</span> &amp; the island of <span class=highlight_yellow>Lcefsoe</span> bearing NW by W, distant 5 or 6 miles.</p>\r\n<p>Took our warm glass of brandy &amp; water &amp; got to bed before 10 o'clock. <span class=highlight_yellow>Looking</span> the sea evidently rising.</p>","pageId":740,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":539,"lock":null}
14:36:41.685 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
