14:36:41.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":616,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Immediately after breakfast to <span class=highlight_yellow>drivzkeys</span> &amp; went to the Arsenal where we found the Baron had been as good as his word. A soldier was in waiting for us, who took us over the different departments. They were very busy making brass cannon. The machinery for boring &amp; polishing them very beautiful. Several rooms ...</p>","pageId":757,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":580,"lock":null}
14:36:41.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/617
14:36:41.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":617,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly close &amp; hot morning. Had a shower or two of rain, but if anything rather warmer afterwards. Bob &amp; I called to take leave upon Mr Dye, Mr Thilky, Mr Gellebrand &amp; Mr Wislaw. The great <span class=highlight_yellow>linen</span> from whom we had received attention &amp; civilities. The heat so oppressive we remained at home. Mr Lindsley with us. By the evening went again to the market.</p>\r\n<p>On our way, stopped at one of the Russian baths, where I think we were more astonished than by anything we have yet seen. There were crowds of people going &amp; coming from the bath. Fortunately for themselves, it being considered a religious ceremony, they frequently get their carcases washed or rather purified or otherwise they would be eaten up with <span class=highlight_yellow>verusin</span> for they never think of washing themselves. But on these occasions, as it is, so filthy are they, that they swarm with lice. They do not <span class=highlight_yellow>team</span> themselves as formally men &amp; women together, but among the lower orders each sex have their separate bath, where they <span class=highlight_yellow>parbait</span> themselves by <span class=highlight_yellow>scores</span>. The men we saw first, some ...</p>","pageId":758,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":581,"lock":null}
14:36:41.713 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/617
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":617,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly close &amp; hot morning. Had a shower or two of rain, but if anything rather warmer afterwards. Bob &amp; I called to take leave upon Mr Dye, Mr Thilky, Mr Gellebrand &amp; Mr Wislaw. The great <span class=highlight_yellow>linen</span> from whom we had received attention &amp; civilities. The heat so oppressive we remained at home. Mr Lindsley with us. By the evening went again to the market.</p>\r\n<p>On our way, stopped at one of the Russian baths, where I think we were more astonished than by anything we have yet seen. There were crowds of people going &amp; coming from the bath. Fortunately for themselves, it being considered a religious ceremony, they frequently get their carcases washed or rather purified or otherwise they would be eaten up with <span class=highlight_yellow>verusin</span> for they never think of washing themselves. But on these occasions, as it is, so filthy are they, that they swarm with lice. They do not <span class=highlight_yellow>team</span> themselves as formally men &amp; women together, but among the lower orders each sex have their separate bath, where they <span class=highlight_yellow>parbait</span> themselves by <span class=highlight_yellow>scores</span>. The men we saw first, some ...</p>","pageId":758,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":581,"lock":null}
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/618
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":618,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning, but by the time we had breakfast, it had cleared up. Paid our account for lodgings etc &amp; got on board the steam boat at 9 o'clock &amp; proceeded to Cronstad, where we ...</p>","pageId":758,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":582,"lock":null}
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/618
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":618,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A wet morning, but by the time we had breakfast, it had cleared up. Paid our account for lodgings etc &amp; got on board the steam boat at 9 o'clock &amp; proceeded to Cronstad, where we ...</p>","pageId":758,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":582,"lock":null}
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/619
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":619,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... arrived before 12 o'clock. Had to take our luggage again to the Customs House to be searched. A mere matter of form, for they only opened the boxes without turning the things over &amp; after a little trouble &amp; delay, we were allowed to carry all on board, accompanied by an officer. Employed ourselves during this afternoon in stowing our traps away &amp; putting everything in order.</p>\r\n<p>After tea the captain, Marsh &amp; I went on shore, called at the butchers &amp; baker &amp; spent the remainder of the evening at a friend's where we had some wine. Got on board again between 11 &amp; 12 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Taken 250 casks of tallow on board</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":583,"lock":null}
14:36:41.714 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/619
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":619,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":17,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... arrived before 12 o'clock. Had to take our luggage again to the Customs House to be searched. A mere matter of form, for they only opened the boxes without turning the things over &amp; after a little trouble &amp; delay, we were allowed to carry all on board, accompanied by an officer. Employed ourselves during this afternoon in stowing our traps away &amp; putting everything in order.</p>\r\n<p>After tea the captain, Marsh &amp; I went on shore, called at the butchers &amp; baker &amp; spent the remainder of the evening at a friend's where we had some wine. Got on board again between 11 &amp; 12 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Taken 250 casks of tallow on board</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":583,"lock":null}
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/62
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":62,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine spring day. Wind SW. Went to Newcastle in the morning. The new register not ready. The old one &amp; certificate not having been sent from Shields. Got &pound;20 of J Tenley on account S W &amp; J Scott</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":59,"lock":null}
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
