14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":62,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>An exceedingly fine spring day. Wind SW. Went to Newcastle in the morning. The new register not ready. The old one &amp; certificate not having been sent from Shields. Got &pound;20 of J Tenley on account S W &amp; J Scott</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":59,"lock":null}
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/620
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":620,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another lighter came down last night with the remainder of our tallow.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast, Bob, JG &amp; I went on shore to order some boots etc. Met with Mr Bartholomew. Went with him &amp; had our dinner on board the David. He left by the steam boat for Petersburg at 5 o'clock. Bab &amp; I went with Stephenson to the Butchers to see the beef salted &amp; afterwards took a stroll.</p>\r\n<p>Got in 120 casks of tallow this day.</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":584,"lock":null}
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/620
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":620,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another lighter came down last night with the remainder of our tallow.</p>\r\n<p>After breakfast, Bob, JG &amp; I went on shore to order some boots etc. Met with Mr Bartholomew. Went with him &amp; had our dinner on board the David. He left by the steam boat for Petersburg at 5 o'clock. Bab &amp; I went with Stephenson to the Butchers to see the beef salted &amp; afterwards took a stroll.</p>\r\n<p>Got in 120 casks of tallow this day.</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":584,"lock":null}
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/621
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":621,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Cleared up about 10 o'clock. Dressed ourselves &amp; went on shore to the English Church, just in time to hear the communion service &amp; sermon. Dined on board at 1 o'clock. Had a good sea pie &amp; some roast mutton, which enjoyed much. In the afternoon went on shore, excepting Bob, took some mead to cool us, a very agreeable &amp; refreshing drink made of honey &amp; ginger, not unlike ginger wine. Looked at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Neger</span> market, a very curious and busy scene, crowded with people bargaining &amp; selling. A great many sailors there, regular jacks, very amusing to hear them. Went in the evening to the gardens, which are open to the public on a Sunday. The walks are very prettily laid out &amp; shaded with young trees. A great many of the fashionables of Cronstat where promenading &amp; an excellent military band played for about a couple of hours.</p>\r\n<p>Got on board early</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":585,"lock":null}
14:36:41.715 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/621
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":621,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A rainy morning. Cleared up about 10 o'clock. Dressed ourselves &amp; went on shore to the English Church, just in time to hear the communion service &amp; sermon. Dined on board at 1 o'clock. Had a good sea pie &amp; some roast mutton, which enjoyed much. In the afternoon went on shore, excepting Bob, took some mead to cool us, a very agreeable &amp; refreshing drink made of honey &amp; ginger, not unlike ginger wine. Looked at the <span class=highlight_yellow>Neger</span> market, a very curious and busy scene, crowded with people bargaining &amp; selling. A great many sailors there, regular jacks, very amusing to hear them. Went in the evening to the gardens, which are open to the public on a Sunday. The walks are very prettily laid out &amp; shaded with young trees. A great many of the fashionables of Cronstat where promenading &amp; an excellent military band played for about a couple of hours.</p>\r\n<p>Got on board early</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":585,"lock":null}
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/622
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":622,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Passed our time in preparing for the voyage in making what purchases we wished. Dined <del>with Mr </del><del>Bartholomew</del> on board <del>the David</del><del>. Took a walk in the evening. </del>Agreed to go to Peterhoff tomorrow with Mr Bartholomew.</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":586,"lock":null}
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/622
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":622,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather. Passed our time in preparing for the voyage in making what purchases we wished. Dined <del>with Mr </del><del>Bartholomew</del> on board <del>the David</del><del>. Took a walk in the evening. </del>Agreed to go to Peterhoff tomorrow with Mr Bartholomew.</p>","pageId":759,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":586,"lock":null}
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/623
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":623,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Could not get to Peterhoff without our papers, which Stephenson required to clear the ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Stayed</span> to give it up. Dined on board the David. Turned out a rainy afternoon. Came down in torrents. Engaged to take tea with Mr Ross but the rain prevented us. Did not leave the ship. </p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":587,"lock":null}
14:36:41.716 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/623
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":623,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Could not get to Peterhoff without our papers, which Stephenson required to clear the ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Stayed</span> to give it up. Dined on board the David. Turned out a rainy afternoon. Came down in torrents. Engaged to take tea with Mr Ross but the rain prevented us. Did not leave the ship. </p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":587,"lock":null}
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/624
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":624,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from the Westward. Several ships arrived. Among them the Herald Yacht with Lady Heytesbury on board, the wife of the British ambassador. We ourselves are cleared and ready for sea, but wind bound. Brought four pairs of boots &amp; two pairs of slippers for which I only gave 30 rubbles equal to about 25/-. Dined on board. Brought seven Caviar for <span class=highlight_yellow>jrbling</span>. Richmond etc. Drank a glass of punch with the Ross &amp; afterwards called at ____.</p>\r\n<p>Much annoyed with a swollen face arising from a decayed tooth &amp; cold. Walked round the man of wars <span class=highlight_yellow>mold</span> &amp; went on board one of their new 74's. the Russian fleet returned from a cruise to be inspected by the Emperor, who it is reported has returned to Petersburg</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":588,"lock":null}
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/624
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":624,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning blowing fresh from the Westward. Several ships arrived. Among them the Herald Yacht with Lady Heytesbury on board, the wife of the British ambassador. We ourselves are cleared and ready for sea, but wind bound. Brought four pairs of boots &amp; two pairs of slippers for which I only gave 30 rubbles equal to about 25/-. Dined on board. Brought seven Caviar for <span class=highlight_yellow>jrbling</span>. Richmond etc. Drank a glass of punch with the Ross &amp; afterwards called at ____.</p>\r\n<p>Much annoyed with a swollen face arising from a decayed tooth &amp; cold. Walked round the man of wars <span class=highlight_yellow>mold</span> &amp; went on board one of their new 74's. the Russian fleet returned from a cruise to be inspected by the Emperor, who it is reported has returned to Petersburg</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":588,"lock":null}
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/625
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":625,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still wind bound, blowing fresh from the SW. Suffered a great deal of pain during the night from my tooth &amp; my face swollen to a giant size. Could with difficulty eat. In no ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":589,"lock":null}
14:36:41.717 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/625
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":625,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Still wind bound, blowing fresh from the SW. Suffered a great deal of pain during the night from my tooth &amp; my face swollen to a giant size. Could with difficulty eat. In no ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":589,"lock":null}
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/626
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":626,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather but still a fresh westerly breeze, which detains us. Relieved from pain by the flannel &amp; hartshorn, but my face still much swollen. Remained on board &amp; upon the mole head all the morning.</p>\r\n<p>Mr Bookers clerk called to demand 15 rubbles brokerage for the copper. Went on shore at 5 o'clock to see him upon the subject. It appears I treated with a broker &amp; nob the merchant or I supposed, the brokerage therefore due. Desired Mr Booker to request Mr Hubbardth to pay it &amp; I should settle it in London, having no Russian money left. Amused ourselves on the mole head all evening</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":590,"lock":null}
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/626
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":626,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather but still a fresh westerly breeze, which detains us. Relieved from pain by the flannel &amp; hartshorn, but my face still much swollen. Remained on board &amp; upon the mole head all the morning.</p>\r\n<p>Mr Bookers clerk called to demand 15 rubbles brokerage for the copper. Went on shore at 5 o'clock to see him upon the subject. It appears I treated with a broker &amp; nob the merchant or I supposed, the brokerage therefore due. Desired Mr Booker to request Mr Hubbardth to pay it &amp; I should settle it in London, having no Russian money left. Amused ourselves on the mole head all evening</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":590,"lock":null}
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/627
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":627,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing very hard during the whole of the day from the westward. Several ships arrived having had fine passages of 13 days from London. Amongst them the Sceptre, <span class=highlight_yellow>Coui</span> Greenhod. Several laden ships having hauled out made the <span class=highlight_yellow>roadshad</span> very <span class=highlight_yellow>throng</span>. On the mole head all the morning. Mr Lendaley came down in the steam boat &amp; brought <span class=highlight_yellow>me </span><span class=highlight_yellow>ec</span> ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":591,"lock":null}
14:36:41.718 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
