14:36:41.719 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":627,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Blowing very hard during the whole of the day from the westward. Several ships arrived having had fine passages of 13 days from London. Amongst them the Sceptre, <span class=highlight_yellow>Coui</span> Greenhod. Several laden ships having hauled out made the <span class=highlight_yellow>roadshad</span> very <span class=highlight_yellow>throng</span>. On the mole head all the morning. Mr Lendaley came down in the steam boat &amp; brought <span class=highlight_yellow>me </span><span class=highlight_yellow>ec</span> ...</p>","pageId":760,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":591,"lock":null}
14:36:41.719 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/628
14:36:41.719 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":628,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... packet from Mr Dye, a present for Emma Galbraith. Mr L took a glass of grog with us &amp; we afterwards accompanied him on board. The Chase, captain Thompson arrived today in 13 days from Hull, and had supper.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":592,"lock":null}
