14:36:41.720 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":628,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":25,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... packet from Mr Dye, a present for Emma Galbraith. Mr L took a glass of grog with us &amp; we afterwards accompanied him on board. The Chase, captain Thompson arrived today in 13 days from Hull, and had supper.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":592,"lock":null}
14:36:41.720 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/629
14:36:41.720 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":629,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning, but exceptionally hot. The wind having got round to the north &amp; an appearance of changing. We after breakfast hauled out of the mole but being quite calm were obliged to get a boat ahead &amp; toe the ship down to the guard ship. Cleared at the guard ship about 12 o'clock &amp; proceeded with a leading wind, but little of it.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":593,"lock":null}
