14:36:41.723 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":634,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":29,"sequence":3.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning at &frac12; past 7 o'clock. Weather changed being quite calm, the alterations took place last night at 12 o'clock with heavy rain, thunder &amp; lightning, which &amp; I did not hear being on a very comfortable <font color=#BFBFBF>birth </font>&amp; sound asleep. In the course of the morning, when off Hanger Head, the wind got to the north (at 2 o'clock wind east) enabling us again to set studding sails, steering a WSW course.</p>\r\n<p>Amused myself all day in reading Roderick Random and Peregrine Pickle. Turned in at 11 o'clock after having our grog. Little wind.</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":596,"lock":null}
14:36:41.723 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/635
14:36:41.723 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":635,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":7,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out before 8 o'clock. A fine morning. A light breeze at ENE going about 3 or 3 &frac12; knots. Studding sails set. About dinner time it began to rain &amp; continued very heavy until 3 o'clock. When we passed round Dago Island &amp; entered the Baltic. At &frac12; past 5 o'clock the wind changed to west ...</p>","pageId":761,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":597,"lock":null}
