14:36:41.725 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":64,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":2,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day day. Wind N by E. Finished with the rigging. Dined at home. At Mrs Greenhows in the evening</p>","pageId":691,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":61,"lock":null}
14:36:41.725 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/640
14:36:41.725 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
