14:36:41.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":640,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning &amp; clear weather, still blowing fresh from the NW which has continued the whole day, with a heavy sea which has prevented us making more than 3 knots. Amused myself the whole of the day reading Peregrine Pickle. At 4 o'clock pm wind got to W by N. At 5 o'clock pm tacked ship &amp; stood across towards Gothland again. By observation at 12 o'clock lat:55.52 Reefed topsail at 2 o'clock pm</p>","pageId":762,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":602,"lock":null}
14:36:41.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/641
14:36:41.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":641,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A delightful change. Now beautiful weather. Wind NW &amp; W. Light breeze &amp; sea very much fallen, only going about 2 knots. At 12 o'clock by observation at lat:55.47N. Employed myself all the morning in preparing the wood for a dog kennel. At 2 o'clock pm the wind got to the WSW course NW. At 5 pm set studding sails, top masts &amp; main top gallant. Sea quite fallen &amp; a fine fresh breeze at 6 o'clock wind S course W by S going 5 knots at 10 o'clock <span class=highlight_yellow>discharged</span> our grog &amp; turned in for the night, ship going 5 &frac12; knots</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":603,"lock":null}
14:36:41.726 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
