14:36:41.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":643,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning at the usual hour. Coppers hot &amp; rather feverish, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>seidletz</span>, very pleasant answering a double purpose. A beautiful morning. Summer returned. A light breeze at SE. At noon by observation in lat 55.10N. Kept our reach the whole of the day. Wind NW. At 8 o'clock tacked ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Reigen</span> Island bearing S by W distant 10 or 12 miles.</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":605,"lock":null}
