14:36:41.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":643,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out this morning at the usual hour. Coppers hot &amp; rather feverish, took a <span class=highlight_yellow>seidletz</span>, very pleasant answering a double purpose. A beautiful morning. Summer returned. A light breeze at SE. At noon by observation in lat 55.10N. Kept our reach the whole of the day. Wind NW. At 8 o'clock tacked ship. <span class=highlight_yellow>Reigen</span> Island bearing S by W distant 10 or 12 miles.</p>","pageId":763,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":605,"lock":null}
14:36:41.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/644
14:36:41.727 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":644,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning &amp; fresh breeze at NNW &amp; N. Employed myself all the morning in drawing. At noon clear weather but still a fresh breeze. <span class=highlight_yellow>Falsterbo</span> light bearing WNW distant 8 miles. A large fleet of ships passed us upward bound. At 5 o'clock tacked ship a little to the southward of <span class=highlight_yellow>Moea</span> Island after which it became quite calm until 9 o'clock when we got a light air from the NNW. Afterwards most favourable. At 10 o'clock after our grog we turned in, the ship proceeding quickly towards Drags in the island <span class=highlight_yellow>Verf</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Amag</span></p>","pageId":764,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":606,"lock":null}
