14:36:41.729 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":649,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":11,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... the west which soon caused a tremendous sea. Obliged to him too under close reefed topsails until about 4 o'clock when we <span class=highlight_yellow>wone</span> ship &amp; lay too under close reefed main topsail. What with the howling of the wind, the rolling &amp; tossing of the ship &amp; creaking of tallow casks besides being leaky &amp; upon a lee shore, we had spent a most uncomfortable day. Did not attempt to go to bed, indeed mine was so damp I could not, but I lay down upon the captains about midnight all standing </p>","pageId":765,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":611,"lock":null}
