14:36:41.735 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":659,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>This morning thick weather the land in sight like a fog bank, but clearing away we found it for certain to be Huntcliff foot, bearing west about five miles. During the morning light <span class=highlight_yellow>wind</span> variable &amp; in the afternoon calm with tremendous heavy rain, thunder &amp; lightning. At night the wind being from the NE light breeze &amp; I very unwell with <span class=highlight_yellow>scumalign</span>. The ship short of Stocks as water coals &amp; pump gear out of order &amp; considering she might reach shields, by daylight, we determined to work to windward &amp; turned in for the night.</p>","pageId":767,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":621,"lock":null}
