14:36:41.737 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":663,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out after a food nights rest at 8 o'clock. The gale as heavy as ever with rain. (Sent top gallant yards driven &amp; struck the mast)</p>\r\n<p>At 11 o'clock finer weather &amp; some appearance of clearing up having had a glimpse of the sun.</p>\r\n<p>Wrote a letter to William &amp; Mr Clark of the Duke of Clarence coming on board. We all went on shore at 12 o'clock to put the letter into the post. Walked about &amp; saw a little of the town of Yarmouth with which I was much pleased. After having some bread &amp; cheese, <span class=highlight_yellow>portion</span> &amp; a glass of grog, we left the jetty about 4 o'clock ...</p>","pageId":768,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":625,"lock":null}
14:36:41.737 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/664
14:36:41.737 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":664,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":23,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... reached the ship in about &frac12; a hour after a heavy pull. Still blowing very hard. Mr Clark took tea with us in the evening.  The weather much improved both sea &amp; wind having fallen.</p>","pageId":769,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":626,"lock":null}
14:36:41.737 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
