14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":666,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear morning, but wind not at all abated, about WNW &amp; the night has been so boisterous with rain, that the master &amp; all the vessels in company have not thought it prudent to move. The people employed in sending down the Royals &amp; setting up the short topgallant masts. Seeing about board a ship near us, we were in no little alarm, lest it should be one of the preventative service &amp; were in a devil of a brush to get our goods and challis stowed away. It however proved a false alarm, being only a pilot boat. Got under way at 12 o'clock &amp; turned to windward with a fresh breeze. At 9 o'clock pm brought up abreast of the hook of the Gunfleet for the night</p>","pageId":769,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":628,"lock":null}
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/667
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":667,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>By daylight this morning. They got the ship underway at low water. When we got up at 8 o'clock the weather much pleasanter &amp; continued fine all day. At noon brought up at high water abreast of Whitaker Beason. Wind SW. At 5 pm,  low water, we again got under way, but were much delayed by a ship giving us a foul birth, the consequence was it became dark before we could work through Shoe hole  &amp; see the mouse buoy, where unfortunately it also turned very squally &amp; blowing a gale of wind. We were working towards the nose light &amp; should have got well up but the overhaul of our gib giving way the ship would not steer &amp; we were obliged, though not unwilling by ...</p>","pageId":769,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":629,"lock":null}
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/667
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":667,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>By daylight this morning. They got the ship underway at low water. When we got up at 8 o'clock the weather much pleasanter &amp; continued fine all day. At noon brought up at high water abreast of Whitaker Beason. Wind SW. At 5 pm,  low water, we again got under way, but were much delayed by a ship giving us a foul birth, the consequence was it became dark before we could work through Shoe hole  &amp; see the mouse buoy, where unfortunately it also turned very squally &amp; blowing a gale of wind. We were working towards the nose light &amp; should have got well up but the overhaul of our gib giving way the ship would not steer &amp; we were obliged, though not unwilling by ...</p>","pageId":769,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":629,"lock":null}
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/668
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":668,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to bring up, being on good riding ground between the nose light &amp; the buoy of the mouse.</p>\r\n<p>At &frac12; past 11 o'clock we got into bed. Blowing a gale &amp; a dismal night</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":630,"lock":null}
14:36:41.738 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.739 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/668
14:36:41.739 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":668,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":26,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... to bring up, being on good riding ground between the nose light &amp; the buoy of the mouse.</p>\r\n<p>At &frac12; past 11 o'clock we got into bed. Blowing a gale &amp; a dismal night</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":630,"lock":null}
14:36:41.739 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/669
14:36:41.739 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":669,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":8,"day":27,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Turned out between 6 &amp; 7 o'clock &amp; soon afterward got underway. Still blowing hard from about the WSW lasting at 12 o'clock &amp; after it blew a perfect hurricane, however we rode well &amp; I slept very sound. A large Garth that we saw to leeward of us yesterday without his main topsail, is this morning upon the Maplin sand, having no doubt missed stage last night. Several smacks near him. This <span class=highlight_yellow>lide</span> we worked up as high as Southend &amp; brought up glad to get into such a good roadstead. At 6 o'clock, low water, the gale heavier &amp; night coming on, we did not think it prudent to get under way. At 8 o'clock we had a warm glass of Hollands &amp; water which we enjoyed. The first we have had for some time, having run out of coals.</p>\r\n<p>I forgot to mention that yesterday while we brought up abreast of the Whitaker, we lowered our boat &amp; went on board the Eliza of South Shields, Captain Young who kindly supplied us with two or three baskets of coals &amp; a cask of water in return we gave him a spare for a topgallant studding sail boom in dial plank &amp; a bottle of Hollands.</p>\r\n<p>He also took a box of Russian slippers &amp; a keg of caviar, to return to us in London. We fearing the officers might seize them</p>","pageId":770,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":631,"lock":null}
14:36:41.739 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
