14:36:41.743 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/676
14:36:41.743 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":676,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine day. Wind NW. Called upon Jobling. He drove me down to Woolwich to see the Lumley's. Eat some cold meat with them &amp; returned to the ship at Greenwich to dinner, where Tom Jobling joined us. Left the ship about 7 o'clock &amp; drove to town. Had a glass of brandy &amp; wine with Jobling &amp; got to bed at &frac12; past 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":771,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":638,"lock":null}
14:36:41.743 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/677
14:36:41.743 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":677,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Bob Marsh &amp; I walked into the city &amp; thence on board the Hope where we dined. The people busy getting the tallow out. Returned to Philpot Lane where we stopped until 6 o'clock with Mary Ann first time. Walked out of the city to chambers &amp; remained all evening. Received a letter from William which came yesterday. Did not answer it.</p>","pageId":772,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":639,"lock":null}
14:36:41.743 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
