14:36:41.748 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":688,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather. Wind about SW. Nothing particular occurred today. Attended chambers. Sam Harry offered me 21/- <span class=highlight_yellow>pload</span> for Hull, having had a letter from Henry, that such freights could be obtained. Agreed to wait till tomorrow when Henry would be in town. Walked to the Blue Ports in Cork Square where we all met &amp; dined.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":646,"lock":null}
14:36:41.748 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/689
14:36:41.748 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":689,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Showery weather. Wind S W. Took a cab into the city and afterwards walked to the docks. Found the people employed hauling the ship out, intending to take her down to Dukes shore. Received from Stephenson &pound;89.7.6 for the lathwood. <span class=underline_double>With Maryann</span>.  Attended chambers. H Harry never made his appearance. Did nothing. Went by a Paddington stage to Nottingham Place where Bob Marsh &amp; I dined with William &amp; enjoyed ourselves much.</p>","pageId":773,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":647,"lock":null}
