14:36:41.753 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":697,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind NE. Took a Paddington stage into the city. Stephenson up, but not cleared for want of papers relative to the sum, from the West India docks. J Galbraith &amp; I walked down to the ship. Dined on board. Got our ballast alongside. Put all my cloths etc. on board the Peggy, captain Hunter, intending to take my passage to Shields in her. She hauled out of the Regents Canal &amp; proceeded down the river to Purfleet to ballast. William &amp; I walked up to the city, calling at Chapmans respecting the clearing papers.</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":655,"lock":null}
14:36:41.753 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/698
14:36:41.753 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":698,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":9,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Been raining very heavy all night. Weather thick. Wind NE. Packed my cloths up. Took a packing coach &amp; went down to the office. Paid &pound;4.12. for 23 gallons of rum at 4/ per gallon. William paid it out of &pound;30 I gave him to place to my <span class=highlight_yellow>Chapmans account</span>. William &amp; I got on board the Pearl Gravesend boat. He accompanied me as far as Woolwich where he landed &amp; I proceeded to the ...</p>","pageId":775,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":656,"lock":null}
