14:36:41.771 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":734,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":21,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind SE. Prepared to set off for Shields, but after breakfast it set in such a determined rainingday that we could not think of moving. I therefore remained at Burnhopeside. Spent a quiet evening at home.</p>","pageId":780,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":689,"lock":null}
14:36:41.771 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/735
14:36:41.771 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":735,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning after a very heavy fall of rain during the night. Wind NW. After breakfast Kit &amp; Joe went to see the Lambleton hounds throw off at Flags &amp; James, Kits servant, drove me in the gig to Durham, where I had to remain all day, the coach not passing through till evening. Showers during the whole of the morning, but in the intervals I strolled about to see all my old haunts etc. Things much in a &quot;status quo&quot;. I could perceive few alterations or improvements. Called upon <span class=highlight_yellow>SKeene</span>. At 8 o'clock took a gig &amp; got to shields at &frac12; past 9 o'clock &amp; went to the whist club for an hour. Received a letter from William.</p>","pageId":780,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":690,"lock":null}
14:36:41.771 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
