14:36:41.772 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":737,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very fine morning. Wind WNW. Towards afternoon it got round to SSE. Several ships got to sea. The lady Jane arrived from Greenland with 9 fish. Called at MisJarre &amp; saw Emma. Also upon <span class=highlight_yellow>M &amp; </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Ino</span> Matthews. Dined at home. Mrs Scott not quite so well today. Took a walk in the evening with A. S__k_s <font color=#BFBFBF>(Ann Stokes) </font><font color=#BFBFBF> </font></p>","pageId":780,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":692,"lock":null}
14:36:41.772 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/738
14:36:41.772 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":738,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW. Attended morning service &amp; heard an excellent sermon by Mr Hollengsworth of Bolton, after which &pound;24 was collected for the Judgement Sick Society. In the afternoon J Tinley, the boys &amp; I walked to Tynemouth &amp; being a most beautiful day as great many people were there. Dined &amp; spent the evening with the Tinleys, it being Mrs T's birth &amp; wedding day</p>","pageId":780,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":693,"lock":null}
