14:36:41.774 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":740,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":10,"day":26,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>Another beautiful morning. Wind about West. Went over the water with H Harry to see Mr S Walkers patent lever to the old windlass worked, but it was unshipped. Wrote to C <span class=highlight_yellow>Kirkmond</span> about the price of <span class=highlight_yellow>mineral</span> timber. Mrs Dixon down to see Mrs Scott, rather more gracious than before. She invited me to Benton.</p>\r\n<p>Dined at home. Drank a couple of tumblers of whiskey toddy with Allen &amp; went to the theatre to see Madam Vestris perform <span class=highlight_yellow>Latit</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ea</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Har</span><span class=highlight_yellow>og</span> in the <span class=highlight_yellow>Billes</span> <span class=highlight_yellow>Shala</span><span class=highlight_yellow>g</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span> &amp; Apollo in Midas. A pretty good house, about &pound;37 in </p>","pageId":780,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":694,"lock":null}
