14:36:41.779 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":751,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":6,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine mild morning with the appearance of rain. Wind WSW. Dined at the George Tavern with William Harrison who had last a <span class=highlight_yellow>diciseen</span> upon the death of Major <span class=highlight_yellow>Wergs</span>. He (WH) saying that the major was killed at Corunna when it was at S<sup>t</sup> Sabastian's. Had an exceedingly pleasant day &amp; excellent dinner &amp; wine. Present J Tinley, Captain French, Mr West &amp; Mr Robinson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment, Mr Allen, William, Tom &amp; Benj Wright, I Craig, Mr Christie of London, Mr Harrison &amp; myself</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":705,"lock":null}
14:36:41.779 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/752
14:36:41.779 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":752,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. The air rather frosty. Intended going to Newcastle with H Harry but prevented by a most disturbing letter from captain Stephenson of the Hope dated <i>Elsinore</i><i> </i>the 24<sup>th</sup> Oct informing me of the loss of poor J Galbraith. He having fallen overboard from the maintop sail yard when reefing pitching upon the top in his fall, poor fellow, his career has been short but &lsquo;tis all for the best. I hope he has left a world of misery &amp; is now I trust happy with his dear parents. Remained in the house all day in consequence of this sad news. Wrote to WBS, Mr Vernon &amp; D Dixon</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":706,"lock":null}
14:36:41.779 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/752
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":752,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful morning. Wind NW. The air rather frosty. Intended going to Newcastle with H Harry but prevented by a most disturbing letter from captain Stephenson of the Hope dated <i>Elsinore</i><i> </i>the 24<sup>th</sup> Oct informing me of the loss of poor J Galbraith. He having fallen overboard from the maintop sail yard when reefing pitching upon the top in his fall, poor fellow, his career has been short but &lsquo;tis all for the best. I hope he has left a world of misery &amp; is now I trust happy with his dear parents. Remained in the house all day in consequence of this sad news. Wrote to WBS, Mr Vernon &amp; D Dixon</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":706,"lock":null}
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/753
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":753,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind NW. In consequence of the account of J Galbraith's death, did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening went &amp; drank tea with J Tinley. Turned out a boisterous night.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":707,"lock":null}
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/753
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":753,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Rather cool. Wind NW. In consequence of the account of J Galbraith's death, did not go to church. Dined at home. In the evening went &amp; drank tea with J Tinley. Turned out a boisterous night.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":707,"lock":null}
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/754
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
14:36:41.780 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/754
14:36:41.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":754,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":9,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine autumnal morning. Wind NW by W. Sea high upon the bar. Took a walk with mark &amp; captain Webb round by Cullercoats. Held the annual meeting at newsrooms. Old Crofs discharged in consequence of his continued disgraceful &amp; insolent conduct. Temple,  Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lins</span><span class=highlight_yellow> </span><span class=highlight_yellow>Rell's</span> late butler appointed in his place. Dined at home at 2 o'clock.</p>\r\n<p>Fanny Smith arrived from Togston for a few days.</p>\r\n<p>Paid <span class=highlight_yellow>Sab</span><sup><span class=highlight_yellow>n</span></sup><sup> </sup>to newsroom 30/.</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":708,"lock":null}
14:36:41.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/755
14:36:41.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":755,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":10,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A damp morning. Wind SW &amp; blowing fresh. Walked out. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Emma came from school for a few days. Spent the evening at home</p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":709,"lock":null}
14:36:41.781 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
