14:36:41.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":757,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":12,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and wet morning. Wind WSW. At the news room &amp; in the house all the morning. Received a notice from Brown of the George to quit in May. Called &amp; told him I would not accept it. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. In the evening went to the whist club being a wet evening Tom Smith would not go. Wrote to <span class=highlight_aqua>Baker Galbraith</span></p>","pageId":782,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":711,"lock":null}
14:36:41.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/758
14:36:41.782 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":758,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":13,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Blowing hard from the SE. Walked to Shields with Tom Smith. He set off for Togston, being such an unpleasant morning. Fanny remained. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Took wine with H Harry &amp; J Cunningham at the Commercial.</p>","pageId":783,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":712,"lock":null}
