14:36:41.789 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":772,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":28,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A thick dull morning with a little rain. Wind about north. Allen &amp; I took a walk to Tynemouth. Government having given up the burial ground to the parish again, excepting 40 feet round the sides of the yard. Dined at home.</p>\r\n<p>Spent the evening with Mr <span class=highlight_yellow>Lewison</span>, H Harry, and A Nicholson at the Duke of York.</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":726,"lock":null}
14:36:41.789 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/773
14:36:41.789 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":773,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":11,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy and damp morning. Wind SW. Received a letter from Stephenson of the Hope being out on Saturday having delivered 279 loads 49 feet of timber equal to 320 loads with deals of broken stowage.</p>\r\n<p>Took Emma to church with me. Dined at home &amp; afterwards took wine with Boswell. H Harry &amp; Allen there.</p>\r\n<p>In the evening at mother Maxwell's</p>","pageId":784,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":727,"lock":null}
