14:36:41.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":777,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very unpleasant damp morning. Wind about south with a heavy sea upon the bar. Two ships have got upon the rock in entering the harbour. Dined at home. Mr Allen came &amp; took wine with me. In the evening attended the whist club.</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":731,"lock":null}
14:36:41.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/778
14:36:41.791 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":778,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Finer weather but still rather foggy &amp; dull. Wind S &amp; S by E. The <span class=highlight_yellow>Qurnoury</span> belonging to <font color=#222222>Messrs</font><font color=#222222> </font>Young son got upon the rocks last night. Allen &amp; I walked round by Tynemouth &amp; the rocks to see them. Dined at home. Boswell treated H Nicholson &amp; me to some punch at the Mulstrum, it being his last night at Shields</p>","pageId":785,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":732,"lock":null}
