14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":796,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A foggy damp and very unpleasant morning. Some snow on the ground, having fallen during the night. Wind, the little there is NNW. Dined at 4 o'clock at Mr Metcalf's in Saville Street. A party there. Spent a pleasant day. Wrote to William. Called at the Bank. Spencer promised to under me what accommodation I <span class=highlight_yellow>may</span> want this Xmas. Paid Linskill &amp; etc &pound;24.11.6 for <span class=highlight_yellow>cordage</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Lane</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Spence</span> &amp; <span class=highlight_yellow>Foster</span> &pound;8.10/- for canvas</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":750,"lock":null}
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/797
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":797,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning. Wind East. H Harry went with me on board the Hope to give me his advice with regard to the repairs. Found they had taken the broken hold beam out &amp; preparing a new one. Ordered several new <span class=highlight_yellow>kne</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> to be put in. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":751,"lock":null}
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/797
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":797,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A frosty morning. Wind East. H Harry went with me on board the Hope to give me his advice with regard to the repairs. Found they had taken the broken hold beam out &amp; preparing a new one. Ordered several new <span class=highlight_yellow>kne</span><span class=highlight_yellow>e</span><span class=highlight_yellow>s</span> to be put in. Dined at home &amp; spent the evening</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":751,"lock":null}
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/798
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":798,"version":0,"year":1829,"month":12,"day":24,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cold frosty morning. Wind E by N. Been blowing a gale all night. A heavy sea upon the bar. On board the Hope. The master &amp; carpenter absent looking for some knees for the hold beans. Dined at home. H Harry came in &amp; took wine with me. Mrs Dixon down &amp; took Emma to Benton with her. Attended the whist club in the evening. Saw Ann Maxwell</p>","pageId":787,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":752,"lock":null}
14:36:41.800 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
