14:36:41.815 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":829,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":1,"day":22,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of fresh weather &amp; been blowing very hard all night from the SE. One ship has got upon the Heard Sand, another upon the rocks &amp; two riding off the Bar. One having cut away her masts &amp; the other with main mast gone. Both these ships &amp; the one on the Heard Sand got into the harbour. Walked to Tynemouth with Nicholson &amp; Cunningham. Dined at home. In the evening H harry, Nicholson &amp; I went to the Duke of York where we found Mr Heweson</p>","pageId":790,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":781,"lock":null}
