14:36:41.823 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":845,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most inferior frost Wind S.W. Received a letter from WBS Went to church in the morning Dined at home at &frac12; past 1 o'clock. In the evening at the Duke of York With T Nicholson and afterwards at the Neuls home. This evening a caped this commenced with rain</p>","pageId":796,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":797,"lock":null}
14:36:41.823 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/846
14:36:41.823 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":846,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":8,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>The thaw continues &amp; the  snow has disappeared. Blowing a gale of wind at WNW. Went by Dunn's coach to Newcastle Fixed the Hope for the Bursaton Walls to be loaded on Monday. Gave Stephenson orders to lay her the shore line. Dined at home at 3 then took wine with I Craig &amp; afterwards spent the evening At Tynemouth Castle with Captain French of The 80<sup>th</sup>. A large Hulk sailed today. Ann Maxwell delivered of a fine boy</p>","pageId":797,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":798,"lock":null}
