14:36:41.829 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":857,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":19,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A course frost. Wind NNW &amp; blowing fresh &amp; although the sea was breaking upon the bar, several small ships ventured out &amp; some were literally smothered in the surf, but all got out safe. Dined with I Readhead on board the Nautalus At the billiard room in the afternoon. Drank tea at home &amp; in the evening With Bode Jerois &amp; afterwards at the Duke Of York</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":809,"lock":null}
14:36:41.829 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/858
14:36:41.829 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":858,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":2,"day":20,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of frost Wind NW. Got up early &amp; went by stream to Newcastle; had a heavy snow storm Returned to dinner at 1 o'clock. Emma G with us. Mrs Dixon came to see Mrs Scott Not water sufficient for the Hope to get to sea. Attended the Whist Club at Allans in the evening</p>\r\n<p>xx</p>","pageId":799,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":810,"lock":null}
14:36:41.829 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
