14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":88,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":3,"day":23,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine clear frosty morning &amp; cold. Wind NNW. Showers of sleet &amp; rain in the afternoon. Attended morning service. Dined at home.  <span class=highlight_yellow>Carlea</span> Sunday</p>","pageId":692,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":84,"lock":null}
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/880
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":880,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cool morning &amp; blown very hard all day at west. Of course in the house. Fanny Smith again exceedingly violent today. More so than before &amp; insulting. Than I was obliged to speak to her in a way that had the effect of making her silent. Wonder ? Be at opposite William BS did not arrive until after 11 o'clock having called &amp; stopped a short time in Westgate Street. Went to bed from after his arrival.</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":832,"lock":null}
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/880
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":880,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cool morning &amp; blown very hard all day at west. Of course in the house. Fanny Smith again exceedingly violent today. More so than before &amp; insulting. Than I was obliged to speak to her in a way that had the effect of making her silent. Wonder ? Be at opposite William BS did not arrive until after 11 o'clock having called &amp; stopped a short time in Westgate Street. Went to bed from after his arrival.</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":832,"lock":null}
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/881
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":881,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning, wind SE Afterwards changed to SW &amp; blowing fresh with fine weather. Brought a large fleet down amongst them the Hope. Dixon &amp; his aid Tom Smith Mrs Yellowley &amp; Emma came down to attend the funeral which took place between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock. Captain Caudisson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment kindly allowing the hearse and carriages to enter the castle ...</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":833,"lock":null}
14:36:41.838 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
