14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":881,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very wet morning, wind SE Afterwards changed to SW &amp; blowing fresh with fine weather. Brought a large fleet down amongst them the Hope. Dixon &amp; his aid Tom Smith Mrs Yellowley &amp; Emma came down to attend the funeral which took place between 12 &amp; 1 o'clock. Captain Caudisson of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment kindly allowing the hearse and carriages to enter the castle ...</p>","pageId":804,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":833,"lock":null}
14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/882
14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":882,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... yard. Mrs Scott's remains placed in the vault above my father. Fanny Smith more violent than ever. Her conduct most disgusting &amp; indecent. Dixon Mrs B &amp; Mr Gallowley returned to Newcastle. Tom Smith accompanied</p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":834,"lock":null}
14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/882
14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":882,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":15,"sequence":2.0000,"text":"<p>... yard. Mrs Scott's remains placed in the vault above my father. Fanny Smith more violent than ever. Her conduct most disgusting &amp; indecent. Dixon Mrs B &amp; Mr Gallowley returned to Newcastle. Tom Smith accompanied</p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":834,"lock":null}
14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/883
14:36:41.839 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":883,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":16,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind NW &amp; rather cold. Tom Smith, his mother &amp; Fanny left us for Foyston &amp; fortunately without any more unpleasantness. After they left us the weather changed &amp; we had a very stormy day, heavy showers of snow Was &amp; I had the servants up &amp; told them of our plans. Robert agreed to remain with me, also Leadbetter. Hutchison of course leaves us, but will stay in the house until she gets a situation or I wish her to leave. Stephenson has been at NCastle  but could obtain nothing for the Hope only 8/6 pecght offering. Ordered Him to unbind the sails. Gave him a draft upon Chapman for &pound;20 to pay wages. At home all the evening</p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":835,"lock":null}
