14:36:41.840 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":884,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull showery day. Wind fresh at NW. Engaged at home in the house with ABS. I gave him his note at 40 days for &pound;75.10/- <font color=#FF0000>Accepted &amp; returned </font><font color=#FF0000>Mrs</font><font color=#FF0000> </font><font color=#FF0000>Bulemer</font><font color=#FF0000> a bill</font> <font color=#FF0000>at</font><font color=#FF0000> 3 </font><font color=#FF0000>hou</font><font color=#FF0000>rs. Due 23 p</font><font color=#FF0000>ricing</font><font color=#FF0000> for Policy presumabl</font><font color=#FF0000>y</font> <font color=#FF0000>almost</font><font color=#FF0000> &pound;16.13.8</font> Dined at home. At 5 o'clock the owner &amp; Master of the Commerce with me about the damages received by him in the wold when the Hope came in contact, agreed to leave it to two gentlemen to decide with have to call in a this. At home all the evening </p>","pageId":805,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":836,"lock":null}
14:36:41.840 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/885
14:36:41.840 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":885,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":3,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very boisterous day. Blowing hard at N &amp; NNW but fine weather. Payed E Ried apprentice &frac14;  years ways &pound;1.8.9 &amp; also Jeaslop the balance of his &frac14; wages &pound;1.3.9 &amp; advanced him 16/3 = &pound;2 Nman &amp; Leng aged all the moral with Robert Taking due account of the wine in the cellar. Mary Carts called &amp; in consequence of Mr Wrights bad conduct to her with whose children she was governess, we asked her to come and stay with us, until she goes to her situation as governess to a school in Newcastle. Dined at home at 2 o'clock. Paid into chapmans WBS; note for &pound;75 Miss Emma &amp; I took a walk round by Cullercoats Sands &amp; came home to tea. At the whist club in the evening.</p>","pageId":806,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":837,"lock":null}
