14:36:41.856 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":913,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":14,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful spring morning. Wind West. Walked with Williams to Preston &amp; looked at the different tenements &amp; ordered what repairs were necessary afterwards we  crofsid the conatrg &amp; called upon Mr Flbceght, Whitley Park when this it began to rain&amp; we got wet through before we reached home &amp; dinner at &frac12; past 2 o'clock Mary Carp left us &amp; returned to Newcastle with A Deighlow. In the evening at the Duke of York with A Harry &amp; Mr Heweson</p>","pageId":812,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":865,"lock":null}
