14:36:41.861 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":924,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":25,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fine weather again &amp; glafs risen considerably since yesterday evening about 1 &frac12;  inch &amp; up to fair. Wind NNW. Attended morning wives. Dined with I Tealeg, Mrs Cumliff &amp; keifs of the These. Walked to Tynemouth in the afternoon; At the S <span class=highlight_yellow>Cellegator</span> off several ships went to sea, bound foreign, the Broderweck, 3 Brothers, Dalsymple, Hannah, Equity les. Spent the evening at <span class=highlight_yellow>Tealegs</span> A heavy rain at night.</p>","pageId":814,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":876,"lock":null}
14:36:41.861 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/925
14:36:41.861 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":925,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":26,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind W by S. Walked to Teymouth; called at Libb's where I met Mrs Ildeston, he returned to Shields with <span class=highlight_yellow>bum</span>. Invited by him to go &amp; stay at <span class=highlight_yellow>Lnasoington</span> with Captain Webb. Dined at home. Jebbs &amp; Webb took wine with over at the Duke of York in the evening</p>","pageId":814,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":877,"lock":null}
