14:36:41.863 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":928,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":29,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A countenance of beautiful weather. Wind ESE. Took a walk to Tynemouth with <span class=highlight_yellow>Lt H</span><span class=highlight_yellow>arry</span>. Dined at home. Onboard the John Dunn in the evening with I <span class=highlight_yellow>Wesglot</span> &amp; afterwards at the Duke of York.</p>","pageId":815,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":880,"lock":null}
14:36:41.863 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/929
14:36:41.863 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":929,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":4,"day":30,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Most beautiful weather. Wind ESE. Went by Steamer to Newcastle could get nothing for the Hope. Dined with D Dixon, a party Tom Smith, Mr Busqter; they all went to the theater to see Liston, I looked in but did not remain long, the house very full for his benefit. Got into a gig &amp; returned to Shields</p>","pageId":815,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":881,"lock":null}
