14:36:41.864 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":930,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A cloudy morning much like rain. Wind WSW Turned out a most beautiful day. Went with H Harry by steam to Newcastle. Could not fix the Hope, but almost determined to talk 11 Gr Kent to Dublin. Returned home to dinner. Tour Seventh A Harry &amp; Emma G: dined with me. Mark came in to wine. In the evening we went to whist club at Allens</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":882,"lock":null}
14:36:41.864 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/931
14:36:41.864 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":931,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind West. Tom Smith &amp; I went to Church. Afterwards called at Mrs Marr's who would not let Emma go up to Newcastle to see Bell Smith. The King by Lodges paper a little better back still in a very precarious start. Dined at home. Pscous to which I Smith left. Walk to Tynemouth in the afternoon &amp; took wine &amp; tea with Libbs</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":883,"lock":null}
14:36:41.864 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
