14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":931,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind West. Tom Smith &amp; I went to Church. Afterwards called at Mrs Marr's who would not let Emma go up to Newcastle to see Bell Smith. The King by Lodges paper a little better back still in a very precarious start. Dined at home. Pscous to which I Smith left. Walk to Tynemouth in the afternoon &amp; took wine &amp; tea with Libbs</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":883,"lock":null}
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/932
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":932,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind about West. By Steam to Newcastle but did not find the Hope to load coal for Dublin as intended as they could not load her before they did of much works. Returned to Dinner on board the Choice in the afternoon. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":884,"lock":null}
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/932
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":932,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another fine morning. Wind about West. By Steam to Newcastle but did not find the Hope to load coal for Dublin as intended as they could not load her before they did of much works. Returned to Dinner on board the Choice in the afternoon. Drank tea with H Harry &amp; In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":816,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":884,"lock":null}
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/933
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":933,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most beautiful weather with a West wind. Turned out at 6 o'clock &amp; took a long walk round by Cullercoat Sands &amp; before breakfast. And afterwards Webb, Mark &amp; I took a walk along the hard sand where I made a sketch of Tynmouth Castle be. Returned home to dinner. In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":885,"lock":null}
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/933
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":933,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A continuance of most beautiful weather with a West wind. Turned out at 6 o'clock &amp; took a long walk round by Cullercoat Sands &amp; before breakfast. And afterwards Webb, Mark &amp; I took a walk along the hard sand where I made a sketch of Tynmouth Castle be. Returned home to dinner. In the evening at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":885,"lock":null}
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/934
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":934,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Glorious weather. Wind very variable between SE &amp; W. Went to Newcastle by steam. Gave up the Dublin charter &amp; returned home to dinner. A Harry took a bottle of port with us &amp; I gave him an order to fix the Hope for anchorage &amp; Hull dealers at &pound;4.7.6 At the Duke of York in the evening</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":886,"lock":null}
14:36:41.865 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/934
14:36:41.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":934,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":5,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Glorious weather. Wind very variable between SE &amp; W. Went to Newcastle by steam. Gave up the Dublin charter &amp; returned home to dinner. A Harry took a bottle of port with us &amp; I gave him an order to fix the Hope for anchorage &amp; Hull dealers at &pound;4.7.6 At the Duke of York in the evening</p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":886,"lock":null}
14:36:41.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/935
14:36:41.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":935,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":5,"day":7,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Delightful weather. Wind East &amp; SE. Walked beyond Marsden Rocks with Webb, Gosling RNW To see <span class=highlight_yellow>exfrenements</span> laid for saving shipwrecked men, my means of a rope ladder &amp; air jacket. Returned home to dinner. Webb &amp; Gosling dinned with us. Afterwards walked to Tynemouth &amp; spent the evening at Webb </p>","pageId":817,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":887,"lock":null}
14:36:41.866 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
