14:36:41.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":963,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":1,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A fine morning. Wind blowing fresh at SW. A Harry, Nicholson took a walk around Tynmouth &amp; at 2 o'clock dined with I Richardson MP at 4 o'clock. We crossed the water to attend the races which were all won easy by chamber horses. Got home at 10 o'clock</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":915,"lock":null}
14:36:41.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/964
14:36:41.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":964,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day, particularly the afternoon. Wind west, Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Met Smiths, Hannah, I Weston. Webb took her &amp; the <span class=highlight_yellow>Blenkensops</span> on board the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mers</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ard</span> Tatter, laying too off the Castle &amp; gave them a few hours sail to the Sunderland. Dined at home &amp; the afternoon being so fine tempted H Harry, for the sake of the walk to go to the tents on the sands but there was no racing. One match</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":916,"lock":null}
14:36:41.879 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/964
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":964,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A most beautiful day, particularly the afternoon. Wind west, Took a walk with Captain Webb to Tynemouth. Met Smiths, Hannah, I Weston. Webb took her &amp; the <span class=highlight_yellow>Blenkensops</span> on board the <span class=highlight_yellow>Mers</span><span class=highlight_yellow>er</span><span class=highlight_yellow>ard</span> Tatter, laying too off the Castle &amp; gave them a few hours sail to the Sunderland. Dined at home &amp; the afternoon being so fine tempted H Harry, for the sake of the walk to go to the tents on the sands but there was no racing. One match</p>","pageId":823,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":916,"lock":null}
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/965
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":965,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with rain. Wind SSE About 11o'clock the weather cleared up, Harry, Nicholson &amp; I walked with I Richardson in his cable up to Mr Sadlers at the Point &amp; then to Jarrow Slake where we had two hours fishing, but very poor sport, we afterwards landed &amp; dined with Sadler &amp; spent a very pleasant day. It turned out a rainy evening &amp; we had a wet &amp; unpleasant walk home</p>","pageId":824,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":917,"lock":null}
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/965
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":965,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning with rain. Wind SSE About 11o'clock the weather cleared up, Harry, Nicholson &amp; I walked with I Richardson in his cable up to Mr Sadlers at the Point &amp; then to Jarrow Slake where we had two hours fishing, but very poor sport, we afterwards landed &amp; dined with Sadler &amp; spent a very pleasant day. It turned out a rainy evening &amp; we had a wet &amp; unpleasant walk home</p>","pageId":824,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":917,"lock":null}
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/966
14:36:41.880 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":966,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A stormy morning. Wind N by W. Accepted Baleracus bill at 5 <span class=highlight_yellow>mos</span> for the archangel <span class=highlight_yellow>prrorraccon</span> for &pound;12.13.8 down 22<sup>nd</sup> but from the great fall of rain last night a heavy fresh in the season, take <span class=highlight_yellow>ch</span> with the wind drove two sloops upon the headland &amp; a brig over the points of the sand where the rode very heavy for 2 or 3 hours, but the life boat pulling some hands on board the got a offering upon his cable &amp; thus succeeded in taking her to sea. Turned out a fine afternoon. Walked in the evening to Tynemouth to near the band of the 80<sup>th</sup> Regiment</p>","pageId":824,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":918,"lock":null}
