14:36:41.884 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":974,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":17,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Fair weather after a great deal of rain in the night but still blowing hard at NE &amp; cold Received a letter &amp; notes from ABS. Took a walk around by Cullercoat Fields &amp; Tynemouth. Found Mrs Dixon at the house on my return. Dined at home &amp; in the evening again walked to Tynemouth. Finished at the Duke of York</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":926,"lock":null}
14:36:41.884 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/975
14:36:41.884 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":975,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":6,"day":18,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>Another wet morning Wind West. Walked to Tynemouth after breakfast &amp; saw the soldiers parading. Returned by the fields. Dined at home. Wrote to Fanny Smith that Emma would meet his at Morpeth on Thursday next. Paid monthly money for the Hope to do which I drew on Chapmans for &pound;20. Turned out a wet evening &amp; at bed time it was a deluge</p>","pageId":826,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":927,"lock":null}
