14:36:41.891 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":99,"version":0,"year":1828,"month":4,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A very cold day with a little rain. Wind NNE. Dined on board the Hope. Had a very pleasant party.  J Tinley, H Harry &amp; Mr Marks. Received a letter from William</p>","pageId":693,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":94,"lock":null}
14:36:41.891 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/990
14:36:41.891 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":990,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After a night of heavy rain the weather cleared up a little. Wind SE &amp; thick. Received a letter from Ryan L Parkinson, Sackville Street, Dublin stating that nothing had been done with the Fitznanances affairs. At 12 o'clock this solders with the band marched out the garrison &amp; afterwards with the peaceful <span class=highlight_yellow>inhabited</span> in procession &amp; winner racecourse of people marched round the town &amp; proclaimed king William 4<sup>th</sup>. In the afternoon a party of us dined at the George Tavern &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":830,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":941,"lock":null}
