14:36:41.891 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":990,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":2,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>After a night of heavy rain the weather cleared up a little. Wind SE &amp; thick. Received a letter from Ryan L Parkinson, Sackville Street, Dublin stating that nothing had been done with the Fitznanances affairs. At 12 o'clock this solders with the band marched out the garrison &amp; afterwards with the peaceful <span class=highlight_yellow>inhabited</span> in procession &amp; winner racecourse of people marched round the town &amp; proclaimed king William 4<sup>th</sup>. In the afternoon a party of us dined at the George Tavern &amp; spent a very pleasant day</p>","pageId":830,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":941,"lock":null}
14:36:41.891 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/991
14:36:41.891 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":991,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. Walked to Tynemouth. Much to my surprise met with Mrs Lumley and Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Bcagdon</span> who had arrived by sea. The long <span class=highlight_yellow>gifore</span>. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon Webb Hopkins the boy &amp; I went in a boat to fish but had no sport, weather unpleasant &amp; thick.</p>","pageId":830,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":942,"lock":null}
14:36:41.891 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
14:36:41.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - publish: topic: diaries/fragments/991
14:36:41.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -          value: {"id":991,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":3,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A beautiful morning. Wind SE. Walked to Tynemouth. Much to my surprise met with Mrs Lumley and Mrs <span class=highlight_yellow>Bcagdon</span> who had arrived by sea. The long <span class=highlight_yellow>gifore</span>. Dined at home &amp; in the afternoon Webb Hopkins the boy &amp; I went in a boat to fish but had no sport, weather unpleasant &amp; thick.</p>","pageId":830,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":942,"lock":null}
14:36:41.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise - Difference detected on topic: diaries/fragments/992
14:36:41.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           DB:   {"id":992,"version":0,"year":1830,"month":7,"day":4,"sequence":1.0000,"text":"<p>A dull morning. Wind ESE Did not go to church. Walked to Tynemouth. Attended afternoon services A Mr Hicks preached. Dined with I Tealey &amp; in the evening again walked to Tynemouth, an immense number of people there</p>","pageId":831,"type":"MARQUEE","imageId":null,"marqueeId":943,"lock":null}
14:36:41.892 [Test worker] INFO  com.rsmaxwell.diaries.responder.sync.Synchronise -           Tree: null
